#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Seeds of Sustenance - The owner of the Spiced Honey Tavern has been having "
"an issue keeping her pantry stocked, as goods have slowly but surely "
"vanishing in the night. Worried about her customers going hungry, she "
"reached out to you, hoping for a moment of your time."
msgstr ""
"Semillas de sustento: a la dueña de la taberna La Miel Especiada le cuesta "
"mantener la despensa llena, porque la mercancía desaparece poco a poco por "
"las noches. Preocupada por que sus clientes pasen hambre, ha acudido a ti "
"con la esperanza de que le dediques un momento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Only the best for Lira. I'll need to harvest some fresh produce, then hand "
"it over."
msgstr ""
"Para Lira, solo lo mejor. Tendré que cosechar productos frescos y luego "
"entregárselos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "These look great, hopefully it'll be enough to last her a while."
msgstr "Tienen una pinta estupenda, ojalá le basten para una temporada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you walk into the warm tavern, a middle-aged woman rushes by you in a blur, carrying a half dozen tankards of ale, then quickly setting them in front of two excited looking patrons.\n"
"The whole place is buzzing with rowdy energy, but it remains light and warm. Despite all people clamoring for her attention, they quickly fall to silence as Lira holds up her hand. She gives you a warm embrace, then pinches your cheek shortly afterward."
msgstr ""
"Al entrar en la cálida taberna, una mujer de mediana edad pasa a toda prisa a tu lado con media docena de jarras de cerveza y las deja enseguida delante de dos clientes con cara de entusiasmo.\n"
"Todo el local bulle de energía alborotada, pero el ambiente sigue siendo alegre y acogedor. Aunque todos reclaman su atención, se quedan en silencio en cuanto Lira levanta la mano. Te da un abrazo cariñoso y, poco después, te pellizca la mejilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's so lovely to see you [i]{0}[/i]. Thank you for coming to see me on such"
" short notice."
msgstr ""
"Qué alegría verte, [i]{0}[/i]. Gracias por venir a verme con tan poco aviso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Of course, Lira, any time. You sounded urgent in the note you sent me, how "
"can I help?"
msgstr ""
"Claro, Lira, cuando quieras. Tu nota sonaba urgente, ¿en qué te puedo "
"ayudar?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We've been running through our food supply far faster than we should be as "
"of these last few weeks. I don't know where it could possibly be going, but "
"it's a problem."
msgstr ""
"Estas últimas semanas estamos gastando las provisiones de comida mucho más "
"rápido de lo normal. No sé adónde puede ir a parar, pero es un problema."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I can only imagine, looks like you're feeding half the town in here. "
"Business is going well, it'd seem?"
msgstr ""
"Me lo imagino, parece que das de comer a medio pueblo. El negocio va bien, "
"por lo que veo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Half of Azamire, and a bit from every nearby town, too. If I don't find a "
"way to get some fresh produce, I might have to start turning folks away."
msgstr ""
"A media Azamire y a un poco de cada pueblo de los alrededores. Si no "
"encuentro la forma de conseguir productos frescos, tendré que empezar a "
"rechazar a la gente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Don't worry, I can always find a bit of time to help out. What do you need "
"the most?"
msgstr ""
"No te preocupes, siempre encuentro un rato para echar una mano. ¿Qué es lo "
"que más necesitas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Thank you so much... I'd like to cook up some stew. Some potatoes and onions"
" would keep this place happy and fed for quite a while, if it's really not "
"too much trouble."
msgstr ""
"Muchísimas gracias... Me gustaría preparar un estofado. Unas patatas y "
"cebollas mantendrían a todos contentos y bien comidos durante un buen "
"tiempo, si de verdad no es mucha molestia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That shouldn't be an issue in the slightest. We'll be back soon!"
msgstr "No será ningún problema. ¡Volveremos pronto!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you turn to leave the Spiced Honey Tavern, the quieted customers start to"
" stir once again, chattering among themselves or asking for refills on their"
" ever dwindling pints."
msgstr ""
"Cuando te das la vuelta para salir de la Taberna de la Miel Especiada, los "
"clientes, ahora callados, empiezan a animarse de nuevo, charlando entre "
"ellos o pidiendo que les rellenen las jarras, cada vez más vacías."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's a large fireplace, it'll take a lot of wood to fill, and a decent bit "
"of effort to get it all burning."
msgstr ""
"Es una chimenea grande, hará falta mucha leña para llenarla y bastante "
"esfuerzo para que arda toda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A few folks begin to crowd around the fire, enjoying the warmth, now all "
"that's left is to wait for Lira's stew. [Burn] X/X [Oak Logs] - [Complete "
"Button]"
msgstr ""
"Unas cuantas personas se arremolinan junto al fuego para disfrutar del "
"calor; ahora solo queda esperar al estofado de Lira. [Burn] X/X [Oak Logs], "
"[Complete Button]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With fresh produce in tow, you make your way back into the Spiced Honey Tavern. A couple of excited looking patrons eye the vegetables, knowing that they'll soon have it cooked and on their table.\n"
"\n"
"Lira beams when she sees you. She motions for you to hand your haul over to a large, bearded man who has an apron half-tied around him."
msgstr ""
"Con los productos frescos a cuestas, vuelves a la Taberna de la Miel Especiada. Un par de clientes entusiasmados miran las verduras, sabiendo que pronto las tendrán cocinadas en la mesa.\n"
"\n"
"Lira sonríe radiante al verte. Te indica con un gesto que entregues lo que traes a un hombre grande y barbudo con un delantal a medio atar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Thank you so much! We'll get them cleaned up and cooking soon. I don't "
"suppose I could trouble you just a little further..?"
msgstr ""
"¡Muchísimas gracias! Las limpiaremos y las pondremos al fuego enseguida. "
"¿Podría molestarte un poquito más...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "With...?"
msgstr "¿Con...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well... The fire's gone out. It's going to take a bit to wash and cut "
"everything, so if you could get it lit for me, it'd be a huge help."
msgstr ""
"Bueno... El fuego se ha apagado. Lavar y cortar todo nos llevará un rato, "
"así que si pudieras encenderlo, me harías un gran favor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm on it, but it's going to cost you..."
msgstr "Me pongo con ello, pero te va a costar..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh..? Well, that's okay, I suppose. You've worked hard, and the tavern is "
"doing well. How much for everything?"
msgstr ""
"¿Ah, sí...? Bueno, supongo que está bien. Has trabajado mucho y a la taberna"
" le va bien. ¿Cuánto por todo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well... I'd say at least two bowls, and two tankards, too?"
msgstr "Pues... yo diría que al menos dos cuencos, y dos jarras también."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And here I thought you were going to ring me dry for saving my business. You"
" get that fire lit and you can drink until I need to get Rowan to come pick "
"you up off the floor."
msgstr ""
"Y yo que pensaba que me ibas a dejar sin blanca por salvarme el negocio. Tú "
"enciende ese fuego y podrás beber hasta que tenga que pedirle a Rowan que te"
" recoja del suelo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Lira gestures to the hearth on the far end of the tavern, and several "
"customers move themselves and their tables away to give you plenty of space "
"to work."
msgstr ""
"Lira señala el hogar del fondo de la taberna, y varios clientes se apartan "
"con sus mesas para dejarte espacio de sobra para trabajar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Lira has Rowan and a few customers help haul out a large stew pot which has been filled with all sorts of hearty vegetables, meats, and a dizzying blend of spices that begins to make your mouth water as the pot slowly begins to bubble. As you wait, Lira is true to her word, and you rarely find your tankards less than half full.\n"
"\n"
"After a couple hours of waiting and a few last dashes of several spices, Lira declares her creation finished. Bowls are distributed and a line quickly forms, everyone eagerly waiting to eat their fill. You enjoy yourself as the tavern becomes more rowdy through the night. Before you know it, you find yourself passed out by the fire, and the tavern mostly empty.\n"
"\n"
"That was a good night."
msgstr ""
"Lira pide a Rowan y a algunos clientes que la ayuden a sacar una gran olla llena de todo tipo de verduras contundentes, carnes y una mezcla vertiginosa de especias que te hace la boca agua mientras la olla empieza a borbotear poco a poco. Mientras esperas, Lira cumple su palabra y tu jarra casi nunca está por debajo de la mitad.\n"
"\n"
"Tras un par de horas de espera y unos últimos pellizcos de especias, Lira da su creación por terminada. Se reparten los cuencos y enseguida se forma una cola; todos esperan con ganas para comer hasta hartarse. Lo pasas en grande mientras la taberna se vuelve cada vez más bulliciosa a lo largo de la noche. Sin darte cuenta, acabas dormido junto al fuego, con la taberna casi vacía.\n"
"\n"
"Fue una buena noche."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Packing Lunch"
msgstr "Preparar el almuerzo"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Packing Lunch - A battle-hardened representative from the Slayers Guild has "
"found himself without the majority of his supplies after a band of robbers "
"stripped him of nearly all his possessions. In shockingly high spirits, the "
"man still wishes to embark on a journey to the nearby Corrupted Farmlands, "
"but will need to restock before he can."
msgstr ""
"Preparar el almuerzo: Un curtido representante del Gremio de Exterminadores "
"se ha quedado sin la mayor parte de sus provisiones después de que una banda"
" de ladrones lo despojara de casi todas sus pertenencias. Con un ánimo "
"sorprendentemente alto, el hombre sigue queriendo emprender un viaje a las "
"cercanas Tierras de cultivo corrompidas, pero antes tendrá que "
"reabastecerse."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What would a man like him even like? Fish, maybe?"
msgstr "¿Qué le gustaría a un hombre como él? ¿Pescado, quizá?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hopefully this will be a suitable enough lunch, then Gol can get on his way."
msgstr "Espero que esto sirva como almuerzo, así Gol podrá seguir su camino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A nearly bare man stands on the side of the road covered by a terrifyingly small loincloth, laughing heartily as a few folks gawk at his form, then rush by while averting their eyes. He flexes in several positions, showing off his incredibly well-built body and empty scabbard, one of the few things the man seems to own. \n"
"\n"
"Hapren quickly approaches you, then points in the man's direction."
msgstr ""
"Un hombre casi desnudo, cubierto solo por un taparrabos terroríficamente pequeño, está a un lado del camino riéndose a carcajadas mientras algunos transeúntes se quedan mirándolo boquiabiertos y luego pasan deprisa apartando la vista. Saca músculo en varias poses, luciendo un cuerpo increíblemente bien formado y una vaina vacía, una de las pocas cosas que parece poseer. \n"
"\n"
"Hapren se te acerca rápidamente y señala al hombre."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "[i]{0}[/i], I beg of you, deal with this man."
msgstr "[i]{0}[/i], te lo suplico, encárgate de este hombre."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Deal with him? What do you want me to do, stab him?"
msgstr "...¿Que me encargue de él? ¿Qué quieres que haga, que lo apuñale?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What?! Heavens, no [i]{0}[/i]! I just want you to talk to him and get him to"
" leave. Or, at the very least, cover up a little."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué? ¡Cielos, no, [i]{0}[/i]! Solo quiero que hables con él y consigas que "
"se vaya. O, como mínimo, que se tape un poco."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And why aren't you doing that already?"
msgstr "¿Y por qué no lo haces tú?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Look at him! The man looks like a tree uprooted itself from the ground, shed"
" its bark, and is now harassing my good citizens! I'll make it worth your "
"while, so please, go!"
msgstr ""
"¡Míralo! ¡Parece un árbol que se ha arrancado del suelo, se ha quitado la "
"corteza y ahora se dedica a acosar a mis buenos ciudadanos! Te compensaré, "
"así que, por favor, ¡ve!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ah! Another comes to admire Gol's form, yes?"
msgstr "¡Ah! Otro que viene a admirar la figura de Gol, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You're an impressive specimen, but no, I'd actually like you to cover up a "
"bit. What brings you around here?"
msgstr ""
"Eres un ejemplar impresionante, pero no, en realidad me gustaría que te "
"taparas un poco. ¿Qué te trae por aquí?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, Gol was making his way towards his target when Gol was accosted by "
"bandits!"
msgstr ""
"¡Pues Gol iba de camino hacia su objetivo cuando unos bandidos asaltaron a "
"Gol!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh! I'm terribly sorry then, let's see if we can get you some clothes and "
"then..."
msgstr ""
"¡Oh! Lo siento muchísimo, a ver si podemos conseguirte algo de ropa y "
"luego..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"HA! Clothes? Nay, they took Gol's supplies and sword! Gol has no need for "
"anything to shield himself from the blows of his enemies."
msgstr ""
"¡JA! ¿Ropa? ¡No, se llevaron las provisiones y la espada de Gol! Gol no "
"necesita nada que lo proteja de los golpes de sus enemigos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So you just... walk around like this?"
msgstr "¿Así que vas por ahí... así?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Aye! They robbers took Gol's lunch as well. Once Gol has had a bite to eat, "
"Gol can continue towards his battle!"
msgstr ""
"¡Sí! Esos ladrones también se llevaron el almuerzo de Gol. ¡En cuanto Gol "
"haya comido algo, Gol podrá seguir hacia su batalla!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I'll see if I can rustle something up for you to eat, then."
msgstr "...Entonces veré si puedo conseguirte algo de comer."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol pats his stomach expectantly as you walk back towards a somewhat "
"relieved Hapren. He gives you a thumbs up and scurries off, leaving you to "
"deal with Gol yourself."
msgstr ""
"Gol se da palmaditas en la barriga, expectante, mientras vuelves junto a un "
"Hapren algo más aliviado. Te levanta el pulgar y se escabulle, dejándote a "
"ti solo con Gol."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I need to make sure the bolts are well-made so they'll hold a man of that "
"size, only way to do that is to do it myself."
msgstr ""
"Tengo que asegurarme de que los virotes estén bien hechos para que aguanten "
"a un hombre de ese tamaño, y la única forma es hacerlos yo mismo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That should do... I hope."
msgstr "Con eso debería bastar... espero."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol looks up expectantly as you approach and hand him the fish. One after "
"another, the man sucks them down, then sighs happily. You're not sure if you"
" saw him chew."
msgstr ""
"Gol levanta la vista, expectante, cuando te acercas y le das el pescado. Uno"
" tras otro, el hombre se los traga y luego suspira feliz. No estás seguro de"
" haberlo visto masticar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Better now?"
msgstr "¿Mejor ahora?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol was pleased by this little snack! The nice lady from the tavern came by "
"with food as well, but battle shall be Gol's main course!"
msgstr ""
"¡Este pequeño tentempié ha complacido a Gol! La amable señora de la taberna "
"también vino con comida, ¡pero la batalla será el plato principal de Gol!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'd imagine that must have been Lira, yeah? Her food's to die for, but I'd "
"imagine that it'd be hard to pay in your current state."
msgstr ""
"Me imagino que sería Lira, ¿no? Su comida está para morirse, pero supongo "
"que te costaría pagarla en tu estado actual."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Only for now! Gol will make back his fortune tenfold once he has pilfered "
"the nearby dungeon. But Gol is not yet set off."
msgstr ""
"¡Solo por ahora! Gol recuperará su fortuna multiplicada por diez en cuanto "
"haya saqueado la mazmorra cercana. Pero Gol aún no ha partido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That would have been too easy, yeah? What's stopping you now?"
msgstr "Habría sido demasiado fácil, ¿no? ¿Qué te lo impide ahora?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Among Gol's possessions was climbing gear that he needed to get to the "
"farmlands. Would you be able to provide some for Gol?"
msgstr ""
"Entre las pertenencias de Gol había equipo de escalada que necesitaba para "
"llegar a las tierras de cultivo. ¿Podrías conseguirle algo a Gol?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh, that's easy, I think there was some boots and hooks left in Lira's "
"tavern. Let me go ge-"
msgstr ""
"Ah, eso es fácil, creo que quedaron unas botas y unos ganchos en la taberna "
"de Lira. Voy a por..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No, no. Traditional gear will neither fit nor hold Gol's magnificent shape. "
"Topaz Bolts will let me climb just fine."
msgstr ""
"No, no. El equipo tradicional no le cabe ni aguanta la magnífica figura de "
"Gol. Con Flechas de metal de topacio podré escalar sin problema."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How??"
msgstr "¿¿Cómo??"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The tips will cut into any surface, if slammed hard enough. Then the iron "
"shafts will hold me!"
msgstr ""
"Las puntas se clavan en cualquier superficie si se golpean con fuerza "
"suficiente. ¡Luego, las varas de hierro me sostendrán!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Are you sure you don't just want the climbing gear..?"
msgstr "¿Seguro que no prefieres el equipo de escalada...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The large man just gestures to his body once again, before striking another-"
"admittedly impressive-pose. You leave to fetch the man his bolts."
msgstr ""
"El hombretón se limita a señalar su cuerpo una vez más antes de adoptar otra"
" pose (hay que reconocer que impresionante). Te marchas a buscarle los "
"virotes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol takes the bolts from you and considers them with a far more meticulous eye than you expected from him. After a while, his face breaks out into a smile as he nods. He claps you on the shoulder hard enough to shake you to your bones, then vows that he will repay you someday. You notice that his loincloth covers even less from behind as he walks away, towards whatever battle he intends to fight.\n"
"\n"
"Hapren and Lira scurry out from inside of the nearby tavern once they see that Gol has departed. Lira asks about the man, seemingly saddened by him not sticking around, as she hoped he'd be able to drink half his weight in ale. Hapren shakes your hand once, thanking you taking care of the man, and says a light prayer hoping that he doesn't return."
msgstr ""
"Gol coge los virotes y los examina con un ojo mucho más meticuloso de lo que esperabas de él. Al cabo de un rato, se le dibuja una sonrisa en la cara y asiente. Te da una palmada en el hombro tan fuerte que te sacude hasta los huesos y jura que algún día te lo pagará. Te fijas en que, por detrás, el taparrabos tapa todavía menos mientras se aleja hacia la batalla que piense librar.\n"
"\n"
"Hapren y Lira salen corriendo de la taberna cercana en cuanto ven que Gol se ha marchado. Lira pregunta por el hombre, algo triste porque no se haya quedado, ya que esperaba que se bebiera la mitad de su peso en cerveza. Hapren te estrecha la mano, te agradece que te hayas ocupado del hombre y reza una breve plegaria para que no vuelva."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Morally Ethical Graverobbing"
msgstr "Saqueo de tumbas moralmente ético"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Morally Ethical Grave Robbing - A long forgotten city filled with treasure, "
"riches, and secrets beyond compare has just been uncovered... maybe. It's "
"quite possible that there's hardly anything at all down there, but there's "
"only one way to find out!"
msgstr ""
"Saqueo de tumbas moralmente ético: Acaban de descubrir una ciudad olvidada "
"hace mucho, llena de tesoros, riquezas y secretos sin igual... o eso parece."
" Es muy posible que ahí abajo no haya casi nada, ¡pero solo hay una forma de"
" averiguarlo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Some steel for the heads, and willow logs for the shafts should be plenty "
"strong enough."
msgstr ""
"Un poco de acero para las cabezas y troncos de sauce para los mangos "
"deberían ser más que resistentes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think this should be plenty to outfit the crew with some new tools."
msgstr ""
"Creo que esto debería bastar para equipar al grupo con herramientas nuevas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A scattered group of dwarves mills about a half excavated hillside, clutching broken tools and caring for what looks like some nasty burns and singed beards. Funnily enough, they seem more worried about their facial hair than their wounds.\n"
"\n"
"An elderly man in a comically large wizard's hat seems surprised, but also pleased, to see you."
msgstr ""
"Un grupo disperso de enanos deambula por una ladera medio excavada, aferrados a herramientas rotas y curándose lo que parecen quemaduras feas y barbas chamuscadas. Curiosamente, parecen más preocupados por su vello facial que por sus heridas.\n"
"\n"
"Un anciano con un sombrero de mago cómicamente grande parece sorprendido, pero también contento, de verte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Why hello there! Say, are you any handy with a pickaxe? Decently strong "
"enough to move rocks from one location to another, maybe?"
msgstr ""
"¡Vaya, hola! Dime, ¿se te da bien el pico? ¿Tienes fuerza suficiente para "
"llevar rocas de un sitio a otro, quizá?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, I'm not too bad at either, but it looks like you've got a whole crew "
"here, why aren't they mining?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, no se me dan mal ninguna de las dos cosas, pero parece que aquí "
"tienes un equipo entero, ¿por qué no están picando?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Because this talentless hack didn't warn us about the tunnel being trapped. "
"It's a good thing that \"Whudgrath Roksmak's Crew is twice the prize at half"
" the size\"... in case you're lookin' for a crew, stranger."
msgstr ""
"Porque este inútil no nos avisó de que el túnel tenía trampas. Menos mal que"
" «el equipo de Whudgrath Roksmak vale el doble con la mitad de altura»... "
"por si buscas un equipo, forastero."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"How dare you sir? I may have wandered off to inspect a few of the enchanted "
"baubles we've found, but I'm far from talentless. Don't you want to learn if"
" it's even worth digging up this hillside before you do so?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo se atreve, señor? Puede que me alejara para examinar algunas de las "
"baratijas encantadas que hemos encontrado, pero de inútil no tengo nada. ¿No"
" quiere saber si merece la pena excavar esta ladera antes de hacerlo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We're dwarves, lad. It's always worth diggin', I just hope my folks can live"
" to tell about it!"
msgstr ""
"Somos enanos, chaval. Siempre merece la pena excavar, ¡solo espero que mi "
"gente viva para contarlo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I thoroughly apologize for my tardiness, but the fact that the ruins are "
"trapped means that there's something inside worth getting at! Most of the "
"trinkets we've unearthed have some kind or form of enchantment as well!"
msgstr ""
"Le pido mil disculpas por mi tardanza, ¡pero que las ruinas tengan trampas "
"significa que dentro hay algo que merece la pena! ¡Además, la mayoría de los"
" cachivaches que hemos desenterrado tienen algún tipo de encantamiento!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll let you two just sort this out..."
msgstr "Os dejo que lo arregléis entre vosotros..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Wait just a sediment. If what Morlin says is true, it sounds like the payday"
" might be worth getting blown up once or twice more."
msgstr ""
"Espera un momento. Si lo que dice Morlin es verdad, parece que la paga "
"podría merecer que nos vuelen por los aires una o dos veces más."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"More than enough for all of us! I'm more interested in the history of the "
"place than anything else, anyway."
msgstr ""
"¡Hay más que suficiente para todos! De todos modos, a mí me interesa más la "
"historia del lugar que cualquier otra cosa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I wouldn't mind myself some fancy magic stuff. What do you need from me?"
msgstr ""
"A mí no me importaría quedarme con algún cacharro mágico elegante. ¿Qué "
"necesitas de mí?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My folks will be fine, but our tools... a little less so. You mind getting "
"us some steel to make more, while we patch ourselves up?"
msgstr ""
"Mi gente se pondrá bien, pero nuestras herramientas... no tanto. ¿Te "
"importaría conseguirnos algo de acero para hacer más mientras nos curamos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll see what I can do."
msgstr "Veré qué puedo hacer."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I have the feeling I'm going to be here a while..."
msgstr "Tengo la sensación de que voy a estar aquí un buen rato..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I must nearly be done..."
msgstr "Ya casi debo de haber terminado..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Whudgrath happily takes the materials from you while his crew gathers round. He snaps his fingers towards Morlin, who quickly heats up the material using few blasts of fire magic.\n"
"\n"
"In a terrifying display of efficiency and speed, using their bare hands and some well-placed smacks of their hammers, the dwarves work the material into shape. Once Morlin cools them, they're then fit to whittled shafts. The whole assembly line starts and finishes just seconds after you take the last bit of material from your bag."
msgstr ""
"Whudgrath coge los materiales con alegría mientras su equipo se reúne a su alrededor. Chasquea los dedos hacia Morlin, que calienta rápidamente el material con unas cuantas ráfagas de magia de fuego.\n"
"\n"
"En una aterradora demostración de eficiencia y rapidez, con sus propias manos y unos martillazos bien colocados, los enanos dan forma al material. Cuando Morlin lo enfría, lo encajan en mangos tallados. Toda la cadena de montaje empieza y termina apenas unos segundos después de que saques el último trozo de material de tu bolsa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Right then! Are we ready to dig?"
msgstr "¡Muy bien! ¿Listos para excavar?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Looks like it! I can only imagine what we could find deeper in... Perhaps "
"more about their way of life? Ties to nearby civilizations?"
msgstr ""
"¡Eso parece! Solo puedo imaginar lo que podríamos encontrar más adentro... "
"¿Quizá más sobre su forma de vida? ¿Vínculos con civilizaciones cercanas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Booze that has been aging for an untold number of years? New, fancy bits and"
" bobs?"
msgstr ""
"¿Licor que lleva envejeciendo un sinfín de años? ¿Chismes nuevos y "
"elegantes?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Am I the only one concerned about there being more traps? Ancient guardians?"
" Diseases that have been lingering for who knows how long? There is a reason"
" this place is a ruin, right?"
msgstr ""
"¿Soy el único al que le preocupa que haya más trampas? ¿Guardianes antiguos?"
" ¿Enfermedades que llevan ahí quién sabe cuánto tiempo? Por algo este lugar "
"está en ruinas, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That all sounds like fun to me. Time to strike the earth!"
msgstr "A mí todo eso me suena divertido. ¡Hora de golpear la tierra!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't suppose I could get you to join them, could I? The sooner this place"
" is dug up, the sooner we can get to exploring it!"
msgstr ""
"¿No podría convencerte de que te unas a ellos? ¡Cuanto antes desenterremos "
"este lugar, antes podremos explorarlo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Before you can get a word in, a pickaxe is thrust into your hands by a "
"passing dwarf, followed by a helmet and a water flask. You're spun around "
"and placed in front of a bit of rubble. Time to get to it."
msgstr ""
"Antes de que puedas decir nada, un enano que pasa te pone un pico en las "
"manos, seguido de un casco y una cantimplora. Te dan la vuelta y te colocan "
"delante de un montón de escombros. Manos a la obra."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Morlin really isn't holding back on asking away, is he?"
msgstr "Morlin no se corta nada a la hora de pedir, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Let's hope that this is everything that Morlin needs to deal with the cursed"
" door."
msgstr ""
"Esperemos que esto sea todo lo que Morlin necesita para encargarse de la "
"puerta maldita."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Sweat pours down your brow as a cart pulled behind a large star-nosed mole the crew has affectionately named 'Moley' swings by.\n"
"The crew loads up the rubble you've broken down as you swing your pickaxe once again. But, instead of the typical smack and shock of resistance you're used to when mining, this time, your tool goes THROUGH the rock. A small, unlit cavern lays in front of you. Just as you call out, the clean-up crew crowds around you, yelling about 'rocks and stones,' whatever that means. Shortly after, you're joined by Whudgrath and Morlin, who filter into the cave and immediately start inspecting a large circular door carved into the wall"
msgstr ""
"El sudor te cae por la frente mientras pasa una carreta tirada por un gran topo de nariz estrellada al que el equipo ha llamado cariñosamente «Topete».\n"
"El equipo carga los escombros que has partido mientras vuelves a blandir el pico. Pero, en lugar del habitual golpe seco y la sacudida de resistencia a la que estás acostumbrado al picar, esta vez tu herramienta ATRAVIESA la roca. Ante ti se abre una pequeña caverna a oscuras. En cuanto das la voz, el equipo de limpieza se agolpa a tu alrededor gritando algo sobre «rocas y piedras», signifique lo que signifique. Poco después se te unen Whudgrath y Morlin, que entran en la cueva y empiezan de inmediato a examinar una gran puerta circular tallada en la pared"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well done! Looks like you've found... something! We've got some kinda door "
"here, hm?"
msgstr ""
"¡Bien hecho! Parece que has encontrado... ¡algo! Aquí tenemos una especie de"
" puerta, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe for a vault?"
msgstr "¿Quizá de una cámara acorazada?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Or to seal something off, perhaps? Either way, it's an exciting find! One "
"that is..."
msgstr ""
"¿O para sellar algo, tal vez? En cualquier caso, ¡es un hallazgo "
"emocionante! Uno que está..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Is... what, exactly?"
msgstr "¿Que está... qué, exactamente?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Trapped, I'm afraid. We're going to have to deactivate it before we go any "
"further."
msgstr ""
"Protegido con una trampa, me temo. Tendremos que desactivarla antes de "
"seguir adelante."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're sure we can't just smack it and run?"
msgstr "¿Seguro que no podemos darle un golpe y salir corriendo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Is that how you blew up last time?"
msgstr "¿Así es como saltasteis por los aires la última vez?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I just like to call it efficiency. I'm coming around to the idea of being "
"blown up, as long as I know it's leading up to a nice payday."
msgstr ""
"Yo prefiero llamarlo eficiencia. Le estoy cogiendo el gusto a eso de saltar "
"por los aires, siempre que sepa que lleva a una buena paga."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No... this one's a curse, from what I'm able to tell. One that'll take a "
"while to remove."
msgstr ""
"No... por lo que puedo ver, esta es una maldición. Una que llevará un tiempo"
" quitar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh? Well, okay then, I can come back later, once you've sorted that out?"
msgstr ""
"¿Ah, sí? Bueno, vale, ¿puedo volver luego, cuando lo hayáis solucionado?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your work is far from done! I'll need you to fetch me some runes required "
"for the spell to lift the curse on the door. I'll have a list done up for "
"you."
msgstr ""
"¡Tu trabajo está lejos de terminar! Necesito que me traigas unas runas para "
"el hechizo que levantará la maldición de la puerta. Te prepararé una lista."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Morlin flicks his hands, and a leaf of paper floats out of his pack and hangs in the air. You can see something already written on it... \"Blindfold, velvet rope, three wheels of cheese...\" But Morlin flicks his hands again and another-blank this time-leaf is produced, while the other immediately combusts. \n"
"\n"
"Words form from nothing, and then the paper floats into your hands. You want to ask about the other list, but decide against it."
msgstr ""
"Morlin agita las manos y una hoja de papel sale flotando de su mochila y se queda suspendida en el aire. Ves que ya hay algo escrito en ella... «Venda para los ojos, cuerda de terciopelo, tres ruedas de queso...». Pero Morlin vuelve a agitar las manos y aparece otra hoja, esta vez en blanco, mientras la primera arde al instante. \n"
"\n"
"Las palabras surgen de la nada y el papel flota hasta tus manos. Te gustaría preguntar por la otra lista, pero decides no hacerlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You are guided down into the dimly lit tunnel as dwarves gather around excitedly, seeing what Morlin has in store. The old wizard gladly takes the runes from you and begins focusing very deeply...\n"
"\n"
"Everyone holds their breath while he works, moving his hands in esoteric swirls and patterns until suddenly, the man... sneezes. But then! With a crack and a flash that bathes the room in cold blue light, a veil of magic slowly rolls off the door and evaporates into the air. Morlin warns everyone not to breathe in the cursed air, and as folks duck and cover their faces with clothes and pulled up shirts, he laughs and swats the air, exclaiming that there's no such thing.\n"
"\n"
"You hold back the urge to take a pickaxe from the wall and stick it into his back as the door slowly rolls into the side of the wall, revealing... a long, cold hallway lined with suits of armor in remarkable condition. At the feet of these, many offerings were laid out ages ago. Withered flowers and fruits have light stains in the stone, almost completely missed because of the small piles of gems, coins, and other small treasures laid out.\n"
"\n"
"Everyone is quite pleased by the discovery, as the immediate payoff is overshadowed by the looming question: What more could lay further below?"
msgstr ""
"Te guían hasta el túnel poco iluminado mientras los enanos se reúnen entusiasmados para ver qué tiene preparado Morlin. El viejo mago coge las runas con gusto y empieza a concentrarse muy profundamente...\n"
"\n"
"Todos contienen la respiración mientras trabaja, moviendo las manos en remolinos y patrones esotéricos hasta que, de repente, el hombre... estornuda. ¡Pero entonces! Con un chasquido y un destello que baña la sala de una fría luz azul, un velo de magia se desprende lentamente de la puerta y se evapora en el aire. Morlin advierte a todos que no respiren el aire maldito, y mientras la gente se agacha y se tapa la cara con ropa y camisas subidas, él se ríe, agita la mano en el aire y exclama que eso no existe.\n"
"\n"
"Contienes las ganas de coger un pico de la pared y clavárselo en la espalda mientras la puerta rueda lentamente hacia el lateral de la pared y revela... un largo y frío pasillo flanqueado por armaduras en un estado notable. A sus pies, hace siglos, se dejaron muchas ofrendas. Las flores y frutas marchitas han dejado leves manchas en la piedra, que casi pasan desapercibidas por los montoncitos de gemas, monedas y otros pequeños tesoros dispuestos alrededor.\n"
"\n"
"A todos les encanta el descubrimiento, aunque la recompensa inmediata queda eclipsada por la pregunta que flota en el aire: ¿qué más podría haber más abajo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Life's A Beach"
msgstr "La vida es una playa"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Life's a Beach - While out for a lovely day of fishing along the Windswept Shores, you managed to find a catch you're not quite sure if you should toss back or not. The grumpy old man is a pain to deal with, but with enough time, he might warm up to you.\n"
"\n"
"Or not."
msgstr ""
"La vida es una playa: Mientras disfrutabas de un día estupendo de pesca a lo largo de las Costas Ventosas, has sacado una captura que no sabes muy bien si devolver al agua o no. El viejo cascarrabias es un incordio, pero con el tiempo suficiente quizá acabe cogiéndote cariño.\n"
"\n"
"O no."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe I'll reel it in, whatever it is."
msgstr "Quizá lo saque, sea lo que sea."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wait a second, I think I've got something!"
msgstr "Espera un momento, ¡creo que he pescado algo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You spend your day relaxing on the coast of the Windswept Shores, enjoying "
"the waves crashing on the beach and sound of wind... sweeping the shore. "
"Like much of the coastline near Azamire, the rocky outcroppings make for "
"dangerous passage for the numerous boats heading up towards the capital, and"
" another victim seems to have dashed itself along the rocks. The shipwreck "
"calls to you, begging you to see what you can pull up from its depths."
msgstr ""
"Pasas el día relajándote en la costa de las Costas Ventosas, disfrutando de "
"las olas que rompen en la playa y del sonido del viento... que azota la "
"costa. Como en buena parte del litoral cercano a Azamire, los salientes "
"rocosos hacen peligroso el paso de los numerosos barcos que se dirigen a la "
"capital, y parece que otra víctima se ha estrellado contra las rocas. El "
"naufragio te llama y te ruega que veas qué puedes sacar de sus "
"profundidades."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Any chance I find something useful? Maybe..."
msgstr "¿Encontraré algo útil? Quizá..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A DIY recipe?"
msgstr "¿Una receta de bricolaje?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "No, no... Who'd toss those out into the water?"
msgstr "No, no... ¿Quién tiraría eso al agua?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A magic bucket?"
msgstr "¿Un cubo mágico?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "No... you can only find those in lakes."
msgstr "No... esos solo se encuentran en los lagos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe an enchanted book?"
msgstr "¿Quizá un libro encantado?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Nah... the pages would be all soggy anyway."
msgstr "Bah... de todos modos las páginas estarían empapadas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You continue thinking of strange things you'd never expect to find in the "
"water while you marrily fish away, occasionally dozing off as you pull in "
"fish after fish. You swear that you can see something floating out by the "
"shipwreck, but every time you look closer, you lose sight of it."
msgstr ""
"Sigues pensando en cosas raras que jamás esperarías encontrar en el agua "
"mientras pescas alegremente, dando alguna que otra cabezada mientras sacas "
"pez tras pez. Juras que ves algo flotando junto al naufragio, pero cada vez "
"que miras con más atención, lo pierdes de vista."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I wonder if I should toss him back..?"
msgstr "¿Debería devolverlo al agua...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe I shouldn't have asked if I could keep him."
msgstr "Quizá no debería haber preguntado si podía quedármelo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your hook is caught on something! It flails and flops and fights like no other fish you've ever caught before. You think for a moment that you've got the ship itself with as much raw energy as your catch fights back with. As you reel in, you see... A MAN!\n"
"\n"
"Waterlogged and a confusing mix of grumpy and appreciative, the man hacks up half the sea once you've pulled him onto shore."
msgstr ""
"¡Tu anzuelo se ha enganchado en algo! Se agita, da coletazos y lucha como ningún otro pez que hayas pescado jamás. Por un momento crees que has enganchado el barco entero, con la energía bruta con la que se resiste tu captura. Al recoger el sedal, ves... ¡UN HOMBRE!\n"
"\n"
"Empapado y con una confusa mezcla de mal humor y gratitud, el hombre escupe medio mar en cuanto lo sacas a la orilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't suppose you're edible, are you?"
msgstr "No serás comestible, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'd quite seriously doubt your morals if you thought so. My name's Dixon, "
"and it seems I've just barely survived a shipwreck."
msgstr ""
"Dudaría muy seriamente de tu moral si lo pensaras. Me llamo Dixon y, al "
"parecer, acabo de sobrevivir por los pelos a un naufragio."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Do I get to keep you?"
msgstr "¿Puedo quedarme contigo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You'd think that you were the one who nearly drowned out there with "
"questions like these. Are you going to tell me where I am?"
msgstr ""
"Con preguntas así, cualquiera diría que eres tú quien casi se ahoga ahí "
"fuera. ¿Vas a decirme dónde estoy?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Currently, you're on my fishing hook, and on the windswept shores."
msgstr "Ahora mismo estás en mi anzuelo, y en las costas ventosas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Most shores I can think of are windswept, you're going to have to be a touch"
" more specific than that."
msgstr ""
"Casi todas las costas que conozco son ventosas, vas a tener que ser un poco "
"más concreto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh, my apologies, I didn't quite emphasize that right. I meant the Windswept"
" Shores. Capital letters n' all."
msgstr ""
"Ay, perdona, no lo he recalcado bien. Me refería a las Costas Ventosas. Con "
"mayúsculas y todo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Far from my home port then. Mind if I join you for a spell?"
msgstr "Lejos de mi puerto, entonces. ¿Te importa que te acompañe un rato?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I just pulled you out of the sea, and the first thing you can think of doing"
" is fishing?"
msgstr ""
"Te acabo de sacar del mar, ¿y lo primero que se te ocurre es ponerte a "
"pescar?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I figured it'd be a good way to get you to pull your damn hook out of my "
"coat."
msgstr ""
"Pensé que sería una buena forma de que sacaras tu maldito anzuelo de mi "
"abrigo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ah... right."
msgstr "Ah... claro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You simply pluck your hook from the man's jacket, then lean away as he "
"coughs up a bit more water. Among the debris that washed ashore, the man "
"finds a decent enough rod and sits down beside you. Any attempts at further "
"conversation are met with grumbles or silence. Eventually, he asks about the"
" nearest town he could rest in, and you mention Azamire. He returns to his "
"silence shortly after."
msgstr ""
"Te limitas a sacar el anzuelo de la chaqueta del hombre y te apartas "
"mientras escupe un poco más de agua. Entre los restos que ha arrastrado la "
"marea, el hombre encuentra una caña bastante decente y se sienta a tu lado. "
"Cualquier intento de seguir conversando recibe gruñidos o silencio. Al "
"final, pregunta por el pueblo más cercano donde pueda descansar y le "
"mencionas Azamire. Poco después vuelve a su silencio."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How do people even use these things?"
msgstr "¿Cómo se usan estas cosas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll stick with a rod for now. Best to give it to Dixon."
msgstr "De momento me quedo con la caña. Mejor se la doy a Dixon."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The man stands and cracks his back, then tosses his catch into a loose bag. "
"He seems to debate if he wants to continue talking to you at all, before he "
"nods."
msgstr ""
"El hombre se levanta, se cruje la espalda y echa su captura en una bolsa "
"holgada. Parece debatirse sobre si quiere seguir hablando contigo antes de "
"asentir."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, thank you for pulling me out of the drink. You might be a touch "
"special, but I can't deny that you helped me out of a jam."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, gracias por sacarme del agua. Puede que seas un poco especial, pero "
"no puedo negar que me has sacado de un apuro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Perhaps it was a little insensitive when I asked if I could eat you."
msgstr "Quizá fue un poco insensible preguntarte si podía comerte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And the other thing?"
msgstr "¿Y lo otro?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well... I did catch you..."
msgstr "Bueno... te pesqué yo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Maybe you should have let me drown."
msgstr "...Quizá deberías haberme dejado ahogarme."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm just kidding, I'm just kidding... Mostly."
msgstr "Es broma, es broma... Casi."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Sure, sure. Speaking of catches, I'm sure you'll catch a lot of junk, but if"
" you stick around here, you might find a decent enough net. You may have "
"even found one already."
msgstr ""
"Ya, ya. Hablando de capturas, seguro que pescarás mucha chatarra, pero si te"
" quedas por aquí, puede que encuentres una red bastante decente. Puede que "
"hasta ya hayas encontrado una."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Interested?"
msgstr "¿Te interesa?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If you wouldn't mind. Usually they run for a decent bit of gold, but perhaps"
" I could offer you a bit of trade instead?"
msgstr ""
"Si no te importa. Normalmente cuestan una buena cantidad de oro, pero ¿quizá"
" podría ofrecerte un intercambio a cambio?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I think we could make something like that work, I'll let you know. I'll find"
" you in town later?"
msgstr ""
"Creo que podríamos llegar a algún acuerdo, ya te diré. ¿Te busco luego en el"
" pueblo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The man nods, seeming content with that, then heads up the road towards "
"Azamire. Maybe you're already feeling wistful, but the shore feels a little "
"bit lonely without his grumbles beside you."
msgstr ""
"El hombre asiente, al parecer conforme, y sube por el camino hacia Azamire. "
"Quizá ya te sientas nostálgico, pero la orilla se siente un poco solitaria "
"sin sus gruñidos a tu lado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Dixon isn't hard to spot. Shortly after arriving back in Azamire, you find that he's already managed to procure himself a cart and he has started to sell off his catch. You offer up the net and he starts to beam, pleased at the quality of it. He mentions that it'll come in handy as a local tavernkeep just swung by, asking if he'd be interested in providing fresh fish for her tavern in exchange for a place to stay, and a bit of pay on top.\n"
"As several more folks begin to crowd around, asking about his prices, he talks about how they happen to be the highest quality fish from far off lands, and that he's basically losing money selling them at these prices. You start to wonder if you could do the same, considering you've got the exact same fish, from the exact same place."
msgstr ""
"No cuesta encontrar a Dixon. Poco después de volver a Azamire, descubres que ya se ha hecho con una carreta y ha empezado a vender su captura. Le ofreces la red y se le ilumina la cara, contento con su calidad. Comenta que le vendrá muy bien, porque una tabernera de la zona acaba de pasar a preguntarle si le interesaría suministrar pescado fresco a su taberna a cambio de alojamiento y un poco de dinero extra.\n"
"Mientras más gente se arremolina a su alrededor preguntando por sus precios, él explica que resulta que es el pescado de mayor calidad de tierras lejanas y que, básicamente, pierde dinero vendiéndolo a esos precios. Empiezas a preguntarte si podrías hacer lo mismo, teniendo en cuenta que tienes exactamente el mismo pescado, del mismo sitio."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Mage in the Making"
msgstr "Maga en ciernes"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Mage in the Making - A young woman has been trying in vain to cram all of "
"her studies into a few fraught hours before her mentor arrives to town, much"
" to the dismay of Lira and her patrons."
msgstr ""
"Maga en ciernes: Una joven intenta en vano meter todos sus estudios en unas "
"pocas horas angustiosas antes de que su mentor llegue al pueblo, para "
"disgusto de Lira y sus clientes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm sure nothing could possibly go wrong arming her."
msgstr "Seguro que darle armas no puede salir mal de ninguna manera."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Right?"
msgstr "¿Verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You hear a cry ring out from the entire tavern followed by several rapid "
"apologies from a distraught lady in the middle of the Spiced Honey Tavern. A"
" concerningly large scorch mark has been left on the floor, with a table or "
"two completely blown to pieces."
msgstr ""
"Oyes un grito que recorre toda la taberna, seguido de varias disculpas "
"atropelladas de una joven angustiada en medio de la Taberna de la Miel "
"Especiada. En el suelo ha quedado una marca de quemadura preocupantemente "
"grande, y una o dos mesas han saltado en pedazos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm sorry! I'm sorry, I- I-, I can pay for that!"
msgstr "¡Lo siento! ¡Lo siento, yo... yo... puedo pagarlo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's fine, sugar, I was needing to replace those tables anyway, and you've "
"already done me the favor of turning them into kindling."
msgstr ""
"No pasa nada, cielo, de todos modos tenía que cambiar esas mesas, y tú ya me"
" has hecho el favor de convertirlas en leña."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Still, your floor, it-"
msgstr "Aun así, tu suelo, está..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Rowan was going to mop today anyway, don't fuss over it so much."
msgstr "Rowan iba a fregar hoy de todos modos, no te preocupes tanto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I know a spell! If I just-"
msgstr "¡Me sé un hechizo! Si solo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think my tavern has seen enough of your magic for now, okay?"
msgstr ""
"Creo que mi taberna ya ha visto bastante de tu magia por ahora, ¿vale?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[i]{0}[/i], how lovely to see you! A new mage has come to town and I'm sure "
"you'd be able to help her out, yeah?"
msgstr ""
"[i]{0}[/i], ¡qué alegría verte! Ha llegado una nueva maga al pueblo y seguro"
" que tú podrías ayudarla, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wait, what? Help her out with-"
msgstr "Espera, ¿qué? Ayudarla con..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"She says she's practicing! It's lovely, I just need her to do it... not "
"here. Thanks, bye!"
msgstr ""
"¡Dice que está practicando! Es un encanto, solo necesito que lo haga... aquí"
" no. ¡Gracias, adiós!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Hi. I'm Magnavous, and I'm... trying to be a mage."
msgstr "...Hola. Soy Magnavous y estoy... intentando ser maga."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think I've gotten a fair bit of the picture. Your studying is..."
msgstr "Creo que me hago una idea. Tus estudios están siendo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Rocky, to say the least. But I think I'm getting close!"
msgstr "Complicados, por decirlo suave. ¡Pero creo que estoy cerca!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Right. Is there anything I can help with?"
msgstr "Ya. ¿Puedo ayudarte en algo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, I seem to have run out of air runes, do you have any that you'd be "
"willing to spare?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, parece que me he quedado sin runas de aire, ¿tienes alguna que puedas"
" darme?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll see if I can come up with some."
msgstr "Veré si puedo conseguir algunas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You and Magnavous were rushed out of Lira's tavern as you talked and found "
"yourself on the porch. Through the window, Lira continues to give you "
"concerned glances, worried she'll have to fix up the front of her "
"establishment. You usher her away from the building, and ask her to practice"
" in a small glade near town, and that you'll come with some air runes as "
"soon as you can."
msgstr ""
"Mientras hablabais, Lira os ha echado a ti y a Magnavous de la taberna y "
"habéis acabado en el porche. A través de la ventana, Lira sigue lanzándote "
"miradas de preocupación, temiendo tener que arreglar la fachada de su local."
" Alejas a la joven del edificio, le pides que practique en un pequeño claro "
"cerca del pueblo y le dices que irás con unas runas de aire en cuanto "
"puedas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I never fancied myself a teacher, but let's take a stab at it."
msgstr "Nunca me he visto como profesor, pero vamos a intentarlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's hope she caught all that."
msgstr "Esperemos que se haya quedado con todo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With the few supplies she had left, it'd seem that Magnavous has turned the "
"serene glade you once adored into a smoking crater. A smouldering tree "
"breaks at the middle and crashes to the ground as you approach."
msgstr ""
"Con las pocas provisiones que le quedaban, parece que Magnavous ha "
"convertido el sereno claro que tanto te gustaba en un cráter humeante. Un "
"árbol que arde sin llama se parte por la mitad y se desploma al suelo cuando"
" te acercas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I suppose no more picnics here for a little while..."
msgstr "Supongo que se acabaron los pícnics aquí durante una temporada..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I might be hopeless..."
msgstr "Quizá no tenga remedio..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No, no, not at all! Honestly, your magic seems... shockingly powerful, just "
"a touch..."
msgstr ""
"¡No, no, para nada! Sinceramente, tu magia parece... sorprendentemente "
"poderosa, solo que un pelín..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Dangerous to myself and everyone around me?"
msgstr "¿Peligrosa para mí y para todos los que me rodean?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I was going to say 'uncontrolled'. I think you're plenty powerful, the issue"
" is more so with the fact that I think you're starting a little too big."
msgstr ""
"Iba a decir «descontrolada». Creo que tienes poder de sobra; el problema es "
"más bien que empiezas demasiado a lo grande."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hmm... But starting small would take more runes, and I can't just ask you to"
" fetch me some every time I want to cast a spell."
msgstr ""
"Mmm... Pero empezar con poco me haría gastar más runas, y no puedo pedirte "
"que me traigas más cada vez que quiera lanzar un hechizo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Have you considered trying to make your own?"
msgstr "¿Has pensado en intentar fabricarlas tú misma?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You can do that?"
msgstr "¿Se puede hacer eso?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Where did you think they came from?"
msgstr "¿De dónde creías que salían?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't know! I was supposed to have a mentor who'd teach me all of this, "
"but he never turned up."
msgstr ""
"¡No lo sé! Se suponía que tendría un mentor que me enseñaría todo esto, pero"
" nunca apareció."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Who was he supposed to be, anyway?"
msgstr "¿Y quién se suponía que era?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I've only heard the stories I've heard in the capital... His name is Morlin,"
" and he's said to be a dashing man."
msgstr ""
"Solo conozco las historias que he oído en la capital... Se llama Morlin y "
"dicen que es un hombre apuesto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"He's a master of the arcane, has felled countless beasts and has unearthed "
"some of the most powerful relics ever found..."
msgstr ""
"Es un maestro de lo arcano, ha abatido a incontables bestias y ha "
"desenterrado algunas de las reliquias más poderosas jamás encontradas..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Um... I think I know him."
msgstr "Eh... Creo que lo conozco."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You've met him!? Is he as wonderful as the stories say? My father sent me "
"here to study under him, and I waited for a long while back in town..."
msgstr ""
"¿¡Lo has conocido!? ¿Es tan maravilloso como dicen las historias? Mi padre "
"me envió aquí a estudiar con él, y lo esperé mucho tiempo en el pueblo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I helped him out for a bit at a dig site nearby... A bit eccentric, but "
"definitely talented."
msgstr ""
"Le ayudé un tiempo en una excavación cercana... Algo excéntrico, pero sin "
"duda con talento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Did he mention me at all? That he had to be off soon to meet his apprentice?"
msgstr ""
"¿Me mencionó? ¿Dijo que tenía que irse pronto para reunirse con su aprendiz?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Uh... No... But the archaeological site he uncovered seems to be quite "
"promising, there's a good chance he's just busy."
msgstr ""
"Eh... No... Pero el yacimiento arqueológico que ha descubierto parece muy "
"prometedor, es muy probable que simplemente esté ocupado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh... okay, hopefully that's what it is! Once I can control my magic a bit "
"better, I can go and meet him myself!"
msgstr ""
"Ah... vale, ¡ojalá sea eso! ¡En cuanto controle un poco mejor mi magia, "
"podré ir a verlo yo misma!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'd like to learn how to make my own runes, can you show me?"
msgstr "Me gustaría aprender a fabricar mis propias runas, ¿me enseñas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You take out a couple of books you had intended to give her and run through "
"the basics of runecrafting. She seems to absorb the information well, "
"nodding along with your explanations even though it was a foreign concept to"
" her just minutes ago."
msgstr ""
"Sacas un par de libros que pensabas darle y repasas con ella los fundamentos"
" de la creación de runas. Parece asimilar bien la información y asiente a "
"tus explicaciones, aunque hace solo unos minutos era un concepto totalmente "
"ajeno para ella."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe she'll be a bit better now?"
msgstr "¿Quizá ahora lo haga un poco mejor?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Fingers crossed."
msgstr "Crucemos los dedos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Magnavous proves to be an exceptionally quick study, and before long she's "
"creating her own air runes with little issue at all. Her propensity to "
"destroy her surroundings with her magic doesn't seem to extend to "
"runecrafting, to which you're incredibly thankful."
msgstr ""
"Magnavous demuestra aprender excepcionalmente rápido, y en poco tiempo ya "
"crea sus propias runas de aire sin apenas problemas. Su tendencia a destruir"
" todo lo que la rodea con su magia no parece extenderse a la creación de "
"runas, cosa que agradeces enormemente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is fantastic! Thank you so much."
msgstr "¡Es fantástico! Muchísimas gracias."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's not a problem at all, I'm happy to help."
msgstr "No es ninguna molestia, me alegra ayudar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Now, maybe I can start a bit smaller..."
msgstr "Ahora quizá pueda empezar con algo más pequeño..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, before you do, how would you feel about using a staff?"
msgstr "Bueno, antes de que lo hagas, ¿qué te parecería usar un bastón?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They helped me focus my magic in the past, but..."
msgstr "En el pasado me ayudaban a concentrar mi magia, pero..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But..?"
msgstr "¿Pero...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My father stopped getting them for me since they got blown up so quickly..."
msgstr ""
"Mi padre dejó de comprármelos porque saltaban por los aires enseguida..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I see. Well, maybe now that you'll be trying with spells a little more "
"suitable to your skill level, it'll go a touch better?"
msgstr ""
"Ya veo. Bueno, quizá ahora que vas a probar con hechizos más adecuados a tu "
"nivel, salga un poquito mejor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What'll I do if I break it though..?"
msgstr "¿Y qué hago si lo rompo...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll make sure to bring a few spares."
msgstr "Me aseguraré de traer unos cuantos de repuesto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'll try practicing with the smaller spells in the meantime! Oh! And maybe "
"I'll make a couple extra runes..."
msgstr ""
"¡Mientras tanto practicaré con los hechizos pequeños! ¡Ah! Y quizá haga un "
"par de runas de más..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you leave Magnavous behind in the crater, you hear a reassuring lack of "
"explosions or other generalized destruction."
msgstr ""
"Al dejar a Magnavous en el cráter, oyes una tranquilizadora ausencia de "
"explosiones y de cualquier otro tipo de destrucción."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Surely... Surely, teaching her to arm herself can't go wrong."
msgstr "Seguro... Seguro que enseñarle a armarse no puede salir mal."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I have faith in her. Kind of."
msgstr "Confío en ella. Más o menos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The crater is no better or worse than you left it, which you'll take as "
"progress. You find Magnavous trying to wash away bits of ash and charred "
"trees with a few well-placed water spells. More often than not the spells "
"completely gouge chunks of earth from the ground, but they more-or-less seem"
" to be going where she's aiming, at least."
msgstr ""
"El cráter no está ni mejor ni peor que como lo dejaste, y lo tomas como un "
"progreso. Encuentras a Magnavous intentando limpiar restos de ceniza y "
"árboles calcinados con unos cuantos hechizos de agua bien dirigidos. La "
"mayoría de las veces los hechizos arrancan trozos enteros de tierra, pero al"
" menos parecen ir más o menos adonde apunta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hello! I'm getting better, I almost don't destroy everything now!"
msgstr "¡Hola! Estoy mejorando, ¡ya casi no destruyo todo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, that's something! Maybe with these, you'll fare even better!"
msgstr "Bueno, ¡algo es algo! ¡Quizá con estos te vaya aún mejor!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They're beautiful! I think these will be perfect for me."
msgstr "¡Son preciosos! Creo que serán perfectos para mí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Thank you, thank you, I try."
msgstr "Gracias, gracias, hago lo que puedo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Soon enough, I'll be able to meet Morlin, and then I'll be able to become a "
"mage worth speaking about, with all of my own tales and adventures..."
msgstr ""
"Muy pronto podré conocer a Morlin, y entonces podré convertirme en una maga "
"digna de mención, con mis propias historias y aventuras..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "About that..."
msgstr "Sobre eso..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Yeah?"
msgstr "¿Sí?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There's a chance your father may have..."
msgstr "Es posible que tu padre te haya..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Lied? I know."
msgstr "¿Mentido? Lo sé."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I know it might be har-"
msgstr "Sé que puede ser du..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wait, what? You already know?"
msgstr "Espera, ¿qué? ¿Ya lo sabes?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yeah. I mean, look around. This is what my magic was like after years of "
"practice."
msgstr ""
"Sí. A ver, mira a tu alrededor. Así era mi magia tras años de práctica."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I got my family into trouble in the capital dozens of times because of my..."
" studies."
msgstr ""
"Metí a mi familia en líos en la capital decenas de veces por mis... "
"estudios."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Being exiled out here isn't all bad, and the fact that Morlin is close... "
"Well, just a happy accident, I suppose!"
msgstr ""
"Que me hayan desterrado aquí no está tan mal, y que Morlin esté cerca... "
"Bueno, ¡supongo que es una feliz casualidad!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're still going to go looking for Morlin anyway?"
msgstr "¿Aun así vas a ir a buscar a Morlin?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Why not? With your help, I'm actually starting to become a bit competent, "
"and if he's just found some new big site to work on..."
msgstr ""
"¿Por qué no? Con tu ayuda estoy empezando a ser algo competente, y si acaba "
"de encontrar un nuevo yacimiento grande en el que trabajar..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Any hands would be helpful, I'm sure."
msgstr "Seguro que cualquier par de manos le viene bien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And if you learn a couple things along the way, help him out here and "
"there..."
msgstr "Y si aprendes un par de cosas por el camino, le ayudas aquí y allá..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "He might legitimately make me his apprentice!"
msgstr "¡Puede que me haga su aprendiz de verdad!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That's not a half bad idea at all."
msgstr "No es mala idea en absoluto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But... before I go... I don't have any more essence. I feel like I'm right "
"on the edge of a breakthrough, could you please get just a bit more for me?"
msgstr ""
"Pero... antes de irme... ya no me queda esencia. Siento que estoy a punto de"
" dar un gran paso, ¿podrías conseguirme un poquito más, por favor?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You sigh, but head off to fetch some more essence to keep Magnavous's "
"studies going somewhat smoothly. If she claims she's close to a "
"breakthrough, might as well foster it."
msgstr ""
"Suspiras, pero vas a buscar más esencia para que los estudios de Magnavous "
"sigan avanzando con cierta normalidad. Si dice que está a punto de dar un "
"gran paso, más vale fomentarlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you come back with essence for Magnavous, you see that the crater is... substantially better? She looks to you with tears in her eyes, before dropping the remnants of a staff and rushing towards you. She wraps you in a hug as you notice that she managed to-you presume-use a combination of water and air spells to clean the ash and soot from her previous attempts as studying, and remove most of the land back to its original shape.\n"
"\n"
"The land is damaged, but her efforts to fix it are clear as day, and you congratulate her on her training and give her a brief hug back. She thanks you for acting as her first mentor, and says that she thinks she's ready to trouble Morlin. You check over her gear and give her the essence and send her on her way. She turns back a few times as she walks off, waving and paying you more compliments than you feel you deserve. You feel as if you've learned just as much as her, just in a different way."
msgstr ""
"Cuando vuelves con la esencia para Magnavous, ves que el cráter está... ¿bastante mejor? Te mira con lágrimas en los ojos, suelta los restos de un bastón y corre hacia ti. Te da un abrazo mientras te das cuenta de que ha conseguido (supones) usar una combinación de hechizos de agua y aire para limpiar la ceniza y el hollín de sus intentos de estudio anteriores y devolver casi todo el terreno a su forma original.\n"
"\n"
"El terreno está dañado, pero sus esfuerzos por repararlo son evidentes, y la felicitas por su entrenamiento y le devuelves un breve abrazo. Te agradece que hayas sido su primer mentor y dice que cree que está lista para importunar a Morlin. Revisas su equipo, le das la esencia y la despides. Se da la vuelta varias veces mientras se aleja, saludando y haciéndote más cumplidos de los que crees merecer. Sientes que has aprendido tanto como ella, solo que de otra manera."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Harvest Festival"
msgstr "Fiesta de la cosecha"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The Harvest Festival - Azamire's Annual Harvest Festival is right around the"
" corner, and everyone is doing their part to help make it as great as it can"
" be. Of course, the town will need your help to make it happen!"
msgstr ""
"La fiesta de la cosecha: la fiesta anual de la cosecha de Azamire está a la "
"vuelta de la esquina y todo el mundo pone de su parte para que salga lo "
"mejor posible. ¡Y, por supuesto, el pueblo necesitará tu ayuda para "
"lograrlo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm not too sure how much they'll need... let's get quite a bit."
msgstr "No sé muy bien cuánto van a necesitar... Mejor consigo bastante."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I hope this is enough."
msgstr "Espero que sea suficiente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"On one of your many frequent outings to Lira's tavern, Hapren sets his "
"sights on you, and immediately beelines over to where you're seated in the "
"corner. He pushes your books aside and flags Lira down, who immediately "
"catches your eye and gives you a sheepish look. She waves away a serving "
"girl who started to walk over, and takes a seat next to you."
msgstr ""
"En una de tus muchas visitas a la taberna de Lira, Hapren te echa el ojo y "
"va directo hacia el rincón donde estás sentado. Aparta tus libros y llama a "
"Lira con un gesto, que enseguida cruza la mirada contigo con cara de apuro. "
"Despacha a una camarera que se acercaba y se sienta a tu lado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well well well, isn't it funny running into you here?"
msgstr "Vaya, vaya, vaya, ¿no es curioso encontrarte aquí?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"When I'm not training or adventuring, I'm basically always here, studying a "
"bit... Why would it be funny to run into me here..."
msgstr ""
"Cuando no estoy entrenando ni de aventuras, prácticamente siempre estoy "
"aquí, estudiando un poco... ¿Por qué iba a ser curioso encontrarme aquí...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Wait, I actually just came in like... two minutes ago. Have you been "
"followin-"
msgstr ""
"Espera, yo acabo de entrar hace... dos minutos. ¿Me has estado sigui...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The specifics aren't important!"
msgstr "¡Los detalles no importan!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What is important is that you deeply care for this town, just like me, "
"right?"
msgstr ""
"Lo que importa es que te preocupas mucho por este pueblo, igual que yo, "
"¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...What do you want?"
msgstr "...¿Qué quieres?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The Harvest Festival is coming up, and we're behind. Please?"
msgstr "Se acerca la fiesta de la cosecha y vamos con retraso. ¿Por favor?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...You could have just asked."
msgstr "...Podrías habérmelo pedido sin más."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But where's the fun in that?"
msgstr "Pero ¿qué gracia tendría eso?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Plus... it's kinda a lot. Lira needs help too."
msgstr "Además... es bastante trabajo. Lira también necesita ayuda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I was kinda the one who told him when you come in here... sorry."
msgstr "Fui yo quien le dijo cuándo sueles venir... lo siento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's okay, but when this is all done, I want enough ale that I cannot walk "
"out of here. Or hear Hapren begging for more assistance."
msgstr ""
"No pasa nada, pero cuando todo esto acabe, quiero tanta cerveza que no pueda"
" salir de aquí por mi propio pie. Ni oír a Hapren suplicando más ayuda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't ask th-"
msgstr "Yo no pido es..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Done."
msgstr "Hecho."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Alright, what do you need?"
msgstr "Muy bien, ¿qué necesitáis?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The two of them go through a whirlwind of planning, talking about decor, food, games, and more while you struggle to both keep up and see your part in it all. Eventually you just settle into the corner and continue pouring over a map you bought off a local surveyor some time ago, until finally, Hapren asks if you caught all of that.\n"
"\n"
"You shake yourself from your stupor and Lira asks if you could bring them enough maple logs to keep the bonfire going, and cook the food for festival. You nod and head out, happy to be away from their prattling."
msgstr ""
"Los dos se lanzan a un torbellino de planes, hablando de decoración, comida, juegos y mucho más, mientras tú te esfuerzas por seguirles el ritmo y por ver cuál es tu papel en todo esto. Al final te acomodas en el rincón y sigues estudiando un mapa que le compraste hace tiempo a un agrimensor de la zona, hasta que por fin Hapren te pregunta si te has enterado de todo.\n"
"\n"
"Sales de tu ensimismamiento y Lira te pregunta si podrías traerles troncos de arce suficientes para mantener la hoguera encendida y cocinar la comida de la fiesta. Asientes y te marchas, contento de alejarte de su parloteo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm going to need you to grow... a bit faster."
msgstr "Vas a tener que crecer... un poco más rápido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They haven't been being very specific about how much stuff they want..."
msgstr "No han concretado mucho cuántas cosas quieren..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you drop off the last load of wood, Hapren claps his hands and pats you "
"on the shoulder, pleased with your work."
msgstr ""
"Cuando dejas la última carga de leña, Hapren da una palmada y te da unas "
"palmaditas en el hombro, satisfecho con tu trabajo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well done! It's genuinely kind of startling just how much you can "
"accomplish."
msgstr "¡Bien hecho! De verdad que asombra todo lo que eres capaz de hacer."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, if it's for Lira and the festival, I'm happy to do it."
msgstr "Bueno, si es para Lira y la fiesta, lo hago con gusto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And for me..?"
msgstr "¿Y para mí...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#. Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json Entities/Quests/create_custom_npc_popup.tscn
msgid "..."
msgstr "..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Where's Lira at?"
msgstr "...¿Dónde está Lira?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Right over here, just checking out what you dropped off! These will be great"
" for the food."
msgstr ""
"¡Aquí mismo, echando un vistazo a lo que has traído! Esto irá de maravilla "
"para la comida."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Yeah? I can't say I've experimented much with the logs I use..."
msgstr ""
"¿Sí? No puedo decir que haya experimentado mucho con los troncos que uso..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"For some dishes, I'd argue it's even more important than the spices you use."
" These maple logs will give our dish a sweet, smoky flavor."
msgstr ""
"Para algunos platos, diría que importa incluso más que las especias. Estos "
"troncos de arce le darán a nuestro plato un sabor dulce y ahumado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Speaking of this dish, I assume we're making Azabuns this year?"
msgstr "Hablando del plato, supongo que este año haremos azabollos, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well of course! We might as well not have the festival at all without 'em! "
"But... we're missing something."
msgstr ""
"¡Pues claro! ¡Sin ellos casi mejor ni celebrar la fiesta! Pero... nos falta "
"algo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What's that?"
msgstr "¿El qué?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, our Harvest Festival is to celebrate... you guessed it, Azamire's "
"harvest, but just like in my pantry, some food has gone missing. But I can't"
" be fussed with that right now."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, nuestra fiesta de la cosecha sirve para celebrar... lo has adivinado,"
" la cosecha de Azamire, pero igual que en mi despensa, ha desaparecido algo "
"de comida. Aunque ahora mismo no puedo preocuparme por eso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We need a fair bit more corn. I've seen you tending the fields from time to "
"time, is that something you can handle?"
msgstr ""
"Necesitamos bastante más maíz. Te he visto cuidar los campos de vez en "
"cuando, ¿podrías encargarte?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll be back before you know it!"
msgstr "¡Volveré antes de que te des cuenta!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You set off for the fields, ready to bolster the last bit of Azamire's "
"harvest for the year, with a bit of your own hard work. Hapren looks on "
"expectantly, waiting to see if you say anything about helping him as well, "
"then turns to Lira with a sad face. She only shakes her head and walks away."
msgstr ""
"Te diriges a los campos, dispuesto a reforzar con tu propio esfuerzo lo que "
"queda de la cosecha de Azamire de este año. Hapren te mira expectante, "
"esperando a ver si dices algo sobre ayudarle a él también, y luego se vuelve"
" hacia Lira con cara triste. Ella solo niega con la cabeza y se aleja."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Take one, cook it, pass it on. Take on, cook it, pass it on..."
msgstr "Coge uno, cocínalo, pásalo. Coge uno, cocínalo, pásalo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think that's almost all of them."
msgstr "Creo que ya casi están todos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You enter the tavern and sling several sacks of corn onto the bar, to which "
"Lira immediately jumps up from her stool, inspects several ears, and nods "
"positively towards you. Without a word, she pushes a tankard of ale into "
"your hands, and waits for you to drink it down."
msgstr ""
"Entras en la taberna y sueltas varios sacos de maíz sobre la barra; Lira "
"salta enseguida de su taburete, examina varias mazorcas y te hace un gesto "
"de aprobación. Sin decir palabra, te pone una jarra de cerveza en las manos "
"y espera a que te la bebas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Thank you, but what's this for?"
msgstr "Gracias, pero ¿y esto a qué viene?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The start of that payment we talked about."
msgstr "Es el primer plazo del pago que acordamos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You know, you ask for ale as payment... often... I know I'm a tavern keeper,"
" but I care for you. Is everything okay at home?"
msgstr ""
"Oye, pides cerveza como pago... a menudo... Sé que soy tabernera, pero me "
"preocupo por ti. ¿Va todo bien en casa?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What..? Yes, of course! Your ale is just to die for, and you know I like the"
" house blend more than anything."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué...? ¡Sí, claro! Es que tu cerveza está de muerte, y sabes que la mezcla"
" de la casa me gusta más que nada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What do you even put in it?"
msgstr "¿Qué le echas, por cierto?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, a bit of coriander, hibiscus, juniper berries, orange peel... But I "
"can't tell you the rest of course, I don't want to lose my leverage over "
"you."
msgstr ""
"Pues un poco de cilantro, hibisco, bayas de enebro, piel de naranja... Pero "
"el resto no te lo puedo decir, claro, no quiero perder mi ventaja sobre ti."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But, speaking of recipes, this corn was the last thing we needed for the "
"Melvor-famous Azabuns!"
msgstr ""
"Pero, hablando de recetas, ¡este maíz era lo último que nos faltaba para los"
" azabollos, famosos en todo Melvor!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'll be calling in some people to help assemble them, but I'll need your "
"help cooking them."
msgstr ""
"Llamaré a algunas personas para que ayuden a montarlos, pero necesitaré que "
"tú los cocines."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't trust these vagabonds to not burn the food, or themselves, but I "
"know you're capable."
msgstr ""
"No me fío de que estos vagabundos no quemen la comida, o a sí mismos, pero "
"sé que tú sabes hacerlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Lira lets out a loud whistle, and like a well-oiled machine the entire tavern pushes the tables together and drapes several clean cloths over them. It'd look like the start of a banquet if it wasn't for the crates of raw ingredients starting to be distributed among the patrons and the couple dozen more citizens that have started filtering in. \n"
"\n"
"The townsfolk crack open the boxes and barrels of raw food and water and get to work in a show of efficency that shocks you. You wonder if Lira has access to some form of magic to make them work with such a fervor. But as you start to guess at her powers, you see tankards distributed and filled as Lira walks around checking progress. Seems you're not the only one taking drinks as payment."
msgstr ""
"Lira suelta un fuerte silbido y, como una máquina bien engrasada, toda la taberna junta las mesas y las cubre con varios manteles limpios. Parecería el comienzo de un banquete si no fuera por las cajas de ingredientes crudos que empiezan a repartirse entre los clientes y la veintena larga de vecinos que han ido entrando. \n"
"\n"
"La gente del pueblo abre las cajas y los barriles de comida cruda y agua y se pone manos a la obra con una eficiencia que te deja de piedra. Te preguntas si Lira tendrá acceso a algún tipo de magia para que trabajen con tanto fervor. Pero, cuando empiezas a especular sobre sus poderes, ves cómo se reparten y se llenan jarras mientras Lira pasea comprobando los avances. Parece que no eres el único que cobra en bebida."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I hope these turn out nicely."
msgstr "Espero que salgan bien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's see what Hapren thinks."
msgstr "A ver qué opina Hapren."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With a good chunk of the town working on them, and a few of Lira's staff helping cook the buns, the work goes faster than expected. It certainly helps that the townsfolk keep the atmosphere lively with several songs while they work and drink, though most of them would be more applicable to working in fields or mines, instead of assembling cute buns.\n"
"\n"
"As you finish, Lira tops off your tankard before she notices someone off near the edge of the tavern. She quickly grabs a tankard from someone nearby who knows better than to argue, and then thrusts it into your hands, then hurries away. You down your fresh drink first, wondering why she gave you another, until-"
msgstr ""
"Con buena parte del pueblo trabajando en ellos y algunos empleados de Lira ayudando a cocinar los bollos, el trabajo avanza más rápido de lo esperado. Ayuda, sin duda, que la gente mantenga el ambiente animado con varias canciones mientras trabaja y bebe, aunque la mayoría pegarían más trabajando en el campo o en las minas que montando bollos monísimos.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando terminas, Lira te rellena la jarra antes de fijarse en alguien que está junto a la entrada de la taberna. Rápidamente le quita la jarra a alguien cercano, que sabe que más vale no discutir, te la pone en las manos y se aleja a toda prisa. Primero te bebes la bebida recién servida, preguntándote por qué te ha dado otra, hasta que..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hello there! How goes the assembly line? Are you free for a second or "
"several?"
msgstr ""
"¡Hola! ¿Qué tal va la cadena de montaje? ¿Tienes un segundo, o varios?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Thanks Lira."
msgstr "...Gracias, Lira."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hmm?"
msgstr "¿Mmm?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Nothing, nothing. Think we're about finished up here, what else do you need?"
msgstr "Nada, nada. Creo que aquí ya casi hemos acabado, ¿qué más necesitas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I've got a lovely idea to light up the town square. I hope to fill some "
"lanterns with some gems from the town's treasury, and when they're lit... I "
"hope it'll glitter beautifully."
msgstr ""
"Tengo una idea preciosa para iluminar la plaza del pueblo. Quiero llenar "
"unos faroles con gemas del tesoro del pueblo y, cuando estén encendidos... "
"espero que brillen de maravilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That's actually... a pretty good idea. Are you worried about thieves at all,"
" though? Sounds like a lot of loot to be leaving out."
msgstr ""
"Eso es... una idea bastante buena. Pero ¿no te preocupan los ladrones? "
"Parece mucho botín para dejarlo a la vista."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They'll be under watch, don't you worry. I've already signed off on the gems"
" being used, but there's just one thing..."
msgstr ""
"Estarán vigilados, no te preocupes. Ya he autorizado el uso de las gemas, "
"pero solo hay una cosa..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You don't have the lanterns and want me to make them?"
msgstr "¿No tienes los faroles y quieres que los haga yo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This is why I always come to you for help! You're always one step ahead of "
"everyone else."
msgstr ""
"¡Por eso siempre acudo a ti en busca de ayuda! Siempre vas un paso por "
"delante de todos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I'll try to be a little less competent in the future."
msgstr "...Intentaré ser un poco menos competente en el futuro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Last thing, I promise. For this event, that is."
msgstr "Es lo último, lo prometo. Para este evento, claro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You leave the assembly line behind as they begin to tidy up and return the "
"tavern back to its usual configuration. Hapren calls out several thank yous "
"as you leave, but you don't turn, lest he throw on another task or two "
"should you pay him any further mind."
msgstr ""
"Dejas atrás la cadena de montaje mientras empiezan a recoger y a devolver la"
" taberna a su disposición habitual. Hapren te da las gracias varias veces "
"mientras te vas, pero no te giras, no vaya a ser que te encargue otra tarea "
"o dos si le prestas más atención."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hapren happily takes the lanterns from you, passing them down a line where a few of Azamire's guards-headed by Jass-drop gemstones into the lanterns and get them hung up. People begin filtering into the square as the sun slowly slips below the horizon. You can't help but start getting swept up in the excitement as more and more of the modest town square is filled with decor, food, and life.\n"
"\n"
"People from all walks of life stop by, many from Azamire, but some from the surrounding villages, bringing plenty of their own special dishes, songs, and traditional garb. Many are just variations on one another, but the differences really stand out between each other.\n"
"\n"
"You dance late into the night and-of course-enjoy your fill of Azabuns and other regional delicacies, pleased with your contributions to the festival, even if you really think Hapren should enlist some more help next time."
msgstr ""
"Hapren recoge encantado los faroles y los pasa por una fila donde varios guardias de Azamire (encabezados por Jass) meten gemas en los faroles y los cuelgan. La gente empieza a llegar a la plaza mientras el sol se oculta poco a poco tras el horizonte. No puedes evitar dejarte llevar por la emoción a medida que la modesta plaza del pueblo se llena de decoración, comida y vida.\n"
"\n"
"Pasa gente de toda condición, mucha de Azamire, pero también de las aldeas de alrededor, que trae sus propios platos especiales, canciones y trajes tradicionales. Muchos son simples variaciones unos de otros, pero las diferencias entre ellos destacan de verdad.\n"
"\n"
"Bailas hasta bien entrada la noche y, por supuesto, te hartas de azabollos y otras delicias de la región, satisfecho con tu aportación a la fiesta, aunque de verdad piensas que Hapren debería buscar algo más de ayuda la próxima vez."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Setting Down Roots"
msgstr "Echar raíces"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Setting Down Roots - The Blackthorn Sisters have made one of their frequent "
"appearances in Azamire, but seem to have brought a bit more than their usual"
" cart of goods. What brings them to town today?"
msgstr ""
"Echar raíces: las hermanas Blackthorn han hecho una de sus frecuentes "
"visitas a Azamire, pero parece que esta vez han traído algo más que su "
"habitual carro de mercancías. ¿Qué las trae hoy al pueblo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I wonder what ever happened to this place?"
msgstr "¿Qué le pasaría a este sitio?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Should be cleaned up enough now. [Talk]"
msgstr "Ya debería estar bastante limpio. [Talk]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You walk up to the large vine and pelt-covered wagon that has parked itself "
"on the edge of town. You see two familiar faces, Petal and Clove, sisters "
"that stop by and sell herbs, potions, pelts, and meat. They sit in front of "
"an old burned-out house on the back of a large wagon packed with furniture, "
"discussing plans for what their new home should look like."
msgstr ""
"Te acercas al gran carro cubierto de enredaderas y pieles que ha aparcado a "
"las afueras del pueblo. Ves dos caras conocidas, Petal y Clove, hermanas que"
" pasan por aquí a vender hierbas, pociones, pieles y carne. Están sentadas "
"en la parte trasera de un gran carro cargado de muebles, frente a una vieja "
"casa calcinada, hablando de cómo debería ser su nuevo hogar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Looks like you've brought a bit more than potions and meat this time, eh?"
msgstr "Parece que esta vez habéis traído algo más que pociones y carne, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's so nice to see you again, it's been too long!"
msgstr "¡Qué alegría volver a verte, ha pasado demasiado tiempo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We finally bit the arrow and decided to set up shop here. It's what Petal "
"wants to do, at least."
msgstr ""
"Por fin nos hemos tragado la flecha y hemos decidido instalarnos aquí. Al "
"menos, es lo que quiere Petal."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Come now, you know I'm looking out for the both of us."
msgstr "Venga ya, sabes que miro por las dos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Plus, Azamire has always been one of our most lucrative stops. Who knows, "
"with how fast this place is growing, maybe we'll do even better than before!"
msgstr ""
"Además, Azamire siempre ha sido una de nuestras paradas más rentables. Quién"
" sabe, con lo rápido que está creciendo este sitio, ¡a lo mejor nos va "
"incluso mejor que antes!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Azamire might be where I rest, but the woods will always be my home. I can't"
" stay tied down for too long."
msgstr ""
"Puede que Azamire sea donde descanso, pero el bosque siempre será mi hogar. "
"No puedo quedarme atada mucho tiempo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, I hope that we'll be able to do our best to make you feel welcome, "
"regardless of where you may be."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, espero que hagamos todo lo posible para que te sientas bienvenida, "
"estés donde estés."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh, don't mind Clove, she's just... trying to appear strong and mysterious."
msgstr ""
"Ay, no le hagas caso a Clove, solo está... intentando parecer fuerte y "
"misteriosa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You know, she always gets excited whenever we get close to Azamire, starts "
"trying to take down big game to show off to yo-"
msgstr ""
"¿Sabes? Siempre se emociona cuando nos acercamos a Azamire, se pone a "
"intentar cazar piezas grandes para lucirse delante de t..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Petal, I prefer animals and monsters, but I can make an exception."
msgstr ""
"Petal, yo prefiero los animales y los monstruos, pero puedo hacer una "
"excepción."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm just teasing you. Just saying that settling down isn't all bad."
msgstr ""
"Solo te estoy tomando el pelo. Solo digo que asentarse no es tan malo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There's certainly worse places to go, I can tell you that."
msgstr "Desde luego, hay sitios peores adonde ir, eso te lo aseguro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Though... I can't say you two have picked the most... lovely of spots in "
"Azamire."
msgstr ""
"Aunque... no puedo decir que hayáis elegido el rincón más... encantador de "
"Azamire."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your mayor said that we could have the place for free, as long as we got it "
"all fixed up."
msgstr ""
"Vuestro alcalde nos dijo que podíamos quedarnos el sitio gratis, siempre que"
" lo arregláramos entero."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"There's so much space for a nice little garden in the back as well! I might "
"not have to constantly trek into the woods to get basic herbs anymore."
msgstr ""
"¡Además, hay muchísimo espacio para un pequeño huerto en la parte de atrás! "
"A lo mejor ya no tengo que adentrarme en el bosque a cada rato para "
"conseguir hierbas básicas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If only there was some strong, helpful individual who'd be willing to help "
"break down all the rubble..."
msgstr ""
"Si al menos hubiera alguien fuerte y servicial dispuesto a ayudar a quitar "
"todos los escombros..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...For a healthy bundle of herbs and meat when we get established?"
msgstr ""
"...¿A cambio de un buen lote de hierbas y carne cuando estemos instaladas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Pass me a shovel, I've got my pickaxe right here."
msgstr "Pásame una pala, el pico ya lo tengo aquí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Petal claps her hands and motions for Clove to hand you a shovel. She rolls "
"her eyes and scoffs, but noticeably shies away-just a bit-when you take it "
"from her. The house is a mess, but the foundation is still good. With a lot "
"of work, it's in a great spot in town, and could be a wonderful home and "
"shop."
msgstr ""
"Petal da una palmada y le indica a Clove que te dé una pala. Ella pone los "
"ojos en blanco y resopla, pero se aparta visiblemente (solo un poco) cuando "
"se la coges. La casa es un desastre, pero los cimientos siguen en buen "
"estado. Con mucho trabajo, y en un sitio tan bueno del pueblo, podría ser un"
" hogar y una tienda magníficos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I wonder what Clove might find for dinner. [Provide] X/X [Steel Arrows] - "
"[Fletching Tab Link]"
msgstr ""
"Me pregunto qué encontrará Clove para cenar. [Provide] X/X [Steel Arrows], "
"[Fletching Tab Link]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "These should do nicely. [Talk]"
msgstr "Con esto debería bastar. [Talk]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Both Petal and Clove work on the house while you break up and remove the "
"rubble. Petal tends to the wild tangle of plants out back, while Clove "
"always seems to be nearby, either breaking down old furniture with a hefty "
"axe, or sweeping up in the spots you've finished. While the two of you work,"
" Clove tries to strike up bits of conversation while Petal stays "
"mysteriously absent, even when she finishes up outside."
msgstr ""
"Petal y Clove trabajan en la casa mientras tú rompes y retiras los "
"escombros. Petal se ocupa de la maraña salvaje de plantas de la parte "
"trasera, mientras que Clove siempre parece estar cerca, ya sea destrozando "
"muebles viejos con un hacha robusta o barriendo las zonas que has terminado."
" Mientras trabajáis, Clove intenta darte conversación, y Petal sigue "
"misteriosamente ausente, incluso cuando acaba fuera."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I guess sticking around here won't be all bad."
msgstr "Supongo que quedarse por aquí no estará tan mal."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No? I don't think so. I get out quite a bit, but it's always nice to have "
"somewhere to come back to."
msgstr ""
"¿No? Yo creo que no. Salgo bastante, pero siempre está bien tener un sitio "
"al que volver."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It doesn't ever feel... smothering? Knowing that people might wonder where "
"you are, fuss after you..."
msgstr ""
"¿Nunca te resulta... asfixiante? Saber que la gente puede preguntarse dónde "
"estás, preocuparse por ti..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Petal doesn't do that already?"
msgstr "¿Petal no lo hace ya?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, yeah, of course, but she's my sister. I don't know, I guess... I don't"
" want folks to start expecting anything of me."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, sí, claro, pero es mi hermana. No sé, supongo que... no quiero que la"
" gente empiece a esperar cosas de mí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't think you'll need to worry too much about that. There's plenty of "
"odd folks around here, you'll fit right in."
msgstr ""
"No creo que tengas que preocuparte mucho por eso. Por aquí hay mucha gente "
"rara, encajarás perfectamente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gee, thanks, I feel welcome already."
msgstr "Vaya, gracias, ya me siento bienvenida."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Any time. I'm kidding, of course, but really, unless you're someone like "
"Lira, who runs the tavern, most people just... go about their days."
msgstr ""
"Cuando quieras. Es broma, claro, pero en serio, a menos que seas alguien "
"como Lira, que lleva la taberna, la mayoría de la gente simplemente... va a "
"lo suyo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Plus, you're a hunter, it's kind of normal that you'll head out for days or "
"even weeks at a time, depending on your mark."
msgstr ""
"Además, eres cazadora, es normal que te ausentes días o incluso semanas, "
"según tu presa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Speaking of which... I don't know the lands too well, I'm used to throwing "
"myself into the woods wherever we travel and just making the best of it."
msgstr ""
"Hablando de eso... No conozco muy bien estas tierras, estoy acostumbrada a "
"meterme en el bosque allá donde viajemos y apañármelas como pueda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But... I think I'll actually start being able to hone my craft a bit, "
"sticking in once place for a while... Getting familar with the landscape and"
" hunting grounds."
msgstr ""
"Pero... creo que por fin voy a poder pulir un poco mi oficio, quedándome en "
"un mismo sitio una temporada... Familiarizarme con el terreno y los cotos de"
" caza."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I might look around a little bit now, and find us some dinner, actually. If "
"you think you can manage without me, that is."
msgstr ""
"Creo que voy a echar un vistazo ahora y buscar algo para cenar, la verdad. "
"Si crees que puedes apañártelas sin mí, claro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll get by, don't worry."
msgstr "Me las arreglaré, no te preocupes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"However... I hope to find us some dinner, too. I know Petal won't let you "
"leave here without feeding you. By any chance, would you happen to have some"
" arrows I could use?"
msgstr ""
"Aunque... también espero encontrar algo para cenar. Sé que Petal no te "
"dejará irte de aquí sin darte de comer. ¿Por casualidad no tendrás unas "
"flechas que pueda usar?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We made a long trek to get here, and I've gone through most of my stock."
msgstr ""
"Hemos hecho un viaje muy largo para llegar aquí y he gastado casi toda mi "
"reserva."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You chuckle at the idea of needing to manage without her, then having her "
"turn around and ask you for help instead. You head out to find some, and as "
"you do, you walk past Petal, who has a dozen or so people in tow, all armed "
"with various tools or carrying lumber. Shockingly efficient, that one."
msgstr ""
"Te ríes por lo bajo de la idea de tener que apañártelas sin ella, para que "
"luego se dé la vuelta y sea ella quien te pida ayuda. Sales a buscar algunas"
" y, al hacerlo, pasas junto a Petal, que lleva detrás a una docena de "
"personas, todas armadas con herramientas diversas o cargando madera. "
"Asombrosamente eficiente, esa mujer."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This stuff grows worse than most weeds. [Cut] X/X [Ambervine Bush] - "
"[Woodcutting Tab Link]"
msgstr ""
"Esto crece peor que la mayoría de las malas hierbas. [Cut] X/X [Ambervine "
"Bush], [Woodcutting Tab Link]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Looking a bit better now. [Talk]"
msgstr "Ya tiene mejor pinta. [Talk]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The arrows you hand to Clove aren't anything special, yet she still takes "
"plenty of time running through a handful of them, inspecting their quality "
"and bend, along with the arrow tips at the end of each, before giving a "
"self-assured nod. She gives a little wave before heading out."
msgstr ""
"Las flechas que le das a Clove no tienen nada de especial, pero aun así se "
"toma su tiempo para revisar un puñado, examinando su calidad y su curvatura,"
" además de las puntas de cada una, antes de asentir con seguridad. Te hace "
"un pequeño gesto con la mano antes de marcharse."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You know, where we come from, giving someone arrows for a hunt is as good as"
" a proposal for marriage?"
msgstr ""
"¿Sabes que, de donde venimos, darle flechas a alguien para una cacería "
"equivale a una propuesta de matrimonio?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Taking an arrow to the shin, I believe it's called, though hardly anyone "
"still believes in that silly custom."
msgstr ""
"Creo que lo llaman «llevarse un flechazo en la espinilla», aunque ya casi "
"nadie cree en esa costumbre tan tonta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Is that so? And where exactly might that be?"
msgstr "¿Ah, sí? ¿Y de dónde es eso exactamente?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's from a district in the capital I highly doubt you've gotten to, don't "
"worry about following up on it."
msgstr ""
"De un barrio de la capital al que dudo mucho que hayas ido, no te molestes "
"en averiguarlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With your professions, I'm surprised you both came from the capital. What "
"made you turn from the city to being..."
msgstr ""
"Con vuestros oficios, me sorprende que las dos vengáis de la capital. ¿Qué "
"os hizo dejar la ciudad para convertiros en...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A couple of women who trek through the boonies and sleep in the dirt?"
msgstr ""
"¿Un par de mujeres que recorren los andurriales y duermen en el suelo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Something like that."
msgstr "Algo así."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Spend that much time around that many people and see what you think of it "
"after a couple decades."
msgstr ""
"Pasa tanto tiempo rodeada de tanta gente y luego me cuentas qué te parece "
"después de un par de décadas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I think we just wanted out, a bit of room to stretch our legs and see what "
"the world had to offer."
msgstr ""
"Creo que simplemente queríamos salir, tener un poco de espacio para estirar "
"las piernas y ver lo que el mundo podía ofrecernos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And now you're settling back down."
msgstr "Y ahora volvéis a asentaros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh, I'm sure we'll still go out and visit all the corners of Melvor from "
"time to time, but you know, neither of us are getting any younger."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, seguro que seguiremos saliendo a visitar todos los rincones de Melvor"
" de vez en cuando, pero ya sabes, ninguna de las dos se está haciendo más "
"joven."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And it's nice to have an occasional bath from time to time. Hard to find "
"that out on the road."
msgstr ""
"Y está bien darse un baño de vez en cuando. Eso cuesta encontrarlo en el "
"camino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I can only imagine. But with how fast your house got put up, I'm sure you "
"could have a whole bathhouse put up in a couple hours if you were so "
"inclined."
msgstr ""
"Me lo imagino. Pero con lo rápido que habéis levantado vuestra casa, seguro "
"que podríais montar unos baños enteros en un par de horas si os lo "
"propusierais."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How'd you get those townsfolk to come and help you so fast?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo has conseguido que la gente del pueblo viniera a ayudarte tan rápido?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, those farmers have plenty of pest issues, I hear, and I just so happen"
" to dabble in poisons along with my normal stock of potions."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, he oído que esos granjeros tienen muchos problemas con las plagas, y "
"da la casualidad de que yo hago mis pinitos con los venenos, además de mi "
"surtido habitual de pociones."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Got anything you think might be handy against... bigger beasts?"
msgstr "¿Tienes algo que pueda servir contra... bestias más grandes?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Not just yet, but I'll keep you in the know. Along with those, I'm working "
"on some herbicides too... took care of most of the tangle in the back, "
"except for those damn Ambervines."
msgstr ""
"Todavía no, pero te mantendré al tanto. Además de eso, estoy trabajando en "
"algunos herbicidas... Me he ocupado de casi toda la maraña de atrás, menos "
"de esas malditas vidámbar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'd ask Clove to go whack them with that axe of hers, but you seemed to have"
" scared her off. Be a dear, would you?"
msgstr ""
"Le pediría a Clove que les diera unos buenos hachazos, pero parece que la "
"has espantado. ¿Me harías el favor?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You roll your eyes and set to work on the brush behind the house, knocking "
"down the Ambervine where you can. Like Petal claimed, many of the other "
"noxious plants that were back here seem to have withered away."
msgstr ""
"Pones los ojos en blanco y te pones a trabajar en la maleza de detrás de la "
"casa, cortando la vidámbar donde puedes. Tal como decía Petal, muchas de las"
" otras plantas nocivas que había aquí parecen haberse marchitado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hopefully Petal hasn't severely poisoned the ground. [Plant] X/X [Sunflower]"
" - [Farming Tab Link]"
msgstr ""
"Ojalá Petal no haya envenenado demasiado la tierra. [Plant] X/X [Sunflower],"
" [Farming Tab Link]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Huh, well, I guess the herbalist knows what she's doing. Who'd guess? "
"[Complete Quest Button]"
msgstr ""
"Vaya, bueno, parece que la herbolaria sabe lo que hace. ¿Quién lo iba a "
"decir? [Complete Quest Button]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You wipe your brow and just start to lean back against the wall of the house"
" when Clove comes in the newly constructed gate and drops several birds on "
"the ground and sets her bow on a nearby crate."
msgstr ""
"Te secas la frente y justo empiezas a apoyarte en la pared de la casa cuando"
" Clove entra por la verja recién construida, deja caer varios pájaros al "
"suelo y apoya el arco en una caja cercana."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"From smacking rocks to whacking bushes, you truly are a menace to the "
"natural world."
msgstr ""
"De machacar rocas a destrozar arbustos, eres una auténtica amenaza para la "
"naturaleza."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Those birds might say the same about you."
msgstr "Esos pájaros podrían decir lo mismo de ti."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't think they'd be saying much of anything at all, anymore. I didn't "
"give them the chance."
msgstr "No creo que ya vayan a decir gran cosa. No les di la oportunidad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You might have sampled one too many of your sister's potions if you think "
"that bushes are any more talkative."
msgstr ""
"Igual has probado una poción de más de tu hermana si crees que los arbustos "
"son más habladores."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Touché."
msgstr "Touché."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Are you about done brutalizing the shrubbery?"
msgstr "¿Has terminado ya de maltratar los matorrales?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They'll bother you no longer, m'lady."
msgstr "No volverán a molestaros, mi señora."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wonderful! Then there's just one final thing for you left to do!"
msgstr "¡Estupendo! ¡Entonces solo te queda una última cosa por hacer!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Where'd the rest of your helpers go?"
msgstr "¿Adónde se han ido el resto de tus ayudantes?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Back to their homes, but they don't get to have dinner here. You do. "
msgstr "A sus casas, pero ellos no cenan aquí. Tú sí. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Plus, it'll put a smile on my dear sister's face. You'd like that, wouldn't "
"you?"
msgstr ""
"Además, le sacará una sonrisa a mi querida hermana. Eso te gustaría, "
"¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Goodness Petal, just get on with it!"
msgstr "¡Por favor, Petal, ve al grano!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Like I mentioned, I want to start growing my own herbs, but I know that "
"blight can be a nasty beast to deal with this time of year."
msgstr ""
"Como te decía, quiero empezar a cultivar mis propias hierbas, pero sé que la"
" plaga puede ser un problema muy serio en esta época del año."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A few sunflowers can do wonders at holding it and a surprising amount of "
"other types of corruption off."
msgstr ""
"Unos cuantos girasoles hacen maravillas para mantenerla a raya, y también "
"una cantidad sorprendente de otros tipos de corrupción."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And how will that put a smile on Clove's face, exactly?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo le va a sacar eso una sonrisa a Clove, exactamente?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They just make me happy... I don't know, always liked 'em."
msgstr "Es que me alegran... No sé, siempre me han gustado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But that hardly matters, the garden is going to be important for keeping any"
" kind of livelihood goin' while we get set up."
msgstr ""
"Pero eso da igual, el huerto va a ser importante para tener algún tipo de "
"sustento mientras nos instalamos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I just hope Petal's herbicides aren't still lingering around."
msgstr "Solo espero que los herbicidas de Petal no sigan rondando por ahí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They shouldn't be, but if you start to feel strange, please take extensive "
"notes, I might want to replicate it for my poisons!"
msgstr ""
"No deberían, pero si empiezas a sentirte raro, por favor, toma notas "
"detalladas, ¡a lo mejor quiero replicarlo para mis venenos!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Petal looks a bit too excited at the prospect of you getting sick from her "
"treated land, while Clove occasionally stops by to check if you're feeling "
"off at all before quickly dismissing herself each time."
msgstr ""
"Petal parece demasiado entusiasmada ante la posibilidad de que enfermes por "
"culpa de su tierra tratada, mientras que Clove se acerca de vez en cuando a "
"comprobar si te encuentras mal, para luego marcharse rápidamente cada vez."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you finish up with the flowers, you catch a whiff of Petal's cooking and let yourself inside. The place isn't 'homey' just yet, but it's far better than the wreck it was just a bit ago, and trust the two of them will give it the final touch-ups it needs.\n"
"\n"
"Clove sets the table and waves you away when you try to help, so you turn to Petal, who brushes past you with three steaming birds balanced on her arm, with a pitcher of... something in the other. \n"
"Using herbs she'd gathered, Petal seasoned the meat to perfection, and Clove produces a few fruits she collected while she was hunting. They pair beautifully with the... concoction that Petal assures you is safe to drink. It's sickly sweet and could be considered tasty, if it weren't for the fact that it leaves you feeling as though you've plunged into an icy lake, but only for a few moments after each sip\n"
"\n"
"Petal pushes your chair towards Clove's every once in a while, and slowly but surely she begins to turn bright red, but plays it off casually. Eventually, you all finish your meals, and Petal takes down a few notes as to how you felt while you drink her beverage. They both thank you for your time, and encourage you to come back once they've set up shop."
msgstr ""
"Cuando terminas con las flores, te llega el aroma de lo que cocina Petal y entras. El sitio aún no es «acogedor», pero está mucho mejor que la ruina que era hace nada, y confías en que las dos le darán los últimos retoques que necesita.\n"
"\n"
"Clove pone la mesa y te aparta con un gesto cuando intentas ayudar, así que te vuelves hacia Petal, que pasa a tu lado con tres pájaros humeantes en equilibrio sobre un brazo y una jarra de... algo en la otra mano. \n"
"Con las hierbas que había recogido, Petal ha sazonado la carne a la perfección, y Clove saca algunas frutas que recogió mientras cazaba. Combinan de maravilla con el... brebaje que Petal te asegura que se puede beber sin peligro. Es empalagosamente dulce y podría considerarse sabroso, de no ser porque te deja la sensación de haberte zambullido en un lago helado, aunque solo durante unos instantes después de cada sorbo.\n"
"\n"
"Petal empuja tu silla hacia la de Clove de vez en cuando, y poco a poco ella empieza a ponerse colorada, aunque disimula con naturalidad. Al final, termináis de cenar y Petal toma unas notas sobre cómo te sientes mientras te bebes su brebaje. Las dos te dan las gracias por tu tiempo y te animan a volver cuando hayan abierto la tienda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A Glittering Trap"
msgstr "Una trampa reluciente"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A Glittering Trap - Gol has been tasked with taking down a beast near "
"Azamire, and what good would a battle be without a friend by your side?"
msgstr ""
"Una trampa reluciente: a Gol le han encargado acabar con una bestia cerca de"
" Azamire, ¿y qué gracia tendría una batalla sin un amigo a tu lado?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Let's make sure these are sturdy enough to handle... whatever we're "
"fighting. [Provide] X/X [Rune Spear] - [Fletching Tab Link]"
msgstr ""
"Asegurémonos de que son lo bastante resistentes para aguantar... lo que sea "
"contra lo que luchemos. [Provide] X/X [Rune Spear], [Fletching Tab Link]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "These look good, let's get Gol. [Talk]"
msgstr "Tienen buena pinta, vamos a por Gol. [Talk]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A small crowd has gathered around in a tight semi-circle near the front of "
"The Spiced Honey Tavern. There are folks cheering, exclaiming for more or "
"begging to be let into the 'act'. Never one to sit out an exciting moment, "
"you make your way into the throngs of people and find Gol, a towering man "
"with more muscles than sense. He sits under a table and hoists it into the "
"air while several tipsy patrons delicately balance on top of it. He laughs "
"as one of them pours a tankard in his mouth from above, then gently lowers "
"the table back down to the ground. He flexes for the crowd as more people "
"climb onto the table, but he stops mid-pose as his eyes meet yours."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño grupo se ha reunido formando un apretado semicírculo cerca de la "
"entrada de la Taberna de la Miel Especiada. Hay gente animando, pidiendo más"
" o rogando que la dejen participar en el «número». Como nunca te pierdes un "
"momento emocionante, te abres paso entre la multitud y encuentras a Gol, un "
"hombre enorme con más músculos que sentido común. Está sentado bajo una mesa"
" y la levanta en el aire mientras varios clientes achispados mantienen el "
"equilibrio sobre ella con cuidado. Se ríe cuando uno de ellos le vierte una "
"jarra en la boca desde arriba y luego baja la mesa suavemente hasta el "
"suelo. Saca músculo ante el público mientras más gente se sube a la mesa, "
"pero se detiene a mitad de la pose cuando sus ojos se cruzan con los tuyos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol must cease his entertainment for now, good people, for Gol has found his"
" friend!"
msgstr ""
"¡Gol debe interrumpir su espectáculo por ahora, buena gente, porque Gol ha "
"encontrado a su amigo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Me?"
msgstr "¿Yo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Of course! You've been instrumental in Gol's rise from a coinless pauper to "
"what he has become today!"
msgstr ""
"¡Por supuesto! ¡Has sido clave en el ascenso de Gol, de mendigo sin una "
"moneda a lo que es hoy!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I will say, you are looking a bit more... put together than last time."
msgstr "He de decir que se te ve un poco más... arreglado que la última vez."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That he is! After Gol's travels, he has found many a coin, armed himself "
"better than before, and is now ready to lead his friend to the same riches!"
msgstr ""
"¡Así es! Tras sus viajes, Gol ha encontrado muchas monedas, se ha armado "
"mejor que antes ¡y ahora está listo para guiar a su amigo hacia las mismas "
"riquezas!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well... I can't say that I'm not a little interested in what you had in "
"mind, but really, that's not necessary. I'm just happy to see you on your "
"feet, and a bit more clothed than last time."
msgstr ""
"Bueno... no voy a negar que me interesa un poco lo que tienes en mente, pero"
" de verdad, no hace falta. Me alegra verte en pie, y un poco más vestido que"
" la última vez."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol must insist! Gol has been tasked with slaying a beast just a short jaunt"
" from here, and with your assistance, Gol is sure to be successful once "
"again!"
msgstr ""
"¡Gol insiste! A Gol le han encargado matar a una bestia a un paseíto de "
"aquí, ¡y con tu ayuda, seguro que Gol vuelve a triunfar!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You may not help Gol fight the creature directly, but setting up a site to "
"fight it is very okay!"
msgstr ""
"Puede que no ayudes a Gol a luchar contra la criatura directamente, ¡pero "
"preparar un lugar para combatirla está más que bien!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh? And what might it be?"
msgstr "¿Ah, sí? ¿Y qué criatura es?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Why remember silly details like the beast's name? Gol only remembers where "
"the beast resides, along with its penchant for gems and shiny things."
msgstr ""
"¿Para qué recordar detalles tontos como el nombre de la bestia? Gol solo "
"recuerda dónde vive la bestia, y su debilidad por las gemas y las cosas "
"brillantes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I'm slightly surprised you used penchant successfully..."
msgstr "...Me sorprende un poco que hayas usado «debilidad» correctamente..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Depending on the day, I’m not sure I’d use that correctly myself."
msgstr "Según el día, no sé si yo mismo la usaría bien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol is smarter than he looks The brain is a muscle just like all others, and"
" should be exercised to keep it sharp."
msgstr ""
"Gol es más listo de lo que parece. El cerebro es un músculo como todos los "
"demás, y hay que ejercitarlo para mantenerlo afilado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"To become smart like Gol, every day, you must split a log with nothing but "
"your head."
msgstr ""
"Para ser listo como Gol, cada día debes partir un tronco sin más ayuda que "
"tu cabeza."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your vision may go fuzzy... and your sense of smell may never be the same. "
"But nothing beats the first time you're able to stoke a fire with wood "
"you've splintered with your own body."
msgstr ""
"Puede que se te nuble la vista... y que tu olfato nunca vuelva a ser el "
"mismo. Pero nada supera la primera vez que avivas un fuego con leña que has "
"astillado con tu propio cuerpo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Do you understand?"
msgstr "¿Lo entiendes?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "More and more by the minute."
msgstr "Cada minuto un poco más."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But... concerning training aside, it really is good to see you well, Gol. "
"I'm down for your adventure. What do we need?"
msgstr ""
"Pero... dejando de lado ese entrenamiento preocupante, me alegra mucho verte"
" bien, Gol. Me apunto a tu aventura. ¿Qué necesitamos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol knew you would be! Gol will lead the way, his sense of direction has "
"been honed as well."
msgstr ""
"¡Gol sabía que te apuntarías! Gol abrirá el camino, también ha perfeccionado"
" su sentido de la orientación."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But before we depart, Gol would like spears, and many of them."
msgstr "Pero antes de partir, a Gol le gustaría tener lanzas, y muchas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The beast Gol has been entrusted to slay is a slippery one, and we will need"
" to prepare an arena to fight it in."
msgstr ""
"La bestia que le han encomendado matar a Gol es escurridiza, y tendremos que"
" preparar una arena donde combatirla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What'll you be doing in the meantime?"
msgstr "¿Y tú qué harás mientras tanto?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"He will consult with the locals to ensure the best path to the beast. Best "
"of luck, friend."
msgstr ""
"Gol consultará a los lugareños para asegurarse del mejor camino hasta la "
"bestia. Mucha suerte, amigo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You watch as Gol dusts himself off and waves to the crowd that has lingered,"
" likely hoping for a bit more amusement before they get on with their days. "
"He calls for Lira with a bit more warmth and familiarity than you were "
"expecting, then the door to the tavern swings shut."
msgstr ""
"Ves cómo Gol se sacude el polvo y saluda a la multitud que se ha quedado, "
"seguramente con la esperanza de divertirse un poco más antes de seguir con "
"su día. Llama a Lira con más calidez y familiaridad de la que esperabas, y "
"luego la puerta de la taberna se cierra tras él."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I feel like I'm arming Gol for war, I hope whatever it is goes down quickly."
" [Provide] X/X [Rune Javelin] - [Fletching Tab Link]"
msgstr ""
"Siento que estoy armando a Gol para una guerra, espero que lo que sea caiga "
"rápido. [Provide] X/X [Rune Javelin], [Fletching Tab Link]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll have a problem if this isn't enough. [Talk]"
msgstr "Tendremos un problema si esto no basta. [Talk]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With your rune spears in tow, you enter the Spiced Honey Tavern and find Gol"
" with several maps laid out in front of him, with a surprisingly methodical "
"route planned out for your journey. Lira comes by and tops off his tankard."
msgstr ""
"Con tus lanzas rúnicas a cuestas, entras en la Taberna de la Miel Especiada "
"y encuentras a Gol con varios mapas desplegados delante, y una ruta "
"sorprendentemente metódica planeada para vuestro viaje. Lira se acerca y le "
"rellena la jarra."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ah, and here's your friend now! You two stay safe, okay?"
msgstr "¡Ah, y aquí llega tu amigo! Tened cuidado los dos, ¿vale?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol is always safe, but he will also ensure his friend's safety as well. You"
" have Gol's word."
msgstr ""
"Gol siempre tiene cuidado, pero también velará por la seguridad de su amigo."
" Tienes la palabra de Gol."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll hold you to that. Best of luck!"
msgstr "Te tomo la palabra. ¡Mucha suerte!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You two seem to get along nicely."
msgstr "Parece que os lleváis muy bien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Lira appreciates Gol's humor and physique in equal measure, along with his "
"ability to drink as much as half her tavern."
msgstr ""
"Lira aprecia el humor y el físico de Gol a partes iguales, además de su "
"capacidad para beberse media taberna."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gol also helps move things around, from time to time."
msgstr "Gol también la ayuda a mover cosas de vez en cuando."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I feel as if you could help her relocate the whole building if you set your "
"mind to it."
msgstr ""
"Me da la sensación de que podrías ayudarla a trasladar el edificio entero si"
" te lo propusieras."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The flimsy building would not hold up to Gol's might. Trust Gol. He has "
"tried before."
msgstr ""
"El endeble edificio no resistiría la fuerza de Gol. Confía en Gol. Ya lo ha "
"intentado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You impress and terrify me."
msgstr "Me impresionas y me aterras a partes iguales."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Are you a building?"
msgstr "¿Eres un edificio?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...No?"
msgstr "...¿No?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Than you have nothing to fear, friend!"
msgstr "¡Entonces no tienes nada que temer, amigo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gol's only enemies are beasts, monsters, and taxes."
msgstr ""
"Los únicos enemigos de Gol son las bestias, los monstruos y los impuestos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not the people that robbed you when we first met?"
msgstr "¿Y la gente que te robó cuando nos conocimos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How'd they pull one over on you, anyway? You're a mountain of a man."
msgstr "Por cierto, ¿cómo consiguieron engañarte? Eres una montaña de hombre."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Nay. Gol refuses to fight people unless his life depends on it."
msgstr ""
"No. Gol se niega a luchar contra personas a menos que su vida dependa de "
"ello."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol has spilled enough blood of his countrymen, Gol wishes to do so no "
"longer."
msgstr ""
"Gol ya ha derramado bastante sangre de sus compatriotas, Gol no desea "
"hacerlo más."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Lucky them, I'd say."
msgstr "Qué suerte la suya, diría yo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Indeed. But this talk has excited Gol. Have you got the spears?"
msgstr ""
"Desde luego. Pero esta charla ha emocionado a Gol. ¿Tienes las lanzas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That I have!"
msgstr "¡Las tengo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Excellent. These look good, but..."
msgstr "Excelente. Tienen buena pinta, pero..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Would you be willing to make some that are also... smaller?"
msgstr "¿Estarías dispuesto a hacer algunas que también sean... más pequeñas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hmmm, you mean like javelins?"
msgstr "Mmm, ¿te refieres a jabalinas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gol is not familiar."
msgstr "Gol no las conoce."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They're... somewhere between bolts and spears, I'd say."
msgstr "Son... algo entre los virotes y las lanzas, diría yo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Then yes, that is what Gol desires! Gol will meet you on the outskirts of "
"town when you are done."
msgstr ""
"¡Entonces sí, eso es lo que Gol desea! Gol se reunirá contigo a las afueras "
"del pueblo cuando acabes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You set off to procure some javelins as well, wondering what kind of beast "
"might need both to take down. You hear a couple passerby call out to Gol, "
"asking if he can spare a moment to help them right an overturned wagon, to "
"which he laughs and asks them to lead the way."
msgstr ""
"Te pones en marcha para conseguir también unas jabalinas, preguntándote qué "
"clase de bestia hará falta abatir con ambas cosas. Oyes a un par de "
"transeúntes llamar a Gol para pedirle que les ayude un momento a enderezar "
"un carro volcado, y él se ríe y les pide que le indiquen el camino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's hope that payout is as good as he claims."
msgstr "Esperemos que la recompensa sea tan buena como dice."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This should be enough to fill a chest or two. [Talk]"
msgstr "Esto debería bastar para llenar un cofre o dos. [Talk]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The javelins have a good heft, and feel solid enough for whatever Gol intends. You wish-not for the first time-that you had more information about what you'd be fighting, but shockingly feel that Gol has the situation handled. The man's... unique, but certainly capable.\n"
"\n"
"When you meet him, he takes the javelins from you and seems pleased, then leads the way deep into the woods. He seems confident about his heading and leads you to a large outcropping that juts from the sand. "
msgstr ""
"Las jabalinas tienen buen peso y parecen lo bastante sólidas para lo que Gol tenga en mente. Deseas (y no por primera vez) tener más información sobre aquello contra lo que vais a luchar, pero, para tu sorpresa, sientes que Gol tiene la situación controlada. El hombre es... peculiar, pero sin duda capaz.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando te reúnes con él, toma las jabalinas y parece satisfecho; luego te guía hasta lo más profundo del bosque. Parece seguro de su rumbo y te lleva hasta un gran saliente rocoso que sobresale de la arena. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This will be an excellent place to lure the sea beast to!"
msgstr "¡Este será un lugar excelente para atraer a la bestia marina!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The sand will dry it out, and the rock will give us solid ground to fight "
"upon, as long as the tide is low."
msgstr ""
"La arena la secará y la roca nos dará suelo firme para luchar, siempre que "
"la marea esté baja."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh, you were being literal when you mentioned it being a slippery beast?"
msgstr ""
"Ah, ¿lo decías en sentido literal cuando dijiste que era una bestia "
"escurridiza?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Aye, so Gol was told, at least. A slimy one at that."
msgstr "Sí, o eso le dijeron a Gol, al menos. Y además viscosa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Out of water, its eyesight is poor, and the beast is said to be quite daft. "
"Gol hopes to lure it up here from the water after preparing a battleground "
"of sorts."
msgstr ""
"Fuera del agua ve mal, y dicen que la bestia es bastante tonta. Gol espera "
"atraerla hasta aquí desde el agua después de preparar una especie de campo "
"de batalla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'll leave the spears with you then, I'm sure you've got something in mind?"
msgstr "Entonces te dejo las lanzas, seguro que tienes algo en mente, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol is something of a visionary when it comes to these kinds of things."
msgstr "Gol es todo un visionario para este tipo de cosas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol has fallen for many a trap in his day, he knows how to think like these "
"beasts."
msgstr ""
"Gol ha caído en muchas trampas en su vida, sabe pensar como estas bestias."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You mentioned it likes shiny things too, hm?"
msgstr "Dijiste que también le gustan las cosas brillantes, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That it does! Again, much like Gol. The beast has good tastes."
msgstr "¡Así es! De nuevo, igual que a Gol. La bestia tiene buen gusto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We will make it seem as if a ship carrying riches has run aground, and "
"spilled forth its plunder."
msgstr ""
"Haremos que parezca que un barco cargado de riquezas ha encallado y ha "
"desparramado su botín."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"There are many wrecks along the coast here, we shall bring them here when "
"the tide rises."
msgstr ""
"Hay muchos naufragios por esta costa, los traeremos aquí cuando suba la "
"marea."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I uh... Don't think I can move whole chunks of ship, Gol."
msgstr "Eh... no creo que pueda mover trozos enteros de barco, Gol."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No, no, of course not. You are better for the finer details, friend, Gol "
"will handle the heavy lifting."
msgstr ""
"No, no, claro que no. Tú eres mejor para los detalles, amigo; Gol se "
"encargará del trabajo pesado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Could you get the gems while Gol finishes up here?"
msgstr "¿Podrías conseguir las gemas mientras Gol termina aquí?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Sounds like a plan to me! See you soon."
msgstr "¡Me parece un buen plan! Hasta pronto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you head off, Gol sets to work on relocating some of the coastal debris. "
"He sinks his fingers into the spongy wood of the back quarter of a wrecked "
"schooner. It's far from a full boat, sure, but even Gol looks small next to "
"it. His feet sink into the sand as he begins to push, and sure enough, the "
"wreck begins to move-slowly but surely-across the sand."
msgstr ""
"Mientras te alejas, Gol se pone manos a la obra para trasladar parte de los "
"restos de la costa. Hunde los dedos en la madera esponjosa de la popa de una"
" goleta naufragada. Desde luego no es un barco entero, pero hasta Gol parece"
" pequeño a su lado. Sus pies se hunden en la arena cuando empieza a empujar "
"y, efectivamente, los restos empiezan a moverse, lento pero seguro, por la "
"arena."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll make this extra messy, so it glows even brighter."
msgstr "Lo dejaré bien desordenado para que brille todavía más."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This should be everything we need. - [Complete Quest Button]"
msgstr "Esto debería ser todo lo que necesitamos. [Complete Quest Button]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You return to the ambush site with enough gems to fill a small chest and "
"find Gol perched on top of his handiwork. The tide is higher than before, "
"sea foam curls and retreats just over the edge of the outcrop. Gol's scene "
"is extraordinarily convincing, with the wreckage arranged to look as though "
"a ship washed ashore and was split on the rocky outcrop. He even seems to "
"have relocated the mast of another ship and propped it up on the wreck, "
"allowing the tattered sail to tangle itself nicely amongst the debris. You "
"carefully wade through the waist-deep water, avoiding the spears jutting out"
" of the sand, and clamber onto the rocky platform."
msgstr ""
"Vuelves al lugar de la emboscada con gemas suficientes para llenar un "
"cofrecito y encuentras a Gol encaramado sobre su obra. La marea está más "
"alta que antes, y la espuma del mar se riza y se retira justo por encima del"
" borde del saliente. La escena de Gol es extraordinariamente convincente, "
"con los restos colocados como si un barco hubiera llegado a la orilla y se "
"hubiera partido contra el saliente rocoso. Hasta parece haber traído el "
"mástil de otro barco y haberlo apuntalado sobre los restos, dejando que la "
"vela hecha jirones se enrede con gracia entre los escombros. Vadeas con "
"cuidado el agua, que te llega a la cintura, esquivando las lanzas que "
"sobresalen de la arena, y trepas a la plataforma rocosa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gol... this is scarily good. You've really outdone yourself!"
msgstr "Gol... esto es aterradoramente bueno. ¡Te has superado!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What can Gol say? He has a knack for setting a good scene."
msgstr "¿Qué puede decir Gol? Tiene un don para montar una buena escena."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The gems look lovely as well. If Gol hadn't assembled this himself, Gol may "
"even wander into this ambush."
msgstr ""
"Las gemas también son preciosas. Si Gol no hubiera montado esto él mismo, "
"puede que incluso cayera en esta emboscada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, do your best not to. You mentioned that the beast had a bounty on its "
"head, yeah?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, intenta no hacerlo. Dijiste que pusieron precio a la cabeza de la "
"bestia, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That it does! It has been tearing through ships like Gol does ale. That's "
"why Gol had this idea in the first place."
msgstr ""
"¡Así es! Ha estado destrozando barcos como Gol se bebe la cerveza. Por eso a"
" Gol se le ocurrió esta idea."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Good line of reasoning, I'd say. So... will the gems be enough, do you "
"think?"
msgstr ""
"Buen razonamiento, diría yo. Entonces... ¿crees que bastará con las gemas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Our hook is good, but Gol thinks we lack bait, still."
msgstr "Nuestro anzuelo es bueno, pero Gol cree que aún nos falta cebo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol is a bit more keen on the... pugilistic arts, and rarely has the "
"patience for fishing."
msgstr ""
"Gol es más aficionado a las... artes pugilísticas, y rara vez tiene "
"paciencia para pescar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol wonders if you know a good way to lure the creature into our ambush."
msgstr ""
"Gol se pregunta si conoces una buena forma de atraer a la criatura a nuestra"
" emboscada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If I were to take some Glowfin and cut them up, I'd say the bait would be "
"pretty convincing for a sea-based monster."
msgstr ""
"Si cogiera unos peces luminosos y los cortara, diría que el cebo resultaría "
"bastante convincente para un monstruo marino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This does sound promising. Gol will put the finishing touches on our "
"battleground while you handle the bait?"
msgstr ""
"Suena prometedor. ¿Gol da los últimos retoques a nuestro campo de batalla "
"mientras tú te encargas del cebo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You nod and set off to gather enough Glowfin bait to lure whatever creature "
"this may be to shore. Gol immediately gets to work on the finer details, "
"putting a surprising amount of care into perfecting the wreck, making it "
"truly look natural."
msgstr ""
"Asientes y te pones en marcha para reunir suficiente cebo de pez luminoso "
"para atraer a la orilla a la criatura que sea. Gol se pone enseguida con los"
" detalles, poniendo un cuidado sorprendente en perfeccionar el naufragio "
"para que parezca de verdad natural."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol seems positively buzzing with energy, pleased to see the plan come together. Gol did a phenomenal job making the wreck look natural, which was only further helped by the tide coming through and helping the wreckage sink into the sand. \n"
"\n"
"You do your best to squeeze the glowfin bait's juice all around the chest before tucking it in amongst the gemstones. In the twilight, the chest looks like a burning beacon, with the glowfin juice refracting off the gemstones radiantly.\n"
"\n"
"Gol leads you away from the chest and you scrub your hands in the water, careful to avoid impaling yourself on the spears tucked into the sand all around your ambush site. After an hour or so of waiting in the water, a wet, hulking monster slowly lifts itself out of the sea and half walks, half slithers towards the gem-filled chest. \n"
"\n"
"Gol slaps your shoulder hard enough to dislocate it, silently yelling in excitment before leaping out of the water and towards the beast, who hardly knows what to make out of the golith running towards it. Gol tosses javelin after javelin, their rune blades sinking into the creature's slimy flesh. He narrowly tucks its large, snapping maw as it turns to retreat towards the water. Like a fish on a barb, the angled spears it walked over now impale it and it shrieks, tearing off long, writhing tail in the process. Gol tries his best to keep hold of the creature, but its thick slime coats him entirely, and it just manages to slip back into the ocean, but not unscathed.\n"
"\n"
"Gol is pleased regardless, claiming that the tail is enough to show most of you twos' efforts. True to his word, he finds you in Azamire several days later with your half of the payout, and you feel it was well-worth the time... but part of you wonders if there's a way to track the beast down and take it out once and for all."
msgstr ""
"Gol parece rebosar energía, contento de ver que el plan sale adelante. Ha hecho un trabajo fenomenal para que el naufragio parezca natural, a lo que también ha ayudado la marea, que ha pasado por encima y ha hundido los restos en la arena. \n"
"\n"
"Haces lo posible por exprimir el jugo del cebo de pez luminoso alrededor del cofre antes de meterlo entre las gemas. En el crepúsculo, el cofre parece un faro en llamas, con el jugo de pez luminoso reflejándose de forma radiante en las gemas.\n"
"\n"
"Gol te aleja del cofre y te frotas las manos en el agua, con cuidado de no empalarte en las lanzas clavadas en la arena alrededor del lugar de la emboscada. Tras una hora o así esperando en el agua, un monstruo enorme y mojado sale lentamente del mar y, medio caminando, medio reptando, se dirige hacia el cofre lleno de gemas. \n"
"\n"
"Gol te da una palmada en el hombro tan fuerte que casi te lo disloca, gritando en silencio de emoción antes de saltar fuera del agua hacia la bestia, que apenas sabe qué pensar del gigantón que corre hacia ella. Gol lanza jabalina tras jabalina, y sus hojas rúnicas se hunden en la carne viscosa de la criatura. Esquiva por poco sus enormes fauces, que se cierran de golpe cuando se da la vuelta para huir hacia el agua. Como un pez en un anzuelo, las lanzas inclinadas sobre las que ha pasado ahora la empalan, y chilla, arrancándose en el proceso su larga y retorcida cola. Gol hace lo posible por sujetar a la criatura, pero su espesa baba lo cubre por completo, y consigue escurrirse de vuelta al océano, aunque no ilesa.\n"
"\n"
"Aun así, Gol está satisfecho y asegura que la cola basta para demostrar el esfuerzo de los dos. Fiel a su palabra, te encuentra en Azamire unos días después con tu mitad de la recompensa, y sientes que ha merecido la pena... pero una parte de ti se pregunta si habrá forma de dar con la bestia y acabar con ella de una vez por todas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The Four Sentries"
msgstr "Los cuatro centinelas"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The Four Sentries - Morlin and his crew have made substantial progress in "
"unearthing the lost civilization you helped uncover, but have run into "
"another roadblock. With your help, perhaps you'll finally uncover the city "
"proper?"
msgstr ""
"Los cuatro centinelas: Morlin y su equipo han avanzado mucho en la "
"excavación de la civilización perdida que ayudaste a descubrir, pero se han "
"topado con otro obstáculo. Con tu ayuda, ¿quizá por fin descubráis la ciudad"
" propiamente dicha?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They're asking for stuff without even seeing me, now..."
msgstr "Ahora me piden cosas sin siquiera verme..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's hope this is plenty. [Talk]"
msgstr "Esperemos que esto sea suficiente. [Talk]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You stumble across Magnavous bumbling through Azamire's square, asking "
"people if they've seen you. Many either shake their heads or mention your "
"various comings and goings, but few have solid answers as to where she could"
" look next. You stand back and watch as she shakes down a couple others, who"
" point you out. She looks pleased to have come across you, and quite a bit "
"more sure of herself than the last time you saw her. She still firmly "
"clutches one of the staves you made her, but she walks far more proudly and "
"confidently."
msgstr ""
"Te encuentras con Magnavous dando tumbos por la plaza de Azamire, "
"preguntando a la gente si te ha visto. Muchos niegan con la cabeza o "
"mencionan tus idas y venidas, pero pocos tienen respuestas claras sobre "
"dónde podría buscar a continuación. Te quedas atrás y observas cómo "
"interroga a un par más, que te señalan. Parece contenta de haberte "
"encontrado, y bastante más segura de sí misma que la última vez que la "
"viste. Todavía aferra con firmeza uno de los báculos que le hiciste, pero "
"camina con mucho más orgullo y confianza."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Having fun standing there and watching me? You could have come and said "
"hello."
msgstr "¿Te diviertes ahí plantado mirándome? Podrías haber venido a saludar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You got there eventually! I wanted to see how long it'd take."
msgstr "¡Al final has llegado! Quería ver cuánto tardabas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, if you've had your fun, we must make haste! I have so much to show "
"you!"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, si ya te has divertido, ¡tenemos que darnos prisa! ¡Tengo muchísimo "
"que enseñarte!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "My mentor Morlin has-"
msgstr "Mi mentor Morlin ha..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wait, he's officially your mentor now?"
msgstr "Espera, ¿ahora es oficialmente tu mentor?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Indeed! With no small part thanks to your help, but I will catch you up "
"along the way."
msgstr ""
"¡Así es! En buena parte gracias a tu ayuda, pero te pondré al día por el "
"camino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The long and short of it-which you'll see when we get there-is that "
"Whudgrath has uncovered what seems to be the gates to the city."
msgstr ""
"Resumiendo (ya lo verás cuando lleguemos), Whudgrath ha desenterrado lo que "
"parecen ser las puertas de la ciudad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But they're locked."
msgstr "Pero están cerradas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But they-"
msgstr "Pero están..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wait, yes, how'd you know?"
msgstr "Espera, sí, ¿cómo lo sabías?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What? Like one of these would ever be simple."
msgstr "¿Qué? Como si alguna de estas cosas fuera a ser sencilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Imagine that. You come out to find me and say, \"Hey [i]{0}[/i], things were"
" incredibly easy and straightforward.\""
msgstr ""
"Imagínatelo. Vienes a buscarme y me dices: «Oye, [i]{0}[/i], todo ha sido "
"facilísimo y sin complicaciones»."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"\"We've taken care of all the hard work, come and collect as many armfuls of"
" treasure as you desire.\""
msgstr ""
"«Ya nos hemos encargado de todo el trabajo duro, ven a llevarte todos los "
"brazados de tesoro que quieras»."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well... yeah, when you put it that way...."
msgstr "Bueno... sí, dicho así..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So, what do ya need?"
msgstr "Bueno, ¿qué necesitas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, the stone is getting harder to work through. Morlin thinks that it may"
" be magically enhanced since we're getting closer to the city."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, cada vez cuesta más abrirse paso por la piedra. Morlin cree que "
"podría estar reforzada con magia, ya que nos acercamos a la ciudad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I have a theory that the properties of Dawnsteel may be enough to get "
"through it but..."
msgstr ""
"Tengo la teoría de que las propiedades del acero del alba podrían bastar "
"para atravesarla, pero..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With all of my magical studies, I wouldn't say I'm particularly suited for "
"mining work."
msgstr ""
"Con todos mis estudios de magia, no diría que estoy especialmente hecha para"
" la minería."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Nothing to be ashamed of. There's a reason Morlin hired a dwarven crew, eh?"
msgstr ""
"No hay nada de qué avergonzarse. Por algo Morlin contrató a un equipo de "
"enanos, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll meet you on the edge of town when I'm ready."
msgstr "Nos vemos a las afueras del pueblo cuando esté listo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You head off in search of enough material to outfit Whudgrath's crew, and "
"then some. No use needing to come back half a dozen times because they "
"needed more tools. Plus, the more useful you make yourself, you could argue "
"in favor of a bigger cut."
msgstr ""
"Te pones en marcha para buscar material suficiente para equipar al equipo de"
" Whudgrath, y algo más. No tiene sentido tener que volver media docena de "
"veces porque necesiten más herramientas. Además, cuanto más útil te hagas, "
"más argumentos tendrás para pedir una parte mayor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm sure this is what I need to do."
msgstr "Estoy seguro de que esto es lo que tengo que hacer."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's see if this stops that vapor. [Insert]"
msgstr "A ver si esto detiene ese vapor. [Insert]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With enough Dawnsteel to outfit a small army, you meet up with Magnavous. She takes you out to the dig site, which has seen some drastic changes since you were here last. The hillside has been completely carved away, revealing that most of what you'd seen previously were ancillary buildings, and possibly even a second, more recent town built over the top of it within the last couple hundred years, according to Magnavous.\n"
"\n"
"Whudgrath meets up with you shortly into your tour of the site, and happily takes the Dawnsteel from you. He leads you on a short walk down a carved out recess in the ground, that ends in two massive doors which rival the capital's famous gate. It’s dim, the ceiling not yet fully carved away, but even so you can make out four enormous slouched statues set into the walls, with all of them being about five times your size, even hunched over as they are. They're all quite weathered, but it's still clear to see they were modeled after wizards of their time, each with painted stone robes and outstretched but empty hands. Most noticeably, they are very obviously not human. They all have four arms and long, rectangular faces. Each has a gemstone set into its forehead and seems to emanate a vapor of some kind..."
msgstr ""
"Con acero del alba suficiente para equipar a un pequeño ejército, te reúnes con Magnavous. Te lleva a la excavación, que ha cambiado drásticamente desde la última vez que estuviste aquí. La ladera ha sido excavada por completo, revelando que la mayor parte de lo que habías visto antes eran edificios auxiliares, y posiblemente incluso un segundo pueblo, más reciente, construido encima en los últimos doscientos años, según Magnavous.\n"
"\n"
"Whudgrath se une a vosotros poco después de empezar la visita y recibe encantado el acero del alba. Os lleva por un breve camino que desciende por una hendidura excavada en el suelo y que termina en dos puertas gigantescas que rivalizan con la famosa puerta de la capital. Está oscuro, porque el techo aún no se ha excavado del todo, pero aun así distingues cuatro enormes estatuas encorvadas incrustadas en las paredes, todas unas cinco veces más grandes que tú, incluso encorvadas como están. Están muy desgastadas, pero aun así se nota que representan a magos de su época, cada uno con túnicas de piedra pintada y manos extendidas, pero vacías. Lo más llamativo es que, a todas luces, no son humanos. Todos tienen cuatro brazos y caras largas y rectangulares. Cada uno tiene una gema engastada en la frente y parece emanar algún tipo de vapor..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Lovely work you've got here... Don't know if you made these or found 'em, "
"but my boys will appreciate it nonetheless."
msgstr ""
"Buen trabajo el que traes... No sé si los has hecho o los has encontrado, "
"pero mis chicos lo agradecerán igualmente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Ha! Won't even make you swing a pick this time, think Morlin's got some more"
" important work for ya."
msgstr ""
"¡Ja! Esta vez ni siquiera te haré blandir un pico, creo que Morlin tiene un "
"trabajo más importante para ti."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yeah? Is it down that same tunnel we found past that cursed door, or... is "
"it... this?"
msgstr ""
"¿Ah, sí? ¿Está por el mismo túnel que encontramos tras aquella puerta "
"maldita, o... es... esto?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Ah, that little passage! Turns out, that was a teeny little side exit that "
"workers used to use..."
msgstr ""
"¡Ah, ese pasadizo! Resulta que era una salida lateral chiquitita que usaban "
"los trabajadores..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Think it ended up leading to a bunkhouse or somethin'."
msgstr "Creo que acabó llevando a un barracón o algo así."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We think these doors lead to the city proper."
msgstr "Creemos que estas puertas llevan a la ciudad propiamente dicha."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And... where our problem lies."
msgstr "Y... ahí está nuestro problema."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'll spare you the finer details, but Whudgrath and his crew have carved out"
" the whole hillside, and we haven't found another way in."
msgstr ""
"Te ahorraré los detalles, pero Whudgrath y su equipo han excavado toda la "
"ladera y no hemos encontrado otra entrada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And I don't assume we can just dig around the doors?"
msgstr "¿Y supongo que no podemos cavar alrededor de las puertas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Be a pretty terrible gate if we could, hm?"
msgstr "Menuda puerta sería si pudiéramos, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Much of what Whudgrath’s crew has dug through seems to be more... loose. The"
" stone of the entrance is magically reinforced."
msgstr ""
"Gran parte de lo que ha excavado el equipo de Whudgrath parece más... "
"suelto. La piedra de la entrada está reforzada con magia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Morlin has been trying-"
msgstr "Morlin ha intentado..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And failing."
msgstr "Sin éxito."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "To find a way to undo it. So, we're stuck with the door."
msgstr ""
"Encontrar la forma de deshacerlo. Así que estamos atascados con la puerta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I see. I don't suppose you've tried knocking?"
msgstr "Ya veo. ¿Supongo que no habéis probado a llamar?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It was the first thing Whudgrath did."
msgstr "Fue lo primero que hizo Whudgrath."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I blew up a lil' bit."
msgstr "Volé un poquito por los aires."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Are you... okay?"
msgstr "¿Estás... bien?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Never better! But now I'm pretty keen on opening it up too. Gotta be "
"something good in there, I'm sure."
msgstr ""
"¡Mejor que nunca! Pero ahora yo también tengo muchas ganas de abrirla. "
"Seguro que dentro hay algo bueno."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Set into the four statues are a set of passages, which, roughly translated, "
"talk about being sealed, armed, and adorned."
msgstr ""
"En las cuatro estatuas hay unos textos que, traducidos a grandes rasgos, "
"hablan de estar sellados, armados y adornados."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, they're wizards, so armed and adorned likely mean... staves and "
"jewelry. As far as sealed though... Maybe it'd stop whatever it is that "
"they're... leaking."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, son magos, así que armados y adornados seguramente significa... "
"báculos y joyas. En cuanto a sellados... Quizá detendría lo que sea que "
"están... soltando."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Ah, the vapor. Morlin took a look at it earlier, worried it was poisonous. "
"It was magical in nature, but it’s anyone’s guess what it was."
msgstr ""
"Ah, el vapor. Morlin le echó un vistazo antes, preocupado por si era "
"venenoso. Era de naturaleza mágica, pero vete a saber qué era."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Any clue on how we can plug them up?"
msgstr "¿Alguna idea de cómo podemos taponarlas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I had a stint in a military company a while back, and it always seemed that "
"the crossbowmen were the best answer to riddling those flimsy little mages "
"with bolts."
msgstr ""
"Hace tiempo pasé una temporada en una compañía militar, y siempre me pareció"
" que los ballesteros eran la mejor respuesta para acribillar a virotazos a "
"esos magos debiluchos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ahem."
msgstr "Ejem."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Er... no offense."
msgstr "Eh... sin ofender."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The gemstones of the four mages stick out to you, and make the answer feel "
"rather clear. If you're to make bolts to 'seal' them, they'd likely line up "
"with the gemstone motif they have going on. "
msgstr ""
"Las gemas de los cuatro magos te llaman la atención y hacen que la respuesta"
" parezca bastante clara. Si vas a hacer virotes para «sellarlas», "
"probablemente deberían seguir el motivo de gemas que tienen. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That seems... pretty sensible, though... morbid."
msgstr "Eso parece... bastante sensato, aunque... macabro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll give it a shot, then."
msgstr "Entonces lo intentaremos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Before you head out, you inspect each of the statues once more while Magnavous and Whudgrath set to work on their own tasks. The site still needs a lot of work. The gate is barely lit by what little sunlight filters in from outside and the few lanterns at its base. You're sure you'll get a better look at the statues when the chamber is fully prepped, but the gemstones still catch the faint cavern light perfectly as you look them over. Topaz, sapphire, ruby, and emerald - all gemstones that'd fit neatly as tips of your bolts.\n"
"\n"
"Feeling self-assured, you head off to prepare to seal the four sentries."
msgstr ""
"Antes de irte, vuelves a inspeccionar cada una de las estatuas mientras Magnavous y Whudgrath se ponen con sus propias tareas. El lugar aún necesita mucho trabajo. La puerta apenas está iluminada por la escasa luz del sol que se filtra desde fuera y por los pocos faroles de su base. Seguro que podrás ver mejor las estatuas cuando la cámara esté del todo preparada, pero las gemas siguen captando a la perfección la tenue luz de la caverna mientras las examinas. Topacio, zafiro, rubí y esmeralda: todas ellas gemas que encajarían a la perfección como puntas de tus virotes.\n"
"\n"
"Con total seguridad, te pones en marcha para preparar el sellado de los cuatro centinelas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "At least I know I'm helping her confidence."
msgstr "Al menos sé que estoy ayudando a su confianza."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Drop off the staves. [Talk]"
msgstr "Entrega los báculos. [Talk]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gemstone-tipped bolts in-hand, you slowly work your way around each of the "
"statues. Each fits in the openings nicely, and lock into place with a firm "
"and resonate snap. Magnavous begins to do the same while Whudgrath holds a "
"lantern aloft. Soon enough, the vapor that twisted and curled up towards the"
" ceiling has been stopped. All at once, the statues seem to heave and twist."
" Where they once hunched and gaunt, sealing them seems to have changed the "
"stone outright, causing the figures to warp into more imposing, able-bodied "
"versions of themselves."
msgstr ""
"Con los virotes con punta de gema en la mano, recorres poco a poco cada una "
"de las estatuas. Cada uno encaja bien en las aberturas y queda fijado con un"
" chasquido firme y resonante. Magnavous empieza a hacer lo mismo mientras "
"Whudgrath sostiene un farol en alto. Al poco, el vapor que se retorcía y se "
"enroscaba hacia el techo se ha detenido. De repente, las estatuas parecen "
"agitarse y retorcerse. Donde antes estaban encorvadas y demacradas, "
"sellarlas parece haber cambiado la piedra por completo, haciendo que las "
"figuras se transformen en versiones más imponentes y robustas de sí mismas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, that seems promising."
msgstr "Bueno, esto pinta bien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Step one down, two more to go. They seem to be in fighting shape..."
msgstr "Un paso menos, quedan dos. Parece que están en forma para luchar..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Time to arm them."
msgstr "Hora de armarlos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Now, I'm as game for a scrap as anyone, but you don't find it concerning at "
"all, giving them weapons?"
msgstr ""
"A ver, a mí me gusta una buena pelea como al que más, pero ¿no te preocupa "
"lo más mínimo darles armas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Just me?"
msgstr "¿Solo a mí?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It feels right. Besides, I'd say they feel more like guardians of this place"
" than combatants."
msgstr ""
"Me parece lo correcto. Además, diría que parecen más guardianes de este "
"lugar que combatientes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Right, and... do you think the city's guardians would take too kindly to us "
"plundering their home?"
msgstr ""
"Ya, y... ¿crees que a los guardianes de la ciudad les hará mucha gracia que "
"saqueemos su hogar?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'll call Morlin in soon, once we determine what we'll arm them with. He'll "
"be able to protect us, if they decide we're a threat."
msgstr ""
"Llamaré pronto a Morlin, cuando decidamos con qué armarlos. Podrá "
"protegernos si deciden que somos una amenaza."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll do my best to appear... friendly. How's my smile?"
msgstr "Haré lo posible por parecer... amigable. ¿Qué tal mi sonrisa?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...It reminds me of a dog baring its teeth..."
msgstr "...Me recuerda a un perro enseñando los dientes..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hmm. Maybe a no on the smile then."
msgstr "Mmm. Mejor nada de sonrisas, entonces."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The four of them look like mages, just like you Magnavous."
msgstr "Los cuatro parecen magos, igual que tú, Magnavous."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And you made me this delightful staff. Think you could do the same here? One"
" for each of the base elements?"
msgstr ""
"Y tú me hiciste este báculo tan bonito. ¿Crees que podrías hacer lo mismo "
"aquí? ¿Uno por cada elemento básico?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They'd be a bit more like toothpicks for them, no?"
msgstr "Para ellos serían más bien palillos, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, Morlin has been teaching me this spell that allows me to take multiple"
" items and combine them into a much larger version of themselves."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, Morlin me ha estado enseñando un hechizo que permite tomar varios "
"objetos y combinarlos en una versión mucho más grande de sí mismos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How oddly convenient... How'd that come up?"
msgstr "Qué curiosamente oportuno... ¿Y cómo salió eso?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It was in his first published book, \"101 Spells To Make You A Master "
"Wizard!\" I've been trying to get through them all since I got here."
msgstr ""
"Estaba en su primer libro publicado, «¡101 hechizos para convertirte en un "
"maestro mago!». Intento aprendérmelos todos desde que llegué."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Huh, alright... Seems simple enough. So, you probably just need a couple of "
"each staff, or..?"
msgstr ""
"Vaya, vale... Parece bastante sencillo. Entonces, ¿seguramente solo "
"necesitas un par de cada báculo, o...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well... I'm not too good at it yet. We've been running all over this dig "
"site for a while now, I haven't had long to practice."
msgstr ""
"Bueno... todavía no se me da muy bien. Llevamos un tiempo corriendo de un "
"lado a otro de esta excavación y no he tenido mucho tiempo para practicar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But you can do it, right?"
msgstr "Pero puedes hacerlo, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Yes! But... it's just not very efficient yet."
msgstr "¡Sí! Pero... todavía no es muy eficiente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I'll get to work then."
msgstr "...Entonces me pongo manos a la obra."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Part of you wishes that Morlin could just come do the spell, but deep down, "
"you know it'll be good for Magnavous to do this for her training. At the "
"very least, it'll help her feel a bit more confident, even if it does mean "
"you have to make... substantially more staves."
msgstr ""
"Una parte de ti desearía que Morlin viniera a lanzar el hechizo, pero en el "
"fondo sabes que a Magnavous le vendrá bien hacerlo para su formación. Como "
"mínimo, la ayudará a sentirse un poco más segura, aunque eso suponga que "
"tengas que hacer... bastantes más báculos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You know, that old man makes a good point..."
msgstr "Pues mira, el viejo tiene razón..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I hope this works...  [Complete Quest Button]"
msgstr "Espero que esto funcione...  [Complete Quest Button]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you hand the staves to Magnavous one by one, they slowly but surely get combined into one. Eventually, they get big enough that Whudgrath and his crew take over in holding them, and then placing them into the statues’ hands. When the four of them are armed, they slam them into the ground and the orb at the end of each begins to glow.\n"
"\n"
"Morlin enters, and lets out a low whistle when he sees the progress that has been made."
msgstr ""
"A medida que le pasas los báculos a Magnavous uno a uno, poco a poco, pero sin pausa, se van combinando en uno solo. Al final se hacen tan grandes que Whudgrath y su equipo se encargan de sostenerlos y de colocarlos en las manos de las estatuas. Cuando las cuatro están armadas, los golpean contra el suelo y el orbe del extremo de cada uno empieza a brillar.\n"
"\n"
"Morlin entra y suelta un silbido grave al ver los avances."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "My my my, I see you all have been making good progress!"
msgstr "¡Vaya, vaya, vaya, veo que habéis avanzado mucho!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That we have! And what have you been up to?"
msgstr "¡Así es! ¿Y tú qué has estado haciendo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Taking a nap!"
msgstr "¡Echarme una siesta!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I've been here for... quite a while."
msgstr "Yo llevo aquí... bastante tiempo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Do you see this beard? Just how old do you think I am? You've got to stay "
"well rested at my age."
msgstr ""
"¿Ves esta barba? ¿Cuántos años crees que tengo? A mi edad hay que estar bien"
" descansado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Plus, my apprentice is becoming quite capable! Thank you for helping her "
"out, by the way. Both here, and before she found her way to the site."
msgstr ""
"¡Además, mi aprendiz se está volviendo muy capaz! Gracias por ayudarla, por "
"cierto. Tanto aquí como antes de que llegara a la excavación."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I think Azamire would be a burning crater if I didn't, but it's my pleasure."
" She's quite capable."
msgstr ""
"Creo que Azamire sería un cráter en llamas si no lo hubiera hecho, pero ha "
"sido un placer. Es muy capaz."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That she is!"
msgstr "¡Desde luego que lo es!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Enough about me, we've only got one more thing to do before we're done!"
msgstr ""
"Basta de hablar de mí, ¡solo nos queda una cosa por hacer antes de terminar!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That's right, but I have no idea what to adorn them in. They've already "
"got... robes, kind of."
msgstr ""
"Así es, pero no tengo ni idea de con qué adornarlos. Ya llevan... túnicas, "
"más o menos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is where a master wizard comes into play, children."
msgstr "Aquí es donde entra en juego un maestro mago, niños."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They're clearly missing their swag, as the kids say."
msgstr "Está claro que les falta estilo, como dicen los jóvenes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I've never heard a kid say that."
msgstr "Nunca he oído a un joven decir eso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Neither have I."
msgstr "...Yo tampoco."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Have to say I'm in agreement."
msgstr "Tengo que darles la razón."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, you clearly aren't hip, like old man Morlin. Behold!"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, está claro que no estáis a la moda como el viejo Morlin. ¡Contemplad!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Morlin throws back his robes to show off a concerning amount of jewelry. Dozens of necklaces, bracelets, and rings adorn his body. They sparkle brilliantly in the low-light, so much so that you worry you'd be blinded if it was any brighter in the cavern. He goes on to talk about how most keep it far too simple, limiting themselves to only a few enchanted pieces of jewelry at a time, but that a master wizard such as himself isn't held back by such limitations. Whudgrath asks if they can just use his jewelry, to which he scoffs. He glances over the statues and produces a list.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Much like last time he tried to make a list, the first page is cryptic, detailing something about an excitable lizard housekeeper and her many cleaning adventures, but he burns it before you can get more than a glance as to its contents. He hands the veritable laundry list of jewelry to you, and assures you that your efforts will be reflected in your cut of... whatever may lie inside."
msgstr ""
"Morlin se abre la túnica para mostrar una cantidad preocupante de joyas. Docenas de collares, pulseras y anillos adornan su cuerpo. Brillan con intensidad en la penumbra, tanto que temes quedarte ciego si la caverna estuviera más iluminada. Se pone a explicar que la mayoría se queda demasiado corta, limitándose a unas pocas joyas encantadas a la vez, pero que a un maestro mago como él no lo frenan esas limitaciones. Whudgrath pregunta si pueden usar sin más sus joyas, a lo que él responde con desdén. Echa un vistazo a las estatuas y saca una lista.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Igual que la última vez que intentó hacer una lista, la primera página es críptica y detalla algo sobre una entusiasta ama de llaves lagarto y sus muchas aventuras de limpieza, pero la quema antes de que puedas echar algo más que un vistazo a su contenido. Te entrega la interminable lista de joyas y te asegura que tu esfuerzo se verá reflejado en tu parte de... lo que sea que haya dentro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Everyone begins layering on the amulets as best they can, taking wild guesses as to how many and where they should be placed. The four statues begin to look positively gaudy by the time you finish, and you start to wonder if it would have been better to use the same enlargement spell as you used for the staves... just as the first of the four begins to stir.\n"
"\n"
"The adornments melt into their stone skin, and each statue's eyes begin to light up one by one, shining with an eerie energy. Magnavous ducks behind you, and Whudgrath behind her, while Morlin waves his staff menacingly at the statues. You all sit in a tense silence as seconds feel as if they stretch into minutes. The statues slam their staves into the ground once again, this time eliciting a shriek from... Morlin, your mighty protector.\n"
"\n"
"In tandem, the statues take position by the colossal gate, and each hammers their staff against it one after another, the whacks shaking the cavern enough to knock you all to your knees. When the sentries cease, they begin to push arduously against it, the bolts you pressed into them fragmenting and shooting out from the gaps in their facades, letting the vapor they held back rise towards the cavern's ceiling once more. \n"
"\n"
"Slowly but surely, the gate grinds open, and the statues don't let up until the doors scrape to a halt. With that, they wander into the darkness, leaving you all behind, wondering what lies beyond the gate."
msgstr ""
"Todos empiezan a colocar amuletos como pueden, haciendo conjeturas a lo loco sobre cuántos poner y dónde. Las cuatro estatuas empiezan a parecer francamente recargadas cuando terminas, y empiezas a preguntarte si no habría sido mejor usar el mismo hechizo de agrandamiento que con los báculos... justo cuando la primera de las cuatro empieza a moverse.\n"
"\n"
"Los adornos se funden con su piel de piedra, y los ojos de cada estatua empiezan a iluminarse uno a uno, brillando con una energía inquietante. Magnavous se esconde detrás de ti, y Whudgrath detrás de ella, mientras Morlin agita su báculo amenazadoramente hacia las estatuas. Os quedáis todos en un silencio tenso mientras los segundos parecen convertirse en minutos. Las estatuas vuelven a golpear el suelo con sus báculos, y esta vez arrancan un chillido de... Morlin, vuestro poderoso protector.\n"
"\n"
"Al unísono, las estatuas se colocan junto a la colosal puerta, y cada una la golpea con su báculo una tras otra; los golpes sacuden la caverna con tanta fuerza que os tiran a todos de rodillas. Cuando los centinelas se detienen, empiezan a empujarla con gran esfuerzo, y los virotes que les clavaste se fragmentan y salen disparados por las grietas de sus fachadas, dejando que el vapor que contenían vuelva a subir hacia el techo de la caverna. \n"
"\n"
"Lenta pero inexorablemente, la puerta se abre con un chirrido, y las estatuas no paran hasta que las hojas se detienen arañando el suelo. Después, se adentran en la oscuridad y os dejan atrás, preguntándoos qué habrá más allá de la puerta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The Sealed Grove"
msgstr "La arboleda sellada"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The Sealed Grove - The leader of Azamire's forces has some concerns about a "
"nearby grove that seems tainted by some kind of dark energy. With the "
"situation beginning the spiral out of control, she has called in the best "
"Azamire has to offer."
msgstr ""
"La arboleda sellada: la jefa de las fuerzas de Azamire está preocupada por "
"una arboleda cercana que parece contaminada por algún tipo de energía "
"oscura. Ahora que la situación empieza a descontrolarse, ha llamado a lo "
"mejor que Azamire puede ofrecer."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "These trees almost grow faster than I can chop them down!"
msgstr "¡Estos árboles crecen casi más rápido de lo que puedo talarlos!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think I see a clearing up ahead! [Push]"
msgstr "¡Creo que veo un claro más adelante! [Push]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"On a stroll by what was once the Soothsayer's Grove, you find yourself "
"startled as a blue vine whips out and lashes itself around your ankles. "
"Startled by the intrusion, you barely have the chance to think about how "
"this was meant to be a 'safe path' until you're hoisted up into the air and "
"tossed around. Suddenly, a tall, dark-haired woman jumps out from the "
"darkness and cleaves the vines in two with a single swipe of her sword, "
"sending you back towards the ground, where you land with a thud."
msgstr ""
"Paseando junto a lo que una vez fue la Arboleda del Adivino, te sobresaltas "
"cuando una enredadera azul sale disparada y se te enrosca en los tobillos. "
"Ante la sorpresa, apenas tienes tiempo de pensar que se suponía que esto era"
" un «camino seguro» antes de que te alcen por los aires y te zarandeen. De "
"repente, una mujer alta de pelo oscuro salta de entre las sombras y corta "
"las enredaderas en dos de un solo tajo de su espada, devolviéndote al suelo,"
" donde caes con un golpe sordo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Ow... Thank you... I think? What are you doing so far from Azamire, Jass? "
"Aren't the militia lost without you?"
msgstr ""
"Ay... Gracias... ¿creo? ¿Qué haces tan lejos de Azamire, Jass? ¿La milicia "
"no está perdida sin ti?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What are you doing near the Soothsayer's Grove? Haven't you seen all the "
"signs I've put up?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué haces tú cerca de la Arboleda del Adivino? ¿No has visto todos los "
"carteles que he puesto?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Do the signs say, \"Beware dangerous sentient vines?\""
msgstr ""
"¿Los carteles dicen «Cuidado con las enredaderas conscientes y peligrosas»?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No, they say, \"Danger,\" and \"Stay Out!\" Someone or something, is causing"
" everything around this place to go absolutely wild."
msgstr ""
"No, dicen «Peligro» y «¡Prohibido el paso!». Alguien, o algo, está haciendo "
"que todo lo que rodea este lugar se vuelva completamente salvaje."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You should really consider my sign idea, it's a lot less vague."
msgstr "Deberías plantearte mi idea para los carteles, es mucho menos vaga."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Would you have stayed out if that's what they said instead?"
msgstr "¿Te habrías mantenido alejado si eso es lo que dijeran?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...No, I would have thought that I could have handled some silly little "
"vines. Point taken."
msgstr ""
"...No, habría pensado que podía con unas enredaderas de nada. Entendido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What's going on here?"
msgstr "¿Qué está pasando aquí?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I wish I knew. Every attempt I've made to get closer to the grove has been "
"met with vines, trees and the occasional monster."
msgstr ""
"Ojalá lo supiera. Cada vez que he intentado acercarme a la arboleda me he "
"topado con enredaderas, árboles y algún que otro monstruo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, no one throws me in the air and gets away with it! Plus, I ought to "
"help you, since you saved me."
msgstr ""
"¡Bueno, nadie me lanza por los aires y se va de rositas! Además, debería "
"ayudarte, ya que me has salvado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Can you keep me on the ground if I cut a path through to the grove?"
msgstr "¿Puedes mantenerme en el suelo si abro un camino hasta la arboleda?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I've done it once already, haven't I? Grab an axe, we're going to make some "
"kindling out of this grove."
msgstr ""
"Ya lo he hecho una vez, ¿no? Coge un hacha, vamos a convertir esta arboleda "
"en leña."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As if it heard Jass's threat, more vines snaked out from the underbrush and "
"towards you. True to her word, Jass takes a firm stance and chops through "
"them like a butcher hacking through meat, giving you an opening to make your"
" way towards the grove."
msgstr ""
"Como si hubiera oído la amenaza de Jass, más enredaderas salen serpenteando "
"de la maleza hacia ti. Fiel a su palabra, Jass adopta una postura firme y "
"las corta como un carnicero troceando carne, abriéndote paso hacia la "
"arboleda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Surely Gol will be able to handle... Whatever is in this forest."
msgstr "Seguro que Gol podrá con... lo que sea que haya en este bosque."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Back into the woods we go. [Talk]"
msgstr "De vuelta al bosque. [Talk]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The bushes and trees are thick, and for every one you chop down, it feels as though three more shoot up in their place. Their rapid growth would be a lot more impressive if it wasn't for its murderous intent. How they stay out of sight is a mystery, but as you cut deeper into the tangle of plants, thunderous bellows and growls sound from nearby creatures you feel lucky not to encounter.\n"
"\n"
"You do your best to make your way inward, and eventually, the outer thicket gives way to a calmer bit of forest. Jass catches her breath and wipes the vegetation from her sword and armor. The two of you stand on a ridgeline surrounding a deep crater, filled with plantlife you've never seen anywhere else. It almost looks like a jungle, with dark trees towering from the pit and threatening to spill out. All manner of dark shadows prowl through the vegetation, and you're very happy to be far above it, at least for now."
msgstr ""
"Los arbustos y los árboles son espesos, y por cada uno que talas, parece que brotan tres más en su lugar. Su rápido crecimiento sería mucho más impresionante si no fuera por sus intenciones asesinas. Cómo se mantienen ocultas es un misterio, pero a medida que te adentras en la maraña de plantas, se oyen bramidos atronadores y gruñidos de criaturas cercanas con las que te alegras de no cruzarte.\n"
"\n"
"Haces lo posible por avanzar hacia el interior y, al final, la espesura exterior da paso a una zona de bosque más tranquila. Jass recupera el aliento y limpia la vegetación de su espada y su armadura. Los dos estáis en una cresta que rodea un profundo cráter, lleno de una vegetación que nunca has visto en ningún otro sitio. Casi parece una jungla, con árboles oscuros que se alzan desde el foso y amenazan con desbordarse. Todo tipo de sombras oscuras merodean entre la vegetación, y te alegras mucho de estar muy por encima, al menos por ahora."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're not going to like what I have to say."
msgstr "No te va a gustar lo que voy a decir."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We are going to have to go down there, aren't we?"
msgstr "Vamos a tener que bajar ahí, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What? No, absolutely not. You can practically see the evil leaking out of "
"the grove."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué? No, ni hablar. Prácticamente se ve el mal saliendo de la arboleda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're going to have to cut out way back out."
msgstr "Vamos a tener que abrirnos paso de vuelta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Honestly, I like the sound of that a lot better than wandering down there. "
"But why'd we come in here in the first place, then?"
msgstr ""
"Sinceramente, eso me suena mucho mejor que bajar ahí. Pero entonces, ¿para "
"qué hemos venido?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I wanted to see for my own eyes how much the jungle in the crater had "
"progressed, before we did."
msgstr ""
"Quería ver con mis propios ojos cuánto había avanzado la jungla del cráter "
"antes de hacer nada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's not good. The crater itself was barren at first, except for a singular "
"pale, twisted tree in the very center. This whole jungle has sprouted up in "
"just a few days..."
msgstr ""
"No pinta bien. Al principio el cráter estaba yermo, salvo por un único árbol"
" pálido y retorcido justo en el centro. Toda esta jungla ha brotado en solo "
"unos días..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The thicket around the crater-which we just hacked through-as at least four "
"times as dense as the other day."
msgstr ""
"La espesura que rodea el cráter (la que acabamos de atravesar) es al menos "
"cuatro veces más densa que el otro día."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You said there was just a single tree in the center of the crater? That "
"feels... odd. Wasn't this place meant to be a grove at one point?"
msgstr ""
"¿Dices que solo había un árbol en el centro del cráter? Eso es... raro. ¿No "
"se suponía que esto fue una arboleda en su día?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Years ago, yes. Until this place was turned into a logging camp and cleared "
"out. Never really had any issues until..."
msgstr ""
"Hace años, sí. Hasta que convirtieron este lugar en un campamento maderero y"
" lo talaron. Nunca hubo problemas hasta que..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Whatever started happening here."
msgstr "Empezó a pasar lo que sea que esté pasando aquí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Aye."
msgstr "Sí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"When we get out, we'll make a plan on what to do about this place. For now, "
"are you ready head back?"
msgstr ""
"Cuando salgamos, haremos un plan sobre qué hacer con este lugar. Por ahora, "
"¿estás listo para volver?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll use my other arm this time."
msgstr "Esta vez usaré el otro brazo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The two of you cut through the thicket back the way you came, and found less resistance exiting than entering. You make your way to Azamire, and started to form a plan while recharging in Lira's tavern. You set yourselves on sealing the grove, keeping whatever may be inside the crater locked away, and hopefully preventing the spread of the outer thicket as well.\n"
"\n"
"As you start to wonder who might be helpful, in slaying corrupted beasts and dealing with wild plants before finally sealing the grove, Lira-who has clearly been listening in-swings by and recommends Gol and Petal for the first steps, and Morlin for the last. Without a word from either of you, she sends a couple of her patrons to fetch them. Sure enough, the two of them are more than up for the challenge, and recommend dealing with the beasts first, then tending to the thicket before sealing it. This works out well, as Magnavous sends a message back on Morlin's behalf, saying that he'll come as soon as he's able to return his sense of gravity-whatever that means."
msgstr ""
"Los dos os abrís paso por la espesura por donde habíais venido, y encontráis menos resistencia al salir que al entrar. Vais a Azamire y empezáis a trazar un plan mientras recuperáis fuerzas en la taberna de Lira. Decidís sellar la arboleda, mantener encerrado lo que sea que haya dentro del cráter y, con suerte, frenar también la expansión de la espesura exterior.\n"
"\n"
"Mientras os preguntáis quién podría ayudar a matar bestias corrompidas y a lidiar con plantas salvajes antes de sellar por fin la arboleda, Lira (que claramente ha estado escuchando) se acerca y os recomienda a Gol y a Petal para los primeros pasos, y a Morlin para el último. Sin que ninguno de los dos diga nada, envía a un par de sus clientes a buscarlos. Efectivamente, los dos están más que dispuestos a aceptar el reto, y recomiendan ocuparse primero de las bestias y luego de la espesura antes de sellarla. Todo encaja, ya que Magnavous envía un mensaje en nombre de Morlin diciendo que vendrá en cuanto recupere su sentido de la gravedad, signifique eso lo que signifique."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This bait positively reeks, but that's kind of the point."
msgstr "Este cebo apesta de verdad, pero de eso se trata."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's see if we can find ourself some monsters. [Bait]"
msgstr "A ver si encontramos algunos monstruos. [Bait]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Excited by the prospect of a new challenge, Gol grips the Dawnsteel javelins tightly, sets off into the outer thicket, and is seemingly swallowed by the vegetation, quickly dipping out of sight. Petal quickly pulls out her poisons while Jass prepares to cut her way through the vines until you hear Gol... laughing?\n"
"\n"
"Much less concerned for his safety, the three of you eventually make it to a clearing where the plants seem to be retreating from him. Gol lays atop the corpse of a beast several orders of magnitude larger than the mountain of a man, making it even larger than the three of you. "
msgstr ""
"Entusiasmado ante la perspectiva de un nuevo reto, Gol agarra con fuerza las jabalinas de acero del alba, se adentra en la espesura exterior y parece que la vegetación se lo traga, pues desaparece enseguida de la vista. Petal saca rápidamente sus venenos mientras Jass se prepara para abrirse paso entre las enredaderas, hasta que oyes a Gol... ¿reírse?\n"
"\n"
"Mucho menos preocupados por su seguridad, los tres llegáis por fin a un claro donde las plantas parecen apartarse de él. Gol está tumbado sobre el cadáver de una bestia muchísimo más grande que aquella montaña de hombre, y por tanto más grande que los tres juntos. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gol quite enjoyed that little bout!"
msgstr "¡A Gol le ha encantado ese combatillo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's a shame about the wee beastie, though."
msgstr "Aunque es una pena lo de la pobre bestezuela."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What, were you hoping for more of a fight?"
msgstr "¿Qué pasa, esperabas más pelea?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gol respects his opponent greatly, it did the best it could."
msgstr "Gol respeta mucho a su rival, hizo lo que pudo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The thicket impeded it as much as it does the rest of us. Nature is very "
"much not in harmony here."
msgstr ""
"La espesura le estorbaba tanto como al resto de nosotros. Aquí la naturaleza"
" no está nada en armonía."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The creature was in pain, Gol did his best to free it."
msgstr "La criatura sufría, Gol hizo lo posible por liberarla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That's... very noble of you. It's clear that something is off here, but... I"
" figured it was kind of the opposite."
msgstr ""
"Eso es... muy noble por tu parte. Está claro que aquí algo va mal, pero... "
"pensaba que era más bien al revés."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I haven't seen much yet, but it'd make sense that this is more of a matter "
"of corruption than nature running wild."
msgstr ""
"Aún no he visto mucho, pero tendría sentido que esto fuera más cosa de la "
"corrupción que de una naturaleza desbocada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'd best seal this as fast as we can. It will only get worse."
msgstr "Más vale que sellemos esto cuanto antes. Solo va a ir a peor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There's no way of driving the corruption out?"
msgstr "¿No hay forma de expulsar la corrupción?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'd need to be five times the herbalist I am, and that's just if it's a "
"poison or plant-based corruption."
msgstr ""
"Tendría que ser cinco veces mejor herbolaria de lo que soy, y eso si es un "
"veneno o una corrupción de origen vegetal."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It could be magic, which I can't do much of anything about."
msgstr "Podría ser magia, y contra eso no puedo hacer casi nada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You're doing plenty, and we're lucky to have you here. Sealing the grove "
"will be more than enough for now."
msgstr ""
"Ya haces mucho, y tenemos suerte de tenerte aquí. Sellar la arboleda será "
"más que suficiente por ahora."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As long as we're able to halt its growth, having a single crater in the "
"middle of the woods locked away should be fine, until we figure out how to "
"fix it."
msgstr ""
"Mientras podamos frenar su crecimiento, tener un solo cráter encerrado en "
"mitad del bosque no debería ser un problema hasta que sepamos cómo "
"arreglarlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gol recommends putting up some better signs though."
msgstr "Aun así, Gol recomienda poner mejores carteles."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "See? Gol and I are on the same page, Jass."
msgstr "¿Lo ves? Gol y yo pensamos igual, Jass."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Though, on second thought I'm not sure if that's a good thing."
msgstr "Aunque, pensándolo mejor, no sé si eso es bueno."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... ugh."
msgstr "Yo... uf."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"So, we can't just throw Gol into the forest and hope that he's able to get "
"every single one of the corrupted beasts."
msgstr ""
"O sea, que no podemos lanzar a Gol al bosque y esperar que acabe con todas y"
" cada una de las bestias corrompidas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No, but it was good to come. We let Petal get her potions and herbs ready. "
"She mentioned needing a fair bit of time to prepare to tame the outer "
"thicket."
msgstr ""
"No, pero ha estado bien venir. Hemos dejado que Petal prepare sus pociones e"
" hierbas. Dijo que necesitaba bastante tiempo para prepararse para domar la "
"espesura exterior."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That's right. I'm making a special brew for this... My hope is that I can "
"stunt the plants' growth, not just poison the land into inhabitability. Not "
"to mention it'd take a lot more poison for that."
msgstr ""
"Así es. Estoy preparando un brebaje especial para esto... Espero poder "
"frenar el crecimiento de las plantas, no solo envenenar la tierra hasta "
"hacerla inhabitable. Por no hablar de que para eso haría falta mucho más "
"veneno."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"While you work on that, Gol and I can bait the creatures back into the "
"crater. That way when we seal it, they'll be locked inside."
msgstr ""
"Mientras trabajas en eso, Gol y yo podemos atraer a las criaturas de vuelta "
"al cráter con cebo. Así, cuando lo sellemos, quedarán encerradas dentro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Sounds sensible. We'll let you know if Morlin manages to find us as well."
msgstr ""
"Parece sensato. Os avisaremos si Morlin consigue encontrarnos también."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The corpse that Gol left behind was staggeringly large, so anything less "
"than bait that is equally large won't do. I'll see what I can come up with, "
"then come back to camp."
msgstr ""
"El cadáver que dejó Gol era tremendamente grande, así que no servirá ningún "
"cebo que no sea igual de grande. Veré qué se me ocurre y luego volveré al "
"campamento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Rosemary is normally pretty pleasant. Will it really repel monsters with "
"Petal's solution?"
msgstr ""
"El romero suele ser bastante agradable. ¿De verdad repelerá a los monstruos "
"con la solución de Petal?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll let her know I'm about done. [Talk]"
msgstr "Le diré que casi he terminado. [Talk]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Giant Fish Bait packed in your spare bag sounded fine and dandy, until you realized that you'd have to walk along the edge of the rampant forest. Gol, by some miracle or stroke of luck, just so happened to be nearby when one of the same beasts as before just about grabbed you in its massive jaws. It let out a terrifying howl, and followed after the two of you. Worried about your pace, eventually Gol decided to throw you over his shoulder and run towards the edge of the crater as the vegetation pulls out of Gol's path, which would have felt a lot more disheartening if it weren't for the scores of eyes following after you. \n"
"\n"
"As the two of you crash through the treeline, you toss the bait-filled bag and send it careening into the crater. Gol dashes to the side and doesn't stop running, even as the beasts go lurching over the edge towards the pack. He doesn't set you down until the forest stops moving, which you don't mind one bit. Eventually, you deem it safe to return to camp, and do so quickly."
msgstr ""
"Llevar cebo para peces gigantes en tu bolsa de repuesto parecía muy buena idea, hasta que te diste cuenta de que tendrías que caminar por el borde del bosque desbocado. Gol, por algún milagro o golpe de suerte, estaba justo cerca cuando una de las mismas bestias de antes estuvo a punto de atraparte entre sus enormes fauces. Soltó un aullido aterrador y os persiguió a los dos. Preocupado por tu ritmo, Gol acabó echándote al hombro y corriendo hacia el borde del cráter mientras la vegetación se apartaba de su camino, lo que habría resultado mucho más desalentador si no fuera por las decenas de ojos que os seguían. \n"
"\n"
"Cuando atravesáis la linde del bosque, lanzas la bolsa llena de cebo y la mandas volando al cráter. Gol se aparta a un lado y no deja de correr, ni siquiera cuando las bestias se precipitan por el borde tras el cebo. No te deja en el suelo hasta que el bosque deja de moverse, cosa que no te importa en absoluto. Al final, consideráis que es seguro volver al campamento, y lo hacéis rápidamente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Friend, Gol fears your bait was a bit more effective than intended!"
msgstr ""
"¡Amigo, Gol teme que tu cebo haya sido un poco más eficaz de lo previsto!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But it worked! I hope. There shouldn't be more than a couple stragglers if "
"anything."
msgstr ""
"¡Pero ha funcionado! Eso espero. No debería quedar más que algún rezagado, "
"si acaso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol thinks you should work on your cardio before trying something like that "
"again."
msgstr ""
"Gol cree que deberías mejorar tu resistencia antes de volver a intentar algo"
" así."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I only got to see a glimpse of it, but it was rather entertaining."
msgstr "Solo pude verlo de refilón, pero fue bastante entretenido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's kinda cute how small you look cradled in Gol's arms."
msgstr "Es casi tierno lo pequeño que pareces en brazos de Gol."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I wasn't cradled, I was heroically and tactically placed on his shoulder."
msgstr "No iba en brazos, me colocó heroica y tácticamente sobre su hombro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If anything, the elevated position was probably even better for making sure "
"the corrupted wildlife smelled the bait."
msgstr ""
"Si acaso, la posición elevada probablemente era todavía mejor para "
"asegurarse de que la fauna corrompida oliera el cebo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It was a smart plan, Gol just wishes you communicated it ahead of time."
msgstr ""
"Fue un plan inteligente, Gol solo desearía que lo hubieras comunicado antes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Sorry Gol, it was a kind of... improvised plan."
msgstr "Perdona, Gol, fue un plan un poco... improvisado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, one way or another, I think we're about ready for the next step. "
"Petal?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, de una forma u otra, creo que estamos casi listos para el siguiente "
"paso. ¿Petal?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[i]{0}[/i], you're rather handy on the farm, no? I remember you helping me "
"with my garden."
msgstr ""
"[i]{0}[/i], la granja se te da bastante bien, ¿no? Recuerdo que me ayudaste "
"con mi huerto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Clove still loves the sunflowers, by the way."
msgstr "Por cierto, a Clove le siguen encantando los girasoles."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I believe that if you plant rosemary along the rim of the crater, with a bit"
" of a boost from one of my infusions, it should be more than enough to keep "
"most of the critters at bay while Morlin seals the grove."
msgstr ""
"Creo que si plantas romero a lo largo del borde del cráter, con un pequeño "
"empujón de una de mis infusiones, debería bastar de sobra para mantener a "
"raya a la mayoría de los bichos mientras Morlin sella la arboleda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Seems like a good plan to me. But... has Morlin gotten here yet?"
msgstr "Me parece un buen plan. Pero... ¿Morlin ya ha llegado?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The man with the bushy beard floated into the sky!"
msgstr "¡El hombre de la barba poblada salió flotando hacia el cielo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Is he... okay?"
msgstr "¿Está... bien?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"He said he would be, still just dealing with some issues from his spell, "
"apparently."
msgstr ""
"Dijo que lo estaría, al parecer aún está lidiando con algunos problemas de "
"su hechizo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "He'll be back... eventually."
msgstr "Volverá... tarde o temprano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You look to Petal and Gol, who shrug-seemingly not too concerned with the "
"flyaway wizard. You make your way back through the growth once again, the "
"hacking motion and dodging of vines becoming quite routine at this point."
msgstr ""
"Miras a Petal y a Gol, que se encogen de hombros, sin parecer muy "
"preocupados por el mago volador. Vuelves a abrirte paso entre la vegetación,"
" y el movimiento de tajar y esquivar enredaderas ya se ha vuelto bastante "
"rutinario."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The runes the old man is asking for... This barrier seems like some nasty "
"work."
msgstr ""
"Las runas que pide el viejo... Esta barrera parece un trabajo de los gordos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I think we're finally ready to put up the barrier. [Complete Quest Button]"
msgstr ""
"Creo que por fin estamos listos para levantar la barrera. [Complete Quest "
"Button]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you finish planting the last bit of rosemary into the ground, Petal comes by and dashes it with her solution, making the seed instantly spring up and twist into a much larger bright blue version of itself. Being next to it starts to make your eyes water, and as you turn your head and cough, you notice Jass and Gol hacking their way through the thicket, clutching vials of Petal's mix that should halt the growth of the plants.\n"
"\n"
"Just then, a scream comes from the sky, and hurtles towards Gol. Morlin the Mage seems to-just barely-slow himself as he reaches Gol, and quickly settles into his arms as the large man catches him."
msgstr ""
"Al terminar de plantar el último romero, Petal se acerca y lo rocía con su solución, haciendo que la semilla brote al instante y se retuerza hasta convertirse en una versión mucho más grande y de un azul brillante. Estar a su lado empieza a hacerte llorar los ojos, y al girar la cabeza y toser, ves a Jass y a Gol abriéndose paso por la espesura, aferrando frascos de la mezcla de Petal que debería frenar el crecimiento de las plantas.\n"
"\n"
"Justo entonces, un grito llega del cielo y cae en picado hacia Gol. Morlin el Mago parece frenar (por los pelos) al llegar a Gol, y enseguida se acomoda en sus brazos cuando el grandullón lo atrapa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I was wondering when you might turn up. We just finished up with our part, "
"you were just about late."
msgstr ""
"Ya me preguntaba cuándo aparecerías. Acabamos de terminar nuestra parte, "
"casi llegas tarde."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A Morlin is never late, nor is he early. He arrives precisely when his anti-"
"gravity spell decides to send him hurtling towards the ground and straight "
"into this strong man's arms."
msgstr ""
"Un Morlin nunca llega tarde, ni pronto. Llega justo cuando su hechizo "
"antigravedad decide lanzarlo en picado hacia el suelo y directo a los brazos"
" de este hombretón."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Also, I must say, this is exquisitely comfortable. You all really should try"
" this."
msgstr ""
"Además, debo decir que esto es exquisitamente cómodo. Deberíais probarlo "
"todos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "One of us already has."
msgstr "Uno de nosotros ya lo ha hecho."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Then good, shall we get this all wrapped up then? What do you need of this "
"masterful mage?"
msgstr ""
"Bien, entonces, ¿terminamos con todo esto? ¿Qué necesitáis de este mago "
"magistral?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Can you call yourself a master if you can't control your spell?"
msgstr "¿Puedes llamarte maestro si no controlas tu hechizo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Considering I haven't seen anyone so much as levitate more than a couple "
"feet off the ground, I'd have to say yes."
msgstr ""
"Teniendo en cuenta que no he visto a nadie levitar ni un par de palmos del "
"suelo, diría que sí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think we're about ready to seal the grove. Petal?"
msgstr "Creo que estamos casi listos para sellar la arboleda. ¿Petal?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We have a bit more of the solution to halt the thicket's growth outside of "
"the crater, but just about. Did either of you see any more beasts?"
msgstr ""
"Nos queda algo más de la solución para frenar el crecimiento de la espesura "
"fuera del cráter, pero casi está. ¿Alguno de vosotros ha visto más bestias?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not one! [i]{0}[/i]'s bait did its job well."
msgstr "¡Ni una! El cebo de [i]{0}[/i] cumplió su función."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ah, well, good, because I seem to have misplaced... all of my runes."
msgstr "Ah, bueno, bien, porque parece que he perdido... todas mis runas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How?!"
msgstr "¡¿Cómo?!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"How do you think you would keep hold of your worldly possessions while "
"flying towards the ground, hm?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo crees que conservarías tus posesiones terrenales mientras vuelas hacia"
" el suelo, eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Please, [i]{0}[/i]?"
msgstr "Por favor, ¿[i]{0}[/i]?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gol can send the old man back into the sky if you'd like, friend! Gol does "
"not need a spell for this."
msgstr ""
"¡Gol puede mandar al viejo de vuelta al cielo si quieres, amigo! Gol no "
"necesita ningún hechizo para eso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No! No no no. Please, could you fetch me some runes? I need a bit of time to"
" reacclimate to the ground..."
msgstr ""
"¡No! No, no, no. Por favor, ¿podrías traerme unas runas? Necesito un poco de"
" tiempo para volver a acostumbrarme al suelo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You glare at the old wizard before finally letting out a sigh and asking for"
" a list of runes he needs for the spell. He goes to produce a page from his "
"bag, but realizes that it is also missing, so he opts to just list them "
"aloud instead, with little fanfare."
msgstr ""
"Fulminas con la mirada al viejo mago antes de soltar por fin un suspiro y "
"pedirle una lista de las runas que necesita para el hechizo. Va a sacar una "
"hoja de su bolsa, pero se da cuenta de que también ha desaparecido, así que "
"opta por enumerarlas en voz alta, sin mucha ceremonia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"On your way back through the thicket-hopefully for the final time-you notice that Petal's solution must be working. The blue vines from before seem... placated, and barely twitch as you walk by, taking care not to step on them. You make it past the worst of the vegetation with little issue, and find yourself back on the rim of the crater. \n"
"\n"
"You find Morlin tied to a tree, the rope seeming to be the only thing stopping him from drifting back skyward. He happily takes the runes from you and gets to work while the rest of the crew finishes applying the last of Petal's solution to the most agitated bits of the forest. With a shout, Morlin claps his hands and a dome begins to materialize over the lip of the crater. Jass starts putting up new signs, taking advice from Gol all the while. Soon enough, warnings of a deadly barrier, evil beasts, and a corrupted array of flora lay below, along with certain death.\n"
"\n"
"As you peer through the translucent barrier, you see that the jungle below looks wild and untamed, just as before. You hope that one day, you'll be able to return to discover what made it grow so rampant in the first place, and maybe even fix it, if you're lucky.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"En tu camino de vuelta por la espesura (con suerte, por última vez), te das cuenta de que la solución de Petal debe de estar funcionando. Las enredaderas azules de antes parecen... apaciguadas, y apenas se mueven cuando pasas a su lado con cuidado de no pisarlas. Dejas atrás lo peor de la vegetación sin mucho problema y vuelves a encontrarte en el borde del cráter. \n"
"\n"
"Encuentras a Morlin atado a un árbol; la cuerda parece ser lo único que impide que vuelva a salir flotando hacia el cielo. Recoge encantado las runas y se pone manos a la obra mientras el resto del grupo termina de aplicar lo que queda de la solución de Petal en las zonas más agitadas del bosque. Con un grito, Morlin da una palmada y una cúpula empieza a materializarse sobre el borde del cráter. Jass empieza a colocar carteles nuevos, siguiendo en todo momento los consejos de Gol. Al poco, hay avisos de una barrera mortal, bestias malvadas y una flora corrompida ahí abajo, además de una muerte segura.\n"
"\n"
"Al mirar a través de la barrera translúcida, ves que la jungla de abajo sigue igual de salvaje e indómita que antes. Esperas que algún día puedas volver para descubrir qué la hizo crecer de forma tan desbocada y, con suerte, incluso arreglarlo.\n"
"\n"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Pointy Preparation"
msgstr "Preparación puntiaguda"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A concerned citizen wants to scrape together some semblance of a fighting "
"force for Azamire's defense against any would-be bandits or those black-"
"robed figures looking to finish the job, but she's barely in fighting shape "
"herself."
msgstr ""
"Una ciudadana preocupada quiere reunir algo parecido a una fuerza de combate"
" para defender Azamire de posibles bandidos o de esas figuras de túnica "
"negra que quieran terminar el trabajo, pero ella misma apenas está en "
"condiciones de luchar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Just putting some pointy rocks on some wood, nothing too tough."
msgstr ""
"Solo hay que poner unas piedras puntiagudas en unos palos, nada demasiado "
"difícil."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think they've gotten the idea."
msgstr "Creo que ya lo han pillado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The cinders from the assault on Azamire have only just fizzled out, much like many of the survivors' will to go on. Everyone that remained had lost something. Their homes. Family members. Friends. You and [Companion Name] sit on the soot covered cobbles that once made up the town's main thoroughfare, watching another family carry what little they have left and shuffle out of town, hoping that some nearby village may have been spared. Neither of you blame them.\n"
"\n"
"A woman with a bloodied stump where her hand should have been approaches the two of you and falls to the ground beside you with a sigh."
msgstr ""
"Las brasas del ataque a Azamire acaban de apagarse, igual que las ganas de seguir adelante de muchos supervivientes. Todos los que se quedaron habían perdido algo. Sus casas. Familiares. Amigos. Tú y [Companion Name] estáis sentados sobre los adoquines cubiertos de hollín que antes formaban la calle principal del pueblo, viendo cómo otra familia carga con lo poco que le queda y se marcha del pueblo arrastrando los pies, con la esperanza de que algún pueblo cercano se haya librado. Ninguno de los dos se lo reprocha.\n"
"\n"
"Una mujer con un muñón ensangrentado donde debería estar su mano se acerca a vosotros y se deja caer al suelo a vuestro lado con un suspiro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well. You two headed out as well?"
msgstr "Bueno. ¿Vosotros también os vais?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I can't turn my back on Azamire. Too many folks have done too much for me, "
"growing up."
msgstr ""
"No puedo darle la espalda a Azamire. Demasiada gente hizo demasiado por mí "
"cuando era pequeño."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Doubt many of 'em are left."
msgstr "Dudo que queden muchos de ellos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The town still is, though."
msgstr "Pero el pueblo sigue aquí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not much of it."
msgstr "No mucho de él."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I take it you're leaving, then? Can't blame you, but this is home for the "
"both of us. Even if... Home's looking a little worse for wear."
msgstr ""
"Entiendo que tú te vas, ¿no? No te culpo, pero este es el hogar de los dos. "
"Aunque... el hogar esté un poco hecho polvo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gods no! No shame to those who are, but those rotters took more than just my"
" hand. Teri... didn't make it."
msgstr ""
"¡Por los dioses, no! No es ninguna vergüenza para quienes se van, pero esos "
"canallas se llevaron mucho más que mi mano. Teri... no lo logró."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh Jass... I'm so sorry."
msgstr "Ay, Jass... Lo siento mucho."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Fool of a man got between me and one of those wretches' beasts. Seemed like "
"he was going to pull through... but then he didn't."
msgstr ""
"El muy tonto se interpuso entre una de las bestias de esos desgraciados y "
"yo. Parecía que iba a salir adelante... pero no fue así."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...We'll make them pay, Jass. [Companion Name] and I won't let this go "
"unanswered."
msgstr ""
"...Se lo haremos pagar, Jass. [Companion Name] y yo no dejaremos esto sin "
"respuesta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You're not alone in your sentiment. I came by to see if you two might be "
"interested in a little project."
msgstr ""
"No eres el único que lo siente así. He venido a ver si os interesaría un "
"pequeño proyecto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A couple of people who aren't running for the hills want to fight back. But "
"they're farmers. Builders."
msgstr ""
"Hay un par de personas que no están huyendo a las colinas y quieren "
"contraatacar. Pero son granjeros. Constructores."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I used to be pretty good with a bow, but it'd be a bit tough with this "
"hand... or lack thereof."
msgstr ""
"Antes se me daba bastante bien el arco, pero ahora sería un poco difícil con"
" esta mano... o con su ausencia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Want us to show them the ropes? Been a little while since I shot a bow, but "
"I can show a couple of farmers where to point it and how not to shoot their "
"friends."
msgstr ""
"¿Quieres que les enseñemos lo básico? Hace tiempo que no disparo con arco, "
"pero puedo enseñar a un par de granjeros hacia dónde apuntar y cómo no "
"dispararles a sus amigos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...Are you forgetting what happened a couple of years ago? I still feel the "
"need to duck every time you-"
msgstr ""
"...¿Te olvidas de lo que pasó hace un par de años? Todavía me entran ganas "
"de agacharme cada vez que tú..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Okay, fine, [Player Name] can do the teaching, maybe I'll learn something "
"too. Is there anything else that I could help with?"
msgstr ""
"Vale, de acuerdo, que enseñe [Player Name], a lo mejor yo también aprendo "
"algo. ¿Hay algo más en lo que pueda ayudar?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Actually, yes. Like I said, most of these folks hardly know anything outside"
" of their trade. Showing them how to put together a couple of arrows could "
"go a long way towards making them self-sufficient."
msgstr ""
"Pues sí. Como decía, la mayoría de esta gente apenas sabe nada fuera de su "
"oficio. Enseñarles a montar un par de flechas podría ayudar mucho a que se "
"valgan por sí mismos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The three of you chat back and forth for a while, putting together the idea of a lesson plan, putting up some ramshackle targets meant to resemble a humanoid figure, and some scavenged gear. Jass brings back a dozen or so dusty villagers from town who seem to carry a wide range of emotions. Some, determined to fight back against the cloaked figures who destroyed the town, some who looked lost and aimless, and some somewhere in between.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] takes half of them and gets to work showing them how to make bows, something they were always better at than actually firing them, while you take the other half and get to work showing them how to make arrows."
msgstr ""
"Los tres charláis un rato, dando forma a la idea de un plan de clases, montando unas dianas improvisadas que pretenden parecer una figura humanoide y reuniendo algo de equipo rescatado. Jass vuelve del pueblo con una docena de aldeanos polvorientos que parecen tener emociones muy variadas. Algunos, decididos a contraatacar a las figuras encapuchadas que destruyeron el pueblo; otros, perdidos y sin rumbo; y algunos, a medio camino.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] se lleva a la mitad y se pone a enseñarles a hacer arcos, algo que siempre se le dio mejor que dispararlos, mientras tú te llevas a la otra mitad y te pones a enseñarles a hacer flechas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "If I didn't know better, I'd say they were aiming at me."
msgstr "Si no supiera que no, diría que me apuntan a mí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I knew they'd be bad, but wow."
msgstr "Sabía que serían malos, pero madre mía."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Many of the folks picked up your teaching pretty quickly. Even Jass, just "
"managing with a single hand, did a fine job putting together some flight-"
"worthy arrows. [Companion Name]'s lesson seemed to go about as smoothly, and"
" they produced a few bows to share amongst themselves for the next bout of "
"training. The villagers quietly, but excitedly, show off what they managed "
"to make, or laugh about how poorly their creations turned out, depending on "
"their results."
msgstr ""
"Muchos aprendieron tus enseñanzas bastante rápido. Incluso Jass, apañándose "
"con una sola mano, hizo un buen trabajo montando unas flechas capaces de "
"volar. La clase de [Companion Name] pareció ir igual de bien, y fabricaron "
"unos cuantos arcos para compartir en la siguiente sesión de entrenamiento. "
"Los aldeanos, en voz baja pero con entusiasmo, enseñan lo que han conseguido"
" hacer o se ríen de lo mal que les han salido sus creaciones, según el "
"resultado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Thank you two for all of this, by the way."
msgstr "Por cierto, gracias a los dos por todo esto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Of course. It'll be important for us to not get caught out like this again."
msgstr ""
"No hay de qué. Es importante que no nos vuelvan a pillar desprevenidos así."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This group has a long way to go, still. We had guards, but they lasted all "
"of a few minutes before those things started cutting through the town."
msgstr ""
"A este grupo aún le queda mucho camino. Teníamos guardias, pero solo "
"aguantaron unos minutos antes de que esas cosas empezaran a abrirse paso por"
" el pueblo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's a start, though. And besides, keeping these people busy is just as "
"important as making sure they're trained."
msgstr ""
"Pero es un comienzo. Y además, mantener ocupada a esta gente es tan "
"importante como asegurarse de que esté entrenada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Dwelling on everything that happened... Well, that's no good for anyone."
msgstr ""
"Darle vueltas a todo lo que pasó... En fin, eso no le hace bien a nadie."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Anyway. Shall we get to shooting?"
msgstr "En fin. ¿Nos ponemos a disparar?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "As long as [Companion Name] doesn't stick me with an arrow, sure."
msgstr "Mientras [Companion Name] no me clave una flecha, claro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] glares at you, but you've known them long enough to know there's no real anger there, just like they know you have no malice in your light banter.\n"
"\n"
"Though, you start to think otherwise when the villagers pick up their bows and start trying to hit the targets. You feel as though their arrows pass by you more often than the targets. You get to work quickly, trying to show them how to draw, aim, and fire, before they really hurt someone."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] te fulmina con la mirada, pero os conocéis desde hace tanto que sabes que no hay verdadero enfado en ello, igual que sabe que no hay malicia en tus bromas.\n"
"\n"
"Aunque empiezas a pensar lo contrario cuando los aldeanos cogen sus arcos e intentan acertar a las dianas. Te da la sensación de que sus flechas pasan más cerca de ti que de las dianas. Te pones manos a la obra enseguida para enseñarles a tensar, apuntar y disparar antes de que hieran de verdad a alguien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You certainly lost a bit of skin from arrows that passed by a bit too close for comfort, but after a while, the villagers' shots start to resemble straight flight paths. A couple folks pick it up faster than the others, among them, [Companion Name], though you still could hardly say you felt safe just yet.\n"
"\n"
"Initially, Jass seemed to be a bit frustrated at not being able to join in the demonstration, but fell into her own role guiding people and repeating your instructions to those that seemed to struggle the first few times around, or giving pointers that even you started to incorporate into your own shots.\n"
"\n"
"By the end of the day, the villagers didn't seem to actively be putting one another in danger, and looked far more determined than they did at the start of the drill, and you entrust them into Jass's tutelage, for better or worse."
msgstr ""
"Sin duda perdiste algo de piel por flechas que pasaron demasiado cerca para tu gusto, pero al cabo de un rato, los tiros de los aldeanos empiezan a parecerse a trayectorias rectas. Un par de personas lo pillan más rápido que el resto, entre ellas [Companion Name], aunque todavía no podrías decir que te sientas a salvo.\n"
"\n"
"Al principio, Jass parecía un poco frustrada por no poder participar en la demostración, pero encontró su propio papel guiando a la gente y repitiendo tus instrucciones a quienes parecían tener dificultades las primeras veces, o dando consejos que incluso tú empezaste a incorporar a tus propios tiros.\n"
"\n"
"Al final del día, los aldeanos ya no parecían ponerse en peligro unos a otros activamente, y se los veía mucho más decididos que al empezar el ejercicio; los dejas bajo la tutela de Jass, para bien o para mal."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 1[/color] Enemy using "
"[color=#FFD16D]Ranged Combat Style[/color]"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar a un enemigo de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de combate "
"1[/color] con el [color=#FFD16D]estilo de combate a distancia[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Fishin' for Trouble"
msgstr "Pescando problemas"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"While out on a fishing trip, a little girl has gone missing with only her "
"fishing pole and a single tooth left behind. Not much to go on, except one "
"small detail. It isn't a human tooth."
msgstr ""
"Durante una salida de pesca, ha desaparecido una niña, y solo ha dejado "
"atrás su caña de pescar y un único diente. No hay mucho por donde empezar, "
"salvo un pequeño detalle. No es un diente humano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Swords are plenty sharp, that'll do."
msgstr "Las espadas están bien afiladas, con eso basta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's hope they can figure out how to swing 'em."
msgstr "Esperemos que sepan cómo blandirlas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You just start to drift off to sleep before a frantic pounding at your door "
"makes you jump up and start grabbing for something nearby to protect "
"yourself. Your door opens a bit more gently than you'd expect considering "
"the knocking, and you find [Companion Name] looking worried with a young "
"woman behind her. She holds up something about as thick as your finger with "
"a sickly pale yellow hue."
msgstr ""
"Estás a punto de quedarte dormido cuando unos golpes frenéticos en la puerta"
" te hacen saltar y buscar algo cerca con lo que defenderte. La puerta se "
"abre con más suavidad de la que esperarías tras esos golpes, y encuentras a "
"[Companion Name] con cara de preocupación y una joven detrás. Sostiene en "
"alto algo tan grueso como tu dedo, de un tono amarillo pálido y enfermizo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Her daughter was out fishing near the river and didn't come home for dinner."
" Sorry to interrupt your sleep, but I figured you'd want to help."
msgstr ""
"Su hija estaba pescando cerca del río y no volvió a casa para cenar. Siento "
"interrumpir tu sueño, pero supuse que querrías ayudar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're not wrong. And the thing you're holding?"
msgstr "No te equivocas. ¿Y eso que sostienes?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Golbin tooth. The only... blood, that was there was blue, so..."
msgstr ""
"Un diente de Golbin. La única... sangre que había era azul, así que..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The girl is okay, at least for now, I'd imagine."
msgstr "La niña está bien, al menos por ahora, me imagino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Good, good. Then, just the two of us are headed out?"
msgstr "Bien, bien. Entonces, ¿vamos solo los dos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Thankfully, no. Jass has been making a bit of progress with her 'militia' "
"and they want to join us."
msgstr ""
"Por suerte, no. Jass ha hecho algunos progresos con su «milicia» y quieren "
"unirse a nosotros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's anyone's guess how many Golbins there will be. It'd be smart to let "
"them come to us."
msgstr ""
"Vete a saber cuántos Golbins habrá. Lo inteligente sería dejar que vengan "
"ellos a nosotros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What if we set the same scene as... the incident, have Jass's people waiting"
" for them?"
msgstr ""
"¿Y si recreamos la misma escena que... el incidente, con la gente de Jass "
"esperándolos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Just please... hurry. I'm hopeful my little Ana is safe, but... it's not "
"like they took her for a fun little stroll around the woods. I know she must"
" be so frightened..."
msgstr ""
"Por favor... daos prisa. Espero que mi pequeña Ana esté a salvo, pero... no "
"es que se la hayan llevado a dar un paseíto por el bosque. Sé que debe de "
"estar muy asustada..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Don't worry, we'll do everything that we can."
msgstr "No te preocupes, haremos todo lo que podamos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You gather your things and leave your bed behind, meeting up with Jass and a"
" couple of folks just outside. Some of them hold the bows [Companion Name] "
"helped them make, some holding new ones they must have created themselves. "
"However, any decent force has variety - archers wouldn't fare well if the "
"Golbins got in their ranks - and their inventiveness hasn't improved in the "
"short time since you helped them last. Jass asks for a couple of new toys "
"for the folks that haven't taken well to the bow."
msgstr ""
"Recoges tus cosas y dejas atrás la cama para reunirte con Jass y un par de "
"personas justo fuera. Algunos llevan los arcos que [Companion Name] les "
"ayudó a hacer, y otros, arcos nuevos que deben de haber fabricado ellos "
"mismos. Sin embargo, toda fuerza decente necesita variedad (a los arqueros "
"no les iría bien si los Golbins llegaran a sus filas), y su inventiva no ha "
"mejorado en el poco tiempo desde que los ayudaste por última vez. Jass pide "
"un par de juguetes nuevos para quienes no se han adaptado bien al arco."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Just catch some fish and don't look suspicious. Easy."
msgstr "Solo hay que pescar algunos peces y no parecer sospechoso. Fácil."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What was that?"
msgstr "¿Qué ha sido eso?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The folks take up their new weapons eagerly. Though it has only been a short"
" time since Jass gathered them, the combined militia now totaled a couple "
"dozen. You notice as you hand out swords, though most don't have any "
"conventional fighting experience, these people tend to lean capable. Lumber "
"Workers and farmers who've built functional bodies through years of hard "
"labour. Against a trained fighting force, sure, they'd hardly stand a "
"chance. But against a group of ragtag Golbins? You like their odds."
msgstr ""
"La gente coge sus nuevas armas con entusiasmo. Aunque ha pasado poco tiempo "
"desde que Jass los reunió, la milicia ya suma un par de docenas. Mientras "
"repartes espadas, te das cuenta de que, aunque la mayoría no tiene "
"experiencia de combate convencional, esta gente tiende a ser capaz. "
"Leñadores y granjeros que han forjado cuerpos funcionales con años de "
"trabajo duro. Contra una fuerza de combate entrenada, desde luego, no "
"tendrían ninguna oportunidad. ¿Pero contra un grupo de Golbins "
"desharrapados? Te gustan sus posibilidades."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Jass, you sure about this?"
msgstr "Jass, ¿estás segura de esto?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They might not have much experience, but the folks that couldn't hit the "
"broad side of a barn - or just otherwise hated trying to use the bows - I've"
" had running drills with sticks and leftover tools."
msgstr ""
"Puede que no tengan mucha experiencia, pero a los que no le darían ni a una "
"pared (o a los que simplemente odiaban usar el arco) los he tenido haciendo "
"ejercicios con palos y herramientas sobrantes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They got a long way to go, but they know enough to hold their own. I'm not "
"sending them in to die, don't worry."
msgstr ""
"Les queda mucho camino, pero saben lo suficiente para defenderse. No los "
"mando a morir, tranquilo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Good, good. Azamire can't get much smaller if we want to keep calling "
"ourselves a town. "
msgstr ""
"Bien, bien. Azamire no puede hacerse mucho más pequeño si queremos seguir "
"llamándonos pueblo. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If this ambush goes well, they won't need to fight much. Just need to look "
"scary and grab one or two of the Golbins to tell us where they brought the "
"girl."
msgstr ""
"Si la emboscada sale bien, no tendrán que luchar mucho. Solo tienen que "
"parecer temibles y atrapar a uno o dos golbins para que nos digan adónde se "
"han llevado a la niña."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "If everyone's ready, let's head out to the river, then?"
msgstr "Si todo el mundo está listo, ¿vamos al río?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] leads you to the river where the girl went missing. You fondly recall learning to swim with [Companion Name] here, years ago, and wish you were here under less dire circumstances. The militia disperses through the surrounding forest, headed by Jass who quietly gives orders, trying to get people hidden as best she can.\n"
"\n"
"You and [Companion Name] settle in by the riverbank, and pull out your rods, hoping to catch a bit more than just a few fish. You're a bit too nervous for idle conversation, so you both quietly fall into a rhythm, just trying to look like two innocuous people fishing late into the night."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] te lleva al río donde desapareció la niña. Recuerdas con cariño cuando aprendiste a nadar aquí con [Companion Name], hace años, y desearías estar aquí en circunstancias menos graves. La milicia se dispersa por el bosque de alrededor, encabezada por Jass, que da órdenes en voz baja e intenta esconder a la gente lo mejor que puede.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] y tú os acomodáis en la orilla y sacáis las cañas, con la esperanza de pescar algo más que unos cuantos peces. Estáis demasiado nerviosos para charlar, así que los dos os sumís en silencio en un ritmo, intentando parecer dos personas inofensivas que pescan hasta altas horas de la noche."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm not going to let [Companion Name] beat me!"
msgstr "¡No voy a dejar que [Companion Name] me gane!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That should be about all of them."
msgstr "Con eso deberían estar casi todos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You worry for a moment that one of the militia members is being too loud "
"before you see it. A group of Golbins, sauntering up with hardly a care in "
"the world, barking orders at one another, trying to surround you and "
"[Companion Name]. It's... more than you expected, and as you start to get up"
" to defend yourself, an arrow sinks right between the leading Golbin's "
"shoulder blades. "
msgstr ""
"Por un momento temes que uno de los milicianos esté haciendo demasiado "
"ruido, antes de verlo. Un grupo de golbins que se acerca pavoneándose sin la"
" menor preocupación, ladrándose órdenes unos a otros e intentando rodearos a"
" [Companion Name] y a ti. Son... más de los que esperabas, y cuando empiezas"
" a levantarte para defenderte, una flecha se clava justo entre los omóplatos"
" del golbin que va en cabeza. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Everyone, now!"
msgstr "¡Todos, ahora!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Make sure to leave a couple breathing!"
msgstr "¡Aseguraos de dejar a un par respirando!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Bet you I'll kill more than you. Try not to die."
msgstr "Te apuesto a que mato más que tú. Intenta no morirte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're on."
msgstr "Hecho."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name]'s look of anxiety hidden under bravado is quickly replaced "
"with confidence as the woods explode with movement. The militia lets loose a"
" volley of arrows that pepper the unprepared Golbins, scattering them and "
"sending a few more to the ground. What's left of them gather themselves and "
"charge towards you and your friend, or the quickly approaching villagers "
"armed with swords."
msgstr ""
"La mirada de ansiedad que [Companion Name] escondía tras su bravuconería se "
"transforma rápidamente en confianza cuando el bosque estalla en movimiento. "
"La milicia suelta una lluvia de flechas que acribilla a los golbins "
"desprevenidos, los dispersa y derriba a unos cuantos más. Los que quedan se "
"reagrupan y cargan contra ti y tu amigo, o contra los aldeanos armados con "
"espadas que se acercan a toda prisa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You look around as the movement begins to settle. The Golbin force was larger than you had anticipated, but your efforts went as well as could be expected. Among the bodies littering the forest floor, from what you could see, only a couple were human, which was better than expected considering their experience.\n"
"\n"
"You rush over as you hear a shout from Jass, who managed to pin a dark green Golbin to ground. The beast would have hardly came up to your hip had it been on its feet, and you could hear it whimpering and begging not to be hurt. It quickly rattles off fragments of information that it thinks could be useful, detailing how its clan was taken over by a rival group led by someone it called the 'Ringleader', its own name - Gloob - and how it really really wants to live. Jass slaps her hand over its mouth and asks it where the girl they kidnapped was, and why they took her. Gloob goes one step further, and says that it'll lead you all there to its nearby camp, and that they were going to try and paint him and sell him off too, whatever that may mean.\n"
"\n"
"You discuss it briefly together, and decide to 'trust' it to do as it says. Surely enough, the camp is close, and the leftover defenders quickly scatter as they see they're vastly outnumbered, leaving their camp behind. You and [Companion Name] quickly find Ana in one of their tents and take her home, while Jass and the militia handle a dozen or so other folks who had been captured from elsewhere throughout the countryside. Ana's mother meets you just outside of Azamire with tears in her eyes, thanking you over and over again for saving her daughter."
msgstr ""
"Miras a tu alrededor mientras el movimiento empieza a calmarse. La fuerza golbin era mayor de lo que habías previsto, pero vuestros esfuerzos han salido todo lo bien que cabía esperar. Entre los cuerpos que cubren el suelo del bosque, por lo que alcanzas a ver, solo un par eran humanos, mejor de lo esperado teniendo en cuenta su experiencia.\n"
"\n"
"Corres hacia allí al oír un grito de Jass, que ha logrado inmovilizar contra el suelo a un golbin verde oscuro. De pie, la criatura apenas te habría llegado a la cadera, y la oyes gimotear y suplicar que no le hagan daño. Suelta a toda prisa retazos de información que cree que podrían ser útiles: cuenta cómo un grupo rival dirigido por alguien al que llama «el Cabecilla» se hizo con su clan, cuál es su nombre (Gloob) y cuánto, pero cuánto, quiere vivir. Jass le tapa la boca con la mano y le pregunta dónde está la niña que secuestraron y por qué se la llevaron. Gloob va un paso más allá y dice que os llevará a todos a su campamento, que está cerca, y que también iban a intentar pintarlo y venderlo, signifique eso lo que signifique.\n"
"\n"
"Lo habláis un momento y decidís «fiaros» de que hará lo que dice. Efectivamente, el campamento está cerca, y los defensores que quedan se dispersan en cuanto ven que los superáis ampliamente en número, abandonando el campamento. [Companion Name] y tú encontráis enseguida a Ana en una de sus tiendas y la lleváis a casa, mientras Jass y la milicia se ocupan de una docena de personas que habían sido capturadas en otros lugares de la región. La madre de Ana os recibe a las afueras de Azamire con lágrimas en los ojos y os da las gracias una y otra vez por salvar a su hija."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 4[/color] Enemy "
"multiple times"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar varias veces a un enemigo de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de "
"combate 4[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Boarish Bonfire"
msgstr "Hoguera del jabalí"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Azamire has slowly but surely begun to get back onto its feet, and that's "
"cause for celebration. The town's impromptu mayor, Hapren, has thought of "
"just the thing to get folks together, a bit of warmth and food in the center"
" of town."
msgstr ""
"Azamire ha empezado, poco a poco, a recuperarse, y eso hay que celebrarlo. "
"El alcalde improvisado del pueblo, Hapren, ha tenido la idea perfecta para "
"reunir a la gente: un poco de calor y comida en el centro del pueblo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A little cleanup could go a long way to making things feel a bit more put "
"together."
msgstr ""
"Un poco de limpieza podría ayudar mucho a que todo parezca más ordenado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Looking a lot nicer."
msgstr "Esto ya tiene mucho mejor aspecto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A handful of people you haven't seen before walk past, likely another group "
"of refugees from one of the nearby villages that fared even worse than "
"Azamire, attacked around the same time. The town's new mayor - the son of "
"the previous mayor that was lost in the attack - welcomes them and directs "
"them towards one of the newly repaired buildings that they were using to "
"shelter people before more buildings could be made to house them. Once he "
"wraps up, he sets his eyes on you and [Companion Name]."
msgstr ""
"Pasa un puñado de personas a las que no habías visto antes, seguramente otro"
" grupo de refugiados de alguna de las aldeas cercanas que salieron aún peor "
"paradas que Azamire, atacadas más o menos a la vez. El nuevo alcalde del "
"pueblo (el hijo del anterior alcalde, que murió en el ataque) les da la "
"bienvenida y los dirige a uno de los edificios recién reparados que usaban "
"para dar cobijo a la gente hasta que pudieran construirse más edificios para"
" alojarla. Cuando termina, fija la mirada en [Companion Name] y en ti."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hey there, you two. I hope that things have been as good as they can be, "
"considering..."
msgstr ""
"Hola, vosotros dos. Espero que las cosas os vayan todo lo bien que pueden "
"ir, teniendo en cuenta..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Everything?"
msgstr "¿Todo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Exactly... There's no easy way to put such a tragedy, huh?"
msgstr ""
"Exacto... No hay una forma fácil de hablar de semejante tragedia, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There really isn't. You inherited quite the mess, didn't you?"
msgstr "La verdad es que no. Has heredado todo un desastre, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Don't suppose either of you would be willing to take over, would you?"
msgstr "No querríais ninguno de los dos ocupar el puesto, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Afraid not. Never had the decorum to fit into a role like that. "
msgstr ""
"Me temo que no. Nunca he tenido el decoro necesario para un papel así. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Didn't figure. Well, would you two mind helping me out with a little "
"project, then?"
msgstr ""
"Ya me lo imaginaba. Bueno, ¿os importaría echarme una mano con un pequeño "
"proyecto, entonces?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What do you have in mind, exactly?"
msgstr "¿Qué tienes en mente, exactamente?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hapren brings the two of you over to the center of town, which has been "
"piled with debris from Azamire's cleanup efforts. He talks about how he'd "
"love to throw a little gathering for the town, just so folks can get to know"
" one another and feel a bit of normalcy despite how hard the last while has "
"been. A few people try their best to break down the rubble into movable "
"chunks, but progress is slow, and Hapren asks for help before starting to "
"work on the pile himself."
msgstr ""
"Hapren os lleva al centro del pueblo, donde se han amontonado los escombros "
"de la limpieza de Azamire. Os cuenta que le encantaría organizar una pequeña"
" reunión para el pueblo, solo para que la gente se conozca y sienta algo de "
"normalidad a pesar de lo duro que ha sido este tiempo. Unas cuantas personas"
" hacen lo que pueden para romper los escombros en trozos que se puedan "
"mover, pero avanzan despacio, y Hapren os pide ayuda antes de ponerse él "
"mismo a trabajar en el montón."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Nothing too flashy, just gotta pull up enough fish to show them how it's "
"done."
msgstr ""
"Nada demasiado vistoso, solo tengo que sacar suficientes peces para "
"enseñarles cómo se hace."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Huh, there really is a lot of junk in the water. Wonder where it's coming "
"from?"
msgstr "Vaya, sí que hay basura en el agua. ¿De dónde saldrá?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With you and [Companion Name]'s help, you manage to break up the debris in short order, and Hapren directs much of the salvageable materials to be stored for reconstruction efforts, and the wood that is too mangled to be used to be left in the square to be used for the bonfire.\n"
"\n"
"Just as you set your tools down, a few tired looking folks make their way into the center of town, fishing gear in hand."
msgstr ""
"Con tu ayuda y la de [Companion Name], conseguís romper los escombros en poco tiempo, y Hapren ordena guardar gran parte de los materiales aprovechables para la reconstrucción, y dejar en la plaza la madera demasiado destrozada para usarla, para la hoguera.\n"
"\n"
"Justo cuando dejas las herramientas, unas cuantas personas de aspecto cansado llegan al centro del pueblo con los aparejos de pesca en la mano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If I couldn't see them swimming around, I'd swear the stock of fish had run "
"dry."
msgstr "Si no los viera nadar por ahí, juraría que se han acabado los peces."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Feels like we're pullin' more junk out of the water than fish."
msgstr "Parece que sacamos más basura del agua que peces."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Rough day?"
msgstr "¿Un día duro?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You could say that. I see that the town square is just about ready, but I'm "
"sorry... It'll take us a week to have enough fish at this rate."
msgstr ""
"Podría decirse. Veo que la plaza del pueblo está casi lista, pero lo "
"siento... A este ritmo tardaremos una semana en tener suficientes peces."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Wait, you're using Mackerel Bait, right? Only way I've managed to pull "
"anything out of there."
msgstr ""
"Un momento, estáis usando cebo de jurel, ¿no? Es la única forma en que he "
"conseguido sacar algo de ahí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...No. Honestly, don't think I've ever used much more than a worm, really."
msgstr "...No. La verdad, no creo haber usado nunca mucho más que un gusano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, you don't need it, but it sure doesn't hurt."
msgstr "Bueno, no te hace falta, pero desde luego no viene mal."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Since we're just about done here... While we get things set up, would you "
"mind lending them a hand?"
msgstr ""
"Ya que aquí casi hemos terminado... Mientras lo preparamos todo, ¿os "
"importaría echarles una mano?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] looks to you and searches your face, trying to gauge your "
"reaction. You shrug, and then offer to help. Getting together a bit of bait "
"to help the fishers out, then showing them how to work with the river "
"shouldn't take too long, and it'd be nice for the town to be able to keep "
"itself fed."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] te mira y escudriña tu cara, intentando adivinar tu "
"reacción. Te encoges de hombros y te ofreces a ayudar. Reunir un poco de "
"cebo para ayudar a los pescadores y luego enseñarles a trabajar con el río "
"no debería llevar mucho tiempo, y estaría bien que el pueblo pudiera "
"alimentarse por sí mismo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There's no helping it, then!"
msgstr "¡No queda otra, entonces!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe Hapren would appreciate the meat?"
msgstr "¿Quizá Hapren agradecería la carne?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You all spend awhile on the pebble bank, sitting and waiting for a fish to "
"bite, as one typically does while fishing. You and [Companion Name] talk to "
"the fishermen for a while and learn that they used to be able to pull out "
"enough fish to feed half the town, even without the bait. When you dump bait"
" in the water, and start using some on your hooks, things pick up, but it's "
"still rather slow. You watch even more junk float by. Bits of tree branches,"
" huge clumps of soil, and then, a dead Golbin. The fishers point out that "
"it's been like this for a few days, minus the Golbins at least."
msgstr ""
"Pasáis un buen rato en la orilla de guijarros, sentados esperando a que "
"pique un pez, como suele hacerse al pescar. [Companion Name] y tú habláis un"
" rato con los pescadores y descubrís que antes sacaban peces suficientes "
"para alimentar a medio pueblo, incluso sin cebo. Cuando echáis cebo al agua "
"y empezáis a ponerlo en los anzuelos, la cosa mejora, pero sigue siendo "
"bastante lento. Ves pasar flotando todavía más basura. Trozos de ramas, "
"enormes terrones de tierra y, luego, un golbin muerto. Los pescadores "
"comentan que lleva así unos días, quitando los golbins, al menos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Something must be going on up river, this is just odd."
msgstr "Algo tiene que estar pasando río arriba, esto es muy raro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You all can keep fishing. Try not to reel in... anything green."
msgstr "Vosotros podéis seguir pescando. Intentad no sacar... nada verde."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're going to go check it out, aren't you?"
msgstr "Vas a ir a echar un vistazo, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Of course we are. You're coming too, obviously. Unless you want to see me "
"floating by, next?"
msgstr ""
"Pues claro que vamos. Tú también vienes, evidentemente. ¿O quieres verme "
"pasar flotando a mí, la próxima vez?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I haven't shown them how I usually tie my hooks yet, I really-"
msgstr ""
"Todavía no les he enseñado cómo suelo atar los anzuelos, de verdad que..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They stop their protesting as you grab their shoulder and pull them behind you. You know from all your time together they'd never really let you go by yourself, but as they grumble behind you, it's clear they're not pleased about running off to find... whatever is, up river.\n"
"\n"
"After a few minute jaunt upstream, you see it. A massive boar standing over a group of dead Golbins. It pulls against ropes that had been tied to trees along the river, and then thrown over the top of the beast. As you approach it catches sight of you both, assumes and breaks the last of its restrains as it charges towards you!"
msgstr ""
"Dejan de protestar cuando les agarras del hombro y tiras de ellos para que te sigan. Sabes, por todo el tiempo que habéis pasado juntos, que nunca te dejarían ir sin compañía, pero mientras refunfuñan detrás de ti, está claro que no les hace ninguna gracia salir corriendo en busca de... lo que sea que haya río arriba.\n"
"\n"
"Tras unos minutos de caminata río arriba, lo ves. Un jabalí enorme plantado sobre un grupo de golbins muertos. Tira de unas cuerdas que habían atado a los árboles junto al río y luego le habían echado por encima. Cuando os acercáis, os ve a los dos, se pone en guardia y rompe las últimas ataduras mientras carga contra vosotros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With the help of some villagers and their carts, you manage to bring back the Golbin's pet taming project. Hapren is shocked, then pleased, as he realizes that this is a far better catch than a few fish from the river.\n"
"\n"
"As the sun sets, the wooden debris from the square is burnt and thick slabs of boar are grilled and given out to everyone in attendance. More and more curious folks poke their heads into the square and are met with warmth and light conversation.  A few folks even start up with light songs as the night progresses and Azamire's paltry stores of booze are enjoyed by those who indulge.\n"
"\n"
"Azamire's attack is far from forgotten, but this quiet moment amongst the survivors does well to begin healing the towns aching wounds."
msgstr ""
"Con la ayuda de algunos aldeanos y sus carros, conseguís traer de vuelta el proyecto de doma de mascota de los golbins. Hapren se queda de piedra y luego se alegra, al darse cuenta de que es una presa mucho mejor que unos cuantos peces del río.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando se pone el sol, se queman los restos de madera de la plaza y se asan gruesas tajadas de jabalí que se reparten entre todos los asistentes. Cada vez más curiosos asoman la cabeza a la plaza y son recibidos con calidez y conversación ligera.  Algunos incluso se ponen a cantar canciones alegres a medida que avanza la noche, y quienes se dan el gusto disfrutan de las escasas reservas de bebida de Azamire.\n"
"\n"
"El ataque a Azamire está lejos de olvidarse, pero este momento de calma entre los supervivientes ayuda a empezar a curar las dolorosas heridas del pueblo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 8[/color] Enemy"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar a un enemigo de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de combate "
"8[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Misty Reconnaissance"
msgstr "Reconocimiento brumoso"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gloob and Jass have been 'working' together for a while, and now need your "
"help to launch a daring mission... or stupidly walk into a Golbin's trap."
msgstr ""
"Gloob y Jass llevan un tiempo «trabajando» juntos y ahora necesitan tu ayuda"
" para emprender una misión audaz... o para meterse estúpidamente en una "
"trampa golbin."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I should be able to follow Gloob's schematics easy enough."
msgstr "Debería poder seguir los planos de Gloob sin problema."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "These should work!"
msgstr "¡Esto debería funcionar!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you walk back into Azamire, you feel a swell of pride at the number of newly constructed buildings. They're small, and it hardly takes you long to count them on two hands, but still, Azamire is rebuilding, bit by bit.\n"
"\n"
"Your delight is interrupted by a shriek as you hear a... Golbin run by, chased by the newly appointed Militia Captain - Jass. The chase doesn't last long, and Gloob is held down while Jass berates it, talking about how she's no fool and knows a trap when she sees one."
msgstr ""
"Al volver a Azamire, sientes una oleada de orgullo al ver la cantidad de edificios recién construidos. Son pequeños, y apenas tardas en contarlos con los dedos de las dos manos, pero aun así, Azamire se está reconstruyendo poco a poco.\n"
"\n"
"Un chillido interrumpe tu alegría cuando oyes pasar corriendo a un... golbin, perseguido por la recién nombrada capitana de la milicia, Jass. La persecución no dura mucho, y Gloob acaba inmovilizado mientras Jass lo reprende, diciendo que no es ninguna tonta y que reconoce una trampa en cuanto la ve."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I see that things are going well."
msgstr "Veo que las cosas van bien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "SHE'S GOING TO EAT ME, PLEASE HELP!"
msgstr "¡ME VA A COMER, AYUDA, POR FAVOR!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're keeping you here because you were meant to help us, beast!"
msgstr "¡Te tenemos aquí porque se suponía que ibas a ayudarnos, bestia!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What I said was true! You should be able to sneak into the Ringleader's "
"fortress at night, it'd be fine!"
msgstr ""
"¡Lo que dije era verdad! ¡Deberíais poder colaros de noche en la fortaleza "
"del Cabecilla, no pasaría nada!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The guards have wood for brains! You'll see what I mean!"
msgstr ""
"¡Los guardias tienen serrín en la cabeza! ¡Ya veréis a qué me refiero!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We'll do no such thing! We ought to string you up for what your little pack "
"did to Ana!"
msgstr ""
"¡No haremos nada de eso! ¡Deberíamos colgarte por lo que tu manada le hizo a"
" Ana!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What's happening, exactly?"
msgstr "¿Qué está pasando, exactamente?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This beast, is trying to get us to sneak into its boss's hideout tonight. "
"Says all the Golbins will be out escorting a shipment."
msgstr ""
"Esta bestia intenta convencernos de que nos colemos esta noche en la guarida"
" de su jefe. Dice que todos los golbins estarán fuera escoltando un "
"cargamento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A shipment of..."
msgstr "Un cargamento de..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...humans. That's what the Ringleader wants from all of the Golbin tribes he"
" subjugates!"
msgstr ""
"...humanos. ¡Es lo que el Cabecilla quiere de todas las tribus golbin que "
"somete!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I told you that when you saved me from that group days ago!"
msgstr "¡Te lo dije cuando me salvaste de aquel grupo hace días!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What do you mean, saved you?"
msgstr "¿Cómo que te salvé?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm... little. Never been useful for much, the other Golbins said. Too 'so-"
"fist-uh-cated', they'd say."
msgstr ""
"Soy... pequeño. Nunca he servido para mucho, decían los otros golbins. "
"Demasiado «so-fis-ti-ca-do», decían."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They were going to tie me up and try to put me in one of the shipments, too,"
" since I wanted to 'act like a human'. "
msgstr ""
"Iban a atarme y a intentar meterme también en uno de los cargamentos, porque"
" quería «comportarme como un humano». "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And why the blazes would they do that?"
msgstr "¿Y por qué demonios iban a hacer eso?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Because if a tribe doesn't pay up with enough people, the Ringleader takes "
"his tithe in other ways. Turns us into ents. "
msgstr ""
"Porque si una tribu no paga con suficientes personas, el Cabecilla cobra su "
"diezmo de otras formas. Nos convierte en ents. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Something about needing a creature's lifeforce. But I wasn't even ever part "
"of that tribe, I got outcast from my own years ago."
msgstr ""
"Algo de que necesita la fuerza vital de una criatura. Pero yo ni siquiera "
"llegué a formar parte de esa tribu, me expulsaron de la mía hace años."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And then they captured you again sometime after the Ringleader took over?"
msgstr ""
"¿Y luego volvieron a capturarte en algún momento después de que el Cabecilla"
" tomara el control?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Why were you in the group that attacked us, then?"
msgstr "Entonces, ¿por qué estabas en el grupo que nos atacó?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"One of the Golbin's fancied himself a knight and wanted to use me as a "
"squire. Carry his weapons n' stuff."
msgstr ""
"Uno de los golbins se creía caballero y quería usarme de escudero. Llevarle "
"las armas y esas cosas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We don't even have knights. But everyone thought it was funny, so they let "
"him until it was going to be time to lump me in with a shipment."
msgstr ""
"Ni siquiera tenemos caballeros. Pero a todos les hacía gracia, así que le "
"dejaron hasta que llegara el momento de meterme en un cargamento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So... You've never even hurt a person?"
msgstr "Entonces... ¿nunca le has hecho daño a nadie?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No! I even traded with some of your people up north. I would make stuff, "
"then sell it for books. I learned lots."
msgstr ""
"¡No! Hasta comerciaba con algunos de los vuestros, allá en el norte. "
"Fabricaba cosas y luego las vendía a cambio de libros. Aprendí mucho."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Jass... A moment?"
msgstr "Jass... ¿Un momento?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You believe this little green booger, don't you?"
msgstr "Te crees a este mocoso verde, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You manage to pull Jass aside long enough to get her to calm down. She apologies, first to you, then even to Gloob, and says that when she learned that they were capturing people to 'send them somewhere' it sent her over the edge. She asks Gloob to fill you in on what he told her. Every full moon, a bunch of robed figures end up coming to the Ringleader's fortress within the Elder Grove. They come with large, wooden wagons, and leave with people that the surrounding Golbin tribes have captured.\n"
"\n"
"He goes on to say that the Golbins at the fortress leave with the robed figures, escorting them... wherever they go, he doesn't know. With the nearing full-moon, it'd be a great chance to get a peek into the fortress, and that he'd even go, but that he'd need some climbing gear and hooks to scale the fort's outer wall. Either hopefully or foolishly, you decide to trust him, and he details how he'd go about making the equipment. You and Jass decide it'd be good to bring [Companion Name] along as well, and that they'd go over Gloob's memory of the fort to plan the scouting mission while you make the gear."
msgstr ""
"Consigues apartar a Jass el tiempo suficiente para que se calme. Se disculpa, primero contigo y luego incluso con Gloob, y dice que cuando se enteró de que capturaban a gente para «mandarla a algún sitio», perdió los estribos. Le pide a Gloob que te ponga al día de lo que le contó. Cada luna llena, un grupo de figuras con túnicas acude a la fortaleza del Cabecilla en la Arboleda Ancestral. Llegan con grandes carros de madera y se marchan con la gente que han capturado las tribus golbin de los alrededores.\n"
"\n"
"Cuenta también que los golbins de la fortaleza se van con las figuras de las túnicas y las escoltan... adondequiera que vayan, eso no lo sabe. Con la luna llena tan cerca, sería una gran oportunidad para echar un vistazo a la fortaleza, e incluso él iría, pero necesitaría equipo de escalada y garfios para trepar por la muralla exterior. Ya sea por esperanza o por insensatez, decides confiar en él, y te explica con detalle cómo fabricaría el equipo. Jass y tú decidís que estaría bien llevar también a [Companion Name], y que repasarán los recuerdos de Gloob sobre el fuerte para planear la misión de exploración mientras tú fabricas el equipo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You, Gloob, and [Companion Name] set off into the Misty Thicket on the night of the full moon. Gloob brings you through the woods quickly, and it's tough to keep up with his speed. You and [Companion Name] find yourselves huffing and puffing just outside of the Ringleader's Fortress. In the moonlight, you all see a train of wagons and hobgolbins heading to the north along an old dirt road, but quickly lose track of it as they slip into the dense thicket.\n"
"\n"
"With them gone, the three of you use the gear you prepared and scale the walls, landing quietly on the other side. Gloob brings you to several spots throughout the relatively open grounds. A small, ramshackle prison, with several ents patrolling just outside. You pass by a handful of sleeping areas for the fort's living guards, until you reach a large wooden hut Gloob says is the Ringleader's home. Finally, he leads you to a stockpile of various bits that a Golbin would find valuable, taken as tribute or looted from nearby towns. Hides, half-rotten food, weapons and armor, gold, and most notably, dozens upon dozens of caskets of flammable oil and booze.\n"
"\n"
"You and [Companion Name] wait for Gloob to lead you into an ambush, but the trap never comes. True to his word, once he finishes with the important parts of the fortress, the three of you scale back over the wall and head back to Azamire. When you return, you immediately begin talks with Jass about launching an assault on the fortress with what you've learned, and set plans into motion to get the town ready. Clearing a path to bring wagons to the fort, and securing an exit route for prisoners will be essential before launching an attack. Plus, it gives Jass more time to get her people ready, too."
msgstr ""
"Gloob, [Companion Name] y tú os adentráis en el Matorral brumoso la noche de luna llena. Gloob os guía rápido por el bosque, y cuesta seguir su ritmo. [Companion Name] y tú acabáis resoplando justo a las afueras de la fortaleza del Cabecilla. A la luz de la luna, veis una caravana de carros y hobgolbins que se dirige al norte por un viejo camino de tierra, pero pronto le perdéis la pista cuando se adentra en la espesura.\n"
"\n"
"Una vez que se han ido, los tres usáis el equipo que habéis preparado para escalar los muros y aterrizáis sin hacer ruido al otro lado. Gloob os lleva a varios puntos del recinto, bastante despejado. Una pequeña prisión destartalada, con varios ents patrullando justo fuera. Pasáis junto a unas cuantas zonas donde duermen los guardias vivos del fuerte, hasta llegar a una gran cabaña de madera que, según Gloob, es la casa del Cabecilla. Por último, os lleva a un almacén de cachivaches diversos que un golbin consideraría valiosos, obtenidos como tributo o saqueados de pueblos cercanos. Pieles, comida medio podrida, armas y armaduras, oro y, sobre todo, docenas y docenas de toneles de aceite inflamable y alcohol.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] y tú esperáis a que Gloob os conduzca a una emboscada, pero la trampa nunca llega. Fiel a su palabra, cuando termina de enseñaros las partes importantes de la fortaleza, los tres volvéis a saltar el muro y regresáis a Azamire. Al volver, empiezas enseguida a hablar con Jass sobre lanzar un asalto a la fortaleza con lo que habéis averiguado, y ponéis en marcha los planes para preparar el pueblo. Abrir un camino para llevar carros hasta el fuerte y asegurar una ruta de huida para los prisioneros será esencial antes de lanzar un ataque. Además, así Jass tendrá más tiempo para preparar a su gente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Rocky Rumble"
msgstr "Estruendo rocoso"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The old Northern Road will take Azamire's wagons close to the Ringleader's "
"Fortress, but due to a rockslide, it's unusable. With a bit of effort, it "
"should be usable once again!"
msgstr ""
"El viejo Camino del Norte llevaría los carros de Azamire cerca de la "
"fortaleza del Cabecilla, pero un desprendimiento lo ha dejado inservible. "
"¡Con un poco de esfuerzo, debería volver a ser transitable!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Chisel first, then make them into volatile bombs. Easy."
msgstr "Primero cincelar y luego convertirlas en bombas volátiles. Fácil."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Don't drop them don't drop them don't drop them."
msgstr "Que no se caigan que no se caigan que no se caigan."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gloob - who is now allowed to freely roam the town after your scouting "
"mission proved his loyalty - fetches you and brings you to Jass's newly "
"constructed 'barracks'. In reality, it was just an enclosed room with some "
"storage for gear and a few targets set up, but it was coming along nicely. "
"Within her office, a map of the surrounding lands was laid out, recently "
"purchased from one of the infrequent caravans that just started to come by "
"once again."
msgstr ""
"Gloob (al que ahora dejan moverse libremente por el pueblo después de que "
"vuestra misión de exploración demostrara su lealtad) va a buscarte y te "
"lleva al «cuartel» recién construido de Jass. En realidad, no era más que "
"una sala cerrada con algo de almacenaje para el equipo y unas cuantas "
"dianas, pero iba tomando forma. En su despacho había desplegado un mapa de "
"las tierras de alrededor, comprado hacía poco a una de las escasas caravanas"
" que acababan de empezar a pasar de nuevo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Ah, [Player Name], you're here. We're planning our path to the fortress, but"
" our scouts ran into a bit of a snag."
msgstr ""
"Ah, [Player Name], ya estás aquí. Estamos planeando la ruta hacia la "
"fortaleza, pero nuestros exploradores se han topado con un problemilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh? Is everyone alright?"
msgstr "¿Ah, sí? ¿Están todos bien?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No one is hurt. But a bit of the Old Northern Road that passes through the "
"Foggy Canyon has been buried under a rock slide. "
msgstr ""
"Nadie ha resultado herido. Pero un tramo del viejo Camino del Norte que "
"atraviesa el Cañón Neblinoso ha quedado sepultado por un desprendimiento. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Then it seems we should just find another path, no?"
msgstr "Entonces parece que deberíamos buscar otro camino, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That'd be great, but this is the only feasible way to bring wagons up to the"
" fortress. We'll need them to carry gear, and... wounded, after the battle."
msgstr ""
"Sería genial, pero es la única forma viable de llevar carros hasta la "
"fortaleza. Los necesitaremos para transportar el equipo y... a los heridos, "
"después de la batalla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Don't fret though! I know how to clear it! I just need a bit of help from "
"you."
msgstr ""
"¡Pero no os preocupéis! ¡Sé cómo despejarlo! Solo necesito un poco de ayuda "
"tuya."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Just... you and me, clearing a rockslide? How well can you swing a pick?"
msgstr ""
"¿Solo... tú y yo, despejando un desprendimiento? ¿Qué tal se te da manejar "
"un pico?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "No no, I have something far better."
msgstr "No, no, tengo algo mucho mejor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gloob gives you the rundown on an idea he's tried before. With a bit of "
"effort, careful chiselling, and sulfur, fire runes could be made into shaped"
" bombs could carefully carve a path through the rockslide. Not only that, "
"he's actually already prepped some runes they traded for, but needs help "
"with the chiselling and then... putting a bit more volatile fire energy into"
" them."
msgstr ""
"Gloob te explica a grandes rasgos una idea que ya ha probado antes. Con un "
"poco de esfuerzo, un cincelado cuidadoso y azufre, las runas de fuego "
"podrían convertirse en bombas con forma capaces de abrir con cuidado un "
"camino a través del desprendimiento. Y no solo eso: ya ha preparado algunas "
"runas que consiguieron en un trueque, pero necesita ayuda con el cincelado y"
" luego para... meterles un poco más de energía de fuego volátil."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't suppose they're interested in talking this one out."
msgstr "No creo que les apetezca resolver esto hablando."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That seems like all of them, for now."
msgstr "Parece que ya están todos, por ahora."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You carefully bring the volatile runes down to the Foggy Canyon along with "
"Gloob and set to work tucking them into the rock. Gloob lights them as you "
"move away, and sure enough, they work exceedingly well. Gloob stands "
"triumphantly as bits of rock pelt the two of you after the series of "
"explosions."
msgstr ""
"Llevas con cuidado las runas volátiles hasta el Cañón Neblinoso junto con "
"Gloob y os ponéis a encajarlas en la roca. Gloob las enciende mientras te "
"alejas y, efectivamente, funcionan de maravilla. Gloob se yergue triunfante "
"mientras trozos de roca os acribillan a los dos tras la serie de "
"explosiones."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And that is why reading is cool! "
msgstr "¡Y por eso leer mola! "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wait, what does this have to do with reading?"
msgstr "Espera, ¿qué tiene que ver esto con leer?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I got the idea for these bombs after reading about a wizard that was "
"banished from her family for blowing up half her estate. Tough luck, right?"
msgstr ""
"Se me ocurrió la idea de estas bombas al leer sobre una maga a la que su "
"familia desterró por volar media finca. Qué mala suerte, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wow, do you think it was on purpose?"
msgstr "Vaya, ¿crees que lo hizo a propósito?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No clue! But it got me thinking about what happens when magic goes wrong, "
"you know?"
msgstr ""
"¡Ni idea! Pero me hizo pensar en lo que pasa cuando la magia sale mal, "
"¿sabes?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I should... be a little more careful with fire spells in the future."
msgstr ""
"Debería... tener un poco más de cuidado con los hechizos de fuego en el "
"futuro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's always good to practice caution! Shall we get back to bombing the crap "
"out of this canyon now?"
msgstr ""
"¡Siempre es bueno ser prudente! ¿Seguimos volando este cañón en mil pedazos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Of course! It actually seems that some of the rocks are already moving out "
"of the way in fear, should be a bit less to handle."
msgstr ""
"¡Claro! De hecho, parece que algunas rocas ya se están apartando de miedo, "
"así que habrá un poco menos que despejar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wait."
msgstr "Espera."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Why are the rocks moving?"
msgstr "¿Por qué se mueven las rocas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As the question leaves your lips, several golems rise from the piles of "
"rock, doubtlessly less than pleased with your explosive intrusion on their "
"turf. They seem quite keen on smashing you into the ground so they can "
"return to their nap."
msgstr ""
"Mientras la pregunta sale de tus labios, varios gólems se alzan de los "
"montones de roca, sin duda nada contentos con tu explosiva intrusión en su "
"territorio. Parecen muy decididos a aplastarte contra el suelo para poder "
"volver a su siesta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Maybe I should ask someone in the mines..? Nah, what's the worst that could "
"happen?"
msgstr ""
"¿Quizá debería preguntar a alguien en las minas...? Bah, ¿qué es lo peor que"
" podría pasar?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think that should hold!"
msgstr "¡Creo que esto debería aguantar!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The golems now lay crushed at your feet. Gloob held his own well, using his "
"speed to distract them and a few carefully placed bombs to take out a few of"
" his own. As the two of you catch your breath, one of the walls of the "
"canyon cracks and Gloob jumps back and wraps himself around your leg in "
"fear. A massive sheet of stone falls to the ground in front of you. After "
"the dust settles, Gloob removes himself from your leg and clears his throat "
"while dusting himself off."
msgstr ""
"Los gólems yacen ahora aplastados a tus pies. Gloob se defendió bien, usando"
" su velocidad para distraerlos y unas cuantas bombas bien colocadas para "
"acabar con algunos él solo. Mientras recuperáis el aliento, una de las "
"paredes del cañón se agrieta y Gloob da un salto atrás y se abraza a tu "
"pierna, muerto de miedo. Una enorme lámina de piedra cae al suelo delante de"
" ti. Cuando se asienta el polvo, Gloob se suelta de tu pierna y carraspea "
"mientras se sacude el polvo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, uh... That's certainly not great."
msgstr "Bueno, eh... Eso no es nada bueno."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Shouldn't be hard to break up and move, but if the canyon walls keep "
"collapsing, we'll hardly have a road left here at all."
msgstr ""
"No debería costar romperla y moverla, pero si las paredes del cañón siguen "
"derrumbándose, aquí apenas nos quedará camino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Or... Even worse, it could come down while people are travelling through. "
msgstr "O... peor aún, podría venirse abajo mientras la gente pasa por aquí. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Then we've got to support the walls, yeah? I... haven't read much on "
"building stuff like that, yet."
msgstr ""
"Entonces hay que apuntalar las paredes, ¿no? Yo... todavía no he leído mucho"
" sobre construir cosas así."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] and I have actually helped out in Azamire's mines a few "
"times through the years."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] y yo hemos echado una mano en las minas de Azamire unas "
"cuantas veces a lo largo de los años."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We'll need some rock bolts, which we can make out of steel, then we drive "
"them into the walls."
msgstr ""
"Necesitaremos unos pernos de anclaje, que podemos hacer de acero, y luego "
"los clavamos en las paredes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You walk Gloob through finding good spots for the bolts, and leave him to "
"mark spots in the canyon that'll work well. Then you start to work out how "
"to create strong enough rock bolts to keep the canyon walls from collapsing "
"in on themselves."
msgstr ""
"Le explicas a Gloob cómo encontrar buenos puntos para los pernos y lo dejas "
"marcando en el cañón los sitios que servirán. Luego te pones a averiguar "
"cómo fabricar pernos de anclaje lo bastante resistentes para evitar que las "
"paredes del cañón se derrumben."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The sides of the Foggy Canyon hold once you and Gloob finish up hammering "
"the bolts into its walls. Even as you finish up blowing up the last of the "
"rock that remains along the old Northern Road, your handiwork holds, and "
"after you've finished your work, you no longer fear having a sheet of stone "
"land on your head. You look down to the little Golbin by your hand who beams"
" with pride at a job well done, ecstatic to have been able to put his mind "
"to something and see something tangible come out. The two of you head back "
"to Azamire to report a job well done, and that the Northern Road is clear to"
" use once again."
msgstr ""
"Las paredes del Cañón Neblinoso aguantan en cuanto Gloob y tú termináis de "
"clavar los pernos. Incluso mientras acabas de volar los últimos restos de "
"roca que quedan en el viejo Camino del Norte, tu obra resiste, y cuando "
"terminas el trabajo, ya no temes que una lámina de piedra te caiga en la "
"cabeza. Miras al pequeño golbin que está junto a tu mano, que rebosa orgullo"
" por el trabajo bien hecho, encantado de haber podido aplicar su ingenio a "
"algo y ver un resultado tangible. Los dos volvéis a Azamire para informar "
"del trabajo bien hecho y de que el Camino del Norte vuelve a estar "
"despejado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 15[/color] [u]Dungeon "
"Boss[/u] multiple times"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar varias veces a un [u]jefe de mazmorra[/u] de "
"[color=#FFD16D]nivel de combate 15[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 25[/color] Enemy "
"multiple times"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar varias veces a un enemigo de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de "
"combate 25[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Dungeon Breakout"
msgstr "Fuga de la mazmorra"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A path must be cleared for the prisoners to get out of the Misty Thicket "
"fortress when you launch the attack against the Ringleader, lest they get "
"caught in the crossfire between you and the fortresses' guard."
msgstr ""
"Hay que despejar un camino para que los prisioneros puedan salir de la "
"fortaleza del Matorral brumoso cuando lances el ataque contra el Cabecilla, "
"no vaya a ser que queden atrapados en el fuego cruzado entre tú y la guardia"
" de la fortaleza."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gold coins aren't good enough, eh?"
msgstr "Las monedas de oro no bastan, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hopefully Gloob's contacts pull through."
msgstr "Ojalá los contactos de Gloob cumplan."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The moon was completely hidden by clouds on the night you found yourself "
"outside of the Ringleader's fortress, yet again. The scouting trips had "
"gotten more frequent, though you only had time to go on a few of them "
"lately. But Jass hadn't brought you out for a scouting mission, this time. "
"The two of you wait for a patrol to pass and she brings you to the covered "
"end of a tunnel. You two climb in and follow it for a while, until hitting "
"what must be the wooden wall of the fortress. Gloob is crouched down here, "
"inspecting the wall, not needing any light to see it clearly."
msgstr ""
"La luna estaba completamente oculta tras las nubes la noche en que volviste "
"a encontrarte a las puertas de la fortaleza del Cabecilla. Las salidas de "
"reconocimiento se habían vuelto más frecuentes, aunque últimamente solo "
"habías tenido tiempo de ir a unas pocas. Pero esta vez Jass no te había "
"traído para explorar. Esperáis a que pase una patrulla y ella te lleva hasta"
" la entrada tapada de un túnel. Os metéis dentro y lo seguís un buen rato, "
"hasta toparos con lo que debe de ser la muralla de madera de la fortaleza. "
"Gloob está agachado aquí, inspeccionando la pared, sin necesidad de luz para"
" verla con claridad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Not sure how far down the wall goes, but we can't just dig down further."
msgstr ""
"No sé hasta qué profundidad llega la muralla, pero no podemos seguir cavando"
" hacia abajo sin más."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If it goes all the way down to stone, I wouldn't even know how start trying "
"to get through the stone. I'm no rockhound."
msgstr ""
"Si llega hasta la roca, no sabría ni por dónde empezar a atravesarla. No soy"
" ningún picapedrero."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And forget about keeping it quiet. I know your people have been at this for "
"a while, right? I'm sure moving all this soil is tough."
msgstr ""
"Y olvídate de hacerlo en silencio. Tu gente lleva tiempo con esto, ¿no? "
"Seguro que mover toda esta tierra es duro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You'd bet. We've got to carry it all out and then sprinkle it through the "
"woods. If a patrol came across a random pile of dirt, that'd be... "
"suspicious."
msgstr ""
"Ya te digo. Tenemos que sacarla toda y luego esparcirla por el bosque. Si "
"una patrulla se topara con un montón de tierra sin más, sería... sospechoso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Makes sense. So, you need to get through this wall. Any ideas?"
msgstr ""
"Tiene sentido. Entonces, necesitáis atravesar esta muralla. ¿Alguna idea?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, Gloob says he can get a tool to get through it... Right Gloob?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, Gloob dice que puede conseguir una herramienta para atravesarla... "
"¿Verdad, Gloob?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Yeah, I'm... known to locate some stuff, from time to time."
msgstr "Sí, digamos que... sé encontrar algunas cosas, de vez en cuando."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I made a lot of contacts when I was traveling about. We'd have to trade for "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Hice muchos contactos cuando iba de viaje. Tendríamos que hacer un trueque."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What would your... contacts, want?"
msgstr "¿Y qué querrían tus... contactos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, they typically deal in silver bars. I think it'd usually be about "
"seven or eight bars, but this tool is special item."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, suelen comerciar con lingotes de plata. Creo que normalmente serían "
"unos siete u ocho lingotes, pero esta herramienta es un objeto especial."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's say ten bars even."
msgstr "Digamos diez lingotes justos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ten it is."
msgstr "Pues diez."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You ask what the tool even is, and Gloob starts to describe a magical length"
" of metal fashioned after a knife that, when activated, starts to vibrate "
"rapidly. It should be enough to quietly carve away at the wall, albeit "
"slowly. You leave Gloob to his inspection of the wall, and head off to get "
"some silver."
msgstr ""
"Preguntas qué es exactamente la herramienta, y Gloob empieza a describir una"
" pieza mágica de metal con forma de cuchillo que, al activarse, vibra a toda"
" velocidad. Debería bastar para ir tallando la muralla en silencio, aunque "
"despacio. Dejas a Gloob con su inspección de la pared y te marchas a por "
"algo de plata."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Just press it into the wall and cut, no problem."
msgstr "Basta con apretarlo contra la pared y cortar, sin problema."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't think anyone heard me."
msgstr "Creo que nadie me ha oído."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You hand off the bars to Gloob back in Azamire, and not long after, he shows"
" up on your doorstep, carrying a sheet wrapped around the vibrating knife he"
" described. He happily hands it over."
msgstr ""
"Le entregas los lingotes a Gloob en Azamire y, poco después, se presenta en "
"tu puerta con una sábana envolviendo el cuchillo vibratorio que había "
"descrito. Te lo entrega encantado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Thankfully, it shouldn't take you too long to get through with this."
msgstr "Por suerte, con esto no deberías tardar mucho en atravesarla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Just kinda... press it into the wood and it'll activate. I've marked the "
"hole you need to cut in red paint, okay?"
msgstr ""
"Solo tienes que... apretarlo contra la madera y se activará. He marcado con "
"pintura roja el agujero que tienes que cortar, ¿vale?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Thank you, Gloob. This is really helpful. I know it might feel a bit odd "
"helping us humans out, but I just wanted to let you know that we appreciate "
"your help."
msgstr ""
"Gracias, Gloob. Esto nos ayuda muchísimo. Sé que puede resultarte un poco "
"raro ayudarnos a los humanos, pero quería que supieras que agradecemos tu "
"ayuda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I hope that folks aren't giving you too much trouble around town, are they?"
msgstr ""
"Espero que la gente no te esté dando demasiados problemas por el pueblo, "
"¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Not at all, actually. Maybe a couple weird looks here and there, sure, but "
"they've been more than welcoming."
msgstr ""
"Para nada, la verdad. Alguna que otra mirada rara aquí y allá, claro, pero "
"me han recibido de maravilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Even your mayor! Sounds like he's going to try and get me set up with a "
"workshop of sorts!"
msgstr ""
"¡Hasta vuestro alcalde! ¡Parece que va a intentar montarme una especie de "
"taller!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh and I'm really starting to grow on Jass, and [Companion Name] is having "
"me do a few things around, and also..."
msgstr ""
"Ah, y le estoy empezando a caer muy bien a Jass, y [Companion Name] me tiene"
" haciendo algunas cosillas, y además..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gloob starts to run through... more of his social life than you bargained "
"for, and around the twenty minute mark you cough and mention that you really"
" ought to get going to the fortress. Completely oblivious, he wishes you "
"luck, and you set off. Back down at the end of the tunnel, sure enough, "
"Gloob has marked a large cutout for you to follow."
msgstr ""
"Gloob empieza a repasar... más de su vida social de lo que esperabas, y "
"hacia el minuto veinte carraspeas y comentas que de verdad deberías ir ya a "
"la fortaleza. Sin enterarse de nada, te desea suerte y te pones en marcha. "
"De vuelta al fondo del túnel, efectivamente, Gloob ha marcado un gran "
"recorte para que lo sigas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You're able to cut through the wall after a fair bit of effort, and finally,"
" the chunk of wood settles. You set the tool down beside you and decide to "
"leave it there, in case anyone needs to improve upon your work. Once you're "
"done, you carefully leave the tunnel and cover the entrance once again, "
"before reporting back to Jass. She sends for a few people to go continue "
"with the rest of the tunnel and assures you that it'll be ready for when you"
" need to get the prisoners out."
msgstr ""
"Tras bastante esfuerzo, logras atravesar la muralla y, por fin, el trozo de "
"madera se asienta. Dejas la herramienta a tu lado y decides dejarla allí, "
"por si alguien necesita mejorar tu trabajo. Cuando terminas, sales con "
"cuidado del túnel y vuelves a tapar la entrada antes de informar a Jass. "
"Ella manda a unas cuantas personas a terminar el resto del túnel y te "
"asegura que estará listo para cuando necesites sacar a los prisioneros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Tree Trimming"
msgstr "Poda de árboles"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] has been strangely absent lately, and on the rare chance "
"you do see them, they usually quickly excuse themselves. What's going on?"
msgstr ""
"Últimamente [Companion Name] ha estado extrañamente ausente y, en las raras "
"ocasiones en que os veis, suele excusarse enseguida. ¿Qué está pasando?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Good food always makes you feel better."
msgstr "La buena comida siempre te hace sentir mejor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe I should have gone for something more nutritious..."
msgstr "Quizá debería haber elegido algo más nutritivo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Late in the evening, you head to the recently built home for [Companion Name]. It's nothing fancy - like most of the new constructions in Azamire - but all of the folks who've been contributing the most were given priority in separate lodgings, and they've done wonders for bringing back a bit of normalcy.\n"
"\n"
"What hasn't been normal is how little you've seen [Companion Name] lately. You've had plenty of times where you weren't attached at the hip over the years you've known one another, but you know they've been around. It almost feels as if they've been avoiding you.\n"
"\n"
"You knock several times to no avail. Just as you turn to go, you see a limping figure approach, notice you, and then turn away."
msgstr ""
"A última hora de la tarde, te diriges a la casa recién construida de [Companion Name]. No es nada del otro mundo (como la mayoría de las nuevas construcciones de Azamire), pero quienes más han contribuido han tenido prioridad para recibir alojamiento propio, y eso ha hecho maravillas para devolver un poco de normalidad.\n"
"\n"
"Lo que no ha sido normal es lo poco que has visto a [Companion Name] últimamente. Durante los años que os conocéis, ha habido muchas temporadas en las que no ibais pegados el uno al otro, pero sabías que andaba por ahí. Casi parece que te haya estado evitando.\n"
"\n"
"Llamas varias veces, sin éxito. Justo cuando te das la vuelta para irte, ves una figura que se acerca cojeando, te ve y luego se da la vuelta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...[Companion Name]?"
msgstr "...¿[Companion Name]?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Ohhhh..! Hello there, ol' buddy ol' pal. I'm just... gonna, go... this "
"way..."
msgstr ""
"¡Ohhhh...! Hola, colega de mi vida. Yo solo... voy a, ir... por aquí..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Forgot that I needed to chat with... Hapren! That's right, needed to chat "
"with Hapren."
msgstr ""
"Se me olvidó que tenía que hablar con... ¡Hapren! Eso es, tenía que hablar "
"con Hapren."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name], I'm not really sure what's going on, but if I did "
"something, please... Let me know, okay?"
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name], no sé muy bien qué está pasando, pero si he hecho algo, "
"por favor... Dímelo, ¿vale?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I didn't forget your birthday or anything, did I? I'm sorry, okay..?"
msgstr ""
"No me habré olvidado de tu cumpleaños ni nada, ¿no? Lo siento, ¿vale...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "[Player Name]..."
msgstr "[Player Name]..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "No, I've just been..."
msgstr "No, es que he estado..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I..."
msgstr "Yo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] turns towards you and wobbles on their feet. Even in the low light, you notice the dark red patch blood on the front of their cloak, and trailing down their arms. You rush towards them and manage to catch your best friend before they hit the ground. You quickly run through a list of places you could bring them before settling on their own place. You quickly fish their key out of their pocket and carry them inside. You'd complain about them being heavy if it weren't for the fact your heart was beating out of your chest, knowing how hurt they are and having no idea on why or how.\n"
"\n"
"Digging through both their supplies and yours, you find enough to get them patched up. Across their chest is a large gash with bits of... wood, sticking out of it? You extract it all, bit by bit, in the lantern light, and stitch them back up before wrapping them in gauze. The rest of their wounds are comparatively minor, and take much less time to deal with, but they are numerous, and in various states of healing, some old, some fresh.\n"
"\n"
"Once you're done, [Companion Name] looks more mummy than person, but they'll live. You cover them up to let them rest, and decide to help along their recovery with their favorite food."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] se gira hacia ti y se tambalea. Incluso con tan poca luz, ves la mancha de sangre roja oscura en la parte delantera de su capa, que le gotea por los brazos. Corres hacia allí y consigues sujetar a tu mejor amistad antes de que caiga al suelo. Repasas a toda prisa una lista de sitios adonde llevarle antes de decidirte por su propia casa. Le sacas la llave del bolsillo rápidamente y le llevas dentro. Te quejarías de lo que pesa si no fuera porque el corazón se te sale del pecho, sabiendo lo mal que está y sin tener ni idea de por qué ni cómo.\n"
"\n"
"Rebuscando entre sus provisiones y las tuyas, encuentras lo suficiente para curarle. Le cruza el pecho un gran tajo con trocitos de... ¿madera clavados? Los extraes todos, uno a uno, a la luz del farol, y le das puntos antes de vendarle con gasas. El resto de heridas son leves en comparación y lleva mucho menos tiempo tratarlas, pero son numerosas y están en distintas fases de curación, unas viejas y otras recientes.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando terminas, [Companion Name] parece más una momia que una persona, pero vivirá. Le tapas para que descanse y decides ayudar a su recuperación con su comida favorita."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Time for a little bit of payback."
msgstr "Hora de devolver un poco el golpe."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They're still... moving a bit."
msgstr "Todavía... se mueven un poco."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] manages to quietly eat the cake you give them, and you "
"decide to wait a while before beginning your round of questioning. Once they"
" finish the first half, your questioning begins, and they fake passing out. "
"You roll your eyes, and threaten to take the rest of the cake away and they "
"spring back up, but quickly nurse their wounds after the sudden movement. "
"You ask what happened, how they feel, and what they why they've been "
"avoiding you, but [Companion Name] remains silent for all of it. When you "
"finally ask why they didn't bring you, tears well up in their eyes."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] consigue comerse en silencio la tarta que le das, y decides"
" esperar un rato antes de empezar con el interrogatorio. Cuando se termina "
"la primera mitad, empiezan tus preguntas, y finge desmayarse. Pones los ojos"
" en blanco y amenazas con llevarte el resto de la tarta, y se incorpora de "
"un salto, aunque enseguida se lleva la mano a las heridas por el movimiento "
"brusco. Le preguntas qué ha pasado, cómo se encuentra y por qué te ha estado"
" evitando, pero [Companion Name] guarda silencio ante todo. Cuando por fin "
"le preguntas por qué no te llevó, se le llenan los ojos de lágrimas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... I couldn't put you in danger, [Player Name]."
msgstr "Yo... No podía ponerte en peligro, [Player Name]."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What do you mean, you couldn't put me in danger?"
msgstr "¿Cómo que no podías ponerme en peligro?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If you were doing something dangerous, then I especially should have been "
"there!"
msgstr ""
"¡Si estabas haciendo algo peligroso, con más razón tendría que haber estado "
"allí!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What were you thinking?"
msgstr "¿En qué estabas pensando?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That I didn't want to lose you too!"
msgstr "¡En que no quería perderte a ti también!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That I had to keep Azamire safe and if I brought you with me, you might not "
"come back!"
msgstr ""
"¡En que tenía que mantener Azamire a salvo y que, si te llevaba, quizá no "
"volverías!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We've already lost twenty more people on the route to the Ringleader's "
"fortress in the past couple weeks."
msgstr ""
"En las últimas dos semanas ya hemos perdido a veinte personas más en el "
"camino a la fortaleza del Cabecilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"All but two of them were to a single weird ent. Way bigger than the rest, "
"and covered in these weird... talismans."
msgstr ""
"Todas menos dos, a manos de un único ent muy raro. Mucho más grande que los "
"demás y cubierto de unos... talismanes extraños."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That's what did this to you?"
msgstr "¿Eso es lo que te ha hecho esto?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I didn't want to bring you in case... It had something we couldn't handle."
msgstr "No quería llevarte por si... Tenía algo que no pudiéramos manejar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We lost so much in the attack, but at least... I still had you. I couldn't "
"lose you, too."
msgstr ""
"Perdimos tanto en el ataque, pero al menos... todavía te tenía a ti. No "
"podía perderte a ti también."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So you tried to fight it on your own? [Companion Name] why-"
msgstr ""
"¿Así que intentaste enfrentarte a él por tu cuenta? [Companion Name], ¿por "
"qué...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I just wanted to see it! I've been practicing on the smaller ones all this "
"time."
msgstr ""
"¡Solo quería verlo! Llevo todo este tiempo practicando con los pequeños."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Tonight, I figured that I could get a look at the big one, learn what it "
"could do, come back to town, and come up with a plan against it."
msgstr ""
"Esta noche pensé que podría echarle un vistazo al grande, ver lo que era "
"capaz de hacer, volver al pueblo y trazar un plan contra él."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So... what happened?"
msgstr "Entonces... ¿qué pasó?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They detail the events of the night. How they came across the creature, and the talismans in its branches flashed with a bright blue light as they tried to run away. How they floated up into the air and were sucked towards the ent while they flailed about in the air, and then how the ent sent them flying after the talismans in its branches flashed bright blue. [Companion Name] was sure they were going to die, until they saw that the talismans in the ent's branches matched the similar charms forming a line in the nearby treeline. The giant ent shuffled back and forth at that line, but wouldn't cross it. Then, they limped all the way back to Azamire.\n"
"\n"
"After a through amount of ridicule and chastisement, you hug them and tell them you're glad they're okay.\n"
"\n"
"In the morning you detail everything that happened to Jass, who gathers up the archers of her militia and send them out with you and a wounded [Companion Name], who leads you to the grove with the giant ent. It seems that it has been joined by several of the smaller ones, but you aren't dissuaded. "
msgstr ""
"Te cuenta lo ocurrido esa noche. Cómo se topó con la criatura, y cómo los talismanes de sus ramas destellaron con una intensa luz azul cuando intentó huir. Cómo se elevó por los aires y algo le arrastró hacia el ent mientras pataleaba en el aire, y cómo luego el ent le mandó por los aires cuando los talismanes de sus ramas volvieron a destellar en azul. [Companion Name] daba por hecho que iba a morir, hasta que vio que los talismanes de las ramas del ent coincidían con unos amuletos parecidos que formaban una línea en la linde del bosque cercano. El ent gigante iba y venía arrastrándose junto a esa línea, pero no la cruzaba. Después, volvió cojeando hasta Azamire.\n"
"\n"
"Tras una buena dosis de burlas y reprimendas, le das un abrazo y le dices que te alegras de que esté bien.\n"
"\n"
"Por la mañana le cuentas todo lo ocurrido a Jass, que reúne a los arqueros de su milicia y los envía contigo y con [Companion Name], que aún arrastra sus heridas y os guía hasta la arboleda del ent gigante. Parece que se le han unido varios de los pequeños, pero eso no te desanima. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's make them a bit smaller, turned into ash."
msgstr "Hagámoslos un poco más pequeños, convertidos en ceniza."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Think that's everything!"
msgstr "¡Creo que eso es todo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The ents are all down, and the archers do their best to shoot the talismans "
"out of the trees incase they do... anything bad. [Companion Name] holds "
"their bow at their side, pleased to have gotten a little payback, then kicks"
" at an ent's branch that seems to be trying to crawl away."
msgstr ""
"Todos los ents han caído, y los arqueros hacen lo posible por derribar a "
"flechazos los talismanes de los árboles, por si acaso hacen... algo malo. "
"[Companion Name] sostiene el arco a un costado, con la satisfacción de haber"
" podido devolver un poco el golpe, y luego le da una patada a la rama de un "
"ent que parece intentar escabullirse arrastrándose."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Thank you... I'm sorry I tried to play the hero."
msgstr "Gracias... Siento haber intentado hacerme el héroe."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If you didn't... I probably would have. I don't want to lose you either."
msgstr ""
"Si no lo hubieras hecho tú... seguramente lo habría hecho yo. Yo tampoco "
"quiero perderte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Please, don't do something like that again, okay? I need you too."
msgstr ""
"Por favor, no vuelvas a hacer algo así, ¿vale? Yo también te necesito."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Okay okay... You too, alright? Promise?"
msgstr "Vale, vale... Tú tampoco, ¿de acuerdo? ¿Lo prometes?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Promise."
msgstr "Lo prometo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Me too."
msgstr "Yo también."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Seems the trees aren't quite 'dead' yet, huh?"
msgstr "Parece que los árboles no están del todo «muertos» todavía, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Doubt they'll survive being turned into ash, don't you think?"
msgstr "Dudo que sobrevivan a convertirse en ceniza, ¿no crees?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Everyone gathers up the ent parts. They don't seem dangerous anymore, but "
"you do notice that - slowly but surely - they're starting to gain new "
"growth. If you waited long enough, they'd likely become a threat again. The "
"archers help by snapping off new branches and tossing them back into the "
"pile, and occasionally making sure that none have managed to crawl away."
msgstr ""
"Todos recogen los restos de los ents. Ya no parecen peligrosos, pero te das "
"cuenta de que, lenta pero inexorablemente, empiezan a echar brotes nuevos. "
"Si esperaras lo suficiente, seguramente volverían a ser una amenaza. Los "
"arqueros ayudan arrancando las ramas nuevas y echándolas de nuevo al montón,"
" y de vez en cuando se aseguran de que ninguna haya logrado escabullirse."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The last bit of smoke goes out as the final pile of burning ent runs out of "
"fuel. You were almost tempted to start trying to grill something, but the "
"idea of the smoke being evil and getting into the food dissuaded any "
"attempts. [Companion Name] leans against you, both for comfort, and because "
"they are far from recovered from their wounds. You tease them lightly about "
"getting smacked around by kindling, to which they reply by driving the butt "
"of their bow into your foot. You tussel their hair and give them a hug, and "
"tell them that you're glad they're safe."
msgstr ""
"La última voluta de humo se apaga cuando el último montón de ent ardiendo se"
" queda sin combustible. Casi te tienta ponerte a asar algo, pero la idea de "
"que el humo fuera maligno y se metiera en la comida te quitó las ganas. "
"[Companion Name] se apoya en ti, en parte para reconfortarse y en parte "
"porque está lejos de haberse recuperado de sus heridas. Le tomas un poco el "
"pelo por haberse dejado zarandear por unas ramitas, y te responde clavándote"
" la culata del arco en el pie. Le revuelves el pelo, le das un abrazo y le "
"dices que te alegras de que esté a salvo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 35[/color] "
"[b][u]Miniboss[/u][/b]"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar a un [b][u]minijefe[/u][/b] de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de "
"combate 35[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "In the Thick of It"
msgstr "En plena refriega"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Azamire is as ready as it ever will be to take down the Ringleader. The old "
"Northern Road is clear, Jass's crew has finished the tunnel to the prison, "
"and you have defeated the worst of the Misty Thicket's roaming guards. Now, "
"all that's left to do is burn the fortress to the ground."
msgstr ""
"Azamire está todo lo preparada que puede estar para acabar con el Cabecilla."
" El antiguo Camino del Norte está despejado, el equipo de Jass ha terminado "
"el túnel hasta la prisión y has derrotado a los peores guardias errantes del"
" Matorral brumoso. Ahora solo queda reducir la fortaleza a cenizas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If I want any supplies, I should take them from the cart before the attack "
"starts in earnest."
msgstr ""
"Si quiero provisiones, debería cogerlas del carro antes de que empiece el "
"ataque de verdad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's time."
msgstr "Ha llegado la hora."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you walk through Azamire, the town is abuzz with nervous energy. Several wagons are lined up and everyone who isn't fighting have come out to wish you well. Hapren approaches, and mentions that the town has gotten together and prepared some combat supplies into the back of one of the carts for you, and hopes that it helps.\n"
"\n"
"You all set off, and as the sun begins to set, the cold mist of the thicket starts to seep into your clothes. The militia is tense, but ready. There are people to save, and taking out the Ringleader would go a long way towards making everyone safer."
msgstr ""
"Mientras recorres Azamire, el pueblo bulle de energía nerviosa. Hay varias carretas en fila y todos los que no van a combatir han salido a desearte suerte. Hapren se acerca y te cuenta que el pueblo se ha organizado para prepararte algunas provisiones de combate en la parte trasera de uno de los carros, y espera que te sirvan.\n"
"\n"
"Os ponéis en marcha y, cuando el sol empieza a ponerse, la fría niebla del matorral empieza a calarte la ropa. La milicia está tensa, pero preparada. Hay gente a la que salvar, y acabar con el Cabecilla contribuiría mucho a que todos estuvieran más seguros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Everyone's ready?"
msgstr "¿Todo el mundo listo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's get this done."
msgstr "Acabemos con esto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Don't have any qualms with this, Gloob?"
msgstr "¿No tienes ningún reparo con esto, Gloob?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I might be green, but I'm no Golbin. Let's take him out."
msgstr "Seré verde, pero no soy ningún golbin. Acabemos con él."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You okay, [Player Name]?"
msgstr "¿Estás bien, [Player Name]?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Never better. Plan is the same, still?"
msgstr "Mejor que nunca. ¿El plan sigue siendo el mismo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That's right. The tunnel under the prison is ready to get the prisoners out,"
" and we'll have people posted at the exit."
msgstr ""
"Así es. El túnel bajo la prisión está listo para sacar a los prisioneros, y "
"tendremos gente apostada en la salida."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As soon as people start escaping down the tunnel, the guards will notice "
"everyone's missing and sound the alarm."
msgstr ""
"En cuanto la gente empiece a escapar por el túnel, los guardias se darán "
"cuenta de que faltan todos y darán la alarma."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Once that happens, archers will try to hit that stockpile you mentioned with"
" flaming arrows."
msgstr ""
"Cuando eso pase, los arqueros intentarán alcanzar con flechas incendiarias "
"ese almacén que mencionaste."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Should deal with most of the ents inside, and make a ton of noise. You'll be"
" providing the fire, of course, we need several braziers lit."
msgstr ""
"Eso debería acabar con la mayoría de los ents de dentro y armar un buen "
"jaleo. Tú pondrás el fuego, claro: necesitamos encender varios braseros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"After that, we head to the gate and hack it down. The archers will keep us "
"covered."
msgstr ""
"Después, vamos a la puerta y la echamos abajo a hachazos. Los arqueros nos "
"cubrirán."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And then we're in. Try to avoid the fire, and head for the Ringleader?"
msgstr ""
"Y entonces estaremos dentro. ¿Evitamos el fuego y vamos a por el Cabecilla?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Exactly. Can't miss 'em. Big blue fella, covered in every gaudy fabric he "
"fancies."
msgstr ""
"Exacto. No tiene pérdida. Un tipo grande y azul, cubierto de todas las telas"
" chillonas que se le antojan."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Things are going to get really hectic once this starts."
msgstr "Las cosas se van a poner muy movidas en cuanto empiece esto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Stay safe, everyone."
msgstr "Tened cuidado, todos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You too, [Player Name]. You too."
msgstr "Tú también, [Player Name]. Tú también."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you finish your conversation, the fortress's outer wall comes into view. "
"Gloob and small group of the militia break off and head for the tunnel while"
" the rest of you set up on the hillside just outside. Several braziers are "
"set up, and everyone starts to load them with wood while you and [Companion "
"Name] get to work."
msgstr ""
"Al terminar la conversación, aparece a la vista la muralla exterior de la "
"fortaleza. Gloob y un pequeño grupo de la milicia se separan y se dirigen al"
" túnel, mientras el resto os apostáis en la ladera justo al lado. Se montan "
"varios braseros y todos empiezan a llenarlos de leña mientras tú y "
"[Companion Name] os ponéis manos a la obra."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We have to get through this gate!"
msgstr "¡Tenemos que atravesar esta puerta!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There! A hole!"
msgstr "¡Ahí! ¡Un agujero!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Alarms start to sound as the militia's arrows are lit. You clutch your weapon in anticipation, wishing you could to go check on the tunnel to see how Gloob's breakout went, but there's no time. The hillside is lit up with the fires you and [Companion Name] started, and hobgolbins on the wall begin to shoot towards you. But it's too late. Burning arrow after arrow soar up and over the wall, towards where you pointed out the stockpile. No one can see over the wall, so it's tough to tell if anyone is on target until a resounding BOOM make you cover your ears, even from this far away.\n"
"\n"
"Many of the defenders are thrown from the wall entirely, and as you and the militia charge, the swordsmen dispatch the stunned hobgolbins that fell on the wrong side of the wall. Arrows start to fall again, as the fort's guards gather themselves, and they're met with your militia's own volleys."
msgstr ""
"Las alarmas empiezan a sonar mientras se encienden las flechas de la milicia. Aprietas el arma, expectante, deseando poder ir a ver cómo ha ido la fuga de Gloob por el túnel, pero no hay tiempo. La ladera está iluminada por los fuegos que habéis encendido tú y [Companion Name], y los hobgolbins de la muralla empiezan a disparar hacia vosotros. Pero es demasiado tarde. Una flecha en llamas tras otra se eleva por encima de la muralla, hacia donde señalaste el almacén. Nadie puede ver por encima de la muralla, así que es difícil saber si alguien ha acertado, hasta que un BUM ensordecedor te obliga a taparte los oídos, incluso desde tan lejos.\n"
"\n"
"Muchos de los defensores salen despedidos de la muralla, y mientras tú y la milicia cargáis, los espadachines rematan a los hobgolbins aturdidos que cayeron en el lado equivocado de la muralla. Las flechas vuelven a caer en cuanto los guardias del fuerte se recomponen, y se topan con las andanadas de tu propia milicia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "FOR AZAMIRE!"
msgstr "¡POR AZAMIRE!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Don't stop running until you hit the gate! "
msgstr "¡No dejéis de correr hasta llegar a la puerta! "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We can do this! Push on!"
msgstr "¡Podemos hacerlo! ¡Adelante!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You and [Companion Name] reach the gate first and take out your axes, "
"followed by a small group of other militia members who follow suit and get "
"to work. Another group comes with large shields that they hold with both "
"hands, more table than shield. But they work well as the shield group form a"
" defensive shell around you and overhead, giving you room to work without "
"worrying about an arrow finding its way in your unprotected back."
msgstr ""
"Tú y [Companion Name] llegáis primero a la puerta y sacáis las hachas, "
"seguidos de un pequeño grupo de milicianos que os imitan y se ponen manos a "
"la obra. Llega otro grupo con grandes escudos que sujetan con ambas manos, "
"más mesas que escudos. Pero funcionan bien: el grupo de escudos forma un "
"caparazón defensivo a vuestro alrededor y por encima, y os da espacio para "
"trabajar sin preocuparos de que una flecha encuentre el camino hasta vuestra"
" espalda desprotegida."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We will not fall. Not this time."
msgstr "No caeremos. Esta vez no."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's... done."
msgstr "Ya... está."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The occasional pained grunt, or worse, the painted gurgles of someone who was struck somewhere lethal, dampen your mood. You knew people would fall today. You can only imagine how the people on the hillside are faring. Just as your mind starts to lose focus, thinking about those you'd lose, you see a burning light at the end of your axe. As you pull it back, you realize you're through! You give a cheer that turns into a battlecry, and your group follows suit. A few more axe strikes and enough holes are opened to let Azamire's troops push through the gate.\n"
"\n"
"The fort grounds are... hellish. Most of the ent guardians already crawl on the ground, crying out with groaning wails as they burn, with nearly every structure already completely engulfed in flames. You wonder for a moment if there's even a point of being inside until a massive blue Golbin covered in singed fabric cries out as he locks eyes with you. The rest of the fort's surviving defenders stand in the middle of the blazing stronghold with the Ringleader, smashing weapons against their shields, waiting for orders. "
msgstr ""
"Algún que otro gruñido de dolor o, peor aún, los gorgoteos agónicos de alguien alcanzado en un punto mortal te ensombrecen el ánimo. Sabías que hoy caería gente. Solo puedes imaginar cómo les va a los de la ladera. Justo cuando tu mente empieza a perder la concentración, pensando en a quiénes perderías, ves una luz ardiente al final de tu hacha. Al retirarla, ¡te das cuenta de que has atravesado la puerta! Sueltas un grito de alegría que se convierte en grito de guerra, y tu grupo te imita. Unos cuantos hachazos más y se abren suficientes huecos para que las tropas de Azamire crucen la puerta.\n"
"\n"
"El recinto del fuerte es... un infierno. La mayoría de los ents guardianes ya se arrastran por el suelo, soltando lamentos y gemidos mientras arden, y casi todas las estructuras están ya envueltas en llamas. Por un momento te preguntas si tiene sentido siquiera estar dentro, hasta que un enorme golbin azul cubierto de telas chamuscadas suelta un grito al cruzar la mirada contigo. El resto de defensores supervivientes del fuerte aguardan en medio de la fortaleza en llamas junto al Cabecilla, golpeando las armas contra los escudos, a la espera de órdenes. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Humans want to be hand delivered to masters?"
msgstr "¿Humanos querer ser entregados en mano a amos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ringleader need new stock, others just ran out."
msgstr "Cabecilla necesitar nueva mercancía, otros acabar de escapar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Come to me. Time for you to die."
msgstr "Venir a mí. Hora de que tú morir."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Keep the rest of them off [Player Name] and [Companion Name]! "
msgstr "¡Mantened al resto lejos de [Player Name] y [Companion Name]! "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Know that we fight not just for those back home, not just to save "
"yourselves..."
msgstr ""
"Sabed que no luchamos solo por los que esperan en casa, ni solo para "
"salvarnos..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But for everyone we've lost!"
msgstr "¡Sino por todos los que hemos perdido!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Together! Go! Now! Kill them all!"
msgstr "¡Juntos! ¡Vamos! ¡Ya! ¡Acabad con todos!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "[Player Name], I'm with you. Trust me! I'll keep you safe!"
msgstr "[Player Name], estoy contigo. ¡Confía en mí! ¡Te protegeré!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Not a single person falters as they stream past you, charging with weapons and heads held high. You don't turn away as you see some being driven through as the Ringleader's forces crash into your own. Time slows as you push through, trusting your people to keep you safe. As you make it through the bodies, the Ringleader stands with a gnarled smirk, holding what must be half a burning tree as its weapon, seemingly unbothered by the flames that flicker up its arm.\n"
"\n"
"You hear people roar in the battle behind you, some in victory, others... likely as their last act of defiance against the opposing force. You steel yourself and step forward, challenging the Ringleader."
msgstr ""
"Ni una sola persona flaquea al pasar a tu lado, cargando con las armas y la cabeza bien altas. No apartas la mirada cuando ves que atraviesan a algunos mientras las fuerzas del Cabecilla chocan con las tuyas. El tiempo se ralentiza mientras te abres paso, confiando en que tu gente te proteja. Al dejar atrás los cuerpos, el Cabecilla te espera con una sonrisa retorcida, empuñando como arma lo que debe de ser medio árbol en llamas, aparentemente impasible ante las llamas que le suben por el brazo.\n"
"\n"
"Oyes a la gente rugir en la batalla a tu espalda, algunos de victoria, otros... seguramente como último acto de desafío contra la fuerza enemiga. Haces acopio de valor y das un paso al frente para desafiar al Cabecilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Before you lies the broken body of the Ringleader, sickly purple blood spilling from his wounds. You finally spare a glance to those around you, and you realize... it's over. Less than half the attacking force remains, but Azamire's people still stand.  Gloob stands among the militia, deep green body covered in the blue blood of hobgolbins, and he lets out a cheer, one that the remaining militia proudly meet. Jass barks out orders, pointing out wounded with the stump of her arm, then starting to pull one of the wounded towards the gate with her other.\n"
"\n"
"Half a dozen emotions cross [Companion Name]'s face the second you look at them, but most among them all, relief. They embrace you for naught but a moment before heading towards the Ringleader, who barely manages a ragged breath. As you approach, the beast lets out a throaty cackle before it devolves into a choking cough. You ask it two questions. Where did the shipments go, and who are the people it works for?\n"
"\n"
"He just sits and smirks, the flames of his burning fortress dancing in his eyes.\n"
"\n"
"\"They'll come back soon.\""
msgstr ""
"Ante ti yace el cuerpo destrozado del Cabecilla, del que mana una enfermiza sangre morada. Por fin echas un vistazo a tu alrededor y te das cuenta de que... se acabó. Queda menos de la mitad de la fuerza atacante, pero la gente de Azamire sigue en pie.  Gloob está entre la milicia, con su cuerpo verde oscuro cubierto de la sangre azul de los hobgolbins, y suelta un grito de júbilo al que la milicia superviviente responde con orgullo. Jass ladra órdenes, señalando a los heridos con el muñón del brazo, y luego empieza a arrastrar con el otro a uno de ellos hacia la puerta.\n"
"\n"
"Media docena de emociones cruzan el rostro de [Companion Name] en cuanto le miras, pero, por encima de todas, alivio. Te abraza apenas un instante antes de dirigirse hacia el Cabecilla, que a duras penas logra respirar. Cuando os acercáis, la bestia suelta una carcajada ronca que degenera en una tos ahogada. Le haces dos preguntas: ¿adónde fueron los cargamentos y quiénes son aquellos para los que trabaja?\n"
"\n"
"Se limita a quedarse ahí sentado con una sonrisita, con las llamas de su fortaleza ardiendo bailándole en los ojos.\n"
"\n"
"«Ellos volver pronto.»"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 36[/color] Enemy "
"multiple times"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar varias veces a un enemigo de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de "
"combate 36[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 39[/color] "
"[b][u]Pinnacle Boss[/u][/b]"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar a un [b][u]jefe supremo[/u][/b] de [color=#FFD16D]nivel"
" de combate 39[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Sand in the Wind"
msgstr "Arena en el viento"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"After a short stay back in Azamire, you and [Companion Name] find it hard to"
" rest. There's still so much to be done. The Ringleader was merely the first"
" step."
msgstr ""
"Tras una breve estancia de vuelta en Azamire, a [Companion Name] y a ti os "
"cuesta descansar. Aún queda mucho por hacer. El Cabecilla solo fue el primer"
" paso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They travelled a long, long way."
msgstr "Viajaron muy, muy lejos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Like, really long."
msgstr "Pero lejísimos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The day following your attack on the Ringleader's fort is met with a mixture of joy, relief, grief, and... uncertainty. \n"
"While the assault was successful, casualties number in the range of a few dozen, a large blow to the already wavering population of your home.\n"
"\n"
"However, with the number of refugees coming and going nowadays, ebbs and flows in the local populace are getting hard to keep track of. While callous, you are thankful that no one you knew well fell - though a few of the original militia recruits you and [Companion Name] trained were among the bodies you brought back on the wagons.\n"
"\n"
"Yesterday's events weren't enough to keep you or [Companion Name] down for long, though. The two of you set off back to the fort at first light, searching for tracks of the caravan you saw leave the fort on your first scouting mission. The set of buildings behind their thick wall still smouldered from the night before, reminding you both of the battle."
msgstr ""
"El día siguiente a vuestro ataque contra el fuerte del Cabecilla llega con una mezcla de alegría, alivio, dolor y... incertidumbre. \n"
"Aunque el asalto tuvo éxito, las bajas rondan unas pocas docenas, un duro golpe para la ya mermada población de tu hogar.\n"
"\n"
"Sin embargo, con la cantidad de refugiados que van y vienen hoy en día, cuesta seguir la pista a los altibajos de la población local. Aunque suene cruel, agradeces que no cayera nadie a quien conocieras bien, aunque entre los cuerpos que trajisteis en los carros había algunos de los primeros reclutas de la milicia que [Companion Name] y tú entrenasteis.\n"
"\n"
"Aun así, los sucesos de ayer no bastaron para hundiros mucho tiempo ni a ti ni a [Companion Name]. Los dos volvéis al fuerte con las primeras luces, buscando huellas de la caravana que visteis salir de allí en vuestra primera misión de reconocimiento. El conjunto de edificios tras su grueso muro aún humea desde la noche anterior y os recuerda a ambos la batalla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Time to stomp around the forest a bit, eh?"
msgstr "Hora de pisotear un poco el bosque, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Heading north... been a while since we've been this far from home."
msgstr "Rumbo al norte... hacía tiempo que no estábamos tan lejos de casa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You've always wanted to see the world. "
msgstr "Siempre has querido ver mundo. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Couldn't ask for better company, either. Though... wish the circumstances "
"were a bit less..."
msgstr ""
"Tampoco podría pedir mejor compañía. Aunque... ojalá las circunstancias "
"fueran un poco menos..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Dour?"
msgstr "¿Sombrías?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We first scouted the fortress out... what, two weeks back?"
msgstr "Exploramos la fortaleza por primera vez hace... ¿qué, dos semanas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Feels like it could have been yesterday, or half a year ago."
msgstr "Parece que podría haber sido ayer o hace medio año."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's been a long two weeks."
msgstr "Han sido dos semanas muy largas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Think we'll still be able to track them?"
msgstr "¿Crees que aún podremos seguirles el rastro?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With several wagons and a pack of hobgolbins, I don't see them as being "
"particularly sneaky."
msgstr ""
"Con varias carretas y una manada de hobgolbins, no creo que sean "
"especialmente sigilosos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And I doubt this stretch of woods sees much traffic, either. Let's see what "
"we can find."
msgstr ""
"Y dudo que por este tramo de bosque pase mucha gente. Veamos qué "
"encontramos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Sure enough, the prisoner caravan cut a long, winding trail that isn't too "
"hard to follow. Torn up grass and foliage here, a few trees moved aside "
"there. Concerningly, the path looks... well-travelled. You're glad Azamire "
"was able to put a stop to the Ringleader's export of people from the area, "
"but you can't help but wonder how many towns fared a similar fate to your "
"own. "
msgstr ""
"Efectivamente, la caravana de prisioneros dejó un rastro largo y sinuoso que"
" no es muy difícil de seguir. Hierba y follaje arrancados por aquí, unos "
"cuantos árboles apartados por allá. Lo preocupante es que el camino "
"parece... muy transitado. Te alegras de que Azamire pudiera acabar con el "
"tráfico de personas que el Cabecilla sacaba de la zona, pero no puedes "
"evitar preguntarte cuántos pueblos corrieron una suerte parecida a la del "
"tuyo. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I should provide some basic supplies to help."
msgstr "Debería aportar algunos suministros básicos para ayudar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That should do it."
msgstr "Con eso debería bastar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Following the caravan takes you ages. You travel north, out of the Elder Grove and just an hour's walk outside of the town of Hirane until the tracks stop. Several wagons were stopped here and burned, presumably by the hobgolbins bringing them. It seems that several captives were killed, though for what reason, you don't know. From what you're able to gather, the group split into well over thirty different parties, all heading off in different directions. Doubtlessly impossible to follow them all, even without the added difficulty of being much harder to track than the wagons.\n"
"\n"
"You worry for a moment about Hirane's safety until you realize that the golbins would have to have a small army to raze a town of their size. Being situated on the Heartroad - one of the main throughputs to the capital of Melvor - certainly had its advantages. Being able to trade for finely crafted arms and armor was chief among them, but the Golbin's presence still gave you pause.\n"
"\n"
"You and [Companion Name] decide to head into town, and the general mood of the place is... tense. Folks who seem to be citizens quickly hurry past haggard, haunted-looking villagers. It's a sight you're well acquainted with, though you're surprised to see it here. You and [Companion Name] are quickly approached by a fussy-looking man with an immaculately cared for mustache and a permanent scowl etched on his face."
msgstr ""
"Seguir a la caravana os lleva una eternidad. Viajáis hacia el norte, fuera de la Arboleda ancestral, hasta que las huellas se detienen a solo una hora a pie de la ciudad de Hirane. Aquí detuvieron e incendiaron varios carros, seguramente los hobgolbins que los conducían. Parece que mataron a varios cautivos, aunque no sabes por qué. Por lo que logras deducir, el grupo se dividió en más de treinta partidas que se marcharon en direcciones distintas. Sin duda es imposible seguirlas a todas, incluso sin la dificultad añadida de que son mucho más difíciles de rastrear que los carros.\n"
"\n"
"Por un momento te preocupa la seguridad de Hirane, hasta que te das cuenta de que los golbins necesitarían un pequeño ejército para arrasar una ciudad de su tamaño. Estar situada en el Camino del Corazón, una de las principales vías hacia la capital de Melvor, sin duda tenía sus ventajas. Poder comerciar con armas y armaduras de gran calidad era la principal, pero la presencia de los golbins aún te hacía dudar.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] y tú decidís entrar en la ciudad, y el ambiente general del lugar es... tenso. La gente que parece ser de la ciudad pasa a toda prisa junto a aldeanos demacrados y de mirada atormentada. Es una imagen que conoces bien, aunque te sorprende verla aquí. Enseguida se acerca a [Companion Name] y a ti un hombre de aspecto quisquilloso, con un bigote impecablemente cuidado y un ceño permanente grabado en la cara."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If you wish to seek refuge within the town's walls, you must go to the "
"registrar's office and submit your documentation."
msgstr ""
"Si deseáis refugiaros dentro de las murallas del pueblo, debéis ir a la "
"oficina del registro y presentar vuestra documentación."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You can expect a wait time of-"
msgstr "Podéis esperar un tiempo de espera de..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And it's a pleasure to me you too. I am [Companion Name], this is [Player "
"Name]."
msgstr ""
"Y es un placer conocerte a ti también. Soy [Companion Name], y esta persona "
"es [Player Name]."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...That's usually how a conversation starts, at least."
msgstr "...Así suele empezar una conversación, al menos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I simply do not have the time for idle chit-chat. You two are just one group"
" of many flowing into town."
msgstr ""
"Sencillamente no tengo tiempo para charlas ociosas. Vosotros dos solo sois "
"uno de los muchos grupos que llegan a la ciudad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I apologize if I come off as rude, I am simply trying to be as efficient as "
"I can be in these trying times."
msgstr ""
"Disculpad si parezco grosero, simplemente intento ser lo más eficiente "
"posible en estos tiempos difíciles."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And what exactly ails your town so?"
msgstr "¿Y qué es exactamente lo que aflige tanto a vuestro pueblo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...The same as everywhere, this side of the sands."
msgstr "...Lo mismo que en todas partes a este lado de las arenas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Cloaked figures attacking with beasts never before seen or heard of."
msgstr "Figuras encapuchadas que atacan con bestias nunca vistas ni oídas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They're razing farmland, attacking trade caravans, and burning hamlets to "
"the ground."
msgstr ""
"Arrasan tierras de cultivo, atacan caravanas comerciales y reducen aldeas a "
"cenizas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You'd think we were at war, with how frequent and destructive the attacks "
"are."
msgstr ""
"Cualquiera diría que estamos en guerra, con lo frecuentes y destructivos que"
" son los ataques."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Anywhere outside of a walled-in town seems to be fair game to them. That... "
"is, why you're here, no?"
msgstr ""
"Para ellos, cualquier sitio fuera de un pueblo amurallado parece presa "
"fácil. Por eso... estáis aquí, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, yes, but not for refuge. We were tracking a convoy belonging to a "
"group of them from the south, but they dispersed about an hour outside of "
"town."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, sí, pero no buscamos refugio. Seguíamos un convoy de un grupo de "
"ellos que venía del sur, pero se dispersaron a una hora del pueblo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That'd be by... the Elder Grove, no? Nasty business with Golbins down there "
"right now, I hear."
msgstr ""
"Eso sería junto a... la Arboleda ancestral, ¿no? He oído que ahora mismo "
"allí abajo hay un asunto feo con los golbins."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not anymore, thankfully."
msgstr "Ya no, por suerte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Unsurprisingly, Curo had no idea what [Companion Name] was talking about, until the two of you walk him through Azamire's attack on the fortress and the defeat of the Ringleader. While skeptical, he sends out a scouting party to confirm your claims. Through an only slightly more pleasant conversation with the man after a light change in disposition, you learn that people have begun flocking to Hirane out of fear, or lack of options.\n"
"\n"
"They've done what they can, but are quickly being stretched short with many of the nearby villages being attacked, and much of the farmland nearby being abandoned out of fear. When you and [Companion Name] press him for more details, he's dismissive, and says he may be able to help, should you prove useful and your claims of razing the Ringleader's fort prove true."
msgstr ""
"Como era de esperar, Curo no tenía ni idea de lo que hablaba [Companion Name], hasta que le contáis el ataque de Azamire a la fortaleza y la derrota del Cabecilla. Aunque escéptico, envía una partida de exploradores para confirmar lo que decís. En una conversación solo un poco más agradable con el hombre, tras un leve cambio de actitud, descubrís que la gente ha empezado a acudir en masa a Hirane por miedo o por falta de opciones.\n"
"\n"
"Han hecho lo que han podido, pero se están quedando cortos rápidamente, con muchas de las aldeas cercanas atacadas y gran parte de las tierras de cultivo de los alrededores abandonadas por miedo. Cuando tú y [Companion Name] le pedís más detalles, se muestra desdeñoso y dice que quizá pueda ayudaros, si demostráis ser útiles y resulta cierto que arrasasteis el fuerte del Cabecilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wow, they're well stocked. That's helpful, at least."
msgstr "Vaya, tienen buenas reservas. Al menos eso ayuda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Seems like they've got it mostly handled, now."
msgstr "Parece que ya lo tienen casi todo bajo control."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You and [Companion Name] drop off another package of supplies, hopeful that what you've been able to provide lightens Hirane's burdens a bit. One of the women in charge of the relief tent cheerfully accepts, a bit surprised by the weight of your goods.\n"
"\n"
"Just as you turn to go, Curo approaches you and [Companion Name] with an uncharacteristic smile, holding a leaflet of paper and being flanked by two people who seem to be scouts. He waves off a few people who vie for his attention."
msgstr ""
"Tú y [Companion Name] entregáis otro paquete de provisiones, con la esperanza de que lo que habéis aportado alivie un poco las cargas de Hirane. Una de las mujeres a cargo de la tienda de socorro lo acepta con alegría, algo sorprendida por el peso de vuestros bienes.\n"
"\n"
"Justo cuando os dais la vuelta para iros, Curo se acerca a ti y a [Companion Name] con una sonrisa impropia de él, sosteniendo una hoja de papel y flanqueado por dos personas que parecen exploradores. Despacha con un gesto a unas cuantas personas que reclaman su atención."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I wasn't expecting the two of you to get to work so quickly."
msgstr "No esperaba que os pusierais manos a la obra tan rápido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Honestly, I only wanted to put you to work since I thought you were full of "
"it, talking about rising up against that fortress."
msgstr ""
"Sinceramente, solo quería poneros a trabajar porque pensaba que era todo "
"palabrería, eso de alzarse contra esa fortaleza."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Believe us now?"
msgstr "¿Ahora nos crees?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Believe you? Based on the reports I've gotten, I feel like I best start "
"commissioning portraits of you to hang in the mayor's home."
msgstr ""
"¿Creeros? Por los informes que me han llegado, creo que debería ir "
"encargando retratos vuestros para colgarlos en la casa del alcalde."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't know how a couple of villages out in the boonies managed to mount "
"such a force, but I say, I'm impressed."
msgstr ""
"No sé cómo un par de aldeas perdidas en el quinto pino lograron reunir "
"semejante fuerza, pero he de decir que estoy impresionado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That fortress being taken care of makes all of us safer."
msgstr "Que se hayan ocupado de esa fortaleza nos hace a todos más seguros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And I'd say... one good deed deserves another, hm?"
msgstr "Y yo diría que... una buena acción merece otra, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That it does. I already have my people working on providing a report, worry "
"not. They'll bring it to you in a few hours."
msgstr ""
"Así es. Mi gente ya está preparando un informe, no os preocupéis. Os lo "
"traerán en unas horas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Make yourselves at home, I'll have the guards know not to give you any "
"trouble. And uh..."
msgstr ""
"Estáis en vuestra casa, avisaré a los guardias para que no os den problemas."
" Y, eh..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not used to doing this... I'm sorry for how we first met."
msgstr "No estoy acostumbrado a esto... Siento cómo empezamos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Curo purses his lips at that, seemingly a bit lost on what to say after that. He opts for a slight nod and then excuses himself, his chaperones following quickly after.\n"
"\n"
"The woman you dropped off your goods with politely, but shyly, asks if the two of you could lend just a bit more help since it sounds like you'll be stuck here anyway. You look to [Companion Name], who just shrugs. Might as well. She quickly leads you off to a nearby cooking tent, where a line of hungry refugees waits eagerly. It seems that the current staff are struggling to keep up."
msgstr ""
"Curo frunce los labios al oírlo, algo perdido sin saber qué decir. Opta por un leve asentimiento y luego se disculpa, y sus acompañantes lo siguen rápidamente.\n"
"\n"
"La mujer a la que entregasteis vuestras mercancías os pregunta con educación, aunque con timidez, si podríais echar una mano un poco más, ya que parece que de todos modos vais a quedaros aquí. Miras a [Companion Name], que se encoge de hombros. Qué más da. Ella os lleva enseguida a una tienda de cocina cercana, donde espera ansiosa una fila de refugiados hambrientos. Parece que el personal actual no da abasto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You and [Companion Name] find yourselves breathless and exhausted after providing as many warm meals as you could. The crowd has been quelled substantially, with only a few stragglers coming up every half an hour or so. The head chef dismisses you, and thanks you dearly for your help, while making sure that you don't leave without a warm meal yourselves.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you start to dig in, right as one of Curo's earlier companions wordlessly jogs up to you and holds out a sealed scroll. Once you take it from his hands, he gives a small salute and turns back the way he came.\n"
"\n"
"You read over the scroll in the dim evening light to see a collection of detailed notes from months of observations. You read of the guard's clashes with armed groups, freed captives, and even a few raids on encampments of the unnamed group. Finally, you find what you're looking for.\n"
"\n"
"You read an entry regarding a skirmish that took Hirane's scouts far to the east, to the edge of a town called Clearwater. The scouts continued to assail a caravan of these armed bandits until a massive sandstorm blew into the region and forced their retreat.\n"
"\n"
"It wasn't much to go off of, but it's a start. The two of you finish your meals quickly and ready yourselves to head east."
msgstr ""
"Tú y [Companion Name] acabáis sin aliento y agotados tras servir todas las comidas calientes que habéis podido. La multitud se ha calmado bastante, y solo llega algún rezagado cada media hora más o menos. El jefe de cocina os despide y os da las gracias de corazón por vuestra ayuda, asegurándose de que no os vayáis sin una comida caliente.\n"
"\n"
"Os disponéis a comer justo cuando uno de los acompañantes de Curo de antes se os acerca trotando sin decir palabra y os tiende un pergamino sellado. En cuanto lo coges de sus manos, hace un pequeño saludo y se vuelve por donde ha venido.\n"
"\n"
"Lees el pergamino a la tenue luz del atardecer y encuentras una recopilación de notas detalladas fruto de meses de observación. Lees sobre los choques de la guardia con grupos armados, cautivos liberados e incluso algunas incursiones en campamentos del grupo sin nombre. Por fin, encuentras lo que buscas.\n"
"\n"
"Lees una entrada sobre una escaramuza que llevó a los exploradores de Hirane muy al este, hasta las afueras de un pueblo llamado Clearwater. Los exploradores siguieron hostigando una caravana de estos bandidos armados hasta que una enorme tormenta de arena azotó la región y les obligó a retirarse.\n"
"\n"
"No era gran cosa por donde empezar, pero es un comienzo. Os termináis la comida rápidamente y os preparáis para poner rumbo al este."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The Path to Melvor"
msgstr "El camino a Melvor"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"After poring over the reports from Hirane's scouts, you're sure of one "
"thing. The hooded figures that attacked Azamire and seem to be kidnapping "
"and transporting townsfolk have headed far to the east. To what end, you "
"couldn't even begin to wager a guess."
msgstr ""
"Tras estudiar a fondo los informes de los exploradores de Hirane, tienes "
"clara una cosa. Las figuras encapuchadas que atacaron Azamire y que parecen "
"secuestrar y trasladar a los habitantes se han dirigido muy al este. Con qué"
" fin, ni siquiera te atreverías a adivinarlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "With enough of these, we should be able to make it to Clearwater!"
msgstr "¡Con suficientes de estas, deberíamos poder llegar a Clearwater!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wow... they're... really sweet."
msgstr "Vaya... son... muy dulces."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You exit Hirane's gate and find yourself deep within the countryside. You travel east along the Heartroad, knowing that if you go far enough, it should be next to impossible to miss Clearwater. From what you were able to gather from folks in Hirane, Clearwater acts as the major waystation between the east and west sides of the Desert Plains. You heard of many small resting points and hamlets between here and there, but few were notable enough to commit to memory.\n"
"\n"
"The Heartroad is generally well constructed and maintained - even this far from the capital - but as grass turned to arid soil, and then eventually sand, the Heartroad becomes harder to keep track of. Despite what the locals in Hirane said about there being places to rest between there and Clearwater, most of the buildings you pass are abandoned, swallowed by the sands.\n"
"\n"
"The sun beats down on you overhead in a way you're unfamiliar with except for on Azamire's hottest summer days. There's no reprieve from the heat, just sand stretching out in what seems endless waves of gold."
msgstr ""
"Sales por la puerta de Hirane y te adentras en plena campiña. Viajas hacia el este por el Camino del Corazón, sabiendo que si llegas lo bastante lejos, será casi imposible no dar con Clearwater. Por lo que pudiste averiguar de la gente de Hirane, Clearwater es la principal parada entre los lados este y oeste de las Llanuras desérticas. Oíste hablar de muchos pequeños lugares de descanso y aldeas entre un sitio y otro, pero pocos eran tan destacables como para recordarlos.\n"
"\n"
"El Camino del Corazón suele estar bien construido y cuidado, incluso tan lejos de la capital, pero a medida que la hierba da paso a la tierra árida y, al final, a la arena, cuesta más seguir su rastro. Pese a lo que decían los lugareños de Hirane sobre los lugares de descanso entre allí y Clearwater, la mayoría de los edificios por los que pasas están abandonados, engullidos por la arena.\n"
"\n"
"El sol cae a plomo sobre ti de una forma que solo conocías de los días más calurosos del verano en Azamire. No hay tregua del calor, solo arena que se extiende en lo que parecen olas doradas infinitas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is... a little warmer than I expected."
msgstr "Esto es... un poco más caluroso de lo que esperaba."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Do we have any water left?"
msgstr "¿Nos queda agua?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "About one more flask between us. Want it now?"
msgstr "Más o menos una cantimplora más entre los dos. ¿La quieres ya?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Already? Wow..."
msgstr "¿Ya? Vaya..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I didn't think so few of the waystations would be abandoned. We'd have had "
"to carry more than both our weights in water to make it to Clearwater "
"without stopping..."
msgstr ""
"No pensaba que tantas paradas de paso estarían abandonadas. Habríamos tenido"
" que cargar con más agua de la que pesamos entre los dos para llegar a "
"Clearwater sin parar..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm not saying it's time to panic, but-"
msgstr "No digo que sea hora de entrar en pánico, pero..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I refuse to lose to the sun, just days after we took down the Ringleader."
msgstr ""
"Me niego a perder contra el sol, a los pocos días de haber derrotado al "
"Cabecilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Got an oasis in your back pocket that I don't know about?"
msgstr "¿Tienes un oasis en el bolsillo del que no sepa nada?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You grab [Companion Name] and pull her to the side, off the Heartroad and "
"crest over one of the dunes. Your eyes don't deceive you - or your mind "
"can't conjure up particularly appealing mirages - the small green crowns you"
" saw from the road belong to large cacti. You stick one with your knife and "
"a miserably thin trickle of slightly sappy water pours out. It isn't white, "
"and after a small taste, it doesn't seem acidic or leave your tongue "
"tingling. It doesn't seem poisonous, and that's good enough. Beats frying to"
" death, anyway."
msgstr ""
"Agarras a [Companion Name] y tiras de su brazo hacia un lado, fuera del "
"Camino del Corazón, hasta la cresta de una de las dunas. Tus ojos no te "
"engañan (o tu mente no es capaz de conjurar espejismos especialmente "
"apetecibles): las pequeñas coronas verdes que viste desde el camino "
"pertenecen a grandes cactus. Pinchas uno con el cuchillo y sale un hilillo "
"miserable de agua algo resinosa. No es blanca y, tras probarla un poco, no "
"parece ácida ni te deja un cosquilleo en la lengua. No parece venenosa, y "
"con eso basta. Mejor que morir frito, en cualquier caso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#. Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That hurt, but I guess it's fair."
msgstr "Eso ha dolido, pero supongo que es justo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You wipe the cactus water from your mouth. The two of you tapped into many "
"of the ones nearby and start to stray from the original patch. You find "
"yourselves giggling and swaying to and fro, despite definitely being more "
"hydrated. You're worried that something may be wrong, but how could it be? "
"You feel so good. [Companion Name] nearly collapses against you in a fit of "
"giggles, the sand undulating in mesmerizing patterns underneath you."
msgstr ""
"Te limpias el agua de cactus de la boca. Los dos habéis sangrado muchos de "
"los cactus cercanos y empezáis a alejaros del grupo original. Os encontráis "
"riendo como tontos y balanceándoos de un lado a otro, aunque sin duda estáis"
" más hidratados. Te preocupa que algo vaya mal, pero ¿cómo iba a ser? Te "
"sientes de maravilla. [Companion Name] casi se desploma sobre ti en un "
"ataque de risa, mientras la arena ondula bajo vuestros pies en patrones "
"hipnóticos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You are the best, you know that, [Player Name]?"
msgstr "Eres lo mejor, ¿lo sabías, [Player Name]?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Nooooooo, no. You are!"
msgstr "Nooooooo, no. ¡Lo eres tú!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No, stop it, stop it. I mean it. I never would have been able to come out "
"all this way if it weren't for you."
msgstr ""
"No, para, para. Lo digo en serio. Nunca habría llegado hasta aquí si no "
"fuera por ti."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And nowwwww I feel so so so good."
msgstr "Y ahoraaaaa me siento tan tan tan bien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Do you think *hic*, that maybe, the cactus water is..."
msgstr "¿Tú crees *hip*, que a lo mejor, el agua de cactus es...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Pffffft. Nooooo. This is how I NORMALLY am. Look at how normal I'm being "
"right now."
msgstr ""
"Pffffft. Noooo. Yo soy así NORMALMENTE. Mira lo normal que me estoy "
"comportando ahora mismo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The cacti that stand in front of you now seem... bigger. And they move. But everything is moving, so that's not particularly strange. What is strange is that one of the cacti swing one of its spiny arms at your head when you try to cut into it with your axe. The needles in the side of your face snap you out of the cactus water's hallucinogenic effects.\n"
"\n"
"Everything around you stops moving, except for the... angry cactus in front of you. And all of the ones behind it. They shift through the sands and reach out with their arms. They're real. You call out to [Companion Name] who seems to be having a similar revelation."
msgstr ""
"Los cactus que tienes delante ahora parecen... más grandes. Y se mueven. Pero todo se mueve, así que no es especialmente raro. Lo que sí es raro es que uno de los cactus te lance un golpe a la cabeza con uno de sus brazos espinosos cuando intentas cortarlo con el hacha. Las púas que se te clavan en la cara te sacan de los efectos alucinógenos del agua de cactus.\n"
"\n"
"Todo a tu alrededor deja de moverse, salvo el... cactus enfadado que tienes delante. Y todos los que hay detrás de él. Se desplazan por la arena y extienden los brazos. Son reales. Llamas a [Companion Name], que parece estar teniendo una revelación parecida."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Individually, these aren't too bad."
msgstr "Por separado, no son tan terribles."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That was worth free passage for life? Huh."
msgstr "¿Eso valía paso libre de por vida? Vaya."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The cacti's spines are rough to contend with, and require a far more protective approach to fighting than you're used to employing, but all is well. The patch of cacti lays slain at your feet, and the... effects of the cactus water seem to have subsided.\n"
"\n"
"You press on to Clearwater, only taking occasional, small sips of the cactus water you collected when you absolutely need to. You're definitely more giggly than usual and sway lightly on your feet, but the worst of the effects never take hold with your moderate approach.\n"
"\n"
"The town of Clearwater is a sight for sore, sun-baked eyes. Your feet ache, your skin is sunburnt, and you're absolutely parched. A small crowd of townsfolk gather about, laughing at your misfortune and warning of some of the dangers you may see deeper within in the desert.\n"
"\n"
"When you ask about the figures, much of the levity is replaced by fear. A good chunk of the population here seems to have come from the abandoned exterior towns fleeing the... Soulsmiths. It feels weird to finally have a name to the group that destroyed your home. Here, dealing with them has been a constant, and the name holds no gravitas. The townspeople say they've seen the caravans head east, towards the capital, and warn you to stay far away from the eastern Heartroad for now. When you and [Companion Name] tell tales of Azamire and the Ringleader, and your goal of seeing the Soulsmiths brought to justice, it seems like half the town opens their homes to you, keeping you fed and hydrated as you two recover.\n"
"\n"
"After some well-deserved rest, the two of you continue east finally out of the dunes and back into grassy fields. You pass into rockier terrain as you approach the Flintcrest Highlands. Large jagged boulders dot the rocky soil, jutting out at odd angles."
msgstr ""
"Las espinas de los cactus son difíciles de afrontar y exigen una forma de luchar mucho más protegida de la que sueles emplear, pero todo sale bien. El grupo de cactus yace abatido a tus pies, y los... efectos del agua de cactus parecen haberse pasado.\n"
"\n"
"Sigues hacia Clearwater, dando solo pequeños sorbos ocasionales al agua de cactus que recogiste cuando de verdad lo necesitas. Sin duda estás más risueño de lo normal y te tambaleas un poco, pero lo peor de los efectos nunca llega gracias a tu moderación.\n"
"\n"
"La ciudad de Clearwater es un alivio para unos ojos cansados y abrasados por el sol. Te duelen los pies, tienes la piel quemada y estás muerto de sed. Se reúne a tu alrededor un pequeño grupo de habitantes, que se ríen de tu desgracia y te advierten de algunos de los peligros que podrías encontrar más adentro del desierto.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando preguntas por las figuras, gran parte de la ligereza da paso al miedo. Buena parte de la población parece venir de los pueblos exteriores abandonados, huyendo de los... Forjaalmas. Resulta extraño tener por fin un nombre para el grupo que destruyó tu hogar. Aquí, lidiar con ellos ha sido una constante, y el nombre no impone ninguna solemnidad. Los habitantes dicen haber visto las caravanas dirigirse al este, hacia la capital, y os advierten de que os mantengáis bien lejos del Camino del Corazón oriental por ahora. Cuando [Companion Name] y tú contáis historias de Azamire y del Cabecilla, y de vuestro objetivo de llevar a los Forjaalmas ante la justicia, parece que media ciudad os abre sus casas y os mantiene alimentados e hidratados mientras os recuperáis.\n"
"\n"
"Tras un merecido descanso, los dos seguís hacia el este y por fin salís de las dunas para volver a los campos de hierba. Pasáis a un terreno más rocoso al acercaros a las Tierras altas de Flintcrest. Grandes rocas irregulares salpican el suelo pedregoso y sobresalen en ángulos extraños."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How do you think they... got like that?"
msgstr "¿Cómo crees que... acabaron así?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What, the boulders?"
msgstr "¿El qué, las rocas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Yeah. Kinda... random, how they're all over the place, no?"
msgstr "Sí. Es un poco... aleatorio que estén por todas partes, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...Maybe. But what, it's not like someone would haul them out here, right?"
msgstr ""
"...Puede. Pero tampoco es que alguien las haya arrastrado hasta aquí, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "To what end?"
msgstr "¿Con qué fin?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With that, [Companion Name] continues to peer over the boulders as the two of you travel along the Heartroad, as if they'd spring to life and tell her where they came from. You've had enough of sentient things that should otherwise not be, so you try to avoid staring too much.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, you arrive at a little inn that seems to have been built into a stone wall and garrison that takes up the expansive entrance of the Broken Pass. The Sleeping Stone is legendary, and for good reason. Not only is it the home of the Slayers Guild for the eastern region of the continent, it attracts world renowned adventurers who wish to venture into the Perilous Peaks to prove themselves to be the best of the best.\n"
"\n"
"The Broken Pass is the quickest way to the capital, but it's typically travelled by highly armed caravans that can both pay the toll to pass the gate, and can fend off any beasts that travelled down from the mountain proper. When you hear of caravans being rerouted south - around the mountain range - due to a particularly feisty pack of Stonehoppers, you're quick to offer you and [Companion Name]'s services. \n"
"\n"
"The owner of the Sleeping Stone does you one better, saying that if you take care of them, you'll get free passage through the Broken Pass for life. The deal's too good to pass up."
msgstr ""
"Dicho esto, [Companion Name] sigue escudriñando las rocas mientras los dos recorréis el Camino del Corazón, como si fueran a cobrar vida y contarle de dónde vienen. Ya has tenido bastante de cosas con conciencia que no deberían tenerla, así que intentas no mirarlas demasiado.\n"
"\n"
"Por fin llegáis a una pequeña posada que parece construida dentro de una muralla de piedra y una guarnición que ocupan la amplia entrada del Paso roto. La Piedra Durmiente es legendaria, y con razón. No solo es la sede del Gremio de Exterminadores en la región oriental del continente, sino que atrae a aventureros de fama mundial que desean aventurarse en los Picos Peligrosos para demostrar que son los mejores de los mejores.\n"
"\n"
"El Paso roto es el camino más rápido a la capital, pero suelen recorrerlo caravanas muy armadas que pueden pagar el peaje para cruzar la puerta y defenderse de cualquier bestia que baje de la montaña. Cuando oyes que están desviando las caravanas hacia el sur, rodeando la cordillera, por culpa de una manada especialmente agresiva de saltapiedras, no tardas en ofrecer tus servicios y los de [Companion Name]. \n"
"\n"
"El dueño de la Piedra Durmiente os ofrece algo aún mejor: si os encargáis de ellos, tendréis paso libre por el Paso roto de por vida. El trato es demasiado bueno para rechazarlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hopefully this will persuade them to come out and say hello."
msgstr "Ojalá esto los convenza para salir a saludar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ugh. My eyes are watering."
msgstr "Puaj. Me lloran los ojos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You tally up the bodies of the tall, awkward beasts. Stonehoppers were a bit of an odd blend of creatures. They were scaly like a lizard and use a long whip-like tail for stability. They have two large wings that aid them in jumping from rock to rock - hence their name - but they were technically flightless. The 'birds' walk on two powerful legs that they use to kick at their prey, which fortunately made it easy to get them tangled up in traps.\n"
"\n"
"What surprised you about them was their number. It felt like every time you caught one, you'd see two more jumping overhead."
msgstr ""
"Haces el recuento de los cuerpos de esas bestias altas y torpes. Los saltapiedras eran una mezcla de criaturas bastante extraña. Tenían escamas como un lagarto y usan una larga cola parecida a un látigo para mantener el equilibrio. Tienen dos grandes alas que los ayudan a saltar de roca en roca (de ahí su nombre), pero técnicamente no podían volar. Estas «aves» caminan sobre dos patas poderosas que usan para dar patadas a sus presas, lo que por suerte facilitaba que se enredaran en las trampas.\n"
"\n"
"Lo que te sorprendió de ellos fue su número. Parecía que cada vez que atrapabas uno, veías otros dos saltando por encima de tu cabeza."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They're getting a bit more wily the further into the pass we go."
msgstr "Se vuelven un poco más astutos cuanto más nos adentramos en el paso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Bigger, too."
msgstr "Y más grandes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And there's so many of them. What do you think they even eat?"
msgstr "Y hay muchísimos. ¿Qué crees que comen?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hopefully not us. "
msgstr "Ojalá que no a nosotros. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Speaking of eating... how do you think they taste?"
msgstr "Hablando de comer... ¿a qué crees que saben?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Like chicken, hopefully. They're about thirty times the size, though. "
"Hopefully not too stringy, with all their muscles."
msgstr ""
"A pollo, con suerte. Aunque son unas treinta veces más grandes. Ojalá no "
"sean demasiado fibrosos, con tanto músculo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But do you think you could eat something that maybe would eat people, if "
"they had the chance?"
msgstr ""
"Pero ¿crees que podrías comerte algo que, si tuviera la ocasión, quizá se "
"comería a la gente?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh without a doubt. I wouldn't do it if it ate someone recently, of course."
msgstr ""
"Ah, sin ninguna duda. Aunque no lo haría si se hubiera comido a alguien hace"
" poco, claro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But what, are you telling me you'd turn down the chance to try dragon?"
msgstr ""
"Pero ¿qué, me estás diciendo que rechazarías la oportunidad de probar "
"dragón?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Depends on the type, you know."
msgstr "Depende del tipo, ya sabes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Some of them breathe poison, can't imagine that meat would do your body any "
"favors."
msgstr ""
"Algunos escupen veneno, no me imagino que esa carne le haga ningún favor a "
"tu cuerpo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Fire-breathing dragons may be a bit burnt tasting..."
msgstr "Los dragones que escupen fuego quizá sepan un poco a quemado..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"OR their meat is naturally smoked with a perfect sear on the inside... "
"imagine slicing one open and being able to dig in..."
msgstr ""
"O su carne está ahumada de forma natural, con un sellado perfecto por "
"dentro... imagínate abrir uno y poder hincarle el diente..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Just know, there's probably something out there talking about doing the same"
" to you and me."
msgstr ""
"Que sepas que seguramente hay algo por ahí hablando de hacernos lo mismo a "
"ti y a mí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Fair's fair, if you ask me. Eat or be eaten, n' all that. Literally."
msgstr ""
"Lo justo es justo, si me preguntas. Comer o ser comido y todo eso. "
"Literalmente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The two of you go back and forth on what creatures may or may not taste good, chatting idly back and forth as you collect the last of your traps.\n"
"\n"
"As you finish prepping the last of the Stonehoppers you caught, you see one that's easily twice the others' size bounding along the cliffside. It jumps downward and pushes into a cave carved into the rock without paying you any mind. [Companion Name] looks to you eagerly.\n"
"\n"
"You both clamber up the rocky wall of the Broken Pass and nearly catch a taloned foot to the face as another of the beasts head back inside to rest, seemingly not very bothered by your presence. Crawling into a beast den would be ill-advised, especially one that can kick so hard it could shatter your bones and send you bouncing around the cavern's walls. Best to smoke them out."
msgstr ""
"Os pasáis el rato debatiendo qué criaturas podrían saber bien o no, charlando tranquilamente mientras recogéis las últimas trampas.\n"
"\n"
"Mientras terminas de preparar los últimos saltapiedras que habéis atrapado, ves uno que fácilmente dobla en tamaño a los demás avanzando a saltos por la pared del acantilado. Salta hacia abajo y se mete en una cueva excavada en la roca sin prestarte la menor atención. [Companion Name] te mira con entusiasmo.\n"
"\n"
"Os encaramáis por la pared rocosa del Paso roto y casi os lleváis un zarpazo en la cara cuando otra de las bestias vuelve dentro a descansar, sin que vuestra presencia parezca molestarle demasiado. Meterse a gatas en una guarida de bestias sería imprudente, sobre todo de unas que dan patadas tan fuertes que podrían destrozarte los huesos y mandarte rebotando contra las paredes de la caverna. Mejor sacarlos con humo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You'd really better taste good."
msgstr "Más os vale estar buenos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How many did I get?"
msgstr "¿Cuántos he cazado?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The Stonehoppers living within the cave are... much larger than the little "
"ones you managed to catch with your traps. The one that passed by as you "
"were climbing must have done so because it didn't even register you as a "
"threat. Now that their den is filled with smoke and the two of you stand "
"with weapons at the ready, they seem to have changed their minds about "
"whether or not they want to take you seriously."
msgstr ""
"Los saltapiedras que viven en la cueva son... mucho más grandes que los "
"pequeños que lograsteis atrapar con las trampas. El que pasó mientras "
"trepabais debió de hacerlo porque ni siquiera os consideró una amenaza. "
"Ahora que su guarida está llena de humo y los dos estáis con las armas en "
"ristre, parecen haber cambiado de opinión sobre si tomaros en serio o no."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Any chance I can go back to catching the comparatively smaller ones, and you"
" can handle these... monsters?"
msgstr ""
"¿Hay alguna posibilidad de que yo vuelva a cazar a los relativamente "
"pequeños y tú te encargues de estos... monstruos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As long as you pay me, every time we come back through the Broken Pass."
msgstr "Siempre que me pagues cada vez que volvamos a pasar por el Paso roto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Can hardly say that you earned free passage for life if I get to have all "
"the fun to myself."
msgstr ""
"Difícilmente podrás decir que te has ganado el paso libre de por vida si me "
"quedo yo con toda la diversión."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Fine then. Let's make it a bet, then. Whichever of us takes down the least "
"cooks dinner out of them, then."
msgstr ""
"Pues vale. Hagamos una apuesta, entonces. El que abata menos prepara la cena"
" con ellos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hope you brought your apron!"
msgstr "¡Espero que hayas traído el delantal!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You're both a touch nervous, despite the friendly wager. It's hard to feel particularly confident when you only come up to the Stonehoppers' thighs, but fortunately, the beasts are mostly leg. As you dodge out of the way of one of their kicks, you flinch when you see the cracks left in the stone where their foot connected.\n"
"\n"
"You're beginning to understand why free passage for life was put on the table. Surely someone would have taken it sooner or later with the inn's usual clientele, but it's no cakewalk, that's for sure."
msgstr ""
"Pese a la apuesta amistosa, los dos estáis algo nerviosos. Cuesta sentirse muy seguro cuando apenas llegas a la altura de los muslos de un saltapiedras, pero, por suerte, estas bestias son casi todo pata. Al esquivar una de sus patadas, te estremeces al ver las grietas que deja en la piedra donde impacta su pie.\n"
"\n"
"Empiezas a entender por qué se ofreció el paso libre de por vida. Seguro que alguien de la clientela habitual de la posada se lo habría ganado tarde o temprano, pero no es ningún paseo, eso desde luego."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I mean... They won't mind if we borrow them, right?"
msgstr "A ver... No les importará que se los tomemos prestados, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Suits them right."
msgstr "Se lo tienen merecido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You and [Companion Name] tally up your kills and... somehow, it's a dead tie. You do a once-over of the den just to make sure you got them all and neither of you could squeak out a last minute victory, but you really did get them all.\n"
"\n"
"You both throw up your hands and congratulate one another on a job well done and camp out in the Broken Pass, cooking a meal together. Usually you just dig into your travel rations, but this is about as good of a chance as you'll get on the road. With some local herbs and a generous bit of seasoning... yeah, it does taste like chicken. Quite a bit more gamey, and virtually zero fat, but a great meal nonetheless.\n"
"\n"
"You settle into your sleeping roll and watch the embers of the fire float up into the sky."
msgstr ""
"Tú y [Companion Name] contáis vuestras presas y... de algún modo, es un empate exacto. Dais un repaso a la guarida, solo para aseguraros de que los habéis abatido a todos y de que ninguno de los dos pueda arañar una victoria de última hora, pero de verdad que los habéis abatido a todos.\n"
"\n"
"Levantáis las manos, os felicitáis mutuamente por el buen trabajo y acampáis en el Paso roto, cocinando una comida juntos. Normalmente os limitáis a tirar de las raciones de viaje, pero esta es la mejor ocasión que vais a tener en el camino. Con unas hierbas de la zona y un buen puñado de condimentos... sí, sabe a pollo. Bastante más a caza y casi sin grasa, pero una comida estupenda de todos modos.\n"
"\n"
"Te acomodas en tu petate y ves cómo las brasas de la hoguera se elevan hacia el cielo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Long way from Azamire."
msgstr "Qué lejos queda Azamire."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't miss it. Much."
msgstr "No lo echo de menos. Mucho."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Always felt just a little too small, didn't it?"
msgstr "Siempre se nos quedó un poco pequeño, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, a bit. I'll be happy when we do go back, but I'm not in any rush."
msgstr ""
"Sí, un poco. Me alegraré cuando volvamos, pero no tengo ninguna prisa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We'll finally be in the capital, soon. I've dreamed about it ever since I "
"was a kid."
msgstr ""
"Pronto estaremos por fin en la capital. He soñado con ella desde la "
"infancia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Me too. But next time, let's charter a boat, hm?"
msgstr "Yo también. Pero la próxima vez, fletemos un barco, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh, without a doubt."
msgstr "Oh, sin ninguna duda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"After a bit of shuteye, the rest of the trip is... uneventful in a positive way. You pass by the eastern gate to the Broken Pass and tell them how you've dealt with the Stonehoppers and show them proof, to which the guards are both impressed and thankful, and promise to let those at the Sleeping Stone know.\n"
"\n"
"You pass by a few villages along the rest of the Heartroad, many of them clearly prospering due to their proximity to the capital. As you pass over the Bridge of Kings, you see the grand gates of Melvor before you, with a long trail of people waiting to be let inside.\n"
"\n"
"Through talking with the crowd and a few guards who do their best to keep the peace, it sounds like the city has been under a light lockdown to new travellers because of an influx of smuggled goods. Only those bearing visitor passes or proof of citizenship are allowed entry. These visitor passes are sold for... rather exorbitant amounts.\n"
"\n"
"A group of pompous aristocrats wave their passes and bottles of wine about flamboyantly and shuffle along the pathway. They let out strings of taunts and insults as they walk past the line of those looking to be let into the capital. You and [Companion Name] look to one another with wry smiles."
msgstr ""
"Tras echar una cabezadita, el resto del viaje transcurre... sin incidentes, para bien. Pasáis por la puerta oriental del Paso roto, les contáis cómo os habéis ocupado de los saltapiedras y les enseñáis pruebas; los guardias quedan impresionados y agradecidos, y prometen avisar a los de la Piedra Durmiente.\n"
"\n"
"Pasáis por unas cuantas aldeas a lo largo del resto del Camino del Corazón, muchas de ellas claramente prósperas gracias a su cercanía a la capital. Al cruzar el Puente de los Reyes, veis ante vosotros las grandiosas puertas de Melvor, con una larga fila de gente esperando a que la dejen entrar.\n"
"\n"
"Hablando con la multitud y con algunos guardias que hacen lo posible por mantener el orden, parece que la ciudad lleva un tiempo con un cierre parcial para los recién llegados debido a la entrada de mercancías de contrabando. Solo pueden entrar quienes llevan un pase de visitante o prueba de ciudadanía. Estos pases de visitante se venden por sumas... bastante desorbitadas.\n"
"\n"
"Un grupo de aristócratas pomposos agita sus pases y botellas de vino con mucha ostentación y avanzan por el camino. Sueltan una retahíla de burlas e insultos mientras pasan junto a la fila de quienes esperan entrar en la capital. Tú y [Companion Name] os miráis con una sonrisa irónica."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You follow the group along for a while until one of the richly dressed men smacks a wide-eyed child on the nose with their pass, then hurries along. The child's mother shouts after them, and the angry line of onlookers finally snaps at the mistreatment. Some of the drunken nobles cower in fear, afraid of the consequences of their own actions, while others egg the crowd on further, clearly enjoying the attention. The guards try to keep the peace, though they are clearly fed up with the 'social elite' as well, judging by their glares.\n"
"\n"
"Taking advantage of the situation, you bump into one of the nobles in the crowd and slip your hand into their coat, withdrawing a sleek sky blue visitor's pass. You keep walking as its original owner shouts after you for daring to touch them, but they're drowned out by the angry mob soon enough. [Companion Name] slides in right beside you, holding one of her own. The two of you open them up, realizing that there's no identifying information that is required, the pass alone is proof enough that you may enter.\n"
"\n"
"Just like that, the gates of the capital won't stop you. You don't even feel a little bad."
msgstr ""
"Seguís al grupo un rato hasta que uno de los hombres ricamente vestidos le da en la nariz con su pase a un niño que lo mira con los ojos como platos, y luego sigue a toda prisa. La madre del niño le grita, y la fila de espectadores, ya furiosa, por fin estalla ante semejante maltrato. Algunos de los nobles borrachos se encogen de miedo, temiendo las consecuencias de sus propios actos, mientras que otros incitan aún más a la multitud, disfrutando claramente de la atención. Los guardias intentan mantener el orden, aunque, a juzgar por sus miradas, también están hartos de la «élite social».\n"
"\n"
"Aprovechando la situación, chocas con uno de los nobles y le metes la mano en el abrigo, sacando un elegante pase de visitante azul celeste. Sigues andando mientras su dueño original te grita por atreverte a tocarle, pero la turba enfurecida no tarda en ahogar sus gritos. [Companion Name] se coloca a tu lado, con otro pase en la mano. Los abrís y os dais cuenta de que no hace falta ningún dato identificativo: el pase por sí solo basta como prueba de que podéis entrar.\n"
"\n"
"Así, sin más, las puertas de la capital ya no os detendrán. Ni siquiera te sientes un poco mal."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 40[/color] Enemy "
"multiple times"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar varias veces a un enemigo de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de "
"combate 40[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 42[/color] Enemy "
"multiple times"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar varias veces a un enemigo de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de "
"combate 42[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 40[/color] "
"[b][u]Miniboss[/u][/b]"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar a un [b][u]minijefe[/u][/b] de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de "
"combate 40[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Rewards.CustomRewards
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Unlocks the Silted Oasis Combat Area."
msgstr "Desbloquea la zona de combate Oasis enlodado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The Big City"
msgstr "La gran ciudad"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"By following crumbs of information regarding the group you now know as the "
"Soulsmiths, you've found yourself thrust into the middle of the capital of "
"Melvor with hardly a clue on what to do or where to go next."
msgstr ""
"Siguiendo las migajas de información sobre el grupo que ahora conoces como "
"los forjaalmas, has acabado en plena capital de Melvor sin apenas idea de "
"qué hacer ni adónde ir a continuación."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Here they come!"
msgstr "¡Ahí vienen!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's grab some feathers and go."
msgstr "Cojamos unas plumas y vámonos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You'd heard tales of the capital many times by those who'd travelled the continent and happened to stop by Azamire for trade or rest, but their stories hardly even begin to scratch just how... much was laid out before the two of you. Thousands of people, many speaking languages that you couldn't even begin to place. Buildings that stretch so high into the sky that you have to crane your neck to fully see. Market stalls filled with an endless number of trinkets and clothes, while some on the other side of the random plaza you'd entered emit smells so strange and tantalizing you involuntarily start to drool.\n"
"\n"
"You try your best to take in everything, excitedly chatting with [Companion Name] as you both try to point out the endless rush of... everything, until you find yourself pushing out of the crowds for the first time. You're thankful for the space, until you feel a strong hand clamp down on your shoulder and yank you backwards. Your hand goes to the weapon at your side until you realize you... walked onto a firing range! An arrow whizzes past your nose as you turn to the person who grabbed you. A tall, tanned man dressed in a gaudy purple cloak and a longbow strapped to his back pulls you out of danger, to [Companion Name] who breathlessly catches up to you."
msgstr ""
"Habías oído muchas historias sobre la capital de boca de quienes habían recorrido el continente y pasaban por Azamire para comerciar o descansar, pero sus relatos apenas empiezan a reflejar todo lo que... se extiende ante vosotros. Miles de personas, muchas hablando idiomas que ni siquiera sabrías situar. Edificios que se elevan tanto hacia el cielo que tienes que estirar el cuello para verlos enteros. Puestos de mercado llenos de un sinfín de baratijas y ropa, mientras que otros, al otro lado de la plaza cualquiera en la que habéis entrado, desprenden olores tan extraños y tentadores que se te hace la boca agua sin querer.\n"
"\n"
"Intentas asimilarlo todo, charlando con entusiasmo con [Companion Name] mientras ambos intentáis señalar el torrente interminable de... todo, hasta que por primera vez sales de entre la multitud. Agradeces el espacio, hasta que notas una mano fuerte que te agarra del hombro y tira de ti hacia atrás. Llevas la mano al arma que llevas al costado hasta que te das cuenta de que... ¡te has metido en un campo de tiro! Una flecha te pasa silbando junto a la nariz mientras te giras hacia la persona que te ha agarrado. Un hombre alto y moreno, vestido con una llamativa capa morada y con un arco largo a la espalda, te aparta del peligro y te lleva junto a [Companion Name], que llega sin aliento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "New to the capital, I presume?"
msgstr "Recién llegados a la capital, supongo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"There's a few dozen things I'd recommend to newcomers for their first day, "
"but getting skewered in the middle of the archery contest is not one of "
"them. But meeting me is at the top of the list. Talm. The pleasure is yours."
msgstr ""
"Hay unas cuantas docenas de cosas que recomendaría a los recién llegados "
"para su primer día, pero acabar ensartado en mitad del concurso de tiro con "
"arco no es una de ellas. Eso sí, conocerme a mí encabeza la lista. Talm. El "
"placer es vuestro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... I..."
msgstr "Yo... yo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There you are! I took my eyes off you for two minutes!"
msgstr "¡Estás aquí! ¡Te he perdido de vista dos minutos!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Sorry, I was a bit distracted by... all of this."
msgstr "Perdón, me he distraído un poco con... todo esto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Can't blame you. Melvor is a real beaute, ain't it?"
msgstr "No te culpo. Melvor es una preciosidad, ¿a que sí?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It is, you have a wonderful city... Thank you for making sure I wasn't "
"impaled."
msgstr ""
"Lo es, tenéis una ciudad maravillosa... Gracias por asegurarte de que no me "
"empalaran."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Of course! Can't have one of my golden geese taken out before you get the "
"chance to help me win!"
msgstr ""
"¡Faltaría más! ¡No puedo dejar que caiga una de mis gallinas de los huevos "
"de oro antes de que tenga la oportunidad de ayudarme a ganar!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...What do you mean?"
msgstr "...¿Qué quieres decir?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My lovely wife has shown me a vision. Me on top of the podium, being crowned"
" the winner of this year's archery contest, with the two of you gleefully "
"cheering me on! Under normal circumstances, about a zero percent chance I'd "
"win..."
msgstr ""
"Mi encantadora esposa me ha mostrado una visión. ¡Yo en lo alto del podio, "
"coronado ganador del concurso de tiro con arco de este año, con vosotros dos"
" animándome entusiasmados! En circunstancias normales, tendría más o menos "
"un cero por ciento de posibilidades de ganar..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But, between you two and I, I plan on cheating as much as I possibly can, "
"and the two of you will help me with that."
msgstr ""
"Pero, entre nosotros, pienso hacer todas las trampas que pueda, y vosotros "
"dos me vais a ayudar con eso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...What makes you think we would do that?"
msgstr "...¿Y qué te hace pensar que haríamos eso?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, first and foremost, Era's visions are never wrong. But secondarily, "
"ask around. Some random noble's family wins this every year, and it's not "
"because they're the most dedicated to their craft, I can tell you that."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, ante todo, las visiones de Era nunca fallan. Pero, además, preguntad "
"por ahí. Cada año gana la familia de algún noble cualquiera, y no es porque "
"sean los más entregados a su oficio, eso os lo aseguro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A combination of bribes and the best bows and arrows that money can buy turn"
" mediocre into world-class talent, apparently. And I'm sick of seein' it."
msgstr ""
"Por lo visto, una combinación de sobornos y los mejores arcos y flechas que "
"se pueden comprar convierten la mediocridad en talento de primera. Y estoy "
"harto de verlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...And let's say we do help you, because we care about the little guy "
"sticking it to the city's nobility oh-so-much, what's in it for us?"
msgstr ""
"...Y digamos que te ayudamos, porque nos importa muchísimo que el pequeño le"
" dé una lección a la nobleza de la ciudad, ¿qué ganamos nosotros?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A reading from my lovely wife, of course. One each. Assuming I win, of "
"course. Trust me, you couldn't afford it, normally."
msgstr ""
"Una lectura de mi encantadora esposa, por supuesto. Una para cada uno. Si "
"gano, claro. Creedme, normalmente no podríais permitírosla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I appreciate you making sure that [Player Name] didn't become an archery "
"target, but-"
msgstr ""
"Te agradezco que te aseguraras de que [Player Name] no se convirtiera en una"
" diana, pero..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...You know, a vision might just even help you with your little Soulsmith "
"problem."
msgstr ""
"...Quién sabe, una visión podría incluso ayudaros con vuestro pequeño "
"problema con los forjaalmas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm winks at the two of you and then holds a finger to his lips, clearly giving no further information than he's already provided. Based on how quickly you and [Companion Name] looked to one another at the mention of Soulsmiths, he knew he had you hooked. Without even asking if you'd be interested, he talks about how arrows fashioned with the feathers of a Sea Griffon always seem to find their mark, and would quite fancy having some of the arrows for himself. Unfortunately, he has no feathers, just the location of one that has been terrorizing a few fishing boats.\n"
"\n"
"You and [Companion Name] leave the capital as quickly as you came, and after a few hours of travel, find the windy cliffside that the nest was said to be. And sure enough, a large pack of the beasts swoop overhead, clearly upset by your arrival."
msgstr ""
"Talm os guiña un ojo y luego se lleva un dedo a los labios, dejando claro que no dará más información de la que ya ha dado. Por lo rápido que tú y [Companion Name] os habéis mirado al oír hablar de los forjaalmas, sabe que os tiene enganchados. Sin preguntar siquiera si os interesa, habla de cómo las flechas hechas con plumas de grifo marino siempre parecen dar en el blanco, y de lo mucho que le gustaría tener algunas. Por desgracia, no tiene plumas, solo la ubicación de uno que ha estado aterrorizando a unos cuantos barcos de pesca.\n"
"\n"
"Tú y [Companion Name] salís de la capital tan rápido como llegasteis y, tras unas horas de viaje, encontráis el acantilado ventoso donde se decía que estaba el nido. Y, efectivamente, una gran bandada de estas bestias sobrevuela vuestras cabezas, claramente molesta por vuestra llegada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "He'd better win."
msgstr "Más le vale ganar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll get that reading one way or another."
msgstr "Conseguiremos esa lectura de un modo u otro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Feathers gathered, the two of you make the trek back to the capital. The "
"city is just as overwhelming as before, but the clear goal of finding Talm "
"again manages to help you push through the enthralling nature of the new "
"sights and smells with ease. Talm is amongst the competitors, warming up. "
"He's doing a remarkable job even without the feathers, nearly splitting his "
"own arrows far down the range, and you begin to wonder why he feels the need"
" to cheat at all."
msgstr ""
"Con las plumas en vuestro poder, emprendéis el camino de vuelta a la "
"capital. La ciudad es tan abrumadora como antes, pero el objetivo claro de "
"volver a encontrar a Talm os ayuda a abriros paso con facilidad entre el "
"embrujo de las nuevas vistas y olores. Talm está entre los participantes, "
"calentando. Lo está haciendo de maravilla incluso sin las plumas, casi "
"partiendo sus propias flechas al fondo del campo de tiro, y empiezas a "
"preguntarte por qué siente la necesidad de hacer trampas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Ah, just who I wanted to see! Hopefully the coastline is one oversized bird "
"safer, thanks to you two?"
msgstr ""
"¡Ah, justo a quienes quería ver! Espero que la costa tenga un pájaro gigante"
" menos gracias a vosotros dos, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...Try a pack. We've got your feathers. Now, it'd be nice to know how you-"
msgstr ""
"...Di más bien una bandada. Tenemos tus plumas. Ahora, estaría bien saber "
"cómo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, what am I to do with feathers? I can't very well throw them to the "
"target, you know."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, ¿y qué hago yo con unas plumas? No puedo lanzarlas a la diana, "
"¿sabéis?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'd appreciate it if you fashioned them into some arrows. Steel tips are "
"fine, that's what everyone else is using, don't want to stick out too much."
msgstr ""
"Os agradecería que las convirtierais en unas flechas. Las puntas de acero "
"están bien, es lo que usan todos los demás, no quiero llamar demasiado la "
"atención."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wait, we said that we'd get the feathers, not make them for you."
msgstr ""
"Espera, dijimos que conseguiríamos las plumas, no que te haríamos las "
"flechas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're an archer, you should know how to do that."
msgstr "Eres arquero, deberías saber hacerlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, yes, of course I know how, but I have to make sure my aim is true "
"regardless."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, sí, claro que sé, pero tengo que asegurarme de que mi puntería sea "
"certera de todos modos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Isn't that what the feathers are for?"
msgstr "¿No es para eso para lo que sirven las plumas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Remember, we're going up against other cheaters too. Every little advantage "
"counts."
msgstr ""
"Recordad que también competimos contra otros tramposos. Cada pequeña ventaja"
" cuenta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You don't get your readings if I don't win."
msgstr "No tendréis vuestras lecturas si no gano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm's sing-songy taunt elicits a glare from [Companion Name], but after a "
"brief standoff, she sighs and hauls you away, grumpily beginning to cut some"
" arrow shafts. You get the impression she'd rather use that knife elsewhere,"
" but has decided to behave, for now."
msgstr ""
"La burla cantarina de Talm le arranca una mirada fulminante a [Companion "
"Name], pero, tras un breve enfrentamiento, suspira y te lleva a rastras, y "
"empieza a cortar astiles de flecha de mal humor. Te da la impresión de que "
"preferiría usar ese cuchillo en otra parte, pero ha decidido portarse bien, "
"de momento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "None of this looks too rare, thankfully."
msgstr "Por suerte, nada de esto parece demasiado raro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This better be enough."
msgstr "Más vale que esto baste."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The two of you make your way back to Talm, this time with a bundle of "
"arrows, to which he receives with a small, polite show of clapping. He takes"
" one and inspects it carefully, before bending it so far that it snaps in "
"two. He tuts to himself and shoves the splintered arrow back into your "
"hands."
msgstr ""
"Volvéis junto a Talm, esta vez con un manojo de flechas, que él recibe con "
"unos pequeños y educados aplausos. Coge una y la inspecciona con cuidado, "
"antes de doblarla tanto que se parte en dos. Chasquea la lengua y te "
"devuelve la flecha astillada a las manos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Now now, this simply won't do. My bow may also be a bit special. Like I "
"said, I really want to win this. With the force I'll be sending these arrows"
" down range, they don't stand a chance."
msgstr ""
"Vaya, vaya, esto no sirve. Puede que mi arco también sea algo especial. Como"
" os dije, quiero ganar esto de verdad. Con la fuerza con la que voy a lanzar"
" estas flechas por el campo de tiro, no tienen ninguna posibilidad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What do you want us to do? Make the shafts out of metal, too?"
msgstr "¿Qué quieres que hagamos? ¿Que hagamos también los astiles de metal?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No no, of course not. Thankfully, Era came through for us and provided me "
"with a little... somethin' somethin' ahead of time."
msgstr ""
"No, no, claro que no. Por suerte, Era nos echó una mano y me dio un... algo "
"de antemano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And now, I leave the responsibility to the two of you. No need to thank me."
msgstr ""
"Y ahora, os dejo la responsabilidad a vosotros dos. No hace falta que me lo "
"agradezcáis."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...You'd better win."
msgstr "...Más te vale ganar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I've never been more sure of anything in my life."
msgstr "Nunca he estado tan seguro de nada en mi vida."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm hands you a scrap of paper that looks more akin to a grocery list than "
"anything that'd directly help win the competition. A handful of ingredients,"
" brought up to temperature and then distilled into a potion called 'True-"
"Shot', could be imbued into the arrows to give them incredible strength and "
"flexibility."
msgstr ""
"Talm te entrega un trozo de papel que parece más una lista de la compra que "
"algo que vaya a ayudar directamente a ganar el concurso. Un puñado de "
"ingredientes, llevados a la temperatura adecuada y luego destilados en una "
"poción llamada «Tiro certero», podría impregnarse en las flechas para darles"
" una fuerza y una flexibilidad increíbles."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You head back to find Talm, hopefully for the final time. Just as you manage to finish applying the solution, Talm is called to the range to take his shots. Each of his arrows finds their mark at the other side of the range, faster and more powerful than any of his opponents. The competition rages on and gets more fierce as competitors are eliminated. Talm's near permanent smile is slowly replaced by a look of genuine concentration his six remaining competitors do their best to outdo one another. Criteria for each shot begin to change as the distance and size of the targets can no longer be changed. The seven of them started shooting at pea-sized targets a few rounds back, so now, they begin to fire upside-down. On horseback. Blindfolded.\n"
"\n"
"Every few rounds, Talm manages to stick around as another competitor misses their mark. Even knowing how much help Talm is getting, you cannot help but cheer with each shot he lands. Unless he's going up against the best archers the world has even seen, you start to believe they have just as much assistance as he does. Talm makes it to the final round. One target, a hair-thin string gently dangling on the other side of the range. Both him and the other competitor fire at the same time, but Talm's blue-feathered arrow knocks the competitor's arrow out of the air, and severs the string on the other side.\n"
"\n"
"The crowd erupts into cheers, and you find yourself cheering as well, as Talm is brought up to the top of the podium and given a trophy about a quarter of his size. After ample celebration, he finds his way back to you and [Companion Name], and after a combination of gloating and thanks, tells you to find him when you're ready for your rewards."
msgstr ""
"Vuelves a buscar a Talm, con suerte por última vez. Justo cuando terminas de aplicar la solución, llaman a Talm al campo de tiro para que haga sus disparos. Cada una de sus flechas da en el blanco al otro lado del campo, más rápida y potente que las de cualquiera de sus rivales. La competición continúa y se vuelve más feroz a medida que se elimina a participantes. La sonrisa casi permanente de Talm da paso poco a poco a un gesto de auténtica concentración mientras sus seis rivales restantes hacen lo posible por superarse unos a otros. Los criterios de cada disparo empiezan a cambiar, ya que la distancia y el tamaño de las dianas no pueden variar más. Los siete empezaron a disparar a dianas del tamaño de un guisante hace unas cuantas rondas, así que ahora empiezan a disparar boca abajo. A caballo. Con los ojos vendados.\n"
"\n"
"Cada pocas rondas, Talm consigue seguir en pie cuando otro participante falla. Aun sabiendo cuánta ayuda está recibiendo Talm, no puedes evitar vitorear cada disparo que acierta. A menos que se enfrente a los mejores arqueros que el mundo haya visto jamás, empiezas a creer que los demás reciben tanta ayuda como él. Talm llega a la ronda final. Una diana: un hilo finísimo que cuelga suavemente al otro lado del campo. Él y el otro participante disparan a la vez, pero la flecha de plumas azules de Talm derriba en el aire la flecha de su rival y corta el hilo al otro lado.\n"
"\n"
"El público estalla en vítores, y te sorprendes vitoreando también mientras suben a Talm a lo más alto del podio y le entregan un trofeo de casi una cuarta parte de su tamaño. Tras una buena celebración, vuelve contigo y con [Companion Name] y, entre fanfarronadas y agradecimientos, os dice que lo busquéis cuando estéis listos para vuestras recompensas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 45[/color] Enemy "
"multiple times"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar varias veces a un enemigo de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de "
"combate 45[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Rewards.CustomRewards
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Unlocks the Sea Cliffside Combat Area"
msgstr "Desbloquea la zona de combate Acantilado marino"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The Ivory Athenaeum"
msgstr "El Ateneo de marfil"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"After helping Talm win Melvor's archery competition, you've done your part. "
"Now, it's time for him to honor his side of the deal and hopefully provide "
"information regarding the Soulsmiths."
msgstr ""
"Tras ayudar a Talm a ganar la competición de tiro con arco de Melvor, ya has"
" cumplido tu parte. Ahora le toca a él cumplir la suya y, con suerte, darte "
"información sobre los Forjaalmas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This mission might be next to impossible."
msgstr "Esta misión podría ser casi imposible."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Now we just... take a little mould of the lock."
msgstr "Ahora solo tenemos que... sacar un pequeño molde de la cerradura."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Even in a city as bustling as Melvor, Talm is a remarkably easy figure to find. After just a few minutes of asking around the range, you find yourself face to face with the tall, smiling man. Without a word he gestures for you to follow him, so you do, trusting he knows what you're after. You're led deep within the alleys and byways of the capital, some better, some worse. As you round a corner you find yourself at the back entrance of a brightly painted stone building, door already open for you to enter. As the three of you enter, the door quietly shuts behind you without any prompting.\n"
"\n"
"You're brought before an absolutely stunning woman who greets the three of you with a wordless smile, and gestures for you to sit on cushions laid out in front of her. You do, and the room quickly fills with a twinkling blue fog. You panic for a moment before deciding that they don't seem to mean you harm, and you inhale deeply.\n"
"\n"
"Your vision fades away, then comes back to you as you're flying far overhead a large white building, whose doors seem to suck you in. You fall through the floor of the building and weave through shelf and shelf of books, all the way to a large vault made of a blend of metals and magic you instinctively know as you pass through its walls. Within, you find a gilded tome that seems to glow with power. The moment you touch it, you snap back awake next to [Companion Name]. She seems... upset, seemingly a bit disturbed by whatever she saw."
msgstr ""
"Incluso en una ciudad tan bulliciosa como Melvor, Talm es alguien muy fácil de encontrar. Tras preguntar unos minutos por el campo de tiro, te encuentras cara a cara con el hombre alto y sonriente. Sin decir palabra, te indica con un gesto que lo sigas, y eso haces, confiando en que sabe lo que buscas. Te guía por los callejones y pasajes de la capital, unos mejores y otros peores. Al doblar una esquina, llegas a la entrada trasera de un edificio de piedra pintado con colores vivos, con la puerta ya abierta para que entres. En cuanto entráis los tres, la puerta se cierra en silencio a vuestra espalda sin que nadie la toque.\n"
"\n"
"Te llevan ante una mujer deslumbrante que os recibe a los tres con una sonrisa muda y os invita con un gesto a sentaros en los cojines dispuestos frente a ella. Lo hacéis, y la sala se llena enseguida de una niebla azul centelleante. Te entra el pánico un momento, pero decides que no parecen querer hacerte daño, e inspiras hondo.\n"
"\n"
"Tu vista se desvanece y vuelve mientras sobrevuelas a gran altura un enorme edificio blanco cuyas puertas parecen absorberte. Atraviesas el suelo del edificio y serpenteas entre estanterías y estanterías de libros, hasta llegar a una gran cámara hecha de una mezcla de metales y magia que reconoces por instinto al atravesar sus muros. Dentro encuentras un tomo dorado que parece brillar de poder. En cuanto lo tocas, despiertas de golpe junto a [Companion Name]. Parece... afectada, algo perturbada por lo que sea que ha visto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What... was that? Did you see the same thing, [Companion Name]?"
msgstr "¿Qué... ha sido eso? ¿Has visto lo mismo, [Companion Name]?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I uh... doubt it. What'd you see?"
msgstr "Eh... lo dudo. ¿Qué has visto tú?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A large white building with what was almost a maze under it, and then a "
"vault."
msgstr ""
"Un gran edificio blanco con algo parecido a un laberinto debajo, y luego una"
" cámara."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ah. You saw the Abyssal Vault, did you?"
msgstr "Ah. Has visto la Cámara abisal, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Best of luck getting inside, I've only been a few times, myself."
msgstr "Mucha suerte para entrar. Yo solo he estado unas pocas veces."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Era, you can't spoil it. That's half the fun."
msgstr "Era, no se lo destripes. Eso es la mitad de la gracia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They have much ground to cover, and little time."
msgstr "Tienen mucho terreno que cubrir y poco tiempo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Isn't that right, [Companion Name]?"
msgstr "¿No es así, [Companion Name]?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What do you mean? [Companion Name] are you alright?"
msgstr "¿Qué quieres decir? [Companion Name], ¿estás bien?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... will be, I promise."
msgstr "Lo... estaré, te lo prometo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What's this about a vault?"
msgstr "¿Qué es eso de una cámara?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Since my dear already spoiled the surprise, it sounds like you two need to "
"engage in a little..."
msgstr ""
"Como mi querida ya ha arruinado la sorpresa, parece que vosotros dos "
"tendréis que hacer un pequeño..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Heist. Of sorts. Should be a cakewalk."
msgstr "Golpe. Más o menos. Debería ser pan comido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We just got to town. I don't think jail is on my list of places I'd like to "
"see."
msgstr ""
"Acabamos de llegar a la ciudad. No creo que la cárcel esté en mi lista de "
"sitios que quiero ver."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It shouldn't have to be, if you're careful."
msgstr "No tendría por qué, si tenéis cuidado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The vault requires a key, but before you can make one, you'll have to obtain"
" a mold of the lock."
msgstr ""
"La cámara necesita una llave, pero antes de fabricarla tendréis que "
"conseguir un molde de la cerradura."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And if we were to do something so unscrupulous, which we aren't by the way, "
"how are we to know you wouldn't turn us in?"
msgstr ""
"Y si hiciéramos algo tan poco escrupuloso, que no es el caso, por cierto, "
"¿cómo sabemos que no nos delataríais?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If you're after information on the Soulsmiths, and it has lead you to the "
"vault, stopping you would be... unwise."
msgstr ""
"Si buscáis información sobre los Forjaalmas y eso os ha llevado hasta la "
"cámara, deteneros sería... poco sensato."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Feel free to try and gain lawful access to the vault if you wish, I promise "
"you it would not be fruitful."
msgstr ""
"Si queréis, intentad conseguir acceso legal a la cámara. Os prometo que no "
"daría ningún fruto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And how do the two of you know about them? And that we're... interested?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo sabéis vosotros dos de ellos? ¿Y que estamos... interesados?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Era and I indulge in the visions she can provide quite often, really. "
msgstr ""
"Era y yo nos damos el gusto de las visiones que ella puede ofrecer bastante "
"a menudo, la verdad. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "One of them showed you two, and through that, what you've been up to."
msgstr ""
"Una de ellas os mostró a vosotros dos y, a través de ella, lo que habéis "
"estado haciendo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And what you must face. Go now, return when you've gotten what you need."
msgstr ""
"Y a lo que debéis enfrentaros. Id ahora, y volved cuando tengáis lo que "
"necesitáis."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And with that, Talm helps Era up and takes her to a room behind a nearby curtain. It doesn't seem like you're invited. You check on [Companion Name] once again, about the vision she had. She gently, tells you that she'll talk about it later, just that it was a bit scary. \n"
"\n"
"The two of you wander around the city, a bit less awestruck than when you first arrived, and soon enough, find yourselves on the doorstep of the Ivory Athenaeum. From what you learn, speaking with some of the guests and staff, it'd seem that the titanic structure holds the largest compilation of humanity's knowledge ever created, with a near endless number of books on every subject one could think of.\n"
"\n"
"You ask about the lower floors, and learn that they are restricted from the general public, needing a direct invitation from the King himself to be let inside, since the books down there contain dangerous information. The process of obtaining an invitation is told to you through a long, well-rehearsed deluge of information. What sticks out to you is the time involved. An average of thirty years for those prestigious enough to be allowed a chance. Too long."
msgstr ""
"Dicho esto, Talm ayuda a Era a levantarse y la lleva a una habitación tras una cortina cercana. No parece que os hayan invitado. Vuelves a preguntar a [Companion Name] por la visión que tuvo. Con delicadeza, te dice que ya hablará de ello más tarde, que solo ha sido un poco aterrador. \n"
"\n"
"Los dos recorréis la ciudad, algo menos asombrados que cuando llegasteis, y pronto os encontráis ante la puerta del Ateneo de marfil. Por lo que averiguas hablando con algunos visitantes y empleados, parece que la colosal estructura alberga la mayor recopilación del saber humano jamás creada, con un número casi infinito de libros sobre cualquier tema imaginable.\n"
"\n"
"Preguntas por las plantas inferiores y descubres que están vetadas al público general: hace falta una invitación directa del mismísimo rey para entrar, ya que los libros de allí abajo contienen información peligrosa. Te explican el proceso para obtener una invitación con un largo y bien ensayado torrente de información. Lo que más te llama la atención es el tiempo que requiere. Una media de treinta años para quienes son lo bastante prestigiosos como para tener una oportunidad. Demasiado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The vision proved particularly useful, didn't it?"
msgstr "La visión resultó especialmente útil, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This looks about right. Back down we go."
msgstr "Esto parece correcto. Volvamos abajo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You want to let out a cheer as the Abyssal Vault comes into view, but you obviously know better than that. You put [Companion Name] up on your shoulders and she slowly but surely presses a wedge of clay into the arcane locking mechanism. The vault is exactly as it appeared in your vision, and you do your best to memorize the magic that courses through it as [Companion Name] deals with the mould. You know from your vision that you'll have to imbue the key with the same magic for it to actually work when you come back and let yourself in.\n"
"\n"
"Now that you've properly mapped out the route to the vault, you're able to get back to the entrance with little trouble. Understandably, the patrolling guards are both few in number and a bit inattentive, it's not like many people would be crazy enough to try this. You and [Companion Name] make it back out of the Ivory Athenaeum, and finally allow yourself to breathe."
msgstr ""
"Te dan ganas de soltar un grito de alegría cuando la Cámara abisal aparece ante tus ojos, pero, evidentemente, sabes que no debes. Subes a [Companion Name] a tus hombros y, despacio pero con seguridad, presiona una cuña de arcilla contra el mecanismo de cierre arcano. La cámara es exactamente como apareció en tu visión, y haces lo posible por memorizar la magia que la recorre mientras [Companion Name] se ocupa del molde. Sabes por tu visión que tendrás que imbuir la llave con esa misma magia para que funcione de verdad cuando volváis a entrar.\n"
"\n"
"Ahora que has trazado bien la ruta hasta la cámara, puedes volver a la entrada sin apenas problemas. Como es lógico, los guardias que patrullan son pocos y algo distraídos; no hay mucha gente tan loca como para intentar algo así. [Companion Name] y tú salís del Ateneo de marfil y por fin os permitís respirar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I can't believe it!"
msgstr "¡No me lo puedo creer!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I can't believe we'll have to do it again."
msgstr "...No me puedo creer que tengamos que hacerlo otra vez."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We already made it in once, what's the worst that could happen?"
msgstr "Ya hemos entrado una vez, ¿qué es lo peor que podría pasar?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't even want to humor that question with a guess."
msgstr "Ni siquiera quiero darle a esa pregunta el gusto de una respuesta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We'll be fineeee, I'm sure of it. 50 gold say we make it back down there and"
" back without a problem."
msgstr ""
"Saldrá todo bieeeen, estoy segura. Te apuesto 50 de oro a que bajamos ahí y "
"volvemos sin ningún problema."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"How about we bet bail on it, hm? I can't even imagine how many years we'd "
"get."
msgstr ""
"¿Y si apostamos la fianza, eh? No me imagino ni cuántos años nos caerían."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, you don't need to imagine. Because we just did it! Let's get started "
"on that key, hm?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, no hace falta imaginarlo. ¡Porque lo acabamos de hacer! Vamos a "
"ponernos con esa llave, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You take the mould and start to jot down everything you'll need onto a piece"
" of paper. Everything for the perfect alloy to match the material of the "
"vault, along with what you remember of the magical barrier that surged "
"through the exterior of the vault."
msgstr ""
"Coges el molde y empiezas a anotar en un trozo de papel todo lo que vas a "
"necesitar. Todo lo necesario para la aleación perfecta que coincida con el "
"material de la cámara, junto con lo que recuerdas de la barrera mágica que "
"recorría el exterior de la cámara."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't think he's going to let us out of here."
msgstr "No creo que vaya a dejarnos salir de aquí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Sorry, big fella."
msgstr "Lo siento, grandullón."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Sure enough, the patrols and traps seem to be exactly the same as the first time you came down here. It isn't particularly a surprise, but it still lets you relax a bit as you slink through the endless rows of bookshelves, back to the door of the vault. Your dark clothes and molded face-mask restrict your breathing a little bit, but on the off-chance that someone sees you, you'll be glad for the anonymity it provides.\n"
"\n"
"You reach up and slide your key into the lock, and with a clunk - one that's a bit louder than you would have hoped for - the Abyssal Vault door cracks open, just a pinch. You and [Companion Name] slip inside and find row after row of plinths, holding not just books, but what look like dangerous phials of liquid, weapons, and maps. [Companion Name] whispers across the vault to you."
msgstr ""
"Efectivamente, las patrullas y las trampas parecen exactamente iguales que la primera vez que bajaste. No es ninguna sorpresa, pero aun así te relaja un poco mientras te deslizas entre las interminables hileras de estanterías hasta la puerta de la cámara. Tu ropa oscura y la máscara moldeada te dificultan un poco la respiración, pero si por casualidad alguien te ve, agradecerás el anonimato que te dan.\n"
"\n"
"Alzas la mano y metes la llave en la cerradura y, con un chasquido (algo más fuerte de lo que esperabas), la puerta de la Cámara abisal se entreabre apenas un poco. [Companion Name] y tú os coláis dentro y encontráis fila tras fila de pedestales que no solo sostienen libros, sino también lo que parecen frascos de líquidos peligrosos, armas y mapas. [Companion Name] te susurra desde el otro lado de la cámara."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What's the title of the book again? There's dozens of them."
msgstr "¿Cómo se llamaba el libro? Aquí hay docenas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I didn't see... It was just bound in black leather, and gilded with gold. "
"Bout... this big."
msgstr ""
"No lo vi... Solo estaba encuadernado en cuero negro, con adornos de oro. "
"Así... de grande, más o menos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll let you know if I see it. Don't die."
msgstr "Te aviso si lo veo. No te mueras."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You too."
msgstr "Tú tampoco."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The two of you quickly search through the displayed items until you find what you're looking for. The black, gilded tome from your vision. Amongst everything else in the vault, you'd almost call it unassuming. \n"
"\n"
"It hums with some unknown magic, and you give it a ginger touch with your hand. When you don't immediately get vaporized by some unknown power, you lift it from its resting place and crack it open. The first page says... Something in a language you've never seen before. You snap it closed and gently wave it for [Companion Name] to see. She carefully crosses the vault and takes the book, and the two of you head back to the entrance. However, the moment your hand touches the metal of the door to push it back open, it snaps shut. A loud hum fills the room, along with what sounds like an alarm outside of the vault.\n"
"\n"
"As you look to [Companion Name], a large golem seems to coalesce from the ground, made of the same alloy as the rest of the vault. [Companion Name] readies her weapon, and you follow suit."
msgstr ""
"Los dos registráis rápidamente los objetos expuestos hasta encontrar lo que buscáis. El tomo negro y dorado de tu visión. Entre todo lo demás que hay en la cámara, casi dirías que pasa desapercibido. \n"
"\n"
"Vibra con una magia desconocida, y lo rozas con cautela. Como no te desintegra al instante ningún poder desconocido, lo levantas de su sitio y lo abres. La primera página dice... algo en un idioma que nunca has visto. Lo cierras de golpe y lo agitas suavemente para que [Companion Name] lo vea. Ella cruza la cámara con cuidado y coge el libro, y los dos volvéis hacia la entrada. Sin embargo, en cuanto tu mano toca el metal de la puerta para empujarla, esta se cierra de golpe. Un fuerte zumbido llena la sala, junto con lo que suena como una alarma fuera de la cámara.\n"
"\n"
"Al mirar a [Companion Name], un gran gólem parece fusionarse a partir del suelo, hecho de la misma aleación que el resto de la cámara. [Companion Name] prepara su arma, y tú haces lo mismo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We need to escape, NOW!"
msgstr "¡Tenemos que escapar, YA!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Phew... that was close."
msgstr "Uf... ha estado cerca."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As the golem falls and melts back into the floor, the door to the vault "
"blessedly clicks open once again. You and [Companion Name] gather yourselves"
" to see... roughly fifty guards running in your direction down the hall, "
"likely with many more behind them."
msgstr ""
"Cuando el gólem cae y vuelve a fundirse con el suelo, la puerta de la cámara"
" se abre de nuevo con un bendito chasquido. [Companion Name] y tú os "
"recomponéis para ver... a unos cincuenta guardias corriendo hacia vosotros "
"por el pasillo, y probablemente muchos más detrás."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You owe me fifty gold!"
msgstr "¡Me debes cincuenta de oro!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I said we'd get down here safe. I didn't say anything about getting back "
"out!"
msgstr ""
"Dije que llegaríamos aquí abajo sanos y salvos. ¡No dije nada de volver a "
"salir!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Now run!"
msgstr "¡Ahora corre!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The two of you begin scaling the bookshelves outside of the vault and run as"
" fast as you can. Fearful of destroying the collection, the guards refuse to"
" fire upon you but give chase back down the halls, slowed by the same traps "
"meant to stop intruders. The tops of the shelves have just as many, if not "
"more traps."
msgstr ""
"Los dos empezáis a trepar por las estanterías de fuera de la cámara y "
"corréis todo lo que podéis. Por miedo a destruir la colección, los guardias "
"se niegan a dispararos, pero os persiguen por los pasillos, frenados por las"
" mismas trampas pensadas para detener a los intrusos. Lo alto de las "
"estanterías tiene tantas trampas o más."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The two of you run like your lives depend on it, because they likely do. Every time you're singed by a magical barrier or narrowly dodge a guardsman's pike, you just think about how many lifetimes you'd likely spend in Melvor's jails. That is, if they didn't just outright execute you. You make sure not to hurt anyone, because murder wouldn't likely get you any better treatment if you were to be captured.\n"
"\n"
"By some miracle, you manage to make it to the stairwell leading up out of the lower floors. Stunned guardsmen scramble to bring their weapons at the ready - clearly not anticipating any intruders actually making it back to the entrance - and the two of you manage to burst back out into the main floor of the athenaeum.\n"
"\n"
"You rush outside and into the throngs of people being evacuated outside. Guards point and shout at the two of you as you melt into the crowds but fail to give chase as you quickly slip deeper and deeper into the mass of concerned citizens. The two of you find yourselves at the edge of a canal and jump in, swimming under the water all the way to an exposed sewer grate. You let yourselves inside and strip off your disguises and toss them into the water, both silent as the adrenaline slowly works its way through your bodies. You quietly laugh and lean against the wall of the sewer with a sick squelch you don't even notice. You did it. You got out, somehow."
msgstr ""
"Los dos corréis como si os fuera la vida en ello, porque seguramente así es. Cada vez que te chamuscas con una barrera mágica o esquivas por poco la pica de un guardia, solo piensas en cuántas vidas pasarías probablemente en las cárceles de Melvor. Eso, si no os ejecutan directamente. Te aseguras de no herir a nadie, porque un asesinato no te iba a conseguir mejor trato si te capturaban.\n"
"\n"
"Por algún milagro, logras llegar a la escalera que sube desde las plantas inferiores. Los guardias, aturdidos, se apresuran a preparar sus armas (está claro que no esperaban que ningún intruso llegara de vuelta a la entrada), y los dos conseguís irrumpir en la planta principal del ateneo.\n"
"\n"
"Salís corriendo y os metéis entre la multitud que están evacuando. Los guardias os señalan y os gritan mientras os fundís con el gentío, pero no logran perseguiros mientras os escabullís cada vez más hondo entre la masa de ciudadanos preocupados. Llegáis a la orilla de un canal y saltáis al agua, nadando bajo la superficie hasta una rejilla de alcantarilla al descubierto. Os metéis dentro, os quitáis los disfraces y los tiráis al agua, ambos en silencio mientras la adrenalina recorre poco a poco vuestros cuerpos. Te ríes en voz baja y te apoyas en la pared de la alcantarilla con un chapoteo asqueroso que ni siquiera notas. Lo habéis conseguido. Habéis salido, de algún modo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 50[/color] [u]Dungeon "
"Boss[/u]"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar a un [u]jefe de mazmorra[/u] de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de"
" combate 50[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Rewards.CustomRewards
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"(Coming Soon) Unlocks the Summoning Skill\n"
"(Coming Soon) Unlocks the Ivory Athenaeum Thieving Location (Summoning themed)"
msgstr ""
"(Próximamente) Desbloquea la habilidad Invocación\n"
"(Próximamente) Desbloquea la ubicación de robo Ateneo de marfil (con temática de Invocación)"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Unfortunate Teller"
msgstr "Desafortunada adivina"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"After the miraculous heist of the Abyssal Vault, it's time to return to Era "
"and Talm. Maybe they'll be able to tell you something about the book you "
"managed to steal, considering you haven't the slightest clue on what it "
"says."
msgstr ""
"Tras el milagroso golpe en la Cámara abisal, es hora de volver con Era y "
"Talm. Quizá puedan contarte algo sobre el libro que conseguiste robar, ya "
"que no tienes ni la más remota idea de lo que dice."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I doubt Talm will let us take his equipment after this. The recipe won't do "
"us any good afterwards."
msgstr ""
"Dudo que Talm nos deje llevarnos su equipo después de esto. La receta no nos"
" servirá de nada luego."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "As useful as it might otherwise be..."
msgstr "Por muy útil que pudiera ser..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] flicks the gilded tome open and closed, looking at it from every angle she can, and trying a few different pages. Like you, she hasn't the foggiest clue about what the book says, and the place that would likely know, is still searching high and low for it. You and [Companion Name] have left your little sewer hideaway and sure enough, the disguises you donned before the heist worked. No one comes to put you in shackles and haul you off to some dark dungeon. As far as anyone else is concerned, you're just one of the many thousands of tourists to the capital.\n"
"\n"
"You head back to Era and Talm's home and find it in flames. Talm worriedly tries to douse the flames with many other passersby, until a capital mage buries the building under a deluge of water. You rush to Talm. Your presence gives him pause, and he gestures for you two to follow him."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] abre y cierra el tomo dorado, mirándolo desde todos los ángulos posibles y probando con distintas páginas. Igual que tú, no tiene ni la menor idea de lo que dice el libro, y el lugar que probablemente lo sabría sigue buscándolo por todas partes. [Companion Name] y tú habéis dejado vuestro pequeño escondite en la alcantarilla y, efectivamente, los disfraces que os pusisteis antes del golpe funcionaron. Nadie viene a poneros grilletes y arrastraros a alguna mazmorra oscura. Para todos los demás, no sois más que dos de los muchos miles de turistas de la capital.\n"
"\n"
"Volvéis a casa de Era y Talm y la encontráis... en llamas. Talm intenta apagar el fuego con preocupación junto a muchos otros transeúntes, hasta que un mago de la capital sepulta el edificio bajo un torrente de agua. Corres hacia Talm. Al veros, se detiene un instante y os indica con un gesto que lo sigáis."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Come on. We need to see what's left!"
msgstr "Vamos. ¡Tenemos que ver qué queda!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Talm, what happened? Is Era with you?"
msgstr "Talm, ¿qué ha pasado? ¿Está Era contigo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "No! She's... she's been taken."
msgstr "¡No! Se la... se la han llevado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "She knew she would be, of course... We just didn't know when."
msgstr "Ella sabía que pasaría, claro... Solo que no sabíamos cuándo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The visions aren't always... precise. Come with me, please."
msgstr "Las visiones no siempre son... precisas. Venid conmigo, por favor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The urgency and pain in his voice spur you and [Companion Name] to follow. The three of you push into the smoking building and find the back room drenched, but relatively untouched by the flames. The room is a disaster and there's signs of a scuffle that are clear even despite the water and fire. Talm sighs, but seems more calm than he was before the two of you arrived.\n"
"\n"
"He opens a chest tucked in a corner and pulls out what seems to be alchemy equipment. He laments how Era will feel about him giving away trade secrets, but shows you how to make the same vision-inducing smoke you inhaled before your heist, saying that it should be able to help the three of you find Era. You think about bringing up the book, but figure it can wait for now."
msgstr ""
"La urgencia y el dolor de su voz os empujan a [Companion Name] y a ti a seguirlo. Los tres entráis en el edificio humeante y encontráis la habitación trasera empapada, pero relativamente intacta por las llamas. La habitación es un desastre y hay señales de forcejeo que se ven con claridad pese al agua y al fuego. Talm suspira, pero parece más tranquilo que antes de que llegarais.\n"
"\n"
"Abre un baúl metido en un rincón y saca lo que parece equipo de alquimia. Se lamenta de lo que pensará Era de que revele secretos del oficio, pero te enseña a preparar el mismo humo que provoca visiones que inhalaste antes del golpe, y dice que debería ayudaros a los tres a encontrar a Era. Piensas en mencionar el libro, pero decides que puede esperar por ahora."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We can take them."
msgstr "Podemos con ellos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Told you."
msgstr "Te lo dije."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm crowds around as you burn the large pouches of the specialized herbal blend. It doesn't seem as strong as the last time you had it, and you're unsure of if you did something wrong or if it's just part of a building tolerance.\n"
"\n"
"Nevertheless, you find yourself feeling much of the same sensation as before, but this time, you float over a small, ramshackle hut deep within what you presume are Melvor's slums. The only distinguishing characteristic is a single crescent-shaped grey marking by its door. As you come back to, Talm blinks his eyes, seemingly coming back to reality as well. [Companion Name] holds her hands over her face, waving the smoke away and asking if you two saw what you needed to."
msgstr ""
"Talm se acerca mientras quemas las grandes bolsas de la mezcla de hierbas especial. No parece tan fuerte como la última vez, y no sabes si has hecho algo mal o si es que vas desarrollando tolerancia.\n"
"\n"
"Aun así, sientes casi lo mismo que antes, pero esta vez flotas sobre una pequeña choza destartalada en lo que supones que son los barrios bajos de Melvor. Lo único que la distingue es una marca gris en forma de media luna junto a la puerta. Al volver en ti, Talm parpadea, como si también regresara a la realidad. [Companion Name] se tapa la cara con las manos, apartando el humo, y os pregunta si habéis visto lo que necesitabais."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You didn't use the smoke, [Companion Name]?"
msgstr "¿No has usado el humo, [Companion Name]?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I will if I need to... but..."
msgstr "Lo usaré si hace falta... pero..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'd really rather not."
msgstr "Preferiría no hacerlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That's understandable, I'm sorry, I didn't think about..."
msgstr "Es comprensible, lo siento, no pensé en..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's okay, really."
msgstr "No pasa nada, de verdad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I saw a building out in the slums. There were... probably hundreds just like"
" it. I'm sorry, but that's all I got."
msgstr ""
"He visto un edificio en los barrios bajos. Había... seguramente cientos como"
" ese. Lo siento, pero es todo lo que tengo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's okay. The Sightsmoke shows you... whatever you need to see. Era would "
"know how to explain it better."
msgstr ""
"No pasa nada. El humo vidente te muestra... lo que necesites ver. Era sabría"
" explicarlo mejor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But don't worry, I saw the path to the area. Just point out if you can, "
"okay?"
msgstr ""
"Pero no te preocupes, he visto el camino hasta la zona. Señálalo si puedes, "
"¿vale?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The three of you set off, leaving the burned building behind. Talm leads you through the city with such ease and purpose you get the feeling he's been here a long, long, time. As you travel, the people you see become less friendly, and more dirty. Desperate. The slums were doubtlessly going to be here, like any other large city, but to see them up close was a staunch difference to when you first arrived in the capital a few weeks ago.\n"
"\n"
"Rougher looking folks give you a large berth when they lock eyes with Talm. The generally friendly man now walks with murderous intent, his bow now set aside for a longsword and shield that he carries openly. He looks back to you frequently, making sure you're looking out for the shack as diligently as he'd hope for. And sure enough, you see it. The crescent shape by the door - just like in your vision - is so loud to your eyes, you almost don't understand how [Companion Name] and Talm don't see it.\n"
"\n"
"You point it out, and without a word, Talm approaches the door and sends it off its hinges with a startlingly powerful kick. You eye [Companion Name], who charges in right behind him. Swords clash almost immediately."
msgstr ""
"Los tres os ponéis en marcha y dejáis atrás el edificio quemado. Talm os guía por la ciudad con tanta soltura y determinación que tienes la sensación de que lleva aquí mucho, mucho tiempo. Mientras avanzáis, la gente que veis se vuelve menos amable y más sucia. Desesperada. Los barrios bajos tenían que estar ahí, como en cualquier otra gran ciudad, pero verlos de cerca era un contraste enorme con tu llegada a la capital hace unas semanas.\n"
"\n"
"La gente de aspecto más duro se aparta de vuestro camino en cuanto cruza la mirada con Talm. El hombre, normalmente amable, camina ahora con intenciones asesinas, con el arco guardado y una espada larga y un escudo que lleva a la vista. Se gira a menudo para asegurarse de que estás buscando la choza con tanto empeño como espera. Y, efectivamente, la ves. La media luna junto a la puerta, igual que en tu visión, resalta tanto a tus ojos que casi no entiendes cómo [Companion Name] y Talm no la ven.\n"
"\n"
"La señalas y, sin decir palabra, Talm se acerca a la puerta y la arranca de sus bisagras de una patada sorprendentemente potente. Miras a [Companion Name], que entra a la carga justo detrás de él. Las espadas chocan casi al instante."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Just like you remember, all that time ago. Hooded figures with beasts you've never seen or heard of, clash with you and your companions. However, unlike back at Azamire, you don't fall. You drive them back into the building, where more of their beasts materialize from nothing, following a few quickly spoken words and a flash of light. They bare down on you, but you push them back, again and again, until the last of the hooded figures falls.\n"
"\n"
"You worry about the commotion until you realize that... the guards likely don't make it out this far.\n"
"\n"
"You search the building and find many of Era's things. Books and scrolls in a similar script to the gilded tome you took from the Abyssal Vault, and many others in different writing that seems to flow and move like water on the page. But the woman herself doesn't seem to be here. Talm slams his fist into a nearby table in anger, splintering the wood.\n"
"\n"
"You look to the man, who hardly seems to notice the few small cuts he took to his arms and side. He doesn't look back to you as he reaches a hand out to one of the dead figures. Their body begins to contort, cracking and lurching with sickening jolts, as the body seems to right itself once again. The man rises, standing on his feet once again despite several wounds that should have left him as nothing but a corpse.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] says it before you can. Soulsmith. Talm turns to you both, finally snapping out of his pure drive to find his wife. He sputters out an apology, and promises to explain everything, he just needs a little time. He begs you to come back in just a little bit, if you can stomach it. [Companion Name] backs away slowly before pushing into you, bringing you both outside, leaving the man alone. "
msgstr ""
"Tal y como lo recuerdas, de hace tanto tiempo. Figuras encapuchadas con bestias que nunca has visto ni oído nombrar se enfrentan a ti y a tus compañeros. Sin embargo, a diferencia de lo ocurrido en Azamire, no caes. Los haces retroceder hacia el edificio, donde más bestias suyas se materializan de la nada tras unas palabras rápidas y un destello de luz. Se abalanzan sobre ti, pero las rechazas una y otra vez, hasta que cae la última de las figuras encapuchadas.\n"
"\n"
"Te preocupa el alboroto hasta que te das cuenta de que... seguramente los guardias no llegan hasta aquí.\n"
"\n"
"Registras el edificio y encuentras muchas cosas de Era. Libros y pergaminos con una escritura parecida a la del tomo dorado que te llevaste de la Cámara abisal, y muchos otros con una escritura distinta que parece fluir y moverse como el agua sobre la página. Pero la mujer no parece estar aquí. Talm golpea con el puño una mesa cercana, furioso, y astilla la madera.\n"
"\n"
"Miras al hombre, que apenas parece notar los pequeños cortes que ha recibido en los brazos y el costado. No te devuelve la mirada mientras extiende una mano hacia una de las figuras muertas. El cuerpo empieza a retorcerse, crujiendo y sacudiéndose con espasmos nauseabundos, hasta que parece enderezarse de nuevo. El hombre se levanta, de nuevo en pie pese a varias heridas que deberían haberlo dejado convertido en un simple cadáver.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] lo dice antes que tú. Forjaalmas. Talm se vuelve hacia vosotros, saliendo por fin de su ciego empeño por encontrar a su esposa. Balbucea una disculpa y promete explicarlo todo; solo necesita un poco de tiempo. Os ruega que volváis dentro de un rato, si sois capaces de soportarlo. [Companion Name] retrocede despacio antes de empujarte, sacándoos a ambos fuera y dejando al hombre solo. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 55[/color] Enemy "
"multiple times"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar varias veces a un enemigo de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de "
"combate 55[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Starlit Sky"
msgstr "Cielo estrellado"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm has revealed himself to have some form of control over the dead, just "
"like the Soulsmiths who burned your home. While he may hold no love for them"
" after the kidnapping of Era, he has a lot to explain. Quickly."
msgstr ""
"Talm ha revelado que tiene algún tipo de control sobre los muertos, igual "
"que los Forjaalmas que quemaron tu hogar. Aunque no sienta ningún aprecio "
"por ellos tras el secuestro de Era, tiene mucho que explicar. Y rápido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I need to improve my techniques."
msgstr "Tengo que mejorar mis técnicas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I feel good."
msgstr "Me siento bien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] and you are still reeling from Talm's reveal. What is he? What'd he do to that Soulsmith? If he has the same powers as them, why is he against them? The two of you bounce questions off one another in an endless, confusing jumble of words until you realize you have none of the answers, and can hardly even begin to guess.\n"
"\n"
"There's only one way to learn. You both enter the shoddy hut on the edge of Melvor's slums, weapons in hand, and find Talm right where you left him. His hands are covered in blood as he seems to be patching the least damaged clothes of the hooded figures together, piling them on top of the... walking corpse until it resembles a living person. Talm seems almost surprised to see you again, manages a few attempts of pleading his allegiance, but then sucks in a deep breath and just... tells you to ask away."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] y tú seguís conmocionados por la revelación de Talm. ¿Qué es? ¿Qué le ha hecho a ese forjaalmas? Si tiene los mismos poderes que ellos, ¿por qué está en su contra? Os lanzáis preguntas el uno al otro en un revoltijo de palabras interminable y confuso hasta que os dais cuenta de que no tenéis ninguna respuesta y apenas podéis empezar a adivinarlas.\n"
"\n"
"Solo hay una forma de saberlo. Entráis los dos en la cochambrosa choza al borde de los barrios bajos de Melvor, armas en mano, y encontráis a Talm justo donde lo dejasteis. Tiene las manos cubiertas de sangre mientras parece remendar las ropas menos dañadas de las figuras encapuchadas, amontonándolas sobre el... cadáver andante hasta que parece una persona viva. Talm parece casi sorprendido de veros de nuevo, intenta un par de veces declarar su lealtad, pero luego toma aire hondo y simplemente... os dice que preguntéis lo que queráis."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Why'd you turn on the Soulsmiths?"
msgstr "¿Por qué traicionaste a los Forjaalmas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I... I didn't turn on them, I've never been on. I'm a Summoner. A very old "
"one, at that."
msgstr ""
"No... no los traicioné, nunca fui uno de ellos. Soy un invocador. Uno muy "
"antiguo, además."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "My clan has... had, similar powers to this upstart band of wannabes."
msgstr ""
"Mi clan tiene... tenía poderes parecidos a los de esta panda de advenedizos "
"que se creen algo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The things we could do back in the day... The Soulsmiths don't even come "
"close. Yet."
msgstr ""
"Las cosas que podíamos hacer en nuestros tiempos... Los Forjaalmas no se "
"acercan ni de lejos. Todavía."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Are you evil?"
msgstr "¿Eres malvado?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I've been called devilish. And I am currently enthralling the corpse of my "
"enemy to take me to my kidnapped wife."
msgstr ""
"Me han llamado diabólico. Y ahora mismo estoy hechizando el cadáver de mi "
"enemigo para que me lleve hasta mi esposa secuestrada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But, for the intention of your question, no. I'm not."
msgstr "Pero, en el sentido de tu pregunta, no. No lo soy."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If anything, I'm rather aligned against the Soulsmiths, and most who seek to"
" use Summoning, for that matter."
msgstr ""
"En todo caso, estoy más bien en contra de los Forjaalmas, y de la mayoría de"
" quienes buscan usar la Invocación, ya puestos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You said you're old. How old?"
msgstr "Has dicho que eres antiguo. ¿Cuánto?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I was around before... this capital. And the one before it. Era too."
msgstr ""
"Ya estaba aquí antes de... esta capital. Y de la anterior. Era también."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How?"
msgstr "¿Cómo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What I, and the clan you know as the Soulsmiths use, is a form of magic "
"called Summoning. You've likely heard bits and pieces of it since you "
"started your journey."
msgstr ""
"Lo que usamos yo y el clan que conocéis como los Forjaalmas es una forma de "
"magia llamada Invocación. Seguramente habéis oído retazos de ella desde que "
"empezasteis vuestro viaje."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Summoning is broken into many different disciplines. My clan is gone, but "
"our discipline, clearly, is not."
msgstr ""
"La Invocación se divide en muchas disciplinas distintas. Mi clan ya no "
"existe, pero nuestra disciplina, claramente, sí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What they use is an offshoot of what I use. My people were called "
"Lifebinders. People after us will call it something else."
msgstr ""
"Lo que usan ellos es una rama de lo que uso yo. A mi pueblo lo llamaban los "
"Vinculavidas. Quienes vengan después lo llamarán de otra forma."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I can more-or-less reverse the effects of aging, and I've done so for myself"
" and Era for many... many years."
msgstr ""
"Puedo revertir más o menos los efectos del envejecimiento, y lo he hecho "
"conmigo y con Era durante muchos... muchos años."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What's the book we got from the Abyssal Vault?"
msgstr "¿Qué es el libro que sacamos de la Cámara abisal?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well it's..."
msgstr "Bueno, es..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Go on then."
msgstr "Venga, dilo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Promise not to be mad?"
msgstr "¿Prometéis no enfadaros?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...sure?"
msgstr "...¿vale?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You raided one of the most secure locations in the capital for... what's "
"basically a children's history book."
msgstr ""
"Habéis asaltado uno de los lugares más seguros de la capital por... lo que "
"viene a ser un libro de historia infantil."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Next question. Can you use that summoning magic on yourself? Because you "
"might need to."
msgstr ""
"Siguiente pregunta. ¿Puedes usar esa magia de invocación contigo mismo? "
"Porque puede que la necesites."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You clearly knew parts of what our visions were going to be. You didn't "
"think to tell us THAT?"
msgstr ""
"Está claro que sabías parte de lo que iban a mostrar nuestras visiones. ¿No "
"se te ocurrió contarnos ESO?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's an IMPORTANT children's history book!"
msgstr "¡Es un libro de historia infantil IMPORTANTE!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It details one of the most defining events in our world's history... I... "
"literally cannot tell you what, though. The few of us from... Those times, "
"are magically bound against it."
msgstr ""
"Narra uno de los acontecimientos más decisivos de la historia de nuestro "
"mundo... Yo... literalmente no puedo deciros cuál. Los pocos que quedamos "
"de... aquellos tiempos estamos atados por magia para no revelarlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Era can help you with reading it more than I can, but suffice to say, if you"
" want to learn about the Soulsmiths and what they want to do, this book is "
"as good as you're going to get for now."
msgstr ""
"Era puede ayudaros a leerlo mejor que yo, pero basta con decir que, si "
"queréis saber de los Forjaalmas y de lo que pretenden, este libro es lo "
"mejor que vais a encontrar por ahora."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Why us? For... all of this."
msgstr "...¿Por qué nosotros? Para... todo esto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Era's visions may have holes, and may be hard to interpret at times, but "
"they're never wrong."
msgstr ""
"Las visiones de Era pueden tener lagunas y a veces cuesta interpretarlas, "
"pero nunca se equivocan."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"From what I've seen... I needed to help you. The whole thing with the "
"archery contest, meeting you two... It wasn't an accident."
msgstr ""
"Por lo que he visto... tenía que ayudaros. Todo lo del concurso de tiro con "
"arco, conoceros a vosotros dos... No fue casualidad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, I didn't expect you to try and get yourself shot, but beyond that, all"
" planned out. For what, I cannot say."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, no esperaba que intentaras que te dispararan, pero, aparte de eso, "
"todo estaba planeado. Para qué, no puedo decirlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Right. Magic binding."
msgstr "Claro. Atadura mágica."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Now. This thrall is about as pretty as I can make him. Shall we see if he "
"can take us to Era?"
msgstr ""
"Bien. Este siervo está todo lo presentable que puedo dejarlo. ¿Vemos si "
"puede llevarnos hasta Era?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You caught [Companion Name]'s flinch when Talm said that Era's visions are never wrong. But why? What'd she see? You've tried asking, gently, over the last couple of weeks, but you've hardly gotten anything other than it being 'bad'.\n"
"\n"
"Talm utters a command in a language you cannot understand to the thrall, and it shudders for a moment, before walking off at a leisurely pace. The three of you follow close behind until you get to the main gates of the capital. You flinch as you approach the guards and Talm pulls the thrall between you and him. He takes on a drunken sway and starts slurring gibberish as the guard looks your party over. The woman pinches her nose and remarks that you 'smell like death' and waves you off.\n"
"\n"
"You do your best to wipe off the thrall's blood that leaked through his pilfered robes once you're out of eyeshot, cursing quietly to yourself. The thrall leads you far out of town and out into the countryside. Once you hit the treeline of a nearby forest, Talm curses and releases his command of the thrall, who slumps to the ground. He says he knows where they went.\n"
"\n"
"You're lead to a large stone tower that blends well into the rocky landscape. It once had a large wooden door that now lays splintered in a dozen large chunks on the ground. Talm exclaims that they attacked his 'real' home, and that the security system was set off."
msgstr ""
"Te diste cuenta del respingo de [Companion Name] cuando Talm dijo que las visiones de Era nunca se equivocan. Pero ¿por qué? ¿Qué vio? Has intentado preguntarle, con tacto, durante las últimas semanas, pero apenas has sacado nada más allá de que era «malo».\n"
"\n"
"Talm pronuncia una orden al siervo en un idioma que no entiendes, y este se estremece un momento antes de echar a andar a paso tranquilo. Los tres lo seguís de cerca hasta llegar a las puertas principales de la capital. Te sobresaltas al acercarte a los guardias, y Talm coloca al siervo entre vosotros. Se pone a tambalearse como un borracho y a farfullar tonterías mientras la guardia examina al grupo. La mujer se tapa la nariz, comenta que «apestáis a muerte» y os hace un gesto para que paséis.\n"
"\n"
"Una vez fuera de su vista, haces lo posible por limpiarte la sangre del siervo que se ha filtrado a través de su túnica robada, maldiciendo en voz baja. El siervo os lleva lejos de la ciudad, hacia el campo. Al llegar a la linde de un bosque cercano, Talm maldice y libera al siervo de su orden, que se desploma en el suelo. Dice que sabe adónde fueron.\n"
"\n"
"Os lleva hasta una gran torre de piedra que se funde bien con el paisaje rocoso. Antes tenía una gran puerta de madera que ahora yace hecha astillas en una docena de grandes trozos por el suelo. Talm exclama que han atacado su hogar «de verdad» y que el sistema de seguridad se ha activado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not these again..."
msgstr "Estos otra vez no..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hopefully that's the last of them."
msgstr "Ojalá sean los últimos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Having dodged your way through an impressive array of traps, you slowly made"
" it up to the tower's uppermost floor. Era lays in a pool of blood at the "
"foot of a large arcane telescope, made of a metal you can't even begin to "
"place."
msgstr ""
"Tras esquivar una impresionante serie de trampas, llegaste poco a poco a la "
"planta más alta de la torre. Era yace en un charco de sangre al pie de un "
"gran telescopio arcano, hecho de un metal que no sabrías ni por dónde "
"empezar a identificar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...None of you will live to regret this."
msgstr "...Ninguno de vosotros vivirá para lamentar esto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Seeing Era on the ground, Talm wordlessly launches himself against the group"
" of Soulsmiths occupying the floor, not seeming to pay any mind to whether "
"or not you and [Companion Name] join him. Of course, you follow right "
"behind. Soulsmiths deserve no quarter."
msgstr ""
"Al ver a Era en el suelo, Talm se lanza sin decir palabra contra el grupo de"
" Forjaalmas que ocupa la planta, sin parecer importarle si [Companion Name] "
"y tú lo seguís. Por supuesto, vais justo detrás. Los Forjaalmas no merecen "
"piedad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What does Era wish for us to see?"
msgstr "¿Qué quiere Era que veamos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh... oh my..."
msgstr "Oh... madre mía..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You lower your weapon as your last opponent falls, with [Companion Name] finishing up right after you. Talm pushes a Soulsmith against the wall of the ringed tower and the man brings his hands up in fear. He chokes out a plea for his life before Talm rams his blade into the man's chest and into the stone behind him, pinning him to the wall.\n"
"\n"
"The three of you breathe silently, taking in the sight around you before... a slight cough sounds from over by the telescope. Talm leaves his weapon in the wall and runs over to his wife's body, immediately reaching out to perform... some form of magic on her, like he did with the man back in the shack. You and [Companion Name] turn away from them, leaving the couple to their privacy, or as much as they can have, considering the circumstances."
msgstr ""
"Bajas el arma cuando cae tu último rival, y [Companion Name] termina justo después. Talm empuja a un forjaalmas contra la pared de la torre circular y el hombre levanta las manos aterrado. Suplica por su vida con la voz entrecortada antes de que Talm le hunda la espada en el pecho y en la piedra que hay detrás, clavándolo a la pared.\n"
"\n"
"Los tres respiráis en silencio, asimilando lo que os rodea antes de que... una leve tos suene junto al telescopio. Talm deja el arma en la pared y corre hacia el cuerpo de su esposa, extendiendo de inmediato las manos para realizar... algún tipo de magia sobre ella, como hizo con el hombre en la choza. [Companion Name] y tú os dais la vuelta para dejar a la pareja en la intimidad, o en toda la que pueden tener dadas las circunstancias."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So... me..."
msgstr "Así que... yo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What was that, my love?"
msgstr "¿Qué has dicho, mi amor?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Messy... You have all... Gotten the place so bloody..."
msgstr "Qué desastre... Lo habéis... dejado todo lleno de sangre..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... Yes. Sorry."
msgstr "Yo... Sí. Perdona."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hur... hurry up."
msgstr "Da... date prisa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Sorry dear."
msgstr "Perdona, cariño."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] and you look at each other, grimacing a bit as the following silence is punctuated by the sounds of tearing flesh and sickening gurgles. You feel a bit faint listening to Talm work on his... not dead wife. If one can reverse the effects of aging then perhaps mending wounds falls under that domain as well. You see [Companion Name] shoot a glance in their direction then quickly avert her eyes, clutching her mouth after a quiet heave. You think better of it.\n"
"\n"
"You nearly leap out of your skin when you feel a couple of light taps on your shoulder and come face to face with the incredibly pale visage of Era. Her wounds stitched together, the only remnant of them being the tears in dress from which any number of weapons pierced her. \n"
"\n"
"She welcomes you to her home and starts to apologize for the mess, before then frowning, realizing your part in its current state. The fact that she was on death's door just moments ago seemingly not bothering her in the slightest. If they're truly as old as Talm claims, you wonder how many times someone could have crossed a similar scene.\n"
"\n"
"Era gestures for [Companion Name] and has Talm bring a chair over, to which she slumps in. She runs her hands over the book with fondness, then gives a few directions for adjusting telescope. She invites the both of you to use it."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] y tú os miráis con una mueca mientras el silencio que sigue se ve salpicado por sonidos de carne desgarrándose y gorgoteos nauseabundos. Te mareas un poco al oír a Talm trabajar en su... esposa no muerta. Si se pueden revertir los efectos del envejecimiento, entonces... quizá curar heridas también entre en ese terreno. Ves que [Companion Name] echa un vistazo hacia ellos y aparta enseguida la mirada, tapándose la boca tras una arcada silenciosa. Decides no mirar.\n"
"\n"
"Casi das un salto cuando notas un par de toquecitos en el hombro y te encuentras cara a cara con el rostro increíblemente pálido de Era. Sus heridas están cosidas, y lo único que queda de ellas son los desgarrones del vestido por donde la atravesaron quién sabe cuántas armas. \n"
"\n"
"Te da la bienvenida a su hogar y empieza a disculparse por el desorden, antes de fruncir el ceño al darse cuenta de tu papel en su estado actual. El hecho de que hace un momento estuviera a las puertas de la muerte no parece importarle lo más mínimo. Si de verdad son tan antiguos como afirma Talm, te preguntas cuántas veces habrán vivido una escena parecida.\n"
"\n"
"Era llama con un gesto a [Companion Name] y hace que Talm traiga una silla, en la que se desploma. Pasa las manos por el libro con cariño y luego da algunas indicaciones para ajustar el telescopio. Os invita a ambos a usarlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The stars stretch out before you, incalculable in number. As you peer up at them through Era's telescope, they twist and turn in so many beautiful arrays and patterns you almost want to weep. As you try to commit them to memory, they dance ever so carefully out of reach again and again. You take breaks when the floor beneath you sways like the gentle rocking of a ship at sea. [Companion Name] takes your place in these bits of downtime. You chat here and there with Era and Talm, who both look at you with a degree of fondness that comes off as... almost warm, though the feeling almost feels misplaced.\n"
"\n"
"The sight is punctuated by that of Talm's new thralls, the broken bodies of the Soulsmiths being twisted to work on... repairs and cleanup. The sight is as macabre as it is absurd. A pair of thralls mop up after one another in a circle, each trying to clean the trailing blood from their comrade. You shudder at the sight. When one of the thralls tries to remove Talm's sword from the wall and ends up tearing its arm out of its socket. \n"
"\n"
"You nearly faint. Talm curses softly, and Era simply chuckles. You make note to never get on either of their bad sides. Ever. You know the Soulsmiths are truly wretched and you'd never spill a tear over them, but the level of... flippance that Era and Talm have at seeing their undead bodies lurch about feels unnerving, at least for now.\n"
"\n"
"You rest and recuperate in their home, taking turns with [Companion Name], peering through the telescope and trying to glean insight from the stars. Once the thralls were disposed of and the traps turned off, the tower really was nice. Though, some of the things you saw may sit with you for a long while."
msgstr ""
"Las estrellas se extienden ante ti, incontables. Al contemplarlas a través del telescopio de Era, giran y se retuercen en tantas formaciones y patrones hermosos que casi te dan ganas de llorar. Cuando intentas memorizarlas, bailan con delicadeza fuera de tu alcance una y otra vez. Descansas cuando el suelo se balancea bajo tus pies como el suave vaivén de un barco en el mar. [Companion Name] ocupa tu lugar en esos ratos. Charlas de vez en cuando con Era y Talm, que te miran con un cariño que resulta... casi cálido, aunque la sensación parece casi fuera de lugar.\n"
"\n"
"La escena se ve salpicada por los nuevos siervos de Talm: los cuerpos destrozados de los Forjaalmas, retorcidos para trabajar en... reparaciones y limpieza. El espectáculo es tan macabro como absurdo. Un par de siervos friegan uno detrás del otro en círculo, cada uno intentando limpiar la sangre que va dejando su compañero. Te estremeces al verlo. Cuando uno de los siervos intenta sacar la espada de Talm de la pared y acaba arrancándose el brazo de cuajo, \n"
"\n"
"casi te desmayas. Talm maldice en voz baja y Era se limita a reír entre dientes. Tomas nota de no ponerte nunca en contra de ninguno de los dos. Jamás. Sabes que los Forjaalmas son unos miserables y nunca derramarías una lágrima por ellos, pero la... ligereza con la que Era y Talm ven tambalearse sus cuerpos no muertos resulta inquietante, al menos por ahora.\n"
"\n"
"Descansas y te recuperas en su hogar, turnándote con [Companion Name] para mirar por el telescopio e intentar descifrar las estrellas. Una vez que se deshicieron de los siervos y desactivaron las trampas, la torre resultaba de lo más agradable. Aunque algunas de las cosas que viste quizá te acompañen durante mucho tiempo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Cold Plunge"
msgstr "Baño helado"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The stars have finally shown you what you needed to see. A lone cold point, "
"deep within the mountain range west of the capital. That is your next "
"target."
msgstr ""
"Las estrellas por fin te han mostrado lo que necesitabas ver. Un único punto"
" frío, en lo más profundo de la cordillera al oeste de la capital. Ese es tu"
" próximo objetivo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Melting alone won't do it. We'll need to hack away at the ice, too."
msgstr "Con derretirlo no basta. También tendremos que picar el hielo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think I can just about crack the door open."
msgstr "Creo que ya casi puedo entreabrir la puerta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your head feels fuzzy, as each breath - if you even are still breathing anymore - feels shaky and labored. You've grown far more accustomed to Era's telescope, but it still makes you feel as if something within your very being is shifting after long enough. You can practice astrology without it, but as you've learned through numerous conversations, Era's telescope is special. While Talm's summoning domain is Soul, Era's is knowledge and divination. You can't even begin to imagine what kind of creatures she can bring forth. The smoke and telescope are just two tools that allow her to practice.\n"
"\n"
"And now you have done so as well. Similarly to how you felt with the Sightsmoke, you feel as if you raise from the tower and pass through its walls. You grasp for the shingled roof, but your hands pass through it without so much as grazing it. You careen up into the sky, far beyond the tower and up amongst the clouds. Your body rights itself, and you feel yourself slingshot towards the Broken Pass, then turn north, to an inlet in the mountains covered with frost and snow. As you shoot towards a stone door carved into the cliffside, you close your eyes... and end up back on the floor of the tower.\n"
"\n"
"You are covered in ice, and your teeth chatter violently, but you feel so... so warm."
msgstr ""
"Sientes la cabeza embotada, y cada respiración (si es que aún respiras) es temblorosa y trabajosa. Te has acostumbrado mucho más al telescopio de Era, pero aun así, al cabo de un rato, sientes como si algo dentro de tu propio ser se desplazara. Puedes practicar la astrología sin él, pero, como has aprendido en numerosas conversaciones, el telescopio de Era es especial. Mientras que el dominio de invocación de Talm es el alma, el de Era es el conocimiento y la adivinación. No te imaginas qué clase de criaturas puede invocar. El humo y el telescopio son solo dos herramientas que le permiten practicar.\n"
"\n"
"Y ahora tú también lo has hecho. Igual que con el humo vidente, sientes que te elevas desde la torre y atraviesas sus muros. Intentas agarrarte al tejado de tejas, pero tus manos lo atraviesan sin siquiera rozarlo. Te elevas a toda velocidad hacia el cielo, mucho más allá de la torre, entre las nubes. Tu cuerpo se endereza y sientes que te lanzan como con una honda hacia Broken Pass, para luego girar al norte, hacia una ensenada entre las montañas cubierta de escarcha y nieve. Mientras vuelas hacia una puerta de piedra tallada en el acantilado, cierras los ojos... y acabas de nuevo en el suelo de la torre.\n"
"\n"
"El hielo te cubre y te castañetean los dientes con violencia, pero sientes tanto... tanto calor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Welcome back, child."
msgstr "Ya estás de vuelta, criatura."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Player Name]! Are you okay? You were here, there was a flash of light, and "
"now you're..."
msgstr ""
"¡[Player Name]! ¿Estás bien? Estabas aquí, hubo un destello de luz y ahora "
"eres..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A block of ice?"
msgstr "¿Un bloque de hielo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...yeah."
msgstr "...sí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I know where we need to go."
msgstr "Sé adónde tenemos que ir."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't know why we need to go there, but I know we do."
msgstr "No sé por qué tenemos que ir allí, pero sé que tenemos que hacerlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You think we'll finally be able to read our children's book if we go risk "
"our lives somewhere?"
msgstr ""
"¿Crees que por fin podremos leer nuestro libro infantil si vamos a jugarnos "
"la vida a algún sitio?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think so. And... so much more, possibly. You interested?"
msgstr "Creo que sí. Y... mucho más, quizá. ¿Te interesa?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Of course I am!"
msgstr "¡Pues claro!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You'll finally be leaving us behind, hm?"
msgstr "Por fin vais a dejarnos atrás, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Aw. Are you feeling sentimental, dear?"
msgstr "Oh. ¿Te estás poniendo sentimental, cariño?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, they did help me win that competition."
msgstr "Bueno, me ayudaron a ganar aquella competición."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wasn't your win already foretold?"
msgstr "¿No estaba ya predicha tu victoria?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well yes, but it was foretold that I'd win because you two helped!"
msgstr ""
"Pues sí, ¡pero estaba predicho que ganaría porque vosotros dos me "
"ayudasteis!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And look at us now."
msgstr "Y míranos ahora."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Was there something in those visions about... using a thrall to serve me "
"breakfast in bed?"
msgstr ""
"¿Había algo en esas visiones sobre... usar un siervo para servirme el "
"desayuno en la cama?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "No, that was a Talm original."
msgstr "No, eso fue un original de Talm."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I know you two are rather squeamish, but you'll be seeing a lot more death "
"before you're through this all."
msgstr ""
"Sé que sois bastante aprensivos, pero vais a ver mucha más muerte antes de "
"terminar con todo esto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't mind corpses, or even making a few myself. But when they show up "
"with a platter of bacon, I might just lose my appetite."
msgstr ""
"No me importan los cadáveres, ni siquiera fabricar unos cuantos yo misma. "
"Pero cuando aparecen con una bandeja de beicon, igual se me quita el "
"apetito."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Era and Talm laugh at that, while you and [Companion Name] may feel a bit more genuinely about the situation. Nevertheless, your goodbyes are heartfelt. The two of them wish you well on your travels, and you get the feeling that this is the last of them you'll see for quite some time.\n"
"\n"
"You and [Companion Name] head west, stopping in a small town by the name of Riverbend to resupply, then make the trek north, to what the locals call Rimeriver Crevice. The place is an uncharacteristically cold bit of land that stretches far into the mountains with 'not much of note'.\n"
"\n"
"You are glad you stocked up, as green, grassy hillocks turn to freezing glaciers and rolling snow dunes over the course of hours. There's doubtlessly something unnatural about the weather, as even you can tell that the sleet is magically enhanced. Each flake seems to chill you to the bone. Your bundled forms eventually reach the doorway you saw, etched into the cliffside, shielded from the weather... mostly. The door itself has immense braziers on either side, and seems to be frozen shut. You wager a guess that it needs to be thawed."
msgstr ""
"Era y Talm se ríen, mientras que [Companion Name] y tú quizá os lo toméis algo más en serio. Aun así, las despedidas son sinceras. Os desean suerte en vuestros viajes, y tienes la sensación de que no los volverás a ver en bastante tiempo.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] y tú partís hacia el oeste, paráis en un pueblecito llamado Riverbend para reabasteceros y luego emprendéis la travesía hacia el norte, a lo que los lugareños llaman Rimeriver Crevice. El lugar es una franja de tierra inusualmente fría que se adentra en las montañas sin «gran cosa que destacar».\n"
"\n"
"Te alegras de haberte aprovisionado, porque en cuestión de horas las verdes colinas de hierba dan paso a glaciares helados y ondulantes dunas de nieve. Sin duda, este clima tiene algo de antinatural, porque hasta tú notas que el aguanieve está potenciada por magia. Cada copo parece helarte hasta los huesos. Vuestras figuras abrigadas llegan por fin a la entrada que viste, tallada en el acantilado y resguardada del temporal... casi del todo. La puerta tiene enormes braseros a ambos lados y parece congelada. Te aventuras a suponer que hay que descongelarla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Good morning?"
msgstr "¿Buenos días?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Good night."
msgstr "Buenas noches."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The ice melts agonizingly slowly, but eventually, with some prodding with your pickaxes between the two stone doors, you're able to push your way inside. Inside the cave is comparatively balmy. The interior is well-furnished, but certainly abandoned. Many of the doorways along the single stone hall you travel are shut and bound by some form of magic that reminds you of the Abyssal Vault, but... much, much older. \n"
"\n"
"The few rooms that are open seem to have once been living quarters, built more for capacity than for luxury. However, there's not a single hint of where anyone could have gone. No bodies. No messages.\n"
"\n"
"You and [Companion Name] push further inside, to a room at the end of the hall that opens up into a large open cavern that seems naturally made. You walk up and bump [Companion Name] with your shoulder as you head deeper into the room."
msgstr ""
"El hielo se derrite con una lentitud exasperante, pero al final, haciendo palanca con los picos entre las dos puertas de piedra, conseguís abriros paso. El interior de la cueva es templado en comparación. Está bien amueblado, pero sin duda abandonado. Muchas de las puertas del único pasillo de piedra que recorréis están cerradas y selladas con algún tipo de magia que te recuerda a la de la Cámara abisal, pero... mucho, mucho más antigua. \n"
"\n"
"Las pocas habitaciones abiertas parecen haber sido viviendas, construidas más para la capacidad que para el lujo. Sin embargo, no hay ni rastro de adónde pudo ir nadie. Ni cuerpos. Ni mensajes.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] y tú avanzáis hasta una sala al final del pasillo que da a una gran caverna abierta de aspecto natural. Te acercas y le das un golpecito con el hombro a [Companion Name] mientras os adentráis en la sala."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It feels like it's been a bit, since it was just you and I, doing something "
"for ourselves."
msgstr ""
"Parece que hace tiempo que no estábamos solos tú y yo, haciendo algo por "
"nosotros mismos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I would never have guessed we'd have gotten wrapped up in something so... "
"much bigger than ourselves."
msgstr ""
"Nunca habría imaginado que acabaríamos metidos en algo tan... muchísimo más "
"grande que nosotros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Neither would I. But it's cool, travelling the world together, no? We always"
" talked about how we wanted to."
msgstr ""
"Yo tampoco. Pero mola, eso de viajar juntos por el mundo, ¿no? Siempre "
"hablábamos de lo mucho que queríamos hacerlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Maybe under different circumstances, but yeah. It's hard to think of just "
"how much has happened in so little time."
msgstr ""
"Quizá en otras circunstancias, pero sí. Cuesta pensar en todo lo que ha "
"pasado en tan poco tiempo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You can say that again. I missed this."
msgstr "Y que lo digas. Echaba de menos esto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"When this is all over, let's do a bit of travelling under better "
"circumstances, hm?"
msgstr ""
"Cuando todo esto acabe, viajemos un poco en mejores circunstancias, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'd drink to that. Where would you want to go?"
msgstr "Brindo por eso. ¿Adónde te gustaría ir?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Somewhere where it doesn't feel like something is going to eat me or stab me"
" every couple of minutes. How about-"
msgstr ""
"A algún sitio donde no parezca que algo va a comerme o apuñalarme cada dos "
"minutos. ¿Qué tal...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With that, a loud rumbling roar tears through the cavern and sends the both of you to your knees. You clamp your hands to your ears and turn your head up to see the call's source. A yeti. The shaggy beast lumbers over, its blue knuckles dragging across the floor as it seemingly wakes from a slumber that must have spanned countless years.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] gives you one of her signature glares, as if your words brought the creature into being. So much for wishful thinking."
msgstr ""
"En ese momento, un fuerte rugido retumbante desgarra la caverna y os hace caer de rodillas a los dos. Te tapas los oídos con las manos y alzas la cabeza para ver de dónde viene. Un yeti. La peluda bestia avanza pesadamente, arrastrando sus nudillos azules por el suelo, como si despertara de un letargo que debe de haber durado incontables años.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] te lanza una de sus típicas miradas fulminantes, como si tus palabras hubieran hecho aparecer a la criatura. Adiós a las ilusiones."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The beast staggers back with a cry as your blows connect with its hard flesh. It falls to the ground with a mighty crash, and slumps back against the cavern wall. It releases a breath and begins to... fade away to crystals of ice that melt shortly afterward. Whatever the beast was, it wasn't natural. As you begin to look over the murals etched and painted into the wall, you feel quite sure of that assumption.\n"
"\n"
"The murals depict the group that once inhabited the cavern. Little blue figures of people living in a beautiful blue forest. Then... the forest burning due to some unknown red assailants riding on similarly colored creatures. After that, there are far fewer blue figures in a blackened forest. The numbers dwindle further and further with each section of wall. Until the blue figures leave the charred forest. The murals show them travelling far... very far. Almost half the cavern wall depicts them travelling from one place to another, in all manner of places. They settle for short periods of time, with each move always predicated by a clash with some new color of figure. Brown, grey, green, red, orange, and even a lighter color blue towards the end. These figures are accompanied by beasts. All drawn simply in nature, but clearly terrifying to those who lived here. You catch yourself wiping your eyes more than once as you spend over an hour trying to follow their story.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, in the last tenth of the wall, it shows the figures... finding what you presume to be this place. They find a book. They create their own creatures. The figures leave the wall and travel across the floor, to spires of ice that jut out from the ground, one nearly touching the ceiling.\n"
"\n"
"You realize, the center of the room looks... similar to a page of the book you cannot read. You lay it out and [Companion Name] holds her lantern overhead as you trace out places that line up. Two pages of the book, when lined up with the central pillar of ice, resemble the eastern portion of the continent. And within that map, a shining tower lays just off the coast. Comparing it to current maps, it'd be far north of the capital. Your next destination.\n"
"\n"
"You spare a last glance to the figures on the ground, crowded around the spire of ice. It's the last of their journey, none left their last destination. You can only imagine what the spire represents, but it's a mystery for another time."
msgstr ""
"La bestia retrocede tambaleándose con un grito cuando tus golpes impactan en su dura carne. Cae al suelo con un estruendo y se desploma contra la pared de la caverna. Suelta un último aliento y empieza a... desvanecerse en cristales de hielo que se derriten poco después. Fuera lo que fuera la bestia, no era natural. Cuando empiezas a examinar los murales grabados y pintados en la pared, te convences bastante de esa suposición.\n"
"\n"
"Los murales muestran al grupo que habitó la caverna. Pequeñas figuras azules de personas que viven en un precioso bosque azul. Luego... el bosque arde por culpa de unos atacantes rojos desconocidos que montan criaturas del mismo color. Después, hay muchas menos figuras azules en un bosque ennegrecido. Su número mengua más y más con cada tramo de pared. Hasta que las figuras azules abandonan el bosque calcinado. Los murales las muestran viajando lejos... muy lejos. Casi la mitad de la pared de la caverna las representa yendo de un sitio a otro, por todo tipo de lugares. Se asientan durante breves periodos, y cada mudanza viene siempre precedida de un choque con figuras de un nuevo color. Marrones, grises, verdes, rojas, naranjas e incluso de un azul más claro hacia el final. A estas figuras las acompañan bestias. Todas dibujadas con sencillez, pero claramente aterradoras para quienes vivieron aquí. Te sorprendes secándote los ojos más de una vez mientras pasas más de una hora intentando seguir su historia.\n"
"\n"
"Por último, en la décima parte final de la pared, muestra a las figuras... encontrando lo que supones que es este lugar. Encuentran un libro. Crean sus propias criaturas. Las figuras dejan la pared y recorren el suelo hasta unas agujas de hielo que brotan del suelo, una de ellas casi tocando el techo.\n"
"\n"
"Te das cuenta de que el centro de la sala se parece... a una página del libro que no puedes leer. Lo extiendes y [Companion Name] sostiene su farol en alto mientras trazas los puntos que coinciden. Dos páginas del libro, alineadas con el pilar central de hielo, representan la parte oriental del continente. Y dentro de ese mapa, una torre resplandeciente se alza justo frente a la costa. Comparándolo con los mapas actuales, estaría muy al norte de la capital. Tu próximo destino.\n"
"\n"
"Echas un último vistazo a las figuras del suelo, reunidas alrededor de la aguja de hielo. Es el final de su viaje: ninguna abandonó su último destino. Solo puedes imaginar qué representa la aguja, pero es un misterio para otro momento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 60[/color] "
"[b][u]Miniboss[/u][/b]"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar a un [b][u]minijefe[/u][/b] de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de "
"combate 60[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ship Shape"
msgstr "A son de mar"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"In their quest to find the shining tower shown to them by the history book "
"stolen from the Ivory Athenaeum, [Player Name] and [Companion Name] find "
"themselves travelling far north of the capital, to a lonely little fishing "
"village tucked into the coast."
msgstr ""
"En su búsqueda de la torre resplandeciente que les mostró el libro de "
"historia robado del Ateneo de marfil, [Player Name] y [Companion Name] "
"viajan muy al norte de la capital, hasta una pequeña y solitaria aldea de "
"pescadores escondida en la costa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Head inland enough, should be able to grow something."
msgstr "Si vamos lo bastante tierra adentro, deberíamos poder cultivar algo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That should be enough. Let's see our vessel."
msgstr "Con eso debería bastar. Veamos nuestra embarcación."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"An old cobbled road takes you and your companion far north, just outside of a town by the name of Tidebreak. The population is said to be rather reclusive, mostly preferring to keep to their own and subsist on what they can fish up. The sea breeze goes from refreshing to... almost sour the further north you get. You get why not many people decided to live up this way, and question the motives of those that do. You push on ahead as the sun begins to set.\n"
"\n"
"The town itself is... quaint. You feel eyes on you everywhere you go, and kids are pulled inside ahead of your path. You find yourself on the coast, where a lone young man works a length of rope, hardly sparing you a glance. Another man, who almost seems like he could be his brother, looks on and even gives you a smile, which you almost find weirder. You try your chances with the rope worker first."
msgstr ""
"Un viejo camino empedrado os lleva a ti y a tu compañera muy al norte, justo a las afueras de un pueblo llamado Tidebreak. Dicen que sus habitantes son bastante huraños: prefieren no mezclarse con nadie y subsistir con lo que pescan. La brisa marina pasa de refrescante a... casi agria cuanto más al norte llegas. Entiendes por qué poca gente decidió vivir por aquí, y te preguntas qué motivos tienen quienes lo hacen. Sigues adelante mientras el sol empieza a ponerse.\n"
"\n"
"El pueblo en sí es... pintoresco. Sientes miradas sobre ti allá donde vas, y meten a los niños en casa antes de que pases. Llegas a la costa, donde un joven solitario trabaja un tramo de cuerda sin apenas dedicarte una mirada. Otro hombre, que casi podría ser su hermano, observa e incluso te sonríe, cosa que te resulta casi más rara. Pruebas suerte primero con el de la cuerda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A pleasure."
msgstr "Un placer."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Aye. I'm sure."
msgstr "Sí. Seguro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You've got a lovely little town here, might I say."
msgstr "Tenéis un pueblecito precioso, si me permites decirlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ya' might, if ya' blind."
msgstr "Lo dirás si estás ciego."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Fortunate enough to still have my vision..."
msgstr "Por suerte aún conservo la vista..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Friendly lot, you are, hm?"
msgstr "Qué simpáticos sois, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh, leave the poor boy be. Joshry's always grumpy when he gets shown up at "
"the Hauling."
msgstr ""
"Oh, deja en paz al pobre chico. Joshry siempre se pone de mal humor cuando "
"lo dejan en evidencia en el Arrastre."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Don't not. "
msgstr "Qué va, no. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Yes ya do, and the rest of 'em too."
msgstr "Claro que sí, y los demás también."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Shove off, Rommard."
msgstr "Lárgate, Rommard."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The what now?"
msgstr "¿El qué?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The Hauling. Weekly little get together when all us sailors show off "
"whatever we managed to scrape off the ocean floor."
msgstr ""
"El Arrastre. Una reunioncita semanal en la que los marineros enseñamos lo "
"que hemos conseguido rascar del fondo del mar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not to inner-esting less you's an academic."
msgstr "No es mu' intresante, a menos que seas un académico."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That's why everyone here cares so much. Bunch of scholars, we are."
msgstr "Por eso aquí a todos les importa tanto. Somos un montón de eruditos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Bet our findings will get added to that big ivory building in the capital, "
"soon enough. Should go take a look at it yourself someday, real purdy."
msgstr ""
"Seguro que nuestros hallazgos acabarán en ese gran edificio de marfil de la "
"capital dentro de nada. Deberíais ir a verlo algún día, es mu' bonito."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You could say we're... familiar."
msgstr "Digamos que nos... suena."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How bout yourself, stranger?"
msgstr "¿Y tú qué, forastero?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, I'm quite over it all, myself. No one here seems to care much about "
"pulling up ten corpses for every half rusted spoon they can dredge out of "
"the ocean."
msgstr ""
"Pues yo ya estoy bastante harto de todo esto. A nadie aquí parece importarle"
" sacar diez cadáveres por cada cuchara medio oxidada que logran dragar del "
"océano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "No one but yours truly. Can't stand it."
msgstr "A nadie salvo a un servidor. No lo soporto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Then why do you?"
msgstr "¿Y entonces por qué lo haces?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Tidebreak look like a place where we've got an abundance of career "
"diversity?"
msgstr "¿Tiene Tidebreak pinta de ser un sitio con mucha variedad de oficios?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Everyone that's been here has been doing what they do for more years than "
"ol' Josh and I put together."
msgstr ""
"Todo el que vive aquí lleva haciendo lo suyo más años que el viejo Josh y yo"
" juntos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Opening comes up when they kick the bucket."
msgstr "Solo queda un puesto libre cuando alguien estira la pata."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Fancy making some gold by ferrying us around, then?"
msgstr ""
"¿Te apetece ganar algo de oro llevándonos de un lado a otro, entonces?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What, you two come here for a bita sightseeing?"
msgstr "¿Qué pasa, habéis venido a hacer un poco de turismo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Close. We want to go to the island way off the coast."
msgstr "Casi. Queremos ir a la isla que está mar adentro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...oh. We don't go other there. Gloomstone's a ba-"
msgstr "...oh. Nosotros no vamos por allí. Gloomstone es un..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Now now now, I'm sure our friends here are well aware of the risks."
msgstr ""
"Vamos, vamos, seguro que nuestros amigos saben bien los riesgos que corren."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Just a bit of choppy water n' the like, of course. Couple beasties if you're"
" tasty. Nothin' they can't handle."
msgstr ""
"Solo un poco de mar picada y cosas así, claro. Un par de bichos si estáis "
"sabrosos. Nada que no puedan manejar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But tell you what. You can have my boat, if you do me a lil' favor."
msgstr ""
"Pero os diré una cosa. Podéis quedaros mi barca si me hacéis un favorcito."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Rommard goes into detail about grand visions for the town. All the little things he wants to do to 'give back'. Neither you nor [Companion Name] buy it for a second, of course, but you feel as though the man in front of you is the best option you'll get. As dire as that sounds.\n"
"\n"
"His ire for having to fish out Gods know what from the sea seems true, as he'd rather work the land and earn his keep that way. Only issue, Tidebreak has never bothered trying to trade for seeds. 'The sea will provide' is something you hear around, often.'"
msgstr ""
"Rommard se explaya sobre sus grandes planes para el pueblo. Todas las cosillas que quiere hacer para «devolver algo». Ni [Companion Name] ni tú os lo creéis ni por un segundo, claro, pero sientes que el hombre que tienes delante es la mejor opción que vas a tener. Por muy lamentable que suene.\n"
"\n"
"Su rechazo a sacar del mar sabe Dios qué parece sincero, ya que preferiría trabajar la tierra y ganarse el pan así. El único problema es que en Tidebreak nunca se han molestado en intentar comerciar con semillas. «El mar proveerá» es algo que se oye a menudo por ahí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll need to make something that'll help it weather the rocky shore."
msgstr "Tendré que fabricar algo que la ayude a resistir la costa rocosa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This ought to do it. Let's see how [Companion Name] is coming along."
msgstr "Esto debería servir. Veamos cómo le va a [Companion Name]."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] and you plant row after row of crops, then run through the details of crop rotations and how to care for seedlings. To his credit, Rommard does actually pay attention and even takes some pretty extensive notes. He does leave the two of you do actually do all the work, though.\n"
"\n"
"Once you're done, Rommard jumps upright and brings you back over to the docks, detailing how all deals are final, and that his boat's a bit of a fixer-upper, but will get you to the island. Probably.\n"
"\n"
"The only 'boat' left on the docks could be mistaken for a wreck that someone tethered to the pier. Rommard presents it with a flourish, then turns on his heel, setting off into town. He calls out to you one last time."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] y tú plantáis hilera tras hilera de cultivos y luego le explicáis los detalles de la rotación de cultivos y cómo cuidar los plantones. Hay que reconocer que Rommard presta atención de verdad e incluso toma notas bastante detalladas. Eso sí, os deja a vosotros dos todo el trabajo.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando termináis, Rommard se levanta de un salto y os lleva de vuelta al muelle, explicando que todos los tratos son definitivos y que su barca necesita algún que otro arreglo, pero que os llevará hasta la isla. Probablemente.\n"
"\n"
"La única «barca» que queda en el muelle podría confundirse con un pecio que alguien hubiera amarrado al embarcadero. Rommard os la presenta con una floritura, luego da media vuelta y se marcha hacia el pueblo. Os grita una última vez."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The F.V. Not My Problem Anymore!"
msgstr "¡El B. P. Ya No Es Mi Problema!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Enjoy!"
msgstr "¡Que la disfrutéis!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That slimy little..."
msgstr "Será canalla el muy..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's not... that bad. Is it?"
msgstr "No está... tan mal. ¿No?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Player Name], it might be easier to start from scratch. I'm shocked the "
"thing's even floating to begin with."
msgstr ""
"[Player Name], puede que sea más fácil empezar de cero. Me asombra que esta "
"cosa siquiera flote."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's just... do our best."
msgstr "Hagamos... lo que podamos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Judging by the coastline, the island's gonna be rocky. And, I don't fancy "
"paddling to a place I can't even see."
msgstr ""
"A juzgar por la costa, la isla va a ser rocosa. Y no me apetece remar hasta "
"un sitio que ni siquiera veo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll work on a keel and a sail."
msgstr "Yo me encargo de una quilla y una vela."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I'll see what I can do about getting this thing... sea-worthy."
msgstr "...Veré qué puedo hacer para que esta cosa sea... navegable."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That's the spirit."
msgstr "Ese es el espíritu."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] grumbles to herself and begins prodding at the boat. It "
"drops concerningly low under the water when she puts her weight on it, which"
" elicits a string of curses."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] refunfuña para sí y empieza a toquetear la barca. Se hunde "
"de forma preocupante bajo el agua cuando apoya su peso en ella, lo que "
"provoca una retahíla de maldiciones."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It can't be that hard, can it?"
msgstr "No puede ser tan difícil, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It was."
msgstr "Lo fue."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You arrive at the docks to see something akin to a miracle. The boat - if "
"you could even call it that - has been worked into a proper skiff. It wasn't"
" fancy, but it looked like it could support a couple of people and make it "
"more than two minutes off the shore without capsizing, which is leagues "
"better than it used to be. [Companion Name] beams with pride."
msgstr ""
"Llegas al muelle y ves algo parecido a un milagro. La barca (si es que se le"
" podía llamar así) se ha convertido en un esquife como es debido. No era "
"nada lujoso, pero parecía capaz de llevar a un par de personas y aguantar "
"más de dos minutos lejos de la orilla sin volcar, lo cual es muchísimo mejor"
" que antes. [Companion Name] sonríe orgullosa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How's this?"
msgstr "¿Qué te parece?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't know how you made it down to the capital and bought a proper boat, "
"but I'm glad you did!"
msgstr ""
"No sé cómo has conseguido ir hasta la capital y comprar una barca de verdad,"
" ¡pero me alegro de que lo hicieras!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As if I was going to let that gross little creature pull one over on us. "
"He'll be begging for this boat back when we're done."
msgstr ""
"Como si fuera a dejar que ese bicho asqueroso se la colara. Nos suplicará "
"que le devolvamos la barca cuando terminemos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Start thinking of a name, hm?"
msgstr "Ve pensando un nombre, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Spite is quite the motivator, ain't it?"
msgstr "El rencor motiva lo suyo, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The two of you get to work, fitting the keel to the boat. It takes ages, "
"replacing the scrap metal that used to serve the same purpose. Once the "
"worst of it is over, [Companion Name] waves you off, telling you to get to "
"weaving or knitting or whatever you need to do for creating a sail."
msgstr ""
"Los dos os ponéis manos a la obra y encajáis la quilla en la barca. Lleva "
"una eternidad sustituir la chatarra que antes cumplía esa función. Una vez "
"superado lo peor, [Companion Name] te despide con un gesto y te dice que te "
"pongas a tejer, a hacer punto o a lo que sea que necesites para crear una "
"vela."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You bring you sail to the dock and find [Companion Name] floating in the water, treating the boat with what you presume to be waterproofing. You set the sail on the ground and help haul them out of the brine, to which they shake like a dog and get you drenched. You threaten to shove them in, so they wrap their arms around you and threaten to haul you both back in. You shove them off and roll your eyes, to which they give one of the first genuine laughs you've heard from them in a long while.\n"
"\n"
"Why they decided that smelling like stale water and rotting wood was their happy place, you may never know, but you can't help but smile after seeing them happy. The two of you fit the sail to your skiff and sit on the dock, admiring your handiwork. You each carve your name into its railing, and give it a firm pat. It's ready for its journey. Are you?"
msgstr ""
"Llevas tu vela al muelle y encuentras a [Companion Name] flotando en el agua, tratando la barca con lo que supones que es impermeabilizante. Dejas la vela en el suelo y la ayudas a salir del agua salada, tras lo cual se sacude como un perro y te empapa. La amenazas con tirarla al agua, así que te rodea con los brazos y amenaza con arrastraros a los dos de vuelta. Te la quitas de encima y pones los ojos en blanco, y ella suelta una de las primeras carcajadas sinceras que le has oído en mucho tiempo.\n"
"\n"
"Por qué ha decidido que oler a agua estancada y madera podrida es su lugar feliz, quizá nunca lo sepas, pero no puedes evitar sonreír al verla contenta. Los dos colocáis la vela en vuestro esquife y os sentáis en el muelle a admirar vuestro trabajo. Cada uno graba su nombre en la barandilla y le da una palmadita firme. Está lista para su viaje. ¿Y tú?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"All signs point to Gloomstone, and you're as ready as you'll ever be. It's "
"time to learn what the Soulsmiths are after, or sink somewhere far off the "
"coast."
msgstr ""
"Todas las señales apuntan a Gloomstone, y nunca vas a estar más a punto. Es "
"hora de descubrir qué buscan los Forjaalmas, o de hundirte en algún lugar "
"lejos de la costa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#. Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Astrology (Following stars through rocks)"
msgstr "Astrología (seguir las estrellas entre las rocas)"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Glass shatters as you break a bottle of wine over the ship's bow. [Companion Name] holds her steady as you jump aboard, cutting the rope loose and gracefully landing on the deck, your momentum carrying the boat out into the water. The sheepish townsfolk of Tidebreak silently watch as you set off, several of them actually tracing marks of good fortune in the air. You're pleasantly surprised.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you move about the skiff, setting the sail and getting it as ready as you can to sail."
msgstr ""
"El cristal estalla cuando rompes una botella de vino contra la proa del barco. [Companion Name] lo sujeta firme mientras saltas a bordo, cortas la cuerda y aterrizas con elegancia en la cubierta, y tu impulso lleva la barca mar adentro. Los tímidos lugareños de Tidebreak os observan en silencio mientras zarpáis, y varios de ellos incluso trazan en el aire señales de buena fortuna. Te llevas una grata sorpresa.\n"
"\n"
"Los dos os movéis por el esquife, izando la vela y preparándolo todo lo posible para navegar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Guess they don't want to haul any fresh bodies out of the water, hm?"
msgstr ""
"Supongo que no quieren tener que sacar cadáveres frescos del agua, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's anyone's guess. Maybe Rommard put in a good word for us?"
msgstr "Vete a saber. ¿Quizá Rommard habló bien de nosotros?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's probably your thing."
msgstr "Seguramente es cosa tuya."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Nice thought, though."
msgstr "Pero es un bonito detalle."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So. How many days of stuff do we got?"
msgstr "Bueno. ¿Para cuántos días tenemos provisiones?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A week, at least. I really hope it doesn't take that long though."
msgstr ""
"Una semana, como mínimo. Aunque espero de verdad que no tardemos tanto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I hope the tower is actually out there."
msgstr "Espero que la torre esté ahí de verdad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The cavern was fine, sure. But this is a bit more... hostile of an "
"environment."
msgstr ""
"La caverna estaba bien, vale. Pero este entorno es un poco más... hostil."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll see when we get there!"
msgstr "¡Ya lo veremos cuando lleguemos!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...if we get there."
msgstr "...si llegamos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'lllllll get there."
msgstr "Llegareeeeemos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...In one piece is a maybe."
msgstr "...Lo de llegar enteros ya es otro cantar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You two chat back and forth, enjoying the pretty peaceful trip. The shore slowly fades further... and further... and further away, until it's just the two of you gliding across the dark blue water. You're long past the point of being able to swim back to shore. Even without your gear on, the water is cold, and hypothermia would set in long before you made it even a tenth of the way back, assuming the current was cooperating with you.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you catch sleep in waves, each trading off, hoping that you're vaguely headed in the right direction. From what you were able to find, Gloomstone is... quite large but even still, half a day into sailing, you start to wonder if you missed it, or if a children's book in a dead language may have not been the best reference material.\n"
"\n"
"You awake to [Companion Name] calling for you. Something is ahead. A lot of somethings. Giant pillars jut from the icy waters like fingers of stone that threaten to pull you into the depths. [Companion Name] mans the sails, and pleads for you to get them through this safely. With the pillars being barely lit by the moon, you turn to the stars."
msgstr ""
"Charláis sin parar, disfrutando del viaje tan tranquilo. La costa se aleja poco a poco... más... y más... hasta que solo quedáis vosotros dos deslizándoos sobre el agua azul oscuro. Hace mucho que pasasteis el punto en el que podríais volver a nado. Incluso sin el equipo puesto, el agua está fría, y la hipotermia llegaría mucho antes de recorrer siquiera una décima parte del camino de vuelta, suponiendo que la corriente colaborara.\n"
"\n"
"Dormís por turnos, relevándoos, con la esperanza de ir más o menos en la dirección correcta. Por lo que pudisteis averiguar, Gloomstone es... bastante grande, pero aun así, tras medio día navegando, empiezas a preguntarte si os la habéis pasado, o si un libro infantil en una lengua muerta quizá no era el mejor material de consulta.\n"
"\n"
"Te despierta [Companion Name] llamándote. Hay algo más adelante. Muchos algos. Pilares gigantescos brotan de las aguas heladas como dedos de piedra que amenazan con arrastraros a las profundidades. [Companion Name] se encarga de las velas y te suplica que os saques de esta sanos y salvos. Con los pilares apenas iluminados por la luna, recurres a las estrellas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think we're doing them a favor."
msgstr "Creo que les estamos haciendo un favor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Rest easy."
msgstr "Descansad en paz."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your boat bumps and scrapes against the rocks, and you're glad you spent so long forging its keel. Wind whips at the sail, pulling the two of you through the stone spires at a breakneck pace. While nothing like using Era's telescope, your skills in astrology prove fruitful, guiding you through the pillars relatively unscathed.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you float further and further into the cluster of rocks until you can make out... land. You scrape along the shore a bit harder than you're comfortable with, but the two of you and your boat seem to be intact. [Companion Name] shouts with joy and nervous energy leaving her body."
msgstr ""
"Tu barca choca y roza contra las rocas, y te alegras de haber dedicado tanto tiempo a forjar su quilla. El viento azota la vela y os arrastra entre las agujas de piedra a una velocidad de vértigo. Aunque no se parece en nada a usar el telescopio de Era, tus habilidades de astrología dan fruto y os guían entre los pilares casi sin un rasguño.\n"
"\n"
"Los dos avanzáis cada vez más hacia el interior del grupo de rocas hasta que distinguís... tierra. Rozáis la orilla con algo más de fuerza de la que os gustaría, pero vosotros dos y la barca parecéis intactos. [Companion Name] grita de alegría mientras la tensión nerviosa abandona su cuerpo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh by the Gods we made it! I can't believe it."
msgstr "¡Oh, por los dioses, lo hemos conseguido! No me lo puedo creer."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "By the Gods? Not used to you referring to them."
msgstr "¿Por los dioses? No suelo oírte mencionarlos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We've been talking with two immortals that play with the dead and fighting "
"against a force that creates monsters from darkness."
msgstr ""
"Hemos estado hablando con dos inmortales que juegan con los muertos y "
"luchando contra una fuerza que crea monstruos a partir de la oscuridad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We fought a golbin horde and travelled across most of the continent. "
msgstr ""
"Hemos luchado contra una horda golbin y hemos recorrido casi todo el "
"continente. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We've saved dozens of people in our travels, and now, we just pulled off one"
" of the most miraculous feats of sailing I've ever seen or heard of."
msgstr ""
"Hemos salvado a decenas de personas en nuestros viajes y ahora acabamos de "
"lograr una de las hazañas de navegación más milagrosas que he visto u oído "
"jamás."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We live in interesting times. If the Gods just so happened to pop out of the"
" sea and ask us for tea, I'd call that a boring day, at this point."
msgstr ""
"Vivimos tiempos interesantes. Si a los dioses les diera por salir del mar e "
"invitarnos a un té, a estas alturas lo llamaría un día aburrido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We... really did make it. That was some fine steering you did."
msgstr "De verdad... lo hemos conseguido. Has llevado el timón de maravilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You're the one that pulled it out of the stars. You pointed, I moved. Let's "
"just call it a joint effort, eh?"
msgstr ""
"Tú eres quien lo sacó de las estrellas. Tú señalabas y yo me movía. Digamos "
"que ha sido un trabajo en equipo, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You nod and give out a shout of your own, happy to have your feet on dry land. You anchor the boat and pull it as far ashore as you can. The skiff is large, and the moment the majority of it leaves the water, you can't pull it any further.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you grab what you need and head inland. One spire stands out amongst them all, and this one is much larger than the rest. After a small trek, you enter into the old tower, its doors surprisingly open, as if something was waiting for you. And once you're inside, you realize... something is. Piles of bodies shift towards you. It reminds you of Talm's thralls on a much larger and more horrific scale. The amalgamations of flesh and metal twist and moan in horrific fashion, and doubtlessly hostile intent."
msgstr ""
"Asientes y sueltas un grito tú también, feliz de pisar tierra firme. Anclas la barca y la arrastras tan lejos de la orilla como puedes. El esquife es grande, y en cuanto la mayor parte sale del agua, ya no puedes moverlo más.\n"
"\n"
"Los dos cogéis lo que necesitáis y os adentráis en la isla. Una aguja destaca entre todas, mucho más grande que las demás. Tras una breve caminata, entráis en la vieja torre, cuyas puertas están sorprendentemente abiertas, como si algo os estuviera esperando. Y una vez dentro, te das cuenta de que... algo os espera. Montones de cuerpos se desplazan hacia vosotros. Te recuerdan a los siervos de Talm, pero a una escala mucho mayor y más horrible. Las amalgamas de carne y metal se retuercen y gimen de forma espantosa, sin duda con intenciones hostiles."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This feels... right."
msgstr "Esto parece... correcto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Bottoms up."
msgstr "¡Salud!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The piles of corpses stop moving, which is as close to dead as you can imagine they'll get. It's not just the bodies, though. The whole tower seems... still. Stale. As if it was frozen in time. \n"
"\n"
"Despite its incredible height, you can only see a single floor, the one you're on. The two of you search high and low, finding... nothing. The place is decorated with stone benches and tables and lit with pale yellow-green lights that make you feel sick, but little else. You sit by the pool in the center of the room, watching the corpse piles slowly turn to ash."
msgstr ""
"Los montones de cadáveres dejan de moverse, que es lo más parecido a estar muertos que puedes imaginar que lleguen a estar. Pero no son solo los cuerpos. Toda la torre parece... inmóvil. Rancia. Como si se hubiera congelado en el tiempo. \n"
"\n"
"Pese a su increíble altura, solo ves una planta, aquella en la que estás. Los dos buscáis por todas partes sin encontrar... nada. El lugar está decorado con bancos y mesas de piedra e iluminado con unas luces pálidas de color verde amarillento que te revuelven el estómago, pero poco más. Te sientas junto al estanque del centro de la sala y observas cómo los montones de cadáveres se convierten lentamente en ceniza."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They must be summoned beasts, like the Yeti we fought."
msgstr "Deben de ser bestias invocadas, como el yeti contra el que luchamos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Reminds you of Talm, doesn't it?"
msgstr "Te recuerda a Talm, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You read my mind. I wonder... Do you think this tower belonged to the..."
msgstr ""
"Me has leído la mente. Me pregunto... ¿Crees que esta torre perteneció a "
"los...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What'd he call them?"
msgstr "¿Cómo los llamó?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Lifebinders..? Could be."
msgstr "¿Vinculavidas...? Podría ser."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How many ages have those miserable piles of souls haunted this place?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cuántas eras llevan esos miserables montones de almas rondando este lugar?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "At least they can rest now. Whoever or whatever they were."
msgstr ""
"Al menos ahora pueden descansar. Fueran quienes fueran, o lo que fueran."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Can't say the same for us, though. I refuse to have come all this way just "
"for a creepy little tower with no answers."
msgstr ""
"Aunque no se puede decir lo mismo de nosotros. Me niego a haber venido hasta"
" aquí solo por una torrecita siniestra sin respuestas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Surely not..."
msgstr "No puede ser..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you trail off, you take a deeper look into the pool. Unlike the rest of the tower, it almost exudes warmth. It's inviting. You pull out the gilded black book and flip through the pages of scrawl you cannot read. Several pages after the map shows the tower. Several pages after that, an overhead view of a circular room. Within that room a smaller circle of... paradise, is the only word that comes to mind.\n"
"\n"
"On the next page, the page is cut in half. On the top half, people stand in water on the 'real' side of the world. These people seem sad, angry, and some even sport wounds in a way that's a bit surprising for what's meant to be a children's book. Among them are people holding purple vials, who seem to be in the process of passing out. Some of the tables in the illustration seem to be open in the center.\n"
"\n"
"The other half of the page is lovely, mirroring the top half. These people are upside down, holding hands and smiling with one another. You look to the sheet of placid water in the center of the room once again, and motion for [Companion Name] to sit beside you.\n"
"\n"
"You come to the same conclusion. You need to pass through. After splashing about in the warm water for a while feeling no different - as crazy as it may be - you come to the same conclusion. You need to find and make the purple vials. You wedge blades into the center of tables around the room until one gives way, revealing the same vials as the book held, along with herbs and ingredients you assume go inside."
msgstr ""
"Mientras tu voz se apaga, miras con más atención el estanque. A diferencia del resto de la torre, casi desprende calidez. Resulta acogedor. Sacas el libro negro y dorado y hojeas sus páginas de garabatos que no puedes leer. Varias páginas después del mapa aparece la torre. Varias páginas más adelante, una vista cenital de una sala circular. Dentro de esa sala, un círculo más pequeño de... paraíso, es la única palabra que te viene a la mente.\n"
"\n"
"En la página siguiente, la hoja está dividida por la mitad. En la mitad superior, unas personas están de pie en el agua, en el lado «real» del mundo. Parecen tristes, enfadadas, y algunas incluso lucen heridas de una forma algo sorprendente para lo que se supone que es un libro infantil. Entre ellas hay personas que sostienen frascos morados y que parecen estar desmayándose. Algunas de las mesas de la ilustración parecen abiertas por el centro.\n"
"\n"
"La otra mitad de la página es preciosa y refleja la mitad superior. Esas personas están del revés, cogidas de la mano y sonriéndose unas a otras. Vuelves a mirar la lámina de agua serena del centro de la sala y le haces un gesto a [Companion Name] para que se siente a tu lado.\n"
"\n"
"Llegáis a la misma conclusión. Tenéis que atravesarlo. Tras chapotear un rato en el agua tibia sin notar nada distinto (por muy loco que parezca), llegáis a la misma conclusión. Tenéis que encontrar y preparar los frascos morados. Metéis cuchillas en el centro de las mesas de la sala hasta que una cede y revela los mismos frascos que mostraba el libro, junto con hierbas e ingredientes que supones que van dentro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is going to be extremely dangerous."
msgstr "Esto va a ser muy peligroso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Phew, that was tough."
msgstr "Uf, ha sido duro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The moment the liquid hits your tongue, you feel... nothing. Your body falls backward into the water, but you're not in it any longer. You watch as the liquid washes over you, then [Companion Name]. You scream, but hear nothing. You want to try to push yourself back into your body, but cannot seem to will yourself forward. You feel still, but your mind cries out over and over again that what's happening is wrong.\n"
"\n"
"Bit by bit you see your body wither away, like the rotting of a fruit sped up a hundred-fold. You feel regret at everything you never got the chance to do. Bitter over falling for such a stupid trick. Remorse for getting [Companion Name] involved. Calm, over knowing that it's... out of your hands now. Warmth for the hundreds of happy memories you've made through the years, even if it was cut short. Thankful for everyone you've gotten to know, good and bad. You're a mixture of countless emotions, good and bad, but this is all you've got. Nothing left to be done about it.\n"
"\n"
"You pass through the other side, your consciousness slamming back into your body. You feel your body materialize and peel away from the sickly sweet membrane of the mirrored pool. You fall through the air and weightlessly hit the stone ground. Feeling slowly returns to your body as you remember how to move. How to breathe.\n"
"\n"
"You rub your eyes as you sit up... You're... in paradise.\n"
"\n"
"Grey flesh coats the walls and pulses like the beat of a heart. The stone beneath you is an endless path of mottled bone held together with sinew. You hear screams echo out around you as you move to your feet. But where is it-"
msgstr ""
"En cuanto el líquido toca tu lengua, no sientes... nada. Tu cuerpo cae de espaldas al agua, pero tú ya no estás en él. Ves cómo el líquido te cubre, y luego a [Companion Name]. Gritas, pero no oyes nada. Quieres intentar volver a tu cuerpo, pero no consigues obligarte a avanzar. Te sientes inmóvil, pero tu mente grita una y otra vez que lo que está pasando no está bien.\n"
"\n"
"Poco a poco ves cómo tu cuerpo se marchita, como una fruta que se pudre cien veces más rápido. Sientes arrepentimiento por todo lo que nunca tuviste ocasión de hacer. Amargura por caer en una trampa tan estúpida. Remordimiento por haber metido en esto a [Companion Name]. Calma, al saber que ya... no está en tus manos. Calidez por los cientos de recuerdos felices que has creado a lo largo de los años, aunque se hayan visto truncados. Gratitud por toda la gente que has llegado a conocer, buena y mala. Eres una mezcla de incontables emociones, buenas y malas, pero esto es todo lo que tienes. Ya no se puede hacer nada.\n"
"\n"
"Atraviesas al otro lado, y tu consciencia vuelve de golpe a tu cuerpo. Sientes cómo tu cuerpo se materializa y se despega de la membrana empalagosamente dulce del estanque reflejado. Caes por el aire y golpeas sin peso el suelo de piedra. La sensibilidad vuelve poco a poco a tu cuerpo mientras recuerdas cómo moverte. Cómo respirar.\n"
"\n"
"Te frotas los ojos al incorporarte... Estás... en el paraíso.\n"
"\n"
"Una carne gris recubre las paredes y palpita como el latido de un corazón. La piedra bajo tus pies es un camino infinito de hueso moteado unido con tendones. Oyes gritos que resuenan a tu alrededor mientras te pones en pie. Pero ¿de dónde viene...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "[Player Name]!!!"
msgstr "¡¡¡[Player Name]!!!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "WE HAVE TO MOVE! NOW!"
msgstr "¡TENEMOS QUE MOVERNOS! ¡YA!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "PLEASE! I WILL NOT LEAVE YOU HERE BUT YOU NEED TO GET UP!"
msgstr "¡POR FAVOR! ¡NO VOY A DEJARTE AQUÍ, PERO TIENES QUE LEVANTARTE!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your eyes snap open. [Companion Name]'s eyes are wide in fear, in a way you haven't seen since the Soulsmiths first attacked Azamire.\n"
"\n"
"You look back and see it. A twisted being formed of... human matter. The creature drags itself down pathway and towards you with frightening speed. Everything about it seems... incompatible with life. With each movement its claws tear into the walls of this hellscape and it pulls itself towards you. Closer. \n"
"\n"
"You grab [Companion Name] by the arm and drag her with you, knowing that if you opened your mouth you'd fail to produce anything other than screams.\n"
"\n"
"You need to leave."
msgstr ""
"Abres los ojos de golpe. [Companion Name] tiene los ojos muy abiertos por el miedo, como no la veías desde que los Forjaalmas atacaron Azamire por primera vez.\n"
"\n"
"Miras atrás y lo ves. Un ser retorcido formado de... materia humana. La criatura se arrastra por el camino hacia ti a una velocidad aterradora. Todo en ella parece... incompatible con la vida. Con cada movimiento, sus garras desgarran las paredes de este paisaje infernal mientras se impulsa hacia ti. Más cerca. \n"
"\n"
"Agarras a [Companion Name] del brazo y tiras de ella, sabiendo que si abrieras la boca no saldría de ella nada más que gritos.\n"
"\n"
"Tienes que salir de aquí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What happened to you..?"
msgstr "¿Qué te ha pasado...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...is it dead?"
msgstr "...¿está muerto?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Arms of gray skin and bone reach out to grab you from the corridor walls. You and [Companion Name] run through the fetid halls along the only path laid out for you. There's nothing else you can do. Each step becomes heavier and heavier as the bone beneath you turns spongy and slick with blood that pours from the ceiling and walls.\n"
"\n"
"You lost track of time ages ago, and focus on your breathing. In. Out. In. Out. You reach out to steady [Companion Name]. Flinch back as she cuts a hand away from your throat.\n"
"\n"
"The tunnel grows more narrow, and all the while, the beast crawls towards you faster and faster. Its breath curls down your back as you sprint through the halls, the feeling reminding you of how the purple vial touching your lips and bringing you to this nightmare felt. You feel the beast's nails bite into your skin. Just a glancing blow, but you know the next time it touches you, it will be fatal.\n"
"\n"
"You see light up ahead. You jump off the bridge.\n"
"\n"
"And then... it ends.\n"
"\n"
"You reach a large room made of the same stone as the tower that brought you here. Your lungs burn and tears stream down your face. [Companion Name] lands beside you with a thud.\n"
"\n"
"You look back, and the tunnel you came from isn't there.\n"
"\n"
"Maybe it never was.\n"
"\n"
"You turn back and see Talm, arm in arm with his wife Era. The two of them look at you with so much hatred that you almost feel like you deserve it, though you haven't the slightest idea on why. Their fingers elongate into claws that scrape against the stone floor, while their bodies twist into malformed ideas of human anatomy."
msgstr ""
"Brazos de piel gris y hueso salen de las paredes del pasillo para agarrarte. [Companion Name] y tú corréis por los pasillos fétidos siguiendo el único camino que tenéis delante. No hay nada más que podáis hacer. Cada paso pesa más y más a medida que el hueso bajo tus pies se vuelve esponjoso y resbaladizo por la sangre que mana del techo y de las paredes.\n"
"\n"
"Hace rato que perdiste la noción del tiempo, y te concentras en respirar. Dentro. Fuera. Dentro. Fuera. Alargas la mano para sujetar a [Companion Name]. Te echas atrás cuando ella aparta de un tajo una mano que iba a por tu garganta.\n"
"\n"
"El túnel se estrecha cada vez más y, mientras tanto, la bestia se arrastra hacia vosotros cada vez más rápido. Sientes su aliento en la espalda mientras corres a toda velocidad por los pasillos, una sensación que te recuerda al vial morado rozándote los labios y trayéndote a esta pesadilla. Notas cómo las uñas de la bestia se te clavan en la piel. Solo es un roce, pero sabes que la próxima vez que te toque será mortal.\n"
"\n"
"Ves luz más adelante. Saltas del puente.\n"
"\n"
"Y entonces... se acaba.\n"
"\n"
"Llegas a una gran sala hecha de la misma piedra que la torre que te trajo hasta aquí. Te arden los pulmones y las lágrimas te corren por la cara. [Companion Name] cae a tu lado con un golpe sordo.\n"
"\n"
"Miras atrás, y el túnel por el que viniste ya no está.\n"
"\n"
"Quizá nunca estuvo.\n"
"\n"
"Te das la vuelta y ves a Talm, del brazo de su esposa Era. Los dos te miran con tanto odio que casi sientes que te lo mereces, aunque no tienes ni la menor idea de por qué. Sus dedos se alargan hasta convertirse en garras que arañan el suelo de piedra, mientras sus cuerpos se retuercen en ideas deformes de la anatomía humana."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is where my people went, all those years ago!"
msgstr "¡Aquí es adonde fue mi pueblo, hace tantos años!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is the culmination of everything they worked towards."
msgstr "Esta es la culminación de todo aquello por lo que trabajaron."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Look upon it and weep."
msgstr "Contémplalo y llora."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That's all we have left."
msgstr "Es todo lo que nos queda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You pull [Companion Name] to her feet. She is breathless, but her body moves on instinct as Era swipes towards her. You hear a clash of metal and hope it was enough. \n"
"\n"
"You barely have time to defend yourself as Talm's full weight slams into you, sending the two of you careening towards the edge of the stone platform. You now see that you stand on disk, and that over the edges of the platform lead to... nothing.\n"
"\n"
"You turn back towards Talm, ready to face him... it... head on."
msgstr ""
"Ayudas a [Companion Name] a ponerse en pie. Le falta el aliento, pero su cuerpo se mueve por instinto cuando Era lanza un zarpazo hacia ella. Oyes un choque de metal y esperas que haya bastado. \n"
"\n"
"Apenas tienes tiempo de defenderte cuando todo el peso de Talm se estrella contra ti y os lanza a los dos hacia el borde de la plataforma de piedra. Ahora ves que estás sobre un disco, y que más allá de los bordes de la plataforma no hay... nada.\n"
"\n"
"Te vuelves hacia Talm, dispuesto a enfrentarte a él... a eso... de frente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm's broken body lays before you. You hold your weapon in front of you, knowing that the moment you look away, it'll lunge for you, looking to take advantage of your weakness. Your breaths come in ragged heaves. The chance that you'd even be able to fend off a casual swat of Talm's claws is bordering on zero, but you stand at the ready regardless. You lost track of [Companion Name] ages ago, and can only hope that she was able to hold Era off.\n"
"\n"
"You stare at the corpse as long as you can, your whole body threatening to collapse. You risk a blink of your eyes... and he's gone. Replaced by the Talm you know. Mostly.\n"
"\n"
"The man before you wears a bright white crown of bone, and regal garb made of blackened leather. You can tell that it's... alive. But life may be be a stretch for the sorrowful creature wrapped around his body. He lets gives you a slow clap, before turning to Era, who dons similar 'clothes'. He whispers something you cannot hear to her, and she smiles slightly.\n"
"\n"
"You take a step back, consciousness fading. Your weapon wavers, but does not fall.\n"
"\n"
"The platform beneath you shifts and begins to descend into darkness."
msgstr ""
"El cuerpo destrozado de Talm yace ante ti. Sostienes tu arma delante, sabiendo que en cuanto apartes la mirada se abalanzará sobre ti para aprovechar tu debilidad. Respiras a bocanadas entrecortadas. Las probabilidades de que pudieras siquiera esquivar un zarpazo casual de Talm rozan el cero, pero aun así te mantienes en guardia. Hace mucho que perdiste de vista a [Companion Name], y solo puedes esperar que haya conseguido contener a Era.\n"
"\n"
"Miras fijamente el cadáver todo lo que puedes, con todo el cuerpo a punto de desplomarse. Te arriesgas a parpadear... y ya no está. En su lugar está el Talm que conoces. Más o menos.\n"
"\n"
"El hombre que tienes delante lleva una corona de hueso de un blanco brillante y ropajes regios de cuero ennegrecido. Notas que está... vivo. Aunque llamar vida a lo que tiene esa criatura afligida que le envuelve el cuerpo quizá sea exagerar. Te dedica un aplauso lento antes de volverse hacia Era, que lleva una «ropa» parecida. Le susurra algo que no alcanzas a oír y ella sonríe levemente.\n"
"\n"
"Das un paso atrás mientras pierdes la consciencia. Tu arma vacila, pero no cae.\n"
"\n"
"La plataforma bajo tus pies se mueve y empieza a descender hacia la oscuridad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 67[/color] Enemy "
"multiple times"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar varias veces a un enemigo de [color=#FFD16D]nivel de "
"combate 67[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.VisualOnlyRequiredRequirements.CustomConditions
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Must be able to defeat a [color=#FFD16D]Combat Level 69[/color] "
"[b][u]Pinnacle Boss[/u][/b]"
msgstr ""
"Debes poder derrotar a un [b][u]jefe supremo[/u][/b] de [color=#FFD16D]nivel"
" de combate 69[/color]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ18"
msgstr "MQ18"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What Comes After - After surviving Talm's initial onslaught, what will "
"become of you next?"
msgstr ""
"Lo que viene después: Tras sobrevivir a la primera embestida de Talm, ¿qué "
"será de ti ahora?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What can you tell me? (Divination)"
msgstr "¿Qué puedes decirme? (Adivinación)"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I feel it coming to me. (Divination)"
msgstr "...Siento que viene hacia mí. (Adivinación)"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The chamber's walls shift as the platform you stand upon descends. Talm's regal form slowly begins to bleed into the darkness as the ground shifts beneath you, descending lower and lower. You try to keep your eyes trained on him, but without moving he fades from your vision. Fatigue sets in as your tense body begins to give out without a target in front of you.\n"
"\n"
"As the gloom begins to swallow you, you feel... warm. At peace. Mentally, you lash out, knowing that something is wrong, but you've pushed yourself beyond your limits. Your weapon slips from your grasp as you collapse sideways. You don't even feel the cold stone floor as you fall. Only warmth.\n"
"\n"
"You dream.\n"
"\n"
"You wear dark grey robe made of a material that dances and swirls chaotically whenever you take your eyes off of it. You stand amidst an endless sea of bodies. Your chest wracks with silent sobs as you gaze upon them, not at all comforted by their peaceful smiles. As you walk amongst them, you make it to your king and lift the pearly white bone crown from his cold brow.\n"
"\n"
"The weight it holds is incomparable to that which still rests on your shoulders. There's still so much work to do.\n"
"\n"
"You awaken with a start and find yourself warm... but not cloying so. You're wrapped in devilishly silken sheets and buried in a bed so plush you fear your worn body won't be able to rise. Era stands far on the opposite corner of the room, stoking a fireplace of smooth, black stone.\n"
"\n"
"You try to move, but every inch of your body screams in protest, and your groan catches her attention. She looks at you with... what'd seem to be genuine concern had she and her husband not just tried to kill you. You involuntarily shudder as she drops her bundle of wood and rushes to your side. She tries to begin speaking several times, before sighing and offering a small chuckle."
msgstr ""
"Las paredes de la cámara se desplazan mientras la plataforma sobre la que estás desciende. La figura regia de Talm empieza a fundirse poco a poco con la oscuridad mientras el suelo se mueve bajo tus pies, bajando más y más. Intentas no apartar la vista de él, pero, sin moverse, se desvanece de tu vista. El cansancio se apodera de ti y tu cuerpo, tenso, empieza a ceder sin un objetivo delante.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando la penumbra empieza a engullirte, sientes... calidez. Paz. Por dentro te rebelas, sabiendo que algo va mal, pero has ido más allá de tus límites. El arma se te escapa de las manos y te desplomas de lado. Ni siquiera notas el frío suelo de piedra al caer. Solo calidez.\n"
"\n"
"Sueñas.\n"
"\n"
"Llevas una túnica gris oscura de un material que baila y se arremolina de forma caótica cada vez que apartas la vista de él. Estás en medio de un mar infinito de cuerpos. Sollozos silenciosos te sacuden el pecho mientras los contemplas, sin encontrar consuelo alguno en sus sonrisas serenas. Caminas entre ellos hasta llegar a tu rey y le quitas de la fría frente la corona de hueso blanco nacarado.\n"
"\n"
"Su peso no es nada comparado con el que aún descansa sobre tus hombros. Aún queda tanto por hacer.\n"
"\n"
"Te despiertas sobresaltado y te encuentras abrigado... pero no de forma agobiante. Estás envuelto en sábanas diabólicamente sedosas, hundido en una cama tan mullida que temes que tu cuerpo agotado no sea capaz de levantarse. Era está lejos, en la esquina opuesta de la habitación, avivando una chimenea de piedra negra y lisa.\n"
"\n"
"Intentas moverte, pero cada centímetro de tu cuerpo protesta a gritos, y tu gemido llama su atención. Te mira con lo que... parecería auténtica preocupación si ella y su marido no acabaran de intentar matarte. Te estremeces sin querer cuando suelta su haz de leña y corre a tu lado. Intenta empezar a hablar varias veces, antes de suspirar y soltar una risita."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hello darling... How do you feel?"
msgstr "Hola, querido... ¿Cómo te encuentras?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...what do you want? Why am I here? Is..."
msgstr "...¿Qué quieres? ¿Por qué estoy aquí? ¿Está...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Is [Companion Name] still..?"
msgstr "¿[Companion Name] sigue...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yes. She's alright. Recovering, like you, though she got it a bit rougher "
"than you did."
msgstr ""
"Sí. Está bien. Recuperándose, como tú, aunque ella se llevó la peor parte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm and I will explain in more detail as we can, but I know you must have "
"several thousand questions, my child. I will do my best to answer them, but "
"you'll come to learn more in time. Even here, there are laws that dictate "
"against what I can and cannot speak."
msgstr ""
"Talm y yo te lo explicaremos con más detalle cuando podamos, pero sé que "
"debes de tener miles de preguntas, hijo mío. Haré lo posible por "
"responderlas, pero con el tiempo irás aprendiendo más. Incluso aquí hay "
"leyes que dictan lo que puedo y lo que no puedo decir."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Welcome to Respite. We're within the domain of the Lifebinders, a... world "
"between worlds, so-to-speak. It was created as a safe haven during the "
"calamity that brought Talm and I together."
msgstr ""
"Bienvenido a Respite. Estamos en el dominio de los Vinculavidas, un... mundo"
" entre mundos, por así decirlo. Se creó como refugio seguro durante la "
"calamidad que nos unió a Talm y a mí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I presume you found the entrance from your pilfered book, yes? The book came"
" from here, and was written for Lifebinder children to act as a source of "
"comfort while the world fell apart around them."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que encontraste la entrada gracias a tu libro robado, ¿verdad? El "
"libro procede de aquí, y se escribió para que los niños de los Vinculavidas "
"encontraran consuelo mientras el mundo se desmoronaba a su alrededor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How could that book, or this place, bring anyone comfort?"
msgstr "¿Cómo puede ese libro, o este lugar, dar consuelo a nadie?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What you've seen of Respite was it's entrance. The beast at the front, its "
"guardian. There are many that would have wished to see Respite burn."
msgstr ""
"Lo que has visto de Respite era su entrada. La bestia de la entrada, su "
"guardián. Había muchos que habrían querido ver arder Respite."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The chamber's walls shift as the platform you stand upon descends. Talm's regal form slowly begins to bleed into the darkness as the ground shifts beneath you, descending lower and lower. You try to keep your eyes trained on him, but without moving he fades from your vision. Fatigue sets in as your tense body begins to give out without a target in front of you.\n"
"\n"
"As the gloom begins to swallow you, you feel... warm. At peace. Mentally, you lash out, knowing that something is wrong, but you've pushed yourself beyond your limits. Your weapon slips from your grasp as you collapse sideways. You don't even feel the cold stone floor as you fall. Only warmth.\n"
"\n"
"You dream.\n"
"\n"
"You wear dark grey robe made of a material that dances and swirls chaotically whenever you take your eyes off of it. You stand amidst an endless sea of bodies. Your chest wracks with silent sobs as you gaze upon them, not at all comforted by their peaceful smiles. As you walk amongst them, you make it to your king and lift the pearly white bone crown from his cold brow.\n"
"\n"
"The weight it holds is incomparable to that which still rests on your shoulders. There's still so much work to do.\n"
"\n"
"You awaken with a start and find yourself warm... but not cloying so. You're wrapped in devilishly silken sheets and buried in a bed so plush you fear your worn body won't be able to rise. Era stands far on the opposite corner of the room, stoking a fireplace of smooth, black stone.\n"
"\n"
"You try to move, but every inch of your body screams in protest. You try not to make a sound, but your involuntary groan catches her attention. She looks at you with... what'd seem to be genuine concern had she and her husband not just tried to kill you. You involuntarily shudder as she drops her bundle of wood and rushes to your side. She tries to begin speaking several times, before sighing and offering a small chuckle."
msgstr ""
"Las paredes de la cámara se desplazan mientras la plataforma sobre la que estás desciende. La figura regia de Talm empieza a fundirse poco a poco con la oscuridad mientras el suelo se mueve bajo tus pies, bajando más y más. Intentas no apartar la vista de él, pero, sin moverse, se desvanece de tu vista. El cansancio se apodera de ti y tu cuerpo, tenso, empieza a ceder sin un objetivo delante.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando la penumbra empieza a engullirte, sientes... calidez. Paz. Por dentro te rebelas, sabiendo que algo va mal, pero has ido más allá de tus límites. El arma se te escapa de las manos y te desplomas de lado. Ni siquiera notas el frío suelo de piedra al caer. Solo calidez.\n"
"\n"
"Sueñas.\n"
"\n"
"Llevas una túnica gris oscura de un material que baila y se arremolina de forma caótica cada vez que apartas la vista de él. Estás en medio de un mar infinito de cuerpos. Sollozos silenciosos te sacuden el pecho mientras los contemplas, sin encontrar consuelo alguno en sus sonrisas serenas. Caminas entre ellos hasta llegar a tu rey y le quitas de la fría frente la corona de hueso blanco nacarado.\n"
"\n"
"Su peso no es nada comparado con el que aún descansa sobre tus hombros. Aún queda tanto por hacer.\n"
"\n"
"Te despiertas sobresaltado y te encuentras abrigado... pero no de forma agobiante. Estás envuelto en sábanas diabólicamente sedosas, hundido en una cama tan mullida que temes que tu cuerpo agotado no sea capaz de levantarse. Era está lejos, en la esquina opuesta de la habitación, avivando una chimenea de piedra negra y lisa.\n"
"\n"
"Intentas moverte, pero cada centímetro de tu cuerpo protesta a gritos. Intentas no hacer ruido, pero se te escapa un gemido que llama su atención. Te mira con lo que... parecería auténtica preocupación si ella y su marido no acabaran de intentar matarte. Te estremeces sin querer cuando suelta su haz de leña y corre a tu lado. Intenta empezar a hablar varias veces, antes de suspirar y soltar una risita."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Given [Companion Name] and I's reception, I see that peaceful nature has "
"died out."
msgstr ""
"Visto el recibimiento que nos disteis a [Companion Name] y a mí, veo que esa"
" naturaleza pacífica se ha extinguido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I won't ask for either of you to forgiven Talm and I's transgressions "
"against you, only explain why we chose this path."
msgstr ""
"No os pediré a ninguno de los dos que perdonéis lo que Talm y yo os hemos "
"hecho, solo que os expliquemos por qué elegimos este camino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My people sought to ascertain the fates through communion with the stars, as"
" you've gathered by now. Our use of summoning itself was rather limited, and"
" focused on the practical, usually creating messengers to help us made sense"
" of the fates."
msgstr ""
"Mi pueblo buscaba desentrañar el destino mediante la comunión con las "
"estrellas, como ya habrás deducido. Nuestro uso de la invocación en sí era "
"bastante limitado y se centraba en lo práctico; normalmente creábamos "
"mensajeros que nos ayudaran a dar sentido al destino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We were called the Fateseekers, and we learned of the calamity far before it"
" ever was set into motion."
msgstr ""
"Nos llamaban los Buscadestinos, y supimos de la calamidad mucho antes de que"
" se pusiera en marcha."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You'll hear more of this calamity as you rest here, I promise you that."
msgstr "Oirás más sobre esa calamidad mientras descansas aquí, te lo prometo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Nevertheless. The Fateseekers' visions all culminated in one final "
"premonition of the future."
msgstr ""
"En cualquier caso. Todas las visiones de los Buscadestinos culminaron en una"
" última premonición del futuro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A creature so vile, born of a nation of sacrificed life. As it let out its "
"first breath, the world in its entirety twisted and died."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura tan vil, nacida de una nación de vidas sacrificadas. Al exhalar"
" su primer aliento, el mundo entero se retorció y murió."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My people's visions can be esoteric at times, but this was seen with perfect"
" clarity across my entire clan."
msgstr ""
"Las visiones de mi pueblo pueden ser crípticas a veces, pero esta la vio con"
" total claridad todo mi clan."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is what the calamity would culminate in."
msgstr "Ahí es donde iba a culminar la calamidad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But this 'calamity' you cannot speak of happened already, no? That's why "
"there aren't many summoners left, outside of the Soulsmiths."
msgstr ""
"Pero esa «calamidad» de la que no puedes hablar ya ocurrió, ¿no? Por eso no "
"quedan muchos invocadores, aparte de los Forjaalmas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Unless the world underwent some kind of rebirth afterward, assuming your "
"clan was even correct in the first place, what does this have to do with why"
" you attacked us?"
msgstr ""
"A menos que el mundo renaciera de algún modo después, y suponiendo que tu "
"clan acertara en primer lugar, ¿qué tiene eso que ver con que nos atacarais?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...My people were correct. The only thing we were unsure of was the "
"timeframe."
msgstr ""
"...Mi pueblo acertó. Lo único de lo que no estábamos seguros era del "
"momento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This creature... It is what the Soulsmiths seek to bring about."
msgstr "Esa criatura... es lo que los Forjaalmas quieren traer al mundo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...why?"
msgstr "...¿por qué?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Before you can understand, you must learn this history of Respite."
msgstr "Antes de poder entenderlo, tienes que conocer la historia de Respite."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But I've already kept you so long, I thank you for your patience. I'll "
"explain more to you, in time, but please, acquaint yourself with this place "
"first. Leave if you must, just come and find me. You may always return "
"later."
msgstr ""
"Pero ya te he entretenido demasiado, gracias por tu paciencia. Te explicaré "
"más con el tiempo, pero, por favor, familiarízate antes con este lugar. "
"Márchate si es necesario, pero ven a buscarme. Siempre podrás volver más "
"tarde."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Era rises from the bedside and offers a small curtsy. Your next question is answered before it even leaves your mouth. [Companion Name] is in the next room over, but hasn't yet awakened.\n"
"\n"
"You follow Era out, who wanders off down the hall. You knock on [Companion Name]'s door before letting yourself in. Like you were, she rests in a large bed and is seemingly unharmed, but you see that she's restless, perhaps having strange dreams like yours before you awoke.\n"
"\n"
"You go to her and speak her name softly, and hold her hand. You feel the first bit of relief you have since you woke, Era's earlier words having more of the opposite effect on you.\n"
"\n"
"You stay for a long while, before heading to the window and pulling open the curtain. You weren't sure what you'd find, but you weren't expecting... endless rows of white lily-like flowers amidst a field of grey grass that stretch out further than you can see. In their own small clusters are other flowers, almost always another distinct color. You see blues, greens, browns, and occasional bright reds as well. They all seem pristine, and the field of dark grass is free from any other growth.\n"
"\n"
"As you look at the sky, the dark purple sky feels alien to you, the stars burn a deep, lush green, their patterns completely unfamiliar to you."
msgstr ""
"Era se levanta de junto a la cama y hace una pequeña reverencia. Tu siguiente pregunta obtiene respuesta antes de que salga de tu boca: [Companion Name] está en la habitación de al lado, pero aún no ha despertado.\n"
"\n"
"Sigues a Era hasta la puerta y ella se aleja pasillo abajo. Llamas a la puerta de [Companion Name] antes de entrar. Igual que tú antes, descansa en una cama grande y parece ilesa, pero ves que está inquieta, quizá teniendo sueños extraños como los tuyos antes de despertar.\n"
"\n"
"Te acercas a ella, pronuncias su nombre en voz baja y le coges la mano. Sientes el primer atisbo de alivio desde que despertaste, pues las palabras de Era te habían causado más bien el efecto contrario.\n"
"\n"
"Te quedas un buen rato antes de ir a la ventana y descorrer la cortina. No sabías qué ibas a encontrar, pero no esperabas... hileras interminables de flores blancas parecidas a lirios en medio de un campo de hierba gris que se extiende más allá de donde alcanza la vista. En pequeños grupos aparte hay otras flores, casi siempre de otro color distinto. Ves azules, verdes, marrones y, de vez en cuando, rojos intensos. Todas parecen impecables, y en el campo de hierba oscura no crece nada más.\n"
"\n"
"Al mirar el cielo, ese púrpura oscuro te resulta ajeno; las estrellas arden con un verde intenso y exuberante, en constelaciones que no conoces en absoluto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Bring me back to what you wish to show me. (Divination)"
msgstr "Llévame de vuelta a lo que quieres mostrarme. (Adivinación)"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I just... hope I can understand it. (Divination)"
msgstr "Solo... espero poder entenderlo. (Adivinación)"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you practice the divination methods Era taught you back in her tower, the green stars push themselves into your mind. Unlike your out-of-body experience then, you find yourself... back in your earlier dream. The bone crown feels more comfortable on your head now, and you feel more... at peace.\n"
"\n"
"You walk amongst the bodies and realize that they aren't corpses. Yet. They lay somewhere between life and death, much like the plane you currently reside.\n"
"\n"
"This was the dream your people, the Lifebinders, chose for themselves. To fall into an endless, beautiful dream, far removed from the horrors the world faces.\n"
"\n"
"Alongside your people are others, from more clans. Respite was open to all who chose it.\n"
"\n"
"You want so desperately to lay down and join them in the grass, but... you know you can't. The ritual isn't complete, and you're the only one who can see it to its end.\n"
"\n"
"You'll pulled out of the dream as you feel a hand on your real shoulder. [Companion Name] looks at you with concern."
msgstr ""
"Mientras practicas los métodos de adivinación que Era te enseñó en su torre, las estrellas verdes se abren paso en tu mente. A diferencia de tu experiencia extracorporal de entonces, te encuentras... de nuevo en tu sueño anterior. La corona de hueso te resulta ahora más cómoda sobre la cabeza, y te sientes más... en paz.\n"
"\n"
"Caminas entre los cuerpos y te das cuenta de que no son cadáveres. Todavía. Yacen en algún punto entre la vida y la muerte, igual que el plano en el que te encuentras ahora.\n"
"\n"
"Este era el sueño que tu pueblo, los Vinculavidas, eligió para sí. Caer en un sueño infinito y hermoso, muy lejos de los horrores a los que se enfrenta el mundo.\n"
"\n"
"Junto a tu pueblo hay otros, de más clanes. Respite estaba abierto a todos los que lo eligieran.\n"
"\n"
"Deseas con todas tus fuerzas tumbarte en la hierba y unirte a ellos, pero... sabes que no puedes. El ritual no está completo, y eres el único que puede llevarlo a término.\n"
"\n"
"Sales del sueño al notar una mano en tu hombro real. [Companion Name] te mira con preocupación."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "[Player Name]? Oh... I'm so happy to see you."
msgstr "¿[Player Name]? Oh... me alegro tanto de verte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Are you okay? Why are you crying?"
msgstr "¿Estás bien? ¿Por qué lloras?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... I don't know. But I'm so glad that you're okay."
msgstr "Yo... no lo sé. Pero me alegro mucho de que estés bien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You are okay, right?"
msgstr "Estás bien, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I think Era killed me."
msgstr "...Creo que Era me mató."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"She clearly didn't do a good enough job, though, since I'm still... here. "
"Wherever here is."
msgstr ""
"Aunque está claro que no hizo bien su trabajo, porque sigo... aquí. Sea "
"donde sea aquí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Back in that dark chamber, after that flesh monster?"
msgstr "¿Allí, en aquella cámara oscura, después de aquel monstruo de carne?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yeah. She ran her claws through my chest. But uh... I don't seem to have so "
"much as a scratch on me."
msgstr ""
"Sí. Me atravesó el pecho con las garras. Pero, eh... no parece que tenga ni "
"un rasguño."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We saw Talm bring Era back from the dead, or close to it. Maybe they did the"
" same for you?"
msgstr ""
"Vimos a Talm traer a Era de vuelta de entre los muertos, o casi. ¿Quizá "
"hicieron lo mismo contigo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I passed out shortly after fighting Talm off."
msgstr "Me desmayé poco después de quitarme a Talm de encima."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So, you beat your opponent, huh? You're gonna make me look bad."
msgstr "Así que venciste a tu rival, ¿eh? Vas a dejarme en mal lugar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...You know, for a dead woman, you seem to be taking things in stride."
msgstr "...¿Sabes? Para ser una muerta, te lo estás tomando con mucha calma."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, I feel like I've gotten the best sleep I've had in months, and you're "
"here, so... I figure we're somewhat safe."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, siento que he dormido mejor que en meses, y tú estás aquí, así que..."
" supongo que estamos más o menos a salvo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But I do hope you'll fill me in on how exactly we got here."
msgstr "Pero espero que me cuentes cómo exactamente hemos llegado hasta aquí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You wipe your face and join [Companion Name] on the bed, and do your best to fill her in on everything you know. She nods along, and asks dozens of questions that you don't have the answers to. Yet, you hope to yourself.\n"
"\n"
"You talk about your dreams, and [Companion Name] speaks of hers. She has seen flashes of time, all over the world in lands neither of you can even begin to guess the location of. In each, clans of summoners from endless walks of life all fighting to survive against... each other.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] describes battle after battle. Some with large armies of man and beast, others... darkly similar to the attack on Azamire, but with creatures far different to those of the Soulsmiths'.\n"
"\n"
"When she finishes, she mentions how it feels like she's been stopped mid-sentence, and needs to know how the stories end. She figures that if you continued to dream while looking at the stars outside, she plans to do the same soon.\n"
"\n"
"You both return to the window and find that the sky has shifted from purple to a hazy pink, with the stars taking on a lighter hue. Whether it's due to the passage of time or what, you cannot begin to tell, but as you gaze at them together, you feel the same draw as before."
msgstr ""
"Te secas la cara, te sientas con [Companion Name] en la cama y haces lo posible por contarle todo lo que sabes. Ella asiente y te hace decenas de preguntas para las que no tienes respuesta. Todavía, esperas para tus adentros.\n"
"\n"
"Habláis de vuestros sueños, y [Companion Name] te cuenta los suyos. Ha visto destellos de otras épocas, por todo el mundo, en tierras cuya ubicación ninguno de los dos alcanza siquiera a imaginar. En cada uno, clanes de invocadores de todo tipo luchaban por sobrevivir contra... los demás.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] describe batalla tras batalla. Algunas con grandes ejércitos de hombres y bestias, otras... siniestramente parecidas al ataque contra Azamire, pero con criaturas muy distintas a las de los Forjaalmas.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando termina, comenta que se siente como si la hubieran interrumpido a mitad de frase, y que necesita saber cómo terminan las historias. Piensa que si tú seguiste soñando mientras mirabas las estrellas de fuera, ella hará lo mismo pronto.\n"
"\n"
"Volvéis los dos a la ventana y veis que el cielo ha pasado del púrpura a un rosa brumoso, y que las estrellas han tomado un tono más claro. No sabrías decir si se debe al paso del tiempo o a otra cosa, pero mientras las contempláis juntos, sientes la misma atracción que antes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"After a long while, you're able to urge yourself back into your dream, but find yourself in a distant land, completely unfamiliar to you. \n"
"\n"
"You clutch a wooden railing tight enough to splinter the wood as you look out over the city in front of you.\n"
"\n"
"Brightly painted wooden structures fly high above a jungle canopy, suspended in the air as if held on strings tied to passing clouds. People float to-and-fro, passing between buildings calmly, living their lives blissfully untouched by the battles their people raged against your own halfway across the world. You're the last of the Lifebinders, all others now peacefully awaiting you to deliver to them the paradise they were promised. An endless dream where they'll never again be subject to the ongoing horrors of the world.\n"
"\n"
"As you withdraw the black gemstone from your cloak, you know you're dooming these people. It doesn't stop you. With shaking hands, you piece the stone with a blackened dagger made exclusively for this day. Dark mist begins to leak from the stone, curling around your hands and forming a thick cloud in front of you. It's not enough for you to release it.\n"
"\n"
"The hungry beast needs guidance. Direction.\n"
"\n"
"You will it forward."
msgstr ""
"Tras un buen rato, consigues volver a sumirte en tu sueño, pero te encuentras en una tierra lejana que te es completamente desconocida. \n"
"\n"
"Aprietas una barandilla de madera con tanta fuerza que la astillas mientras contemplas la ciudad que tienes delante.\n"
"\n"
"Estructuras de madera de vivos colores se alzan muy por encima de la copa de una selva, suspendidas en el aire como si colgaran de hilos atados a las nubes que pasan. La gente flota de aquí para allá, pasando de un edificio a otro con calma, viviendo felices sin que les afecten las batallas que su pueblo libró contra el tuyo en la otra punta del mundo. Eres el último de los Vinculavidas; todos los demás esperan ya en paz a que les entregues el paraíso que se les prometió. Un sueño infinito en el que nunca más estarán sometidos a los horrores incesantes del mundo.\n"
"\n"
"Al sacar de tu capa la gema negra, sabes que estás condenando a esta gente. Eso no te detiene. Con manos temblorosas, perforas la piedra con una daga ennegrecida hecha exclusivamente para este día. Una niebla oscura empieza a brotar de la piedra, enroscándose en tus manos y formando una densa nube delante de ti. No basta con que la liberes.\n"
"\n"
"La bestia hambrienta necesita guía. Dirección.\n"
"\n"
"La obligas a avanzar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ19"
msgstr "MQ19"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The Price of Paradise - Little by little, Respite has begun to show you what"
" it took to build, yet, you've only scratched the surface of what summoning "
"has wrought upon the land."
msgstr ""
"El precio del paraíso: Poco a poco, Respite ha empezado a mostrarte lo que "
"costó construirlo y, aun así, solo has arañado la superficie de lo que la "
"invocación ha causado en estas tierras."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Damn him."
msgstr "Maldito sea."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That should be enough."
msgstr "Con eso debería bastar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You feel... wrong. The body you inhabited was doubtlessly Talm's, though untold centuries past. What... how could someone be so driven to do something they know is so horrifically wrong. You felt his very being recoil as he carved into the gemstone, but... it didn't stop him.\n"
"\n"
"You need to know.\n"
"\n"
"You leave the room and [Companion Name] behind you, who still seems lost within her own mind.\n"
"\n"
"The halls are lined with endless murals and depictions of the world, but you hardly see them as you're driven forward with righteous purpose. You find yourself outside. The monster you seek sits far out in the field of grey grass, in front of a set of two white flowers.\n"
"\n"
"The path through the grass is well-worn, seemingly travelled countless times."
msgstr ""
"Te sientes... mal. El cuerpo que habitabas era sin duda el de Talm, aunque de hace incontables siglos. ¿Qué... cómo puede alguien sentirse tan impulsado a hacer algo que sabe que está tan horriblemente mal? Sentiste cómo todo su ser se estremecía mientras tallaba la gema, pero... eso no lo detuvo.\n"
"\n"
"Necesitas saberlo.\n"
"\n"
"Sales de la habitación y dejas atrás a [Companion Name], que todavía parece perdida en su propia mente.\n"
"\n"
"Los pasillos están llenos de murales interminables y representaciones del mundo, pero apenas los ves mientras avanzas impulsado por un propósito justo. Acabas fuera. El monstruo que buscas está sentado lejos, en el campo de hierba gris, frente a un par de flores blancas.\n"
"\n"
"El camino a través de la hierba está muy gastado, como si se hubiera recorrido incontables veces."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...What did you do?"
msgstr "...¿Qué hiciste?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm afraid you'll need to be a bit more specific than that."
msgstr "Me temo que vas a tener que ser algo más concreto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The floating city. The gemstone. I saw it."
msgstr "La ciudad flotante. La gema. Lo vi."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Ah. And here I thought you'd be a bit more interested in why I tried to kill"
" you."
msgstr ""
"Ah. Y yo que pensaba que te interesaría más saber por qué intenté matarte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll get to that."
msgstr "Ya llegaremos a eso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I can't even recall the name of the city anymore."
msgstr "Ya ni siquiera recuerdo el nombre de la ciudad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But the people, the Brazi..."
msgstr "Pero la gente, los Brazi..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Amongst the dozens of clans my people fought, none were more... through in "
"their eradication on the Lifebinders."
msgstr ""
"De las decenas de clanes contra los que luchó mi pueblo, ninguno fue más... "
"implacable en su empeño por erradicar a los Vinculavidas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You've seen what I've done for Era, back in the tower. My people were "
"exceptional healers."
msgstr ""
"Ya viste lo que hice por Era, allí en la torre. Mi pueblo eran sanadores "
"excepcionales."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Lifebinders focused more on the body than the Soulsmiths, who focus more on "
"the... Well. You can puzzle that one out."
msgstr ""
"Los Vinculavidas se centraban más en el cuerpo que los Forjaalmas, que se "
"centran más en el... Bueno. Eso puedes deducirlo tú."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But our control of one's spirit was quite impressive as well. These skills "
"made us incredibly sought after allies in the calamity."
msgstr ""
"Pero nuestro control sobre el espíritu también era bastante impresionante. "
"Esas habilidades nos convirtieron en aliados muy codiciados durante la "
"calamidad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Get to the point."
msgstr "Ve al grano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Better yet. How about you ask my people yourself?"
msgstr "Mejor aún. ¿Por qué no se lo preguntas tú mismo a mi pueblo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"After all this time, I'm sure they're quite tired of having me as their sole"
" point of contact with the outside world."
msgstr ""
"Después de tanto tiempo, seguro que están bastante hartos de que yo sea su "
"único contacto con el mundo exterior."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...what? "
msgstr "...¿qué? "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You want to learn, don't you?"
msgstr "Quieres aprender, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'll tell you whatever you want to know after you speak to the Dreamers."
msgstr ""
"Te contaré todo lo que quieras saber después de que hables con los "
"Soñadores."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't want to do this, but I doubt you'll listen to me otherwise..."
msgstr "No quiero hacer esto, pero dudo que me hagas caso de otro modo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Sit."
msgstr "Siéntate."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"All thoughts of resistance vanish as you find yourself dropping to your "
"knees against your will after Talm snaps his fingers, the muscles in your "
"legs giving out completely. Talm slowly cups one of the white flowers in "
"front of him and plucks several petals from it with a mix of reverence and "
"practiced effort, as though he's done it a million times before. He waves "
"you off, telling you to go gather as many as wish. Just as you consider "
"telling him to do it himself, he sighs, saying that it's 'for your own "
"good'."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier idea de resistirte se desvanece cuando, tras un chasquido de dedos"
" de Talm, caes de rodillas contra tu voluntad; los músculos de las piernas "
"te fallan por completo. Talm toma con cuidado una de las flores blancas que "
"tiene delante y le arranca varios pétalos con una mezcla de reverencia y "
"destreza, como si lo hubiera hecho un millón de veces. Te despacha con un "
"gesto y te dice que vayas a recoger tantos como quieras. Justo cuando "
"piensas en decirle que lo haga él, suspira y dice que es «por tu propio "
"bien»."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The Dreamers... what can they teach me?"
msgstr "Los Soñadores... ¿qué pueden enseñarme?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You thought multiple times about ripping the flowers from the ground as you "
"delicately plucked a few petals from each, but felt like you'd look more "
"like a rebelling child than properly offering any form of legitimate "
"resistance. You move throughout the fields efficiently, taking care not to "
"step on any of the flowers, and return once you've gathered a sizeable "
"number of petals."
msgstr ""
"Pensaste varias veces en arrancar las flores del suelo mientras recogías con"
" delicadeza unos pocos pétalos de cada una, pero te pareció que quedarías "
"más como un niño rebelde que como alguien que opone una resistencia "
"legítima. Recorres los campos con eficiencia, con cuidado de no pisar "
"ninguna flor, y vuelves cuando has reunido una cantidad considerable de "
"pétalos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There. What do you want these for?"
msgstr "Toma. ¿Para qué los quieres?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I told you. To speak with the Dreamers."
msgstr "Ya te lo dije. Para hablar con los Soñadores."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Take my hand, I'll show you."
msgstr "Dame la mano, te lo enseñaré."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Please?"
msgstr "¿Por favor?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm raises his hand once again, preparing to snap, but you begrudgingly sigh and take the man's hand. He slowly walks you through the process of... bringing Dreamers forth from the petals. Talm does so in seconds, and a pale, wispy silhouette of a young girl dances forth from one of the petals he took from you. She greets Talm warmly, asking how long it's been for him since the last she awoke. The two go back and forth for a time until the girl notices you, and she excitedly runs through more questions than you can possibly keep up with, all before you even get your name out.\n"
"\n"
"Talm calms her, saying that you're there to learn about the Dreamers, and to tell the others within the Dream to prepare themselves. Her silhouette dissipates a second later.\n"
"\n"
"The man walks you through the process, and you find it very similar to summoning creatures, but a lot harder than anything you've done before. Talm's effortless display earlier clearly came from an untold amount of practice."
msgstr ""
"Talm vuelve a levantar la mano, preparado para chasquear los dedos, pero suspiras a regañadientes y le das la mano. Te guía despacio por el proceso de... hacer surgir a los Soñadores de los pétalos. Talm lo hace en segundos, y la silueta pálida y etérea de una niña surge bailando de uno de los pétalos que le diste. Saluda a Talm con cariño y le pregunta cuánto tiempo ha pasado para él desde la última vez que despertó. Los dos charlan un rato hasta que la niña se fija en ti y, emocionada, te lanza más preguntas de las que puedes seguir, todo antes de que llegues a decir tu nombre.\n"
"\n"
"Talm la calma, le dice que has venido a aprender sobre los Soñadores y que avise a los demás dentro del Sueño para que se preparen. Su silueta se disipa un segundo después.\n"
"\n"
"El hombre te guía por el proceso, y te parece muy similar a invocar criaturas, pero mucho más difícil que nada de lo que hayas hecho antes. La facilidad con la que Talm lo hizo antes viene sin duda de una práctica incalculable."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#. Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "[Exclusive Content Agility] X/X [Exclusive Content Agility]"
msgstr "[Exclusive Content Agility] X/X [Exclusive Content Agility]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The last petal withers away in your hand, the last Dreamer you spoke with having left to go check on her child somewhere deep within the Dream. You feel... exhausted. You're unsure of just how long passed, as time within Respite doesn't seem to move like it does in the real world. You feel no hunger, no fatigue, but time does seem to pass. At the very least, the sky changes colors, though not in any pattern you were able to notice. It could have been hours, or it could have been months since you started talking to the Dreamers, you simply don't know or have any way of telling.\n"
"\n"
"The Dreamers you spoke with all shared the same initial excitement the first girl had at seeing a stranger, and countless questions about what the world was like. Like Talm had said, it'd seem that he's the only one they've talked to outside of the dream since they first entered. [Companion Name] eventually came out to join some of the conversations, and then once she was shown the process, have her own. Not everyone was from the Lifebinders... dozens of names were given, all in-line with some different discipline or school of thought, all joined the Lifebinders here in Respite to escape.\n"
"\n"
"They told you what Era and Talm couldn't. What they lived through.\n"
"\n"
"The Titan Wars.\n"
"\n"
"That was the calamity they spoke of.\n"
"\n"
"Titans were beasts that dwarved even the Ivory Athenaeum by several magnitudes of size. What the Dreamers described sounded more like forces of nature or vengeful Gods rather than anything a group of people could bring forth. When the Titans of two rival summoning clans fought, it was heard across the continent. Mountains were crushed to dust, a quarter of the mainland was buried under water, lakes of fire rose from the ground and killed thousands... \n"
"\n"
"Clans that did not raise their own Titan for protection were quickly destroyed by those that did. Each clan saw one another as a threat that could generate a world-changing force, and the only way to stay alive was to have your own and use it against the others, or create a plane of existence like Respite and lose the metaphorical key.\n"
"\n"
"Talm approaches quietly as the last Dreamer fades away."
msgstr ""
"El último pétalo se marchita en tu mano; la última Soñadora con la que hablaste se ha ido a ver cómo está su hijo, en algún lugar en lo más profundo del Sueño. Te sientes... agotado. No sabes cuánto tiempo ha pasado, ya que en Respite el tiempo no parece transcurrir como en el mundo real. No sientes hambre ni cansancio, pero el tiempo sí parece pasar. Al menos, el cielo cambia de color, aunque no siguiendo ningún patrón que hayas podido notar. Podrían haber sido horas o meses desde que empezaste a hablar con los Soñadores; sencillamente no lo sabes ni tienes forma de saberlo.\n"
"\n"
"Todos los Soñadores con los que hablaste compartían la misma emoción inicial que la primera niña al ver a un desconocido, e incontables preguntas sobre cómo era el mundo. Como había dicho Talm, parece que es el único con quien han hablado fuera del sueño desde que entraron en él. Con el tiempo, [Companion Name] salió a unirse a algunas de las conversaciones y, cuando le enseñaron el proceso, a tener las suyas. No todos procedían de los Vinculavidas... se dieron decenas de nombres, todos ligados a alguna disciplina o escuela de pensamiento distinta, y todos se unieron aquí, en Respite, a los Vinculavidas para escapar.\n"
"\n"
"Te contaron lo que Era y Talm no podían. Lo que vivieron.\n"
"\n"
"Las Guerras de los Titanes.\n"
"\n"
"Esa era la calamidad de la que hablaban.\n"
"\n"
"Los Titanes eran bestias que empequeñecían incluso al Ateneo de marfil por varios órdenes de magnitud. Lo que describían los Soñadores sonaba más a fuerzas de la naturaleza o a dioses vengativos que a algo que un grupo de personas pudiera hacer surgir. Cuando luchaban los Titanes de dos clanes de invocadores rivales, se oía en todo el continente. Montañas reducidas a polvo, una cuarta parte del continente sepultada bajo el agua, lagos de fuego que brotaban del suelo y mataban a miles... \n"
"\n"
"Los clanes que no alzaban su propio Titán para protegerse eran destruidos enseguida por los que sí lo hacían. Cada clan veía a los demás como una amenaza capaz de generar una fuerza que podía cambiar el mundo, y la única forma de seguir con vida era tener uno propio y usarlo contra los demás, o crear un plano de existencia como Respite y perder la llave, en sentido figurado.\n"
"\n"
"Talm se acerca en silencio mientras el último Soñador se desvanece."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... I don't know what to say."
msgstr "Yo... no sé qué decir."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Assuming this isn't all one horrid trick... that each of these people truly "
"are... somewhere... in this Dream."
msgstr ""
"Suponiendo que todo esto no sea un truco horrible... que cada una de estas "
"personas esté de verdad... en algún lugar... de este Sueño."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I know."
msgstr "Lo sé."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The calamity was so horrid, and the dangers of the outside world so "
"prevalent, my people decided to never face it again."
msgstr ""
"La calamidad fue tan horrible, y los peligros del mundo exterior tan "
"constantes, que mi pueblo decidió no volver a enfrentarse a ellos jamás."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No living summoner from my time can speak of it, but you know what we faced."
" We couldn't compete. We wouldn't have wanted to even if we could."
msgstr ""
"Ningún invocador vivo de mi época puede hablar de ello, pero ya sabes a qué "
"nos enfrentábamos. No podíamos competir. Ni aunque hubiéramos podido, "
"habríamos querido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And so, the Dream was born."
msgstr "Y así nació el Sueño."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The book from the Archive is a history book. How Respite came to be and... "
"the Dream we were building towards."
msgstr ""
"El libro del Archivo es un libro de historia. Cuenta cómo surgió Respite "
"y... el Sueño por el que trabajábamos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A world without war. Without death. Without wondering if we'd make it "
"through the next year. That book let kids hold onto hope for a better "
"future."
msgstr ""
"Un mundo sin guerra. Sin muerte. Sin preguntarnos si sobreviviríamos al año "
"siguiente. Ese libro permitía a los niños aferrarse a la esperanza de un "
"futuro mejor."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The city you attacked... they had people that wished for the same, I'm sure."
msgstr ""
"La ciudad que atacaste... seguro que allí también había gente que deseaba lo"
" mismo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I know that. Do you think for a moment that I don't know that?"
msgstr "Lo sé. ¿Crees por un momento que no lo sé?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There's never a night where my actions don't haunt me."
msgstr "No hay una sola noche en que mis actos no me atormenten."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Then how could you do it?"
msgstr "Entonces, ¿cómo pudiste hacerlo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Their souls."
msgstr "Sus almas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I needed a source of power to enact the ritual that let my people enter the "
"Dream."
msgstr ""
"Necesitaba una fuente de poder para llevar a cabo el ritual que permitió a "
"mi pueblo entrar en el Sueño."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Other clans got their power in other ways, but it always came from "
"somewhere."
msgstr ""
"Otros clanes obtenían su poder de otras formas, pero siempre salía de algún "
"sitio."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A forest clan, the Vieshar, when they brought forth their... you know."
msgstr ""
"Un clan del bosque, los Vieshar, cuando hicieron surgir a su... ya sabes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The energy it required caused all of the plant-life across half the "
"continent to wither and die. Millions starved when their plants couldn't "
"grow as the ground was fallow for a decade."
msgstr ""
"La energía que hizo falta marchitó y mató toda la vegetación de medio "
"continente. Millones murieron de hambre cuando sus cultivos no pudieron "
"crecer, pues la tierra quedó yerma durante una década."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That doesn't mean-"
msgstr "Eso no significa..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My people gave so much to create Respite, but it wasn't enough. There's a "
"reason we have that beast at the front. We were still pursued by those who "
"sought our power."
msgstr ""
"Mi pueblo dio muchísimo para crear Respite, pero no fue suficiente. Por algo"
" tenemos a esa bestia en la entrada. Seguían persiguiéndonos quienes "
"ansiaban nuestro poder."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We tried so hard to be left in peace. My people needed a place where they "
"could never be hurt again."
msgstr ""
"Nos esforzamos muchísimo para que nos dejaran en paz. Mi pueblo necesitaba "
"un lugar donde nunca más pudieran hacerle daño."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...I killed thousands all those years ago. I will never not feel the weight "
"of what I did."
msgstr ""
"...Maté a miles hace tantos años. Jamás dejaré de sentir el peso de lo que "
"hice."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But now, my people, my kids, are safe. So are thousands of others. Each and "
"every single one of these flowers was a person saved through what I did that"
" day."
msgstr ""
"Pero ahora mi pueblo, mis niños, están a salvo. Y también miles de otros. "
"Todas y cada una de estas flores son una persona que se salvó gracias a lo "
"que hice aquel día."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...I don't expect you to understand. But I do want you to know that what I "
"did was hardly even a footnote in history."
msgstr ""
"...No espero que lo entiendas. Pero sí quiero que sepas que lo que hice "
"apenas es una nota a pie de página en la historia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Why did you and Era bring us here, Talm?"
msgstr "¿Por qué nos trajisteis aquí Era y tú, Talm?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Go ask Era yourselves. She'll be waiting where you entered. There's nothing "
"more for us to show you."
msgstr ""
"Id a preguntárselo a Era vosotros mismos. Os estará esperando por donde "
"entrasteis. No tenemos nada más que enseñaros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I mean this sincerely, good luck."
msgstr "Os lo digo de corazón: buena suerte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm takes a shaky breath and waves you and [Companion Name] off, looking back down at the two flowers you first saw him tending to. The two of you look to each other, not even knowing where to begin with everything dropped on you. [Companion Name] brings you to a tower that stretches endlessly into the sky, and once you enter, you realize the circular platform was the one you fought Era and Talm on.\n"
"\n"
"After a ride to the top, the horrid, fleshy hallway you were chased in stretches out in front of you. Only one way out, it'd seem."
msgstr ""
"Talm respira hondo, tembloroso, y os despide a [Companion Name] y a ti con un gesto, volviendo a mirar las dos flores que estaba cuidando cuando lo viste por primera vez. Os miráis el uno al otro, sin saber siquiera por dónde empezar con todo lo que os ha caído encima. [Companion Name] te lleva hasta una torre que se alza sin fin hacia el cielo y, al entrar, te das cuenta de que la plataforma circular es aquella en la que luchasteis contra Era y Talm.\n"
"\n"
"Tras subir hasta lo más alto, el horrible pasillo de carne por el que os persiguieron se extiende ante vosotros. Solo hay una salida, por lo que parece."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This 'ought to be good!"
msgstr "¡Esto promete!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That's the best I've felt in a while."
msgstr "Hacía tiempo que no me sentía tan bien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The fetid hallway offers more resistance than it did before. Arms of twisted, mottled flesh grasp at the pair of you as you run by, narrow passages threaten to crush you as you pass. No beast chases you this time, but the urgency you feel to leave is no lesser for it.\n"
"\n"
"True to Talm's word, Era waits for you by the exit with a sad smile."
msgstr ""
"El pasillo fétido opone más resistencia que antes. Brazos de carne retorcida y moteada intentan agarraros al pasar, y los pasadizos estrechos amenazan con aplastaros. Esta vez no os persigue ninguna bestia, pero la urgencia por salir no es menor por ello.\n"
"\n"
"Tal como dijo Talm, Era os espera junto a la salida con una sonrisa triste."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I saw that you two and Talm talked..."
msgstr "He visto que habéis hablado con Talm..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I trust that you're ready to leave?"
msgstr "¿Supongo que estáis listos para marcharos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yes. We learned of... The Titan Wars, and bringing forth the Dreamers was..."
" enlightening when it came to practicing Summoning."
msgstr ""
"Sí. Hemos sabido de... las Guerras de los Titanes, y hacer surgir a los "
"Soñadores ha sido... revelador a la hora de practicar la invocación."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Though I don't know if I want anything to do with it after... all of this."
msgstr ""
"Aunque no sé si quiero tener nada que ver con ella después de... todo esto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Running from your pet was great for cardio, and when you ran me through with"
" your claws, I learned an important lesson about never trusting summoners "
"again."
msgstr ""
"Huir de vuestra mascota fue un gran ejercicio de cardio, y cuando me "
"atravesaste con tus garras aprendí una lección importante: no volver a "
"fiarme nunca de un invocador."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What we don't get is... why. Why all of this? If you fought so hard to bring"
" us here, why are you just... letting us go?"
msgstr ""
"Lo que no entendemos es... por qué. ¿Por qué todo esto? Si luchasteis tanto "
"para traernos aquí, ¿por qué ahora... nos dejáis marchar sin más?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "To prepare you."
msgstr "Para prepararos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I've seen what you two must face as you continue to face off against the "
"Soulsmiths."
msgstr ""
"He visto a lo que tendréis que enfrentaros mientras sigáis plantando cara a "
"los Forjaalmas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What was... described to you by the Dreamers is nothing compared to what the"
" Fateseekers saw all those years ago, at the end of the calamity."
msgstr ""
"Lo que... os han descrito los Soñadores no es nada comparado con lo que "
"vieron los Buscadestinos hace tantos años, al final de la calamidad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Going off of what Talm was saying..."
msgstr "Por lo que nos decía Talm..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Bringing forth a Titan comes at an enormous cost to the world, but it "
"wouldn't outright end it. "
msgstr ""
"Hacer surgir a un Titán tiene un coste enorme para el mundo, pero no "
"acabaría con él del todo. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is true... if the Soulsmiths intended to stop there."
msgstr "Es cierto... si los Forjaalmas pretendieran detenerse ahí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They will go further than any clan of my time ever could, as there are none "
"who can keep them in check."
msgstr ""
"Llegarán más lejos de lo que ningún clan de mi época pudo llegar jamás, "
"porque no hay nadie que pueda frenarlos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The calamity my people lived through shaped the world into what it is today."
" Despite the devastation, there was a delicate balance between the clans."
msgstr ""
"La calamidad que vivió mi pueblo dio forma al mundo tal como es hoy. Pese a "
"la devastación, existía un delicado equilibrio entre los clanes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Each had clan a... the same level of power. After decades of war, the world "
"was nearly uninhabitable."
msgstr ""
"Cada clan tenía un... el mismo nivel de poder. Tras décadas de guerra, el "
"mundo era casi inhabitable."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "To prevent their own extinction, those that remained released their..."
msgstr "Para evitar su propia extinción, los que quedaban liberaron a sus..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Titans..."
msgstr "¿Titanes...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yes. Back to the world. Plants grew again. The winds blew through the trees."
" Rain fell anew. The world began to heal with its natural power restored."
msgstr ""
"Sí. De vuelta al mundo. Las plantas volvieron a crecer. El viento volvió a "
"soplar entre los árboles. La lluvia volvió a caer. El mundo empezó a sanar "
"al recuperar su poder natural."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...But what does this have to do with us?"
msgstr "...Pero ¿qué tiene que ver esto con nosotros?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] and I... We came to the capitol chasing after ghosts, "
"wanting to know why our home was burnt to the ground by the Soulsmiths. To "
"make them pay, and return our people if they still lived."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] y yo... Vinimos a la capital persiguiendo fantasmas, "
"queriendo saber por qué los Forjaalmas redujeron nuestro hogar a cenizas. "
"Para hacérselo pagar y recuperar a nuestra gente si seguía con vida."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Why did you and Talm test us? To what end?"
msgstr "¿Por qué nos pusisteis a prueba Talm y tú? ¿Con qué fin?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your people will be used as fuel for the Soulsmith's beast. Like "
"thousands... no... millions, of others will be."
msgstr ""
"Vuestra gente servirá de combustible para la bestia de los Forjaalmas. Igual"
" que lo serán miles... no... millones de otros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The two of you are the first new summoners to learn the art within "
"centuries, outside of the Soulsmiths themselves."
msgstr ""
"Sois los primeros invocadores nuevos en aprender este arte en siglos, aparte"
" de los propios Forjaalmas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"How and why could we ever hope to stop them? Why does this fall on us, and "
"not you and Talm?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo y por qué íbamos a tener la menor esperanza de detenerlos? ¿Por qué "
"nos toca a nosotros y no a Talm y a ti?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Talm and I have been around for centuries, child."
msgstr "Talm y yo llevamos aquí siglos, criatura."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"In the few years the two of you have existed on this world in comparison, "
"you've already long-since exceeded our potential."
msgstr ""
"En los pocos años que lleváis vosotros en este mundo, en comparación, ya "
"hace tiempo que habéis superado nuestro potencial."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I will never expect you to understand or forgive our appearent betrayal, but"
" I promise you..."
msgstr ""
"Nunca esperaré que entendáis ni perdonéis nuestra aparente traición, pero os"
" prometo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This was the fastest, most effective way we could see to help you continue "
"to surpass us."
msgstr ""
"Que era la forma más rápida y eficaz que vimos de ayudaros a seguir "
"superándonos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...We didn't ask for this."
msgstr "...Nosotros no pedimos esto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I wish with all my heart that this was not your burden to bare."
msgstr "Desearía con todo mi corazón que esta carga no fuera vuestra."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But the world is unkind to us all, some more than others."
msgstr ""
"Pero el mundo es cruel con todos nosotros, con unos más que con otros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...What if we just... stopped? What then? Went back to Azamire, settled "
"down, and never thought about any of this ever again?"
msgstr ""
"...¿Y si simplemente... lo dejáramos? ¿Qué pasaría? ¿Volver a Azamire, "
"asentarnos y no volver a pensar en nada de esto nunca más?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Could you, knowing that there's even a sliver of a chance I'm correct?"
msgstr ""
"¿Podríais, sabiendo que hay aunque sea una mínima posibilidad de que yo "
"tenga razón?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Where would we even begin, without you and Talm?"
msgstr "...¿Por dónde íbamos a empezar siquiera, sin Talm y sin ti?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Far to the west are the Perilous Peaks, as I'm sure you know. Deep within, "
"the Nalidasi Dwarves maintain archives that far predate even the oldest "
"human civilizations."
msgstr ""
"Muy al oeste están los Picos Peligrosos, como sin duda sabéis. En lo más "
"profundo, los enanos nalidasi mantienen archivos mucho más antiguos incluso "
"que las civilizaciones humanas más remotas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...That's where I would start."
msgstr "...Yo empezaría por ahí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"For what it's worth, I'm sorry that this what Talm and I could offer you. I "
"wish we had more time to do this the right way."
msgstr ""
"Por si sirve de algo, siento que esto sea lo que Talm y yo hemos podido "
"ofreceros. Ojalá hubiéramos tenido más tiempo para hacerlo como es debido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] seems like she may have more to say, but turns a second later and reaches upward. The moment her hand touches the still, reflected pool of water that brought you into Respite, she bolts upward and out of the plane. You look to Era for only a moment before following after her.\n"
"\n"
"The trek back to the mainland is much calmer than the one here, especially now with experience. You and [Companion Name] hardly share a word the entire trip back.\n"
"\n"
"You sail further south than Tidebreak, heading back towards the capitol, unsure of what to do or where to go. Both of you go through the motions as you arrive at port, register your vessel, and pay for it to remain docked for some time. Checking with locals and accounting for travel to and from Gloomstone, it'd seem you were only in Respite for an hour, but you know it was much longer than that, and you guess that time moves differently there.\n"
"\n"
"You wander the streets for a while before [Companion Name] suggests a nearby tavern. The two of you share a room, feeling a bit too unsteady to be apart for now. You don't even know where to begin, and your best friend seems to feel similarly, until she tosses your weapon to you. She's determined not to let anyone get the best of her again, and wants to spar. You smile for the first time in a while."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] parece tener algo más que decir, pero un segundo después se da la vuelta y alarga la mano hacia arriba. En cuanto su mano toca el estanque de agua quieta y reflectante que os trajo a Respite, sale disparada hacia arriba y abandona el plano. Miras a Era solo un instante antes de seguirla.\n"
"\n"
"El viaje de vuelta al continente es mucho más tranquilo que el de ida, sobre todo ahora que tenéis experiencia. [Companion Name] y tú apenas cruzáis palabra en todo el trayecto.\n"
"\n"
"Navegáis más al sur que Tidebreak, de vuelta hacia la capital, sin saber qué hacer ni adónde ir. Los dos hacéis las cosas de forma mecánica al llegar a puerto: registráis vuestra embarcación y pagáis para que siga amarrada una temporada. Tras preguntar a los lugareños y calcular el viaje de ida y vuelta a Gloomstone, parece que solo estuvisteis en Respite una hora, pero sabes que fue mucho más, y supones que allí el tiempo transcurre de otra forma.\n"
"\n"
"Vagáis un rato por las calles hasta que [Companion Name] propone ir a una taberna cercana. Compartís habitación, pues os sentís demasiado inestables para separaros por ahora. Ni siquiera sabes por dónde empezar, y tu mejor amiga parece sentir lo mismo, hasta que te lanza tu arma. Está decidida a no dejar que nadie vuelva a poder con ella, y quiere entrenar. Sonríes por primera vez en mucho tiempo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your time in Respite left you shaken and unsure of yourself. You definitely grew in the untold amount of time you stayed there, but if you were to follow the path laid out for you, is there any amount of growth that'd prepare you for what's to come? These thoughts come and go as you clash with [Companion Name]. As the two of you duel into the night, doubtlessly disturbing the other guests, you slowly let your time in Respite wash away from your mind.\n"
"\n"
"Whatever tomorrow brings will be tomorrow's problem. For now, [Companion Name] is safe, alive, and so are you.\n"
"\n"
"And for now, that's enough."
msgstr ""
"Tu estancia en Respite te ha dejado conmocionado e inseguro. Sin duda creciste durante el tiempo incalculable que pasaste allí, pero si siguieras el camino que te han trazado, ¿habría crecimiento suficiente para prepararte para lo que se avecina? Estos pensamientos van y vienen mientras chocas armas con [Companion Name]. Mientras os batís en duelo hasta bien entrada la noche, molestando sin duda al resto de huéspedes, dejas que tu tiempo en Respite se vaya borrando poco a poco de tu mente.\n"
"\n"
"Lo que traiga el mañana será problema del mañana. Por ahora, [Companion Name] está a salvo, con vida, y tú también.\n"
"\n"
"Y por ahora, eso basta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ20"
msgstr "MQ20"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Path to the Peaks - The next leg of your journey has been laid out before "
"you. The Perilous Peaks lay far to the north, the surrounding lands mostly "
"untouched by civilization, but with no better leads, it remains your best "
"path forward."
msgstr ""
"Camino a los Picos: El siguiente tramo de tu viaje se extiende ante ti. Los "
"Picos Peligrosos se alzan muy al norte, rodeados de tierras casi vírgenes de"
" civilización, pero sin mejores pistas, sigue siendo tu mejor camino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I've got first watch, I suppose."
msgstr "Supongo que me toca la primera guardia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Something's out there!"
msgstr "¡Hay algo ahí fuera!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Stocked up on provisions and as mentally prepared as you can be, you and [Companion Name], set off, leaving the capitol far behind. Things remain in this strange state of... flux, where the both of you try your best to pretend the weight of everything that happened in Respite hasn't been weighing on your shoulders.\n"
"\n"
"As you sit by this night's campfire, several days into your journey now, [Companion Name] drives her hatchet into a log she was splitting for kindling and turns to face you."
msgstr ""
"Con provisiones de sobra y tan preparados mentalmente como podéis estar, [Companion Name] y tú os ponéis en marcha y dejáis atrás la capital. Las cosas siguen en este extraño estado de... cambio, en el que ambos intentáis por todos los medios fingir que el peso de todo lo ocurrido en Respite no os lastra los hombros.\n"
"\n"
"Mientras estáis sentados junto a la hoguera de esta noche, ya con varios días de viaje a cuestas, [Companion Name] clava su hacha en un tronco que estaba partiendo para hacer astillas y se vuelve hacia ti."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I loathe this, [Player Name]."
msgstr "Odio esto, [Player Name]."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't mind splitting the wood tonight, just give me a sec-"
msgstr "No me importa partir la leña esta noche, dame un segundo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You know that's not what I mean."
msgstr "Sabes que no me refiero a eso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This whole... funk. It's like we both died a little in Respite and have been"
" little walking corpses ever since."
msgstr ""
"Todo este... bajón. Es como si los dos hubiéramos muerto un poco en Respite "
"y desde entonces fuéramos dos cadáveres andantes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I haven't been me, and you... haven't been you."
msgstr "Yo no he sido yo, y tú... no has sido tú."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I know."
msgstr "...Lo sé."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't know... how we're meant to act, now."
msgstr "No sé... cómo se supone que tenemos que actuar ahora."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I feel so deep in over my head. We came out here to find a couple people "
"from Azamire and now we're..."
msgstr ""
"Siento que esto me viene enorme. Vinimos aquí a buscar a un par de personas "
"de Azamire y ahora estamos..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What, heading to the home of the Dwarves to learn about Summoning? To what "
"end?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué, de camino al hogar de los enanos para aprender sobre la invocación? "
"¿Con qué fin?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I always knew that you'd leave Azamire and do something great, but me?"
msgstr "Siempre supe que te irías de Azamire y harías algo grande, pero ¿yo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You've gone through everything I have, and I'd argue more. "
msgstr "Has pasado por todo lo que he pasado yo, y diría que por más. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I have no idea if what Era says is true. I truly hope it isn't."
msgstr ""
"No tengo ni idea de si lo que dice Era es cierto. Espero de verdad que no lo"
" sea."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But... Despite how stupid their little test was, and how much I wish they "
"would have just been honest from the get go..."
msgstr ""
"Pero... Aunque su pruebecita fuera una estupidez, y por mucho que desee que "
"hubieran sido sinceros desde el principio..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Era is right, at least about needing to help. I've seen too much to just... "
"go back home."
msgstr ""
"Era tiene razón, al menos en que hay que ayudar. He visto demasiado como "
"para... volver a casa sin más."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I mean, how could we? I feel that our days back in Azamire, even before the "
"attack, are so far behind us."
msgstr ""
"Es decir, ¿cómo íbamos a hacerlo? Siento que nuestros días en Azamire, "
"incluso antes del ataque, han quedado muy atrás."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I just... don't know where we belong anymore."
msgstr "Es que... ya no sé cuál es nuestro sitio."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Believe me, I'm in the same boat..."
msgstr "Créeme, estoy en las mismas..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't want to lose ourselves while we figure out where that is."
msgstr "No quiero que nos perdamos mientras averiguamos dónde está."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You leave it there as [Companion Name] sits beside you on your log-turned-"
"seat and rests her head on your shoulder. You feel... lighter, and only hope"
" that you find your place in all this mess. You shift a bit, getting ready "
"to stand before you hear [Companion Name] start to snore."
msgstr ""
"Lo dejáis ahí mientras [Companion Name] se sienta a tu lado en el tronco que"
" os sirve de asiento y apoya la cabeza en tu hombro. Te sientes... más "
"ligero, y solo esperas encontrar tu lugar en todo este lío. Te mueves un "
"poco para levantarte, justo antes de oír a [Companion Name] empezar a "
"roncar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It looks like a whole pack has come out to greet us."
msgstr "Parece que ha venido toda una manada a saludarnos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're gonna have to move camp."
msgstr "Vamos a tener que mover el campamento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your mind wasn't playing tricks on you. The small snap of a branch here, something disturbing the underbrush there. It's always difficult to differentiate between the general comings and goings of creatures in the night, and when something is actively stalking you.\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately, this is the later. You bolt upright and draw your weapon, waking [Companion Name] in the process as a particularly large Rockwolf charges right for you."
msgstr ""
"Tu mente no te estaba jugando una mala pasada. El chasquido de una rama por aquí, algo que agita la maleza por allá. Siempre cuesta distinguir entre el ir y venir habitual de las criaturas nocturnas y algo que te está acechando.\n"
"\n"
"Por desgracia, esto es lo segundo. Te incorporas de un salto y desenvainas tu arma, despertando de paso a [Companion Name], mientras un lobo de roca especialmente grande carga directo hacia ti."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ughhh, what... are you doing?"
msgstr "Uffff, ¿qué... estás haciendo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "[Companion Name] wake up!"
msgstr "¡[Companion Name], despierta!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Dinner came to us tonight, it looks like."
msgstr "Parece que esta noche la cena ha venido a nosotros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Seeing you prepared for it, the beast diverts its charge and instead runs past you, and darting back into the woods, outside of the light of your campfire.\n"
"\n"
"Just outside of the clearing you can see the firelight reflect off of eyes. Lots of eyes."
msgstr ""
"Al ver que estás preparado, la bestia desvía su carga y pasa de largo junto a ti, volviendo a meterse en el bosque, fuera de la luz de vuestra hoguera.\n"
"\n"
"Justo al borde del claro ves la luz del fuego reflejada en unos ojos. Muchos ojos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is some of the toughest meat I've worked with..."
msgstr "Esta es de las carnes más duras con las que he trabajado..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This smells and looks way better than expected."
msgstr "Esto huele y tiene mucha mejor pinta de lo que esperaba."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Huffing and puffing the cool night air, you hold your weapon aloft, "
"challenging more of the beasts to come out. Far fewer of the pack remain, "
"and those that do decide that they've bitten off more than they can chew "
"once the biggest of them lies dead at your feet and dart off into the trees,"
" but not before one grabs your pack of provisions out of the tree it was "
"hung up in. No one had said anything about wolves about the size of horses, "
"so you didn't think to hang your food that high."
msgstr ""
"Jadeando en el fresco aire nocturno, mantienes el arma en alto, desafiando a"
" más bestias a salir. Quedan muchos menos miembros de la manada, y los que "
"quedan deciden que han mordido más de lo que pueden masticar cuando el más "
"grande de ellos yace muerto a tus pies, y huyen hacia los árboles, aunque no"
" sin que uno se lleve vuestra bolsa de provisiones del árbol en el que "
"estaba colgada. Nadie había dicho nada de lobos del tamaño de caballos, así "
"que no se te ocurrió colgar la comida tan alto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well... good morning, [Companion Name]."
msgstr "Bueno... buenos días, [Companion Name]."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You know how I always told you I wanted a dog?"
msgstr "¿Te acuerdas de que siempre te decía que quería un perro?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I might get a cat instead."
msgstr "Puede que me compre un gato."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Don't bring that evil on us, I know there's some scary kitties up in the "
"Peaks."
msgstr ""
"No nos eches ese mal fario, sé que hay unos gatitos que dan miedo allá "
"arriba, en los Picos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Knowing our luck, we'd wake up with one nibbling one of our arms."
msgstr ""
"Con la suerte que tenemos, nos despertaríamos con uno mordisqueándonos un "
"brazo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A girl can dream."
msgstr "Soñar es gratis."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wolves took our food, didn't they?"
msgstr "Los lobos se llevaron nuestra comida, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If they just wanted that, they could have grabbed it and been gone without "
"trying to go for our throats."
msgstr ""
"Si solo querían eso, podrían haberla cogido y largarse sin intentar ir a por"
" nuestras gargantas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think they just took it as a consolation prize."
msgstr "Creo que se la llevaron como premio de consolación."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They'll need some consoling after eating it. Hardtack and some... absolutely"
" foul pemmican isn't exactly the height of camping food."
msgstr ""
"Van a necesitar consuelo después de comérsela. Galletas de barco y un "
"pemmican... absolutamente asqueroso no son precisamente lo mejor de la "
"comida de acampada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, we do still have to eat something. Nothing stopping us from having "
"them, right?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, algo tenemos que comer. Nada nos impide comérnoslos a ellos, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gotta do something with the bodies."
msgstr "Algo habrá que hacer con los cuerpos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I've never had wolf before, but they have to be stringy right?"
msgstr "Nunca he comido lobo, pero tiene que ser fibroso, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And I don't know how keen I am on eating something that has maybe eaten a "
"person before."
msgstr ""
"Y no sé si me apetece mucho comer algo que quizá se haya comido a una "
"persona."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's a rare day someone comes this far north, I'd say the odds they've eaten"
" someone are low."
msgstr ""
"Rara vez alguien llega tan al norte; yo diría que las probabilidades de que "
"se hayan comido a alguien son bajas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That doesn't sound like zero."
msgstr "Eso no suena a cero."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But well, when in Emor."
msgstr "Pero bueno, si a Amor fueres, haz lo que vieres."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Where's that?"
msgstr "...¿Dónde está eso?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Dunno. Something I heard people in the capitol saying."
msgstr "...Ni idea. Algo que le oí decir a la gente en la capital."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You get some rest, I'll work on getting all these bodies prepared."
msgstr "Descansa un poco, yo me encargo de preparar todos estos cuerpos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Surely nothing will get attracted by all the corpses."
msgstr "Seguro que todos estos cadáveres no atraen a nada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Surely."
msgstr "Seguro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll feed you to them first, if you just jinxed us."
msgstr "Si nos acabas de gafar, te daré de comer a ellos el primero."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I will never expect you to understand or forgive our apparent betrayal, but "
"I promise you..."
msgstr ""
"Nunca esperaré que entendáis ni perdonéis nuestra aparente traición, pero os"
" prometo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's almost like they don't want people coming up here!"
msgstr "¡Es casi como si no quisieran que la gente subiera hasta aquí!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Surely they'll be glad to see us."
msgstr "Seguro que se alegran de vernos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The magic-enhanced tools you picked up back in the capitol help you make quick work of the pile, at least compared to what it'd usually take you. [Companion Name] takes the freshly cooked steaks as you finish with them and gives them a bit of extra love and seasoning once you're done. With fresh food and better spirits, you pack up camp and head further towards the peaks.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you nibble smoked strips of rockwolf as you walk. It's very crunchy."
msgstr ""
"Las herramientas mejoradas con magia que compraste en la capital te ayudan a despachar el montón en poco tiempo, al menos comparado con lo que te costaría normalmente. [Companion Name] coge los filetes recién hechos a medida que los terminas y les da un toque extra de cariño y condimento cuando acabas. Con comida fresca y mejor ánimo, recogéis el campamento y avanzáis hacia los picos.\n"
"\n"
"Los dos vais mordisqueando tiras ahumadas de lobo de roca mientras camináis. Son muy crujientes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wow, this is... really good!"
msgstr "Vaya, esto está... ¡buenísimo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I think every meal is made a little better if it tried to eat you first."
msgstr ""
"Creo que cualquier comida sabe un poco mejor si antes intentó comerte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I mean, really, it's only fair when you think about it. Spite tastes good."
msgstr "O sea, en serio, si lo piensas es lo justo. El rencor está rico."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Though, these herbs you found definitely help. "
msgstr "Aunque estas hierbas que encontraste ayudan, sin duda. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The forest provides. Makes me wonder what other kinds of creatures taste "
"like."
msgstr "El bosque provee. Me hace preguntarme a qué sabrán otras criaturas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I really liked that Stonehopper back in the Broken Pass, too."
msgstr "A mí también me gustó mucho aquel saltapiedras del Paso roto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, both these and the wolves are pretty much just bigger, scarier "
"versions of creatures we already know."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, tanto estos como los lobos no son más que versiones más grandes y "
"aterradoras de criaturas que ya conocemos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I didn't expect to like the wolf this much, but what about some weird stuff?"
msgstr "No esperaba que me gustara tanto el lobo, pero ¿y algo raro?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Like... Slimes?"
msgstr "¿Como... los viscosos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ooo, that's interesting. Maybe they'd be like some kind of... gelatin?"
msgstr "Uy, eso es interesante. ¿Serán como una especie de... gelatina?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I hope so."
msgstr "...Eso espero."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If we run out of food, maybe we go check out a dungeon and see what kind of "
"creatures we can find?"
msgstr ""
"Si nos quedamos sin comida, ¿qué tal si vamos a echar un vistazo a una "
"mazmorra y vemos qué criaturas encontramos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Might be delicious, might poison us and we die horribly."
msgstr ""
"Puede que estén deliciosas, o puede que nos envenenen y muramos de forma "
"horrible."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm down."
msgstr "Me apunto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you travel onward, the dense forest gives way to rocky slopes. Little by "
"little you find yourselves walking less and scrambling more, until the "
"journey has turned into an outright climb. The entrance to the Dwarves' home"
" is not one they wanted visitors to get to easily, it'd seem."
msgstr ""
"A medida que avanzáis, el denso bosque da paso a laderas rocosas. Poco a "
"poco camináis menos y trepáis más, hasta que el viaje se convierte en una "
"escalada en toda regla. Por lo que parece, los enanos no querían que la "
"entrada a su hogar fuera fácil de alcanzar para los visitantes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You and [Companion Name] take turns lugging your gear up the mountainside. You're sure you were told the entrance to the dwarven capitol was somewhere around here, but \"lower eastern side of those mountains over there\" weren't exactly prime directions from a group of what seemed to be well-meaning schoolkids. They said the entrance was hidden, and that those seeking the dwarves would likely have to climb for days or weeks, to find the entrance. Nevertheless, blissfully far from the peak but still not easy to access, a large gate carved into the stone stands before you, presumably leading deeper into the mountain. On a low wall flanking either side of the gate, a squat dwarf with a short-trimmed blond beard naps soundly, resting his chin on the pommel of his large maul in what appears to be a heavily practiced position.\n"
"\n"
"You clear your throat a couple of times, trying to get his attention, but to no avail. So, you walk up and his helmet with your knuckle, just barely able to reach him atop the wall. He wakes with a shout, wide-eyed and startled by your presence, so much so that he careens backward off the wall. You quickly scramble after him and find the dwarf unconscious - but breathing - on the other side.\n"
"\n"
"You don't know how you're going to explain this to the rest of the dwarves."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] y tú os turnáis para cargar con el equipo ladera arriba. Estás seguro de que os dijeron que la entrada a la capital enana estaba por aquí, pero «la parte baja de la ladera este de aquellas montañas de allí» no eran precisamente unas indicaciones de primera, viniendo de un grupo de escolares que parecían tener buena intención. Dijeron que la entrada estaba oculta, y que quienes buscaran a los enanos probablemente tendrían que escalar durante días o semanas para encontrarla. Aun así, por suerte lejos de la cima pero todavía de difícil acceso, ante vosotros se alza una gran puerta tallada en la piedra, que se supone que se adentra en la montaña. Sobre un muro bajo que flanquea la puerta, un enano rechoncho con una barba rubia bien recortada duerme a pierna suelta, con la barbilla apoyada en el pomo de su enorme mazo, en lo que parece una postura muy practicada.\n"
"\n"
"Carraspeas un par de veces para llamar su atención, pero en vano. Así que te acercas y le das unos golpecitos en el casco con los nudillos, alcanzándolo a duras penas en lo alto del muro. Se despierta con un grito, con los ojos como platos y tan sobresaltado por tu presencia que cae de espaldas por el otro lado del muro. Te apresuras a ir tras él y encuentras al enano inconsciente (pero respirando) al otro lado.\n"
"\n"
"No sabes cómo vas a explicarle esto al resto de los enanos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ21"
msgstr "MQ21"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Dwarf Blood - With the sole Nalidasi guard unconscious at your feet and a "
"gate blocking your path, you're going to have some explaining to do."
msgstr ""
"Sangre enana: Con el único guardia nalidasi inconsciente a tus pies y una "
"puerta cortándote el paso, vas a tener que dar muchas explicaciones."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It it a pull door..?"
msgstr "¿Es una puerta de tirar...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ah! A push door! Oh... wait, no."
msgstr "¡Ah! ¡Una puerta de empujar! Oh... espera, no."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You quickly look around as [Companion Name] scrambles up the low wall after "
"you. She lightly thumps your back once she stands beside you, then bends "
"down to check the dwarf."
msgstr ""
"Echas un vistazo rápido a tu alrededor mientras [Companion Name] trepa el "
"muro bajo detrás de ti. Te da una palmadita en la espalda en cuanto está a "
"tu lado y luego se agacha para examinar al enano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They should consider making you an ambassador, truly remarkable work [Player"
" Name]."
msgstr ""
"Deberían nombrarte embajador, un trabajo verdaderamente admirable, [Player "
"Name]."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "He was sleeping, I just wanted to wake him up!"
msgstr "¡Estaba dormido, solo quería despertarlo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Just giving you a hard time."
msgstr "Solo te estoy tomando el pelo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Unfortunately - intentions aside - it looks like you've had a bit of the "
"opposite effect."
msgstr ""
"Por desgracia, intenciones aparte, parece que has conseguido justo lo "
"contrario."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I guess we'll have to let ourselves in, and then find some way of "
"explaining... this."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que tendremos que entrar por nuestra cuenta y luego buscar la forma "
"de explicar... esto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You look over the gate and wall and just barely spot it. A small stone hatch, likely more typically used as an entrance so they don't have to open and close the main gate all the time. Though, with a path like the one you travelled, it's a wonder they made such a gate in the first place.\n"
"\n"
"As expected the hatch is shut and locked, with no apparent keyhole or method of opening. You get to work trying to open it regardless while [Companion Name] wraps the dwarf's head."
msgstr ""
"Examinas la puerta y el muro y apenas logras distinguirla. Una pequeña trampilla de piedra, que seguramente se usa más a menudo como entrada para no tener que abrir y cerrar la puerta principal todo el tiempo. Aunque, con un camino como el que has recorrido, es un misterio que llegaran a construir semejante puerta.\n"
"\n"
"Como era de esperar, la trampilla está cerrada con llave, sin cerradura visible ni forma aparente de abrirla. Aun así, te pones manos a la obra para intentar abrirla mientras [Companion Name] venda la cabeza del enano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's see what this dwarf has got!"
msgstr "¡Veamos de qué es capaz este enano!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not bad, not bad."
msgstr "Nada mal, nada mal."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You try half a dozen methods of opening the hatch until you realize that it's magically imbued. While there are methods for figuring out the words for opening magic locks, you hardly feel you have the time to do so. Eventually you give up on any gentle method of opening and just jam your tools through the side and start to pry while saying every version of 'open' you can think of.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually, it gives way, and you're not sure about what worked specifically, but it hardly matters. You peer down the hatch to find a squat tunnel. You grab the unconscious dwarf and throw him over your shoulder, then head down the tunnel with [Companion] just behind you.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually the tunnel opens up into a small chamber with two dwarves cheerfully playing some form of dice game. The two look at you with shock, the shorter of the two runs for the door leading out and latches it - keeping you from progressing further - while the one who is more stout hefts a large blade in your direction and frowns."
msgstr ""
"Pruebas media docena de métodos para abrir la trampilla hasta que te das cuenta de que está imbuida de magia. Aunque existen métodos para averiguar las palabras que abren las cerraduras mágicas, no crees tener tiempo para ello. Al final renuncias a cualquier método delicado, metes tus herramientas por el lateral y empiezas a hacer palanca mientras dices todas las versiones de «ábrete» que se te ocurren.\n"
"\n"
"Al final cede, y no sabes muy bien qué ha funcionado exactamente, pero da igual. Te asomas por la trampilla y ves un túnel bajo. Coges al enano inconsciente, te lo echas al hombro y bajas por el túnel con [Companion] justo detrás de ti.\n"
"\n"
"Al final, el túnel desemboca en una pequeña cámara donde dos enanos juegan alegremente a algún tipo de juego de dados. Los dos te miran estupefactos; el más bajo corre hacia la puerta de salida y la atranca (impidiéndote avanzar), mientras el más fornido levanta una gran espada en tu dirección con el ceño fruncido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oi! What are you doin' with Humphrey?"
msgstr "¡Eh! ¿Qué haces con Humphrey?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Attackers! Thought you'd pull a fast one on us, eh?"
msgstr "¡Atacantes! Creíais que nos la ibais a colar, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "No, no! Easy now, I'm not here to hurt anyone."
msgstr "¡No, no! Tranquilos, no he venido a hacer daño a nadie."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Little late for that, don't ya think?"
msgstr "Un poco tarde para eso, ¿no crees?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I-"
msgstr "Yo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your friend was so startled by seeing two humans pop up over the cliff that "
"he fell off the wall he was sitting on."
msgstr ""
"Vuestro amigo se asustó tanto al ver a dos humanos aparecer por el borde del"
" acantilado que se cayó del muro en el que estaba sentado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Ah."
msgstr "...Ah."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Yeah, that sounds like our Humphrey. Thanks for haulin' him down here"
msgstr ""
"Sí, eso suena a nuestro Humphrey. Gracias por traerlo hasta aquí abajo"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So, are we okay?"
msgstr "Entonces, ¿estamos en paz?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Suppose so. I'm Tee, human. Short one over there is Pout."
msgstr "Supongo que sí. Soy Tee, humano. El bajito de ahí es Pout."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What're your names?"
msgstr "¿Cómo os llamáis?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's a pleasure, sorry we gave you and your friend quite the start."
msgstr ""
"Es un placer, sentimos haberos dado semejante susto a ti y a tu amigo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Meh, it's good to get the heart racing every once in a while."
msgstr "Bah, viene bien que el corazón se acelere de vez en cuando."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Gotta ask ya though, why'd you come up through our expedition entrance?"
msgstr ""
"Pero tengo que preguntaros, ¿por qué habéis subido por nuestra entrada de "
"expediciones?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...is there a different entrance?"
msgstr "...¿hay otra entrada?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh yeah, just another stone's throw north. Got it all freshly paved n' "
"everything."
msgstr ""
"Pues sí, un poco más al norte, a tiro de piedra. Recién pavimentada y todo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's real nice, you shoulda gone there. We don't get visitors often, "
"especially not humans."
msgstr ""
"Está muy bien, deberíais haber ido por allí. No solemos recibir visitas, y "
"menos de humanos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This one is for our... well, don't know if we can share that. But suffice to"
" say, it's mainly an exit. "
msgstr ""
"Esta es para nuestras... bueno, no sé si podemos contarlo. Pero digamos que "
"es más bien una salida. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Honestly surprised you even found it, let alone climbed up here!"
msgstr ""
"La verdad, ¡me sorprende que la encontrarais, y más que subierais hasta "
"aquí!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll buy ya a drink later if we see ya, wanna hear about that climb!"
msgstr ""
"¡Os invitamos a una copa luego si os vemos, quiero que nos contéis esa "
"escalada!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm going to find those kids when we get back to the capitol."
msgstr "Pienso ir a buscar a esos niños cuando volvamos a la capital."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well! It's a pleasure to meet you both. Shall we leave Humphry with you, "
"then?"
msgstr ""
"¡Bueno! Es un placer conoceros a los dos. ¿Os dejamos a Humphry, entonces?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...Well, we'll bring ya to the capitol, but we need to go ask around first. "
"I think the two of you are the first human visitors we've had in a few years"
" at least!"
msgstr ""
"...Bueno, os llevaremos a la capital, pero antes tenemos que preguntar por "
"ahí. ¡Creo que sois los primeros visitantes humanos que tenemos en al menos "
"unos cuantos años!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Tee nods at the statement and unlatches the door and heads out to whether it may lead. Pout fishes around in a pouch on his waist and withdraws a flask and wafts it under Humphrey's nose, who groggily comes to. He takes the flask and takes a sip, instantly regaining his ruddy complexion. As he looks around in a daze, he blushes, embarrassed by the whole endeavor.\n"
"\n"
"As the four of you wait, Humphrey asks if you'd give him a chance to regain a bit of his pride with a little bout."
msgstr ""
"Tee asiente ante el comentario, abre la puerta y sale hacia donde quiera que lleve. Pout rebusca en una bolsa que lleva a la cintura, saca un frasco y se lo pasa por debajo de la nariz a Humphrey, que vuelve en sí aturdido. Coge el frasco, da un sorbo y recupera al instante su tez rubicunda. Mientras mira a su alrededor desconcertado, se sonroja, avergonzado por todo el asunto.\n"
"\n"
"Mientras los cuatro esperáis, Humphrey te pregunta si le darías la oportunidad de recuperar un poco de su orgullo con un pequeño combate."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Don't have much of a choice now, do we?"
msgstr "Ahora no tenemos mucha elección, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Even the king?!"
msgstr "...¡¿Hasta el rey?!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Every time you knock the dwarf down, he sips a bit from the flask again and gets right back up, ready to go again. He's a good fighter, and though you are better, it feels like you are fighting a small platoon one-by-one. [Companion Name] steps in a few times as well, either looking to give you a break or flex her own skills.\n"
"\n"
"Despite the fact that the chamber is well-lit and Pout dragged all the furniture out of the way, the low ceilings make for a cramped fighting place for the two of you, and you have to spend a lot of mental energy to not bash your head or weapons on the ceiling while dodging the dwarf's blows.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually Tee re-enters the room with another dwarf alongside him. The newcomer has a bushy white beard that nearly trails down to the floor, and sits atop a floating disk of metal, lit by intricate patterns of runes and glowing engravings all throughout its surface. You hardly have the time to inspect it before the newcomer clears his throat."
msgstr ""
"Cada vez que derribas al enano, da otro sorbo del frasco y se levanta enseguida, listo para seguir. Es un buen luchador y, aunque tú eres mejor, sientes que te enfrentas a un pequeño pelotón uno a uno. [Companion Name] también interviene unas cuantas veces, ya sea para darte un respiro o para lucir sus propias habilidades.\n"
"\n"
"Aunque la cámara está bien iluminada y Pout ha apartado todos los muebles, el techo bajo convierte el lugar en un espacio estrecho para que luchéis, y tienes que gastar mucha energía mental para no golpearte la cabeza ni el arma contra el techo mientras esquivas los golpes del enano.\n"
"\n"
"Al final, Tee vuelve a entrar en la sala acompañado de otro enano. El recién llegado tiene una poblada barba blanca que casi le llega al suelo y va sentado sobre un disco de metal flotante, iluminado por intrincados patrones de runas y grabados brillantes por toda su superficie. Apenas tienes tiempo de examinarlo antes de que el recién llegado carraspee."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"*Ahem*. Greetings, tall-folk. I am the grand Archivist and royal advisor to "
"the king."
msgstr ""
"*Ejem*. Saludos, gente alta. Soy el gran Archivero y consejero real del rey."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I bring tidings from our 37th ruler, Oyadazminis, who welcomes you into our "
"home to look upon our works, cherish our history, and hopefully... and I "
"quote, \"drink until you hit the floor.\""
msgstr ""
"Os traigo noticias de nuestro 37.º soberano, Oyadazminis, que os da la "
"bienvenida a nuestro hogar para que contempléis nuestras obras, apreciéis "
"nuestra historia y, con suerte... y cito textualmente, «bebáis hasta caer "
"redondos»."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If you have any other desires or aspirations while visiting Koganusan, they "
"may be granted, should we deem you worthy of such requests."
msgstr ""
"Si tenéis cualquier otro deseo o aspiración durante vuestra visita a "
"Koganusan, puede que se os conceda, si os consideramos dignos de tales "
"peticiones."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This may be too lofty of an ask - please forgive our trespasses if so - but "
"we hear the Nalidasi Archives are quite the sight to behold."
msgstr ""
"Puede que sea pedir demasiado (y si es así, perdonad nuestro atrevimiento), "
"pero hemos oído que los Archivos nalidasi son todo un espectáculo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...is that so? I can count the number of times a human has been allowed into"
" our archives on one hand since Koganusan was just a hole in the dirt."
msgstr ""
"...¿ah, sí? Puedo contar con los dedos de una mano las veces que se ha "
"permitido a un humano entrar en nuestros archivos desde que Koganusan no era"
" más que un agujero en la tierra."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So, forgive me if I think you're full of silt."
msgstr "Así que perdonadme si creo que estáis llenos de cieno."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...They've almost doubtlessly changed their names through the years, but do "
"Era and Talm ring a bell?"
msgstr ""
"...Es casi seguro que se han cambiado el nombre con los años, pero ¿os "
"suenan Era y Talm?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not even remotely."
msgstr "Ni lo más mínimo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What about two ageless Sum-"
msgstr "¿Y qué hay de dos eternos invoca...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As the word starts to leave your mouth, the Archivist's eyes go wide and he snaps his fingers, and you find the words silent as they leave your mouth. He chuckles and bids the guards farewell, then snaps again. You find yourselves in front of a grand throne that's equal parts imposing and gaudy. In it sits a dwarf you'd guess is middle aged, with a dark beard studded with gemstones and clasps of metal, similar to the crown atop his head.\n"
"\n"
"You've been brought into what would seem to be a lavish banquet as table after table of divine looking food and immaculately dressed dwarves fill the throne room.\n"
"\n"
"The guests look at your studden entrance with curiosity and excitement, which you consider to be better than suspicion and fear. The Archivist floats up to the king and whispers in his ear, and his eyes go from interest, to shock, and then... excitement. He claps his hands once and hands before the room, then announces to everyone that the entertainment has arrived.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you are ushered into the center of the room, then, one by one, several of the more rugged nobles in the room, along with their guards, encircle you.\n"
"\n"
"The king announces that you're not to be killed, only to be given a proper welcome to the kingdom, whatever that may mean. You don't know if it particularly matters based on how quickly you're swarmed by the nobles and their guards."
msgstr ""
"En cuanto la palabra empieza a salir de tu boca, el Archivero abre mucho los ojos y chasquea los dedos, y te das cuenta de que las palabras salen de tu boca sin sonido. Suelta una risita, se despide de los guardias y vuelve a chasquear los dedos. Os encontráis ante un gran trono a partes iguales imponente y recargado. En él se sienta un enano que dirías de mediana edad, con una barba oscura tachonada de gemas y broches de metal, a juego con la corona que lleva en la cabeza.\n"
"\n"
"Os han llevado a lo que parece un banquete fastuoso: mesa tras mesa de comida de aspecto divino y enanos impecablemente vestidos llenan la sala del trono.\n"
"\n"
"Los invitados miran vuestra repentina entrada con curiosidad y entusiasmo, lo cual consideras mejor que la sospecha y el miedo. El Archivero flota hasta el rey y le susurra al oído, y su mirada pasa del interés a la sorpresa y luego... al entusiasmo. Da una palmada y alza las manos ante la sala, y anuncia a todos que ha llegado el entretenimiento.\n"
"\n"
"Os conducen a los dos al centro de la sala y, entonces, uno a uno, varios de los nobles más robustos de la sala, junto con sus guardias, os rodean.\n"
"\n"
"El rey anuncia que no se os debe matar, solo daros una buena bienvenida al reino, signifique eso lo que signifique. No sabes si importa demasiado, a juzgar por lo rápido que se os echan encima los nobles y sus guardias."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Nothing too scary, then?"
msgstr "Nada demasiado aterrador, entonces, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "She seems pleased."
msgstr "Parece satisfecha."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you beat down the guards and nobles who look at you expectantly, you wouldn't have guessed the king himself would have risen to join in on the fun, but through no small deal of effort, he fell like the rest of his people. You tried your best to not kill the man, but with how hard he hit the ground, you wonder if you overdid it.\n"
"\n"
"You clutch your weapon, covered in more blood than you ever would have expected for a 'friendly' bout. With the Nalidaian king at your feet, you eye the Archivist, worried that despite the promise of this just being for 'entertainment,' you'd find yourself at the hands of a much more upset populace. Instead, he shrugs towards you and gives a small nod.\n"
"\n"
"Oyadazminis groans and pushes himself up, he beams with a giant smile, several of his missing teeth having been replaced by intricately carved gemstones. If this is 'entertainment' to these dwarves, you're surprised he's not missing more.\n"
"\n"
"He waves to the nobles and grabs you and [Companion Name] by your shoulders, dragging you off behind the throne room to an lavishly decorated room, with the Archivist following closely behind. The floating man waves his hand over the door, causing the entrance to vanish entirely under a waterfall of blue sparks."
msgstr ""
"Mientras derrotas a los guardias y nobles que te miran expectantes, no habrías imaginado que el propio rey se levantaría para unirse a la diversión, pero, con no poco esfuerzo, cayó como el resto de los suyos. Intentaste por todos los medios no matarlo, pero, con lo fuerte que se dio contra el suelo, te preguntas si te has pasado.\n"
"\n"
"Agarras tu arma, cubierta de más sangre de la que jamás habrías esperado en un combate «amistoso». Con el rey nalidasi a tus pies, miras al Archivero, temiendo que, pese a la promesa de que esto era solo «entretenimiento», acabes a merced de una población mucho más enfadada. En lugar de eso, se encoge de hombros y te dedica un leve asentimiento.\n"
"\n"
"Oyadazminis gruñe y se incorpora; sonríe de oreja a oreja, y varios de los dientes que le faltan han sido sustituidos por gemas talladas con esmero. Si esto es «entretenimiento» para estos enanos, te sorprende que no le falten más.\n"
"\n"
"Saluda a los nobles con la mano y os agarra a ti y a [Companion Name] por los hombros, arrastrándoos tras la sala del trono hasta una estancia lujosamente decorada, con el Archivero siguiéndoos de cerca. El hombre flotante pasa la mano por encima de la puerta y hace que la entrada desaparezca por completo bajo una cascada de chispas azules."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Haven't had a proper bout like that in half a dozen years!"
msgstr "¡Hacía media docena de años que no tenía un combate como es debido!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Don't get visitors with as much fire n' 'em as the both of you everyday. "
"Thanks for indulging my people, they'll like you a lot more for that."
msgstr ""
"No todos los días recibimos visitas con tanto fuego dentro como vosotros "
"dos. Gracias por darle el gusto a mi gente, os apreciarán mucho más por "
"ello."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It didn't seem that any of you were particularly keen on letting us not "
"participate."
msgstr ""
"No parecía que ninguno de vosotros tuviera muchas ganas de dejarnos no "
"participar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You could have gone crying to your mothers at any moment, but you would have"
" been laughed out of the courtroom."
msgstr ""
"Podríais haber ido llorando a vuestras madres en cualquier momento, pero os "
"habrían echado de la sala entre risas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The Archivist told me what you seek. At least, part of it."
msgstr "El Archivero me ha contado lo que buscáis. Al menos, una parte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If I were to let anyone into the Archives, they'd have to work their stones "
"off for half a human lifetime to even glimpse the outermost door."
msgstr ""
"Si dejara entrar a alguien en los Archivos, tendría que dejarse la piel "
"durante media vida humana para siquiera vislumbrar la puerta más exterior."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't imagine the two of you have the time for such things, if you're "
"telling the truth about our... mutual acquaintances."
msgstr ""
"Dudo que tengáis tiempo para esas cosas, si es verdad lo que decís de "
"nuestros... conocidos mutuos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't know if I'd call them that at this point..."
msgstr "No sé si a estas alturas los llamaría así..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But the two of you are familiar with Talm and Era, then?"
msgstr "Pero entonces, ¿conocéis a Talm y a Era?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Aye. They translated half the... special materials we've got in the Archives"
" long ago."
msgstr ""
"Así es. Hace mucho tradujeron la mitad de los... materiales especiales que "
"tenemos en los Archivos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Decided that as payment, they'd take the other half. So many years of "
"history lost..."
msgstr ""
"Y decidieron que, como pago, se llevarían la otra mitad. Tantos años de "
"historia perdidos..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Under normal circumstances I'd agree, but if those books had anything to do "
"with the nastiness that tall fella could do..."
msgstr ""
"En circunstancias normales estaría de acuerdo, pero si esos libros tenían "
"algo que ver con las barbaridades que podía hacer aquel tipo alto..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Good riddance, I say."
msgstr "Pues que se vaya con viento fresco, digo yo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We got rather well acquainted with it ourselves. "
msgstr "Nosotros mismos llegamos a conocerla bastante bien. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Why we need to get into the Archives is a long story, but... it was under "
"their recommendation."
msgstr ""
"Por qué necesitamos entrar en los Archivos es una larga historia, pero... "
"fue por recomendación suya."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I believe that, which is the only reason I didn't toss you out the second it"
" was mentioned."
msgstr ""
"Eso me lo creo, y es la única razón por la que no os he echado en cuanto se "
"mencionó."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That whole art... It's dangerous. Most everyone at my level of station "
"across the continent is at least loosely aware of Summoning."
msgstr ""
"Todo ese arte... es peligroso. Casi todos los de mi rango en el continente "
"conocen al menos por encima la Invocación."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Mostly because each nation has their own collection of histories and magic "
"under lock and key. Too treacherous to share. Using it is out of the "
"question."
msgstr ""
"Sobre todo porque cada nación guarda bajo llave su propia colección de "
"historias y magia. Es demasiado traicionero compartirla. Usarla, ni "
"pensarlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"To be honest, your arrival and need for said materials has us more... "
"concerned more than anything."
msgstr ""
"Para ser sincero, vuestra llegada y vuestra necesidad de dichos materiales "
"nos tienen más... preocupados que otra cosa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm and Era are two of the most trusted individuals to the kingdom, but we "
"cannot simply give the materials to you."
msgstr ""
"Talm y Era son dos de las personas de mayor confianza del reino, pero no "
"podemos daros los materiales sin más."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Aye. We trust their judgement, but both protocol and public perception hold "
"a lot of sway here."
msgstr ""
"Así es. Confiamos en su criterio, pero tanto el protocolo como la opinión "
"pública pesan mucho aquí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Can we do anything else that doesn't involve public beatdowns or ballroom "
"brawls to earn our way in, then?"
msgstr ""
"¿Entonces podemos hacer algo más para ganarnos la entrada que no incluya "
"palizas públicas ni peleas en salones de baile?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yes, and it'll be your great pleasure to do so. My lovely daughter will be "
"your ward. You couldn't find yourself in better hands if you tried."
msgstr ""
"Sí, y será un gran placer para vosotros. Mi encantadora hija será vuestra "
"tutora. No podríais estar en mejores manos aunque lo intentarais."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As Oyadazminis finishes, there's a shimmer in the corner of the room. A young red haired dwarf steps out from seemingly thin air, a cloak of woven blue metal thread billowing out around her. She introduces herself as Redilok and gives a small curtsy and mentions she enjoyed watching you give her father quite the wallop out in the ballroom. The king turns about as red as his daughter's hair and shakes his head before motioning for the Archivist to rematerialize the door, then the two of them depart.\n"
"\n"
"The princess opens a new door in a different section of wall and motions for the two of you to follow. You pass through the doorway and find yourselves on the balcony of a large tower connected to - what you presume is - the castle you were just in. The balcony overlooks the whole of Koganusan, the whole of the capitol fitting within an unbelievable hollow under the Perilous Peaks. You hardly have the time to take it in before the princess starts running through its extensive history, and that of their western neighbors, a smaller kingdom of dwarves who live under a large volcanic mountain range.\n"
"\n"
"What she wants your assistance with is no small task. Connecting the two kingdoms via a magical transport line that allows a stone platform to accelerate to incredible speeds. The 'Stoneway' as she calls it is already well underway, but still needs an extraordinary amount of work. Before you're allowed to begin though, you must show her how you go about summoning creatures, purely to satisfy her curiosity. If she's to vouch for you, she wants to know just what secrets her father intends to give away to humans."
msgstr ""
"Cuando Oyadazminis termina, algo resplandece en una esquina de la sala. Una joven enana pelirroja sale de la nada, con una capa de hilo de metal azul tejido ondeando a su alrededor. Se presenta como Redilok, hace una pequeña reverencia y comenta que le ha encantado ver cómo le dabas a su padre semejante paliza en el salón de baile. El rey se pone casi tan rojo como el pelo de su hija y niega con la cabeza antes de indicar al Archivero que vuelva a materializar la puerta; luego los dos se marchan.\n"
"\n"
"La princesa abre una puerta nueva en otra parte de la pared y os indica a los dos que la sigáis. Cruzáis el umbral y os encontráis en el balcón de una gran torre conectada a lo que supones que es el castillo en el que acabáis de estar. El balcón domina todo Koganusan: la capital entera cabe en un hueco increíble bajo los Picos Peligrosos. Apenas tienes tiempo de contemplarlo antes de que la princesa empiece a repasar su extensa historia y la de sus vecinos del oeste, un reino más pequeño de enanos que viven bajo una gran cordillera volcánica.\n"
"\n"
"Lo que quiere que hagáis no es poca cosa: conectar los dos reinos mediante una línea de transporte mágica que permite a una plataforma de piedra acelerar a velocidades increíbles. La «Vía de Piedra», como ella la llama, está ya muy avanzada, pero aún necesita muchísimo trabajo. Sin embargo, antes de que puedas empezar, debes enseñarle cómo invocas criaturas, solo para satisfacer su curiosidad. Si va a responder por ti, quiere saber exactamente qué secretos piensa regalar su padre a los humanos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Since she was in the room when her father mentioned the closely guarded art of Summoning, you don't find any harm in indulging the princess's request. You and [Companion Name] show princess Redilok several of the creatures you've learned to create over your journey here, much to her pleasure. She takes several sketches of the beasts, and asks for you to make them perform... all manner of things, some practical, some a bit silly. She questions you on your journey here throughout the 'tests' as she calls them. You fill her in. The Soulsmiths, your travels. Talm and Era's trials. She listens without a single comment, enraptured by your tales.\n"
"\n"
"After a long while and the summoning of several more creatures, Redilok closes her notepad and makes it vanish, much like the Archivist did with the door, earlier. She thanks you for your time and asks you to make yourself at home, and that she'll be in touch very soon regarding the Stoneway, then promptly slips off the balcony backward and disappears.\n"
"\n"
"After confirming you didn't just witness the princess fall to her untimely death, you enter what seems to be 'your' room from the balcony and find a room that likely cost several thousand gold just to furnish, let alone build. A two plush four poster beds, a pool of steaming water kept warm by some arcane source you're unfamiliar with. Thick carpet, beautiful silken drapes, and various pieces of artwork depicting lands you've never seen nor heard of.\n"
"\n"
"The sight is made a bit warmer by the fact that [Companion Name] has already launched herself at the nearest bed and started to snore before even making contact with the pillow, a sentiment you cannot help but share moments later."
msgstr ""
"Como estaba en la sala cuando su padre mencionó el arte celosamente guardado de la Invocación, no ves nada de malo en complacer la petición de la princesa. [Companion Name] y tú le mostráis a la princesa Redilok varias de las criaturas que has aprendido a crear durante tu viaje hasta aquí, para su gran deleite. Hace varios bocetos de las bestias y te pide que las hagas realizar... todo tipo de cosas, algunas prácticas, otras un poco absurdas. Durante las «pruebas», como ella las llama, te pregunta por tu viaje. Se lo cuentas todo: los forjaalmas, tus viajes, las pruebas de Talm y Era. Escucha sin hacer un solo comentario, cautivada por tus relatos.\n"
"\n"
"Al cabo de un buen rato y de invocar varias criaturas más, Redilok cierra su cuaderno y lo hace desaparecer, igual que el Archivero hizo antes con la puerta. Te da las gracias por tu tiempo, te pide que te sientas como en casa y te dice que pronto se pondrá en contacto contigo por lo de la Vía de Piedra; acto seguido, se deja caer de espaldas por el balcón y desaparece.\n"
"\n"
"Tras comprobar que no acabas de presenciar la muerte prematura de la princesa, entras desde el balcón en lo que parece ser «tu» habitación y te encuentras un cuarto cuyo mobiliario seguramente costó varios miles de monedas de oro, por no hablar de construirlo. Dos mullidas camas con dosel y una piscina de agua humeante que mantiene caliente alguna fuente arcana que no conoces. Alfombras gruesas, preciosas cortinas de seda y varias obras de arte que representan tierras que nunca has visto ni oído mencionar.\n"
"\n"
"La escena resulta aún más acogedora porque [Companion Name] ya se ha lanzado sobre la cama más cercana y ha empezado a roncar antes incluso de tocar la almohada, un sentimiento que no puedes evitar compartir momentos después."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ22"
msgstr "MQ22"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Stoneway Yourway - After a warm welcome to the kingdom of the Nalidasi "
"Dwarves, Princess Redilok is primed to accept your help in finishing the "
"last of the Stoneway, which will earn your entry into the Royal Archives."
msgstr ""
"Vía de Piedra, vía libre: Tras una cálida bienvenida al reino de los enanos "
"nalidasi, la princesa Redilok está lista para aceptar tu ayuda para terminar"
" lo que queda de la Vía de Piedra, lo que te permitirá entrar en los "
"Archivos Reales."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I've been working on the Stoneeeeway~"
msgstr "He estado trabajando en la Vía de Piedraaaaa~"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "All the live long... is it daytime down here?"
msgstr "Todo el santo día... ¿aquí abajo es de día?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You wake to find breakfast floating towards you, with Princess Redilok floating just behind it. She pours over a large scroll, as your meal assembles itself on a silver tray inches above your lap. You feel horrendously underdressed and disheveled to be in the presence of royalty, but she hardly seems to notice. Her fault for coming unannounced. You still do your best to make yourself marginally more presentable, then lightly pick at the meal in front of you. You glance towards [Companion Name] who seems even more flustered by the princess's sudden arrival. You catch her eye and lightly wipe at the corner of your mouth, trying to get her to wipe the drool away. She hardly contains a groan before doing so as subtly as she can.\n"
"\n"
"Once satisfied with whatever she was looking through, Redilok looks up to address you both, her smile as sweet as the flaky pastry you bite into."
msgstr ""
"Te despiertas y ves el desayuno flotando hacia ti, con la princesa Redilok flotando justo detrás. Examina un gran pergamino mientras tu comida se monta sola en una bandeja de plata a pocos centímetros de tu regazo. Sientes que tu ropa y tu aspecto dejan muchísimo que desear para estar en presencia de la realeza, pero ella apenas parece darse cuenta. Culpa suya por presentarse sin avisar. Aun así, haces lo que puedes para tener un aspecto algo más presentable y luego picoteas la comida que tienes delante. Miras a [Companion Name], que parece aún más azorada por la repentina llegada de la princesa. Le llamas la atención y te tocas suavemente la comisura de la boca para que se limpie la baba. Apenas contiene un gruñido antes de hacerlo con todo el disimulo que puede.\n"
"\n"
"Una vez satisfecha con lo que estaba revisando, Redilok levanta la vista para dirigirse a vosotros, con una sonrisa tan dulce como el hojaldre al que le das un mordisco."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Please, you two. If you couldn't tell by the way my father welcomed you to "
"our home with a kerfuffle by all the top-brass in the kingdom, we do things "
"a bit differently here."
msgstr ""
"Por favor, vosotros dos. Por si no os habéis dado cuenta por cómo mi padre "
"os recibió en nuestro hogar con un alboroto de todos los altos mandos del "
"reino, aquí hacemos las cosas un poco distinto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your human modesty and decorum will only get you funny looks here. Dig in!"
msgstr ""
"Vuestra modestia y decoro humanos solo os valdrán miradas raras aquí. ¡A "
"comer!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...We're honored, princess."
msgstr "...Es un honor, princesa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Tsk tsk. What'd I just say?"
msgstr "Tsk, tsk. ¿Qué acabo de decir?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"None of that stuffy business. You need to eat up if you're going to help our"
" Stoneway workers."
msgstr ""
"Nada de formalidades estiradas. Tenéis que comer bien si vais a ayudar a "
"nuestros trabajadores de la Vía de Piedra."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'd like to ask... if you already have people working on this project, why "
"would our aid be needed, exactly?"
msgstr ""
"Me gustaría preguntar... si ya tenéis gente trabajando en este proyecto, "
"¿para qué necesitáis exactamente nuestra ayuda?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And not that we mind, but that's all it'll take to get us into the archives?"
msgstr ""
"Y no es que nos importe, pero ¿con eso bastará para que entremos en los "
"archivos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Good questions!"
msgstr "¡Buenas preguntas!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The tunnel to excavate the Stoneway met with a bit of a... snag. There was a"
" cavern right near the middle of our kingdoms that seemed man or dwarfmade."
msgstr ""
"El túnel para excavar la Vía de Piedra se topó con un pequeño... "
"contratiempo. Había una caverna justo a medio camino entre nuestros reinos "
"que parecía hecha por humanos o por enanos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Not too uncommon considering the distance, but the cavern was guarded by "
"beasts made of the same magic I had you show me earlier."
msgstr ""
"No es tan raro teniendo en cuenta la distancia, pero la caverna estaba "
"custodiada por bestias hechas de la misma magia que os pedí que me "
"enseñarais antes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"For such scary beasties, they didn't put up much of a fight and we finished "
"excavating the route for the Stoneway. Not without some losses, though."
msgstr ""
"Para ser unas bestias tan aterradoras, no opusieron mucha resistencia y "
"terminamos de excavar la ruta de la Vía de Piedra. Aunque no sin algunas "
"pérdidas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Seems a bit miraculous to stumble across a cavern filled with ancient "
"beasts."
msgstr ""
"Parece casi un milagro toparse con una caverna llena de bestias antiguas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're on the same page, then."
msgstr "Entonces estamos de acuerdo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My father - bless the foolhardy man - is sure it was a trap set by the "
"Flamberian Dwarves, despite the fact the Stoneway is meant to connect us."
msgstr ""
"Mi padre (bendito sea, el muy temerario) está seguro de que fue una trampa "
"de los enanos flamberianos, aunque la Vía de Piedra está pensada para "
"unirnos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...And help bury old grudges..."
msgstr "...Y para ayudar a enterrar viejos rencores..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You don't seem to share the sentiment though. You think it was someone else?"
msgstr ""
"Pero tú no pareces compartir esa opinión. ¿Crees que fue otra persona?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I do. There was a war between our kingdoms long before my father was even a "
"pebble in his father's eye, but Dwarven grudges run deep."
msgstr ""
"Así es. Hubo una guerra entre nuestros reinos mucho antes de que mi padre "
"fuera siquiera un guijarro en los ojos de su padre, pero los rencores enanos"
" calan hondo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Despite the years, our elders are worried something will go awry and are "
"jumping at the chance to reignite the old war."
msgstr ""
"A pesar de los años, a nuestros ancianos les preocupa que algo salga mal y "
"se lanzan a la mínima oportunidad de reavivar la vieja guerra."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The tunnel to excavate the Stoneway met with a bit of a... snag. There was a"
" cavern right near the middle of our kingdoms that seemed man or dwarf-made."
msgstr ""
"El túnel para excavar la Vía de Piedra se topó con un pequeño... "
"contratiempo. Había una caverna justo a medio camino entre nuestros reinos "
"que parecía hecha por humanos o por enanos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I've been working with their prince for half a decade on the Stoneway now, "
"and he's an honest man. This wasn't them."
msgstr ""
"Llevo media década trabajando con su príncipe en la Vía de Piedra y es un "
"hombre honesto. No fueron ellos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Maybe something else, then? You remember the Soulsmiths from our stories "
"earlier?"
msgstr ""
"¿Quizá otra cosa, entonces? ¿Recuerdas a los forjaalmas de nuestras "
"historias de antes?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'd be surprised, but it's not as though there's other Summoning clans "
"running amok nowadays, are there?"
msgstr ""
"Me sorprendería, pero tampoco es que haya otros clanes de Invocación "
"campando a sus anchas hoy en día, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If there are, we haven't had the misfortune of meeting them. Can you think "
"of any reason why they'd target your people?"
msgstr ""
"Si los hay, no hemos tenido la desgracia de conocerlos. ¿Se te ocurre algún "
"motivo por el que irían a por tu pueblo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No, I can't, and that's what worries me, and why I want the two of you there"
" as we complete the Stoneway."
msgstr ""
"No, no se me ocurre, y eso es lo que me preocupa, y por eso os quiero a los "
"dos allí cuando terminemos la Vía de Piedra."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The rulers won't be there in person, but several high-ranking nobles - along"
" with the Flamberian Prince and myself - will hold a small celebration in "
"the center of the Stoneway as it's finished."
msgstr ""
"Los gobernantes no estarán en persona, pero varios nobles de alto rango "
"(junto con el príncipe flamberiano y yo) celebraremos una pequeña fiesta en "
"el centro de la Vía de Piedra cuando esté terminada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And we're to be there incase something happens with the Soulsmiths."
msgstr "Y nosotros estaremos allí por si pasa algo con los forjaalmas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Redilok nods, then leaves to let the two of you eat and get prepared. When she returns, another magical doorway that she creates takes you to what she calls the Stoneway Station. Several deep set rails of metal stretch along the ground, far, far into a tunnel that stretches into the distance. The underground pathway is lit by blue-green balls of floating light spaced evenly apart, giving as much light as if the Stoneway was above ground instead of thousands of meters below it. \n"
"\n"
"Dozens of dwarves carry lengths of rails etched with glowing runes onto the stone platform hovering above the metal path. Making sure you're not in the way, you step upon the rectangular 'Slabglider' at Redilok's request. The Slabglider is the length of several carts stacked end-to-end, with comfy seating along its outer edge, with plenty of space for the rails and cargo between.\n"
"\n"
"Once fully loaded, Redilok smiles and snaps her fingers, sending the platform cruising through the tunnel at dizzying speed. Despite how fast the three of you hurtle down the path, the ride seems remarkably calm. Your body feels still, but the lights whizzing by faster than your eyes can track show you're definitely moving.\n"
"\n"
"It's not long before the Slabglider begins to slow and then stop. You worry something is wrong before Redilok confirms that you're near the center of the Stoneway, meaning that you crossed nearly a fourth of the continent in minutes. It's hard to even wrap your head around.\n"
"\n"
"Once you disembark, several dwarves - some Nalidasi, some Flamberian - jump aboard and start unloading metal rails. You figure you 'ought to help instead of just standing around waiting."
msgstr ""
"Redilok asiente y se marcha para que comáis y os preparéis. Cuando vuelve, crea otra puerta mágica que os lleva a lo que ella llama la Estación de la Vía de Piedra. Varios raíles de metal bien hundidos se extienden por el suelo, muy, muy adentro de un túnel que se pierde en la distancia. El camino subterráneo está iluminado por esferas flotantes de luz verdeazulada, colocadas a intervalos regulares, que dan tanta luz como si la Vía de Piedra estuviera en la superficie en lugar de miles de metros bajo ella. \n"
"\n"
"Decenas de enanos cargan tramos de raíl grabados con runas brillantes sobre la plataforma de piedra que flota encima del camino de metal. Procurando no estorbar, subes al «Deslizalosas» rectangular a petición de Redilok. El Deslizalosas tiene la longitud de varios carros puestos uno detrás de otro, con asientos cómodos a lo largo del borde exterior y mucho espacio entre ellos para los raíles y la carga.\n"
"\n"
"Una vez cargado, Redilok sonríe y chasquea los dedos, y la plataforma sale disparada por el túnel a una velocidad vertiginosa. A pesar de lo rápido que avanzáis los tres por el camino, el viaje parece notablemente tranquilo. Sientes el cuerpo quieto, pero las luces que pasan zumbando más rápido de lo que tus ojos pueden seguir demuestran que, sin duda, os estáis moviendo.\n"
"\n"
"No pasa mucho tiempo antes de que el Deslizalosas empiece a frenar y luego se detenga. Temes que algo vaya mal, hasta que Redilok confirma que estáis cerca del centro de la Vía de Piedra, lo que significa que habéis cruzado casi una cuarta parte del continente en minutos. Cuesta hasta asimilarlo.\n"
"\n"
"En cuanto bajáis, varios enanos (unos nalidasi, otros flamberianos) suben de un salto y empiezan a descargar raíles de metal. Te parece que deberías ayudar en lugar de quedarte ahí esperando."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Come on... Someone has to be out of place..."
msgstr "Vamos... Algo tiene que estar fuera de sitio..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There!"
msgstr "¡Ahí!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You're able to follow along with the dwarves quite well, and they're a bit impressed as you and [Companion Name] keep up with laying the railings and locking them into place. The Flamberians get to work as you set each in place and you finally take a good look at them. Each appears almost molten lacking any traditional skin and instead seeming to be made out of a stone-like material with bright red magma heating the rock as some sort of vein system, serving a purpose you can't even begin to guess at. Among them is their own royal, Prince Cintak.\n"
"\n"
"They grip the newly connected rails at heat it until it's red-hot, binding individual sections together into one fully linked pathway. Once that's done, the Nalidasi etch in a last set of runes, activating the section of rail. Both Redilok and Cintak are active participants in the Stoneway creation, though you do note they do disappear alone together more than a few times throughout your time working on the path.\n"
"\n"
"Construction goes on for a long time, and you end up returning to Koganusan several times, eating, sleeping, and enjoying the luxuries of staying within the royal palace, getting more acquainted with Redilok and several nobles within the kingdom's upper-ranks.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, days after you began, the blue lights that light the corridor give way to red, and the rail you lay connects to that of the Flamberian's side of the Stoneway. It isn't sealed into place just yet, as this will be done at the ceremony Redilok informs you is called the 'Linking'."
msgstr ""
"Consigues seguir el ritmo de los enanos bastante bien, y se quedan algo impresionados de que [Companion Name] y tú les sigáis el paso colocando los raíles y fijándolos en su sitio. Los flamberianos se ponen manos a la obra a medida que colocas cada uno y por fin te fijas bien en ellos. Todos parecen casi fundidos: no tienen piel como tal y parecen hechos de un material similar a la piedra, con magma de un rojo intenso que calienta la roca a modo de sistema de venas, con una función que no alcanzas ni a imaginar. Entre ellos está su propio miembro de la realeza, el príncipe Cintak.\n"
"\n"
"Agarran los raíles recién unidos y los calientan hasta ponerlos al rojo vivo, soldando cada tramo en un único camino totalmente unido. Una vez hecho, los nalidasi graban un último conjunto de runas que activa ese tramo de raíl. Tanto Redilok como Cintak participan activamente en la construcción de la Vía de Piedra, aunque te fijas en que desaparecen juntos y a solas más de unas cuantas veces mientras trabajas en el camino.\n"
"\n"
"La construcción dura mucho tiempo y acabas volviendo a Koganusan varias veces para comer, dormir y disfrutar de los lujos de alojarte en el palacio real, donde vas conociendo mejor a Redilok y a varios nobles de las altas esferas del reino.\n"
"\n"
"Por fin, días después de empezar, las luces azules que iluminan el corredor dan paso a luces rojas, y el raíl que colocas se une al del lado flamberiano de la Vía de Piedra. Todavía no está sellado en su sitio, ya que eso se hará en la ceremonia que, según te cuenta Redilok, se llama «el Enlace»."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Several years in the making... I can hardly believe we're done."
msgstr ""
"Varios años de trabajo... Casi no me puedo creer que hayamos terminado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hopefully the first step among many in soothing the wounds of the past."
msgstr ""
"Ojalá sea el primero de muchos pasos para curar las heridas del pasado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Though I'm surprised Redilok sought it fit to bring along two humans, I "
"trust her judgement."
msgstr ""
"Aunque me sorprende que Redilok haya considerado oportuno traer a dos "
"humanos, confío en su criterio."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...thanks, I think?"
msgstr "...¿Gracias, supongo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're just happy we could help out."
msgstr "Nos alegra haber podido ayudar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm sure... Though, I know you're here to ensure the Linking goes well. The "
"royal princess has informed me of such."
msgstr ""
"No lo dudo... Aunque sé que estáis aquí para asegurar que el Enlace salga "
"bien. La princesa real me lo ha contado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You have my gratitude. Please ensure her safety over mine. I couldn't bare "
"it to-"
msgstr ""
"Tenéis mi gratitud. Os lo ruego, poned su seguridad por delante de la mía. "
"No soportaría que..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Cinny, please! All this propriety is going to put them off."
msgstr "¡Cinny, por favor! Tanta formalidad los va a espantar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Cinny?"
msgstr "...¿Cinny?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's just a nickname of sorts the royal princess is fond of. It really "
"doesn't mean much, pay it no mind."
msgstr ""
"No es más que una especie de apodo que le gusta a la princesa real. En "
"realidad no significa gran cosa, no le deis importancia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Doesn't mean much, hm? You told me you loved it."
msgstr "¿No significa gran cosa, eh? Me dijiste que te encantaba."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Of course I do my precious little cabochon! I-"
msgstr "¡Claro que me encanta, mi preciosa cabujoncita! Yo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...*ahem*."
msgstr "...*ejem*."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The two of you are observant, I'm sure you've noticed the princess and "
"I's..."
msgstr ""
"Sois observadores; seguro que os habéis fijado en que la princesa y yo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Disappearances off into the dark of the tunnels?"
msgstr "¿Desaparecéis en la oscuridad de los túneles?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Alone?"
msgstr "¿A solas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Yes."
msgstr "Sí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I am in no position to ask this of you, but I must do so anyway."
msgstr ""
"No estoy en posición de pediros esto, pero debo hacerlo de todos modos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Please keep this between yourselves for now. After the Linking the two of us"
" intend to announce..."
msgstr ""
"Os ruego que esto quede entre nosotros por ahora. Después del Enlace, los "
"dos pensamos anunciar..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The royal princess and I-"
msgstr "La princesa real y yo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh Cinny. I'm sure they figured it out on day one."
msgstr "Ay, Cinny. Seguro que lo adivinaron el primer día."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're in loveeeeee~"
msgstr "¡Estamos enamoraaaaados~!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Neither of us have any reason to mind, but isn't that a bit..."
msgstr "A ninguno de los dos nos parece mal, pero ¿no es un poco...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Scandalous? Daring? Risqué, maybe?"
msgstr "¿Escandaloso? ¿Atrevido? ¿Picante, quizá?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh it is. "
msgstr "Oh, lo es. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Tell. Us. Everything."
msgstr "Cuéntanos. Absolutamente. Todo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...but the Linking."
msgstr "...pero el Enlace."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Cinny darling, it's a party! Drop a couple stones and lighten up, I've never"
" gotten to tell anyone about this~"
msgstr ""
"Cinny, cariño, ¡es una fiesta! Suelta un par de piedras y relájate, nunca he"
" podido contarle esto a nadie~"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Prince Cintak simply holds his stony face in his hands as the princess starts to divulge far more detail than you would have thought she'd offer up. The Slabglider departs back towards Koganusan and comes back with half a village of dwarves, tables, decor, and liquor. Then it speeds off towards the Flamberian capitol and brings back even more. Just like that, the Linking is underway.\n"
"\n"
"You and [Companion Name] stroll about the thrown together party. The Stoneglider comes and goes multiple times, bringing more people, food, and furnishings, all of which are tucked into the carved out alcove you all reside in. The atmosphere is lively, sometimes too much so. It'd seem the king isn't the only one with longstanding grudges, and several scuffles break out through the celebration, but they're quickly quelled.\n"
"\n"
"You're on edge, waiting for any sign of the Soulsmiths. You scan every new arrival, take stock of each good brought in, and... the small hint of blood left on one of the chairs.\n"
"\n"
"With the small fights, rowdy dwarves, and free flowing alcohol, it's no wonder someone could have gotten hurt, but the chair hadn't been unloaded from the Slabglider yet.\n"
"\n"
"Something is awry, you just don't know what yet."
msgstr ""
"El príncipe Cintak se limita a hundir su rostro pétreo entre las manos mientras la princesa empieza a contar muchos más detalles de los que habrías pensado que compartiría. El Deslizalosas parte de vuelta hacia Koganusan y regresa con medio pueblo de enanos, mesas, decoración y licor. Luego sale disparado hacia la capital flamberiana y trae aún más. Y así, sin más, el Enlace está en marcha.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] y tú paseáis por la fiesta improvisada. El Deslizalosas va y viene varias veces, trayendo más gente, comida y mobiliario, que se colocan en la cavidad excavada donde estáis todos. El ambiente es animado, a veces demasiado. Parece que el rey no es el único con rencores antiguos, y estallan varias reyertas durante la celebración, aunque se sofocan enseguida.\n"
"\n"
"Estás en tensión, esperando cualquier señal de los forjaalmas. Examinas a cada recién llegado, revisas cada mercancía que traen y... el pequeño rastro de sangre que queda en una de las sillas.\n"
"\n"
"Con las pequeñas peleas, los enanos alborotados y el alcohol corriendo a raudales, no sería extraño que alguien se hubiera hecho daño, pero esa silla aún no se había descargado del Deslizalosas.\n"
"\n"
"Algo va mal, solo que todavía no sabes qué."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh no..."
msgstr "Oh, no..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Where is the princess?!"
msgstr "¡¿Dónde está la princesa?!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You move through the crowds and finally spot who you were looking for. The Nalidasi dwarf is almost indistinguishable from everyone else, except the fact that she's a bit more pale, and seems far less into the festivities than anyone else. She carries a large barrel draped in cloth and tucks it amongst many others at the back of the alcove.\n"
"\n"
"You stop her by grabbing her arm, and the pale dwarf doesn't even react to your presence. [Companion Name] pulls up the dwarf's sleeve and you see her arm coated by a thick stream of blood. The woman drops the barrel, but stands motionless in your grip, lifeless eyes staring up at you. Quickly checking the woman over, you peel back her collar, you see that the blood on her arm must have come from her slit neck, which was intentionally hidden under her bulky garb. The dwarf's blank look reminds you of Talm controlling the Soulsmith back in the capitol, and judging by her state, you know she's being controlled by someone. \n"
"\n"
"But it's too late. Volatile runes spill out from the dropped barrel, similar to those you made with Gloob, though these look substantially better crafted.\n"
"\n"
"Another dwarf - this one Flamberian - breaks the top of a barrel at the back of the room and sinks his hands inside of it before heating himself red hot.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] draws her bow and shoots at the dwarf, but the damage is done. You hear the sizzling of the volatile runes and cry out to anyone nearby."
msgstr ""
"Te abres paso entre la multitud y por fin ves a quien buscabas. La enana nalidasi es casi indistinguible de los demás, salvo porque está algo más pálida y parece mucho menos metida en la fiesta que nadie. Lleva un gran barril cubierto con una tela y lo esconde entre muchos otros al fondo de la cavidad.\n"
"\n"
"La detienes agarrándola del brazo, y la enana pálida ni siquiera reacciona a tu presencia. [Companion Name] le sube la manga y ves que tiene el brazo cubierto por un espeso reguero de sangre. La mujer suelta el barril, pero se queda inmóvil mientras la sujetas, mirándote con ojos sin vida. Al examinarla rápidamente, le apartas el cuello de la ropa y ves que la sangre del brazo debe de venir de su cuello rajado, que estaba escondido a propósito bajo su voluminosa vestimenta. La mirada vacía de la enana te recuerda a cuando Talm controlaba al forjaalmas en la capital, y, a juzgar por su estado, sabes que alguien la está controlando. \n"
"\n"
"Pero es demasiado tarde. Del barril caído salen runas volátiles, parecidas a las que hiciste con Gloob, aunque estas parecen mucho mejor elaboradas.\n"
"\n"
"Otro enano, este flamberiano, rompe la tapa de un barril al fondo de la sala, mete las manos dentro y se calienta hasta ponerse al rojo vivo.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] tensa el arco y le dispara al enano, pero el daño ya está hecho. Oyes el chisporroteo de las runas volátiles y gritas a todo el que está cerca."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Everyone! Get down!"
msgstr "¡Todos! ¡Al suelo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're under attack!"
msgstr "¡Nos atacan!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You see several dwarves by the wall turn towards you, startled by the arrow whizzing in their direction and your shout. They disappear as the runes in the barrel and several others nearby explode with a burst of magical energy, swallowing them entirely in a flash of white light.\n"
"\n"
"The whole world heaves upward. [Companion Name] grabs you as you're sent careening out of the alcove and down the tunnel, crashing to the ground with a sickening series of cracks then rolling several meters.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you stagger towards your feet and rush back inside to see that half the cavity has been reduced to rubble, and many of those attending were killed instantly by the blast. The cleared out section is... far larger than it should be, as a large cavern is revealed by the blast. Soulsmiths adorned with gold trimmed robes and long, black metal weapons begin to flood out from the hole and descend on the Dwarves alongside their dark summoned monsters. \n"
"\n"
"The sight is horrifyingly similar to that dark night in Azamire.\n"
"\n"
"Behind the cultists is a slug-like monster that pulls itself along the ground on countless sets of arms, pulling itself into the opening with sickening, twitchy movements. The creature is nearly as long as the Stoneglider, and twice as tall. A large black metal vessel protrudes from the beast's back, seemingly fused to it. You watch the device on its back begins to glow as it pulls itself towards the dead dwarves on the ground.\n"
"\n"
"A pulse of dark green light washes over the bombed-out alcove.\n"
"\n"
"Then the dead begin to move again. "
msgstr ""
"Ves que varios enanos junto a la pared se giran hacia ti, sobresaltados por la flecha que silba en su dirección y por tu grito. Desaparecen cuando las runas del barril y de varios otros cercanos estallan con una ráfaga de energía mágica que los engulle por completo en un destello de luz blanca.\n"
"\n"
"El mundo entero se levanta. [Companion Name] te agarra mientras salís despedidos de la cavidad y túnel abajo; chocáis contra el suelo con una serie de crujidos espantosos y rodáis varios metros.\n"
"\n"
"Los dos os ponéis en pie a trompicones y volvéis corriendo dentro, donde veis que media cavidad ha quedado reducida a escombros y que muchos de los asistentes han muerto al instante por la explosión. La zona despejada es... mucho más grande de lo que debería, ya que la explosión ha dejado al descubierto una gran caverna. Forjaalmas vestidos con túnicas ribeteadas de oro y largas armas de metal negro empiezan a salir en tropel del agujero y se abalanzan sobre los enanos junto a sus oscuros monstruos invocados. \n"
"\n"
"La escena se parece horriblemente a aquella noche oscura en Azamire.\n"
"\n"
"Detrás de los sectarios hay un monstruo parecido a una babosa que se arrastra por el suelo sobre innumerables pares de brazos y se mete en la abertura con movimientos repugnantes y espasmódicos. La criatura es casi tan larga como el Deslizalosas y el doble de alta. Un gran recipiente de metal negro sobresale de la espalda de la bestia, aparentemente fusionado con ella. Ves cómo el artefacto de su espalda empieza a brillar mientras se arrastra hacia los enanos muertos del suelo.\n"
"\n"
"Un pulso de luz verde oscura baña la cavidad arrasada por la explosión.\n"
"\n"
"Y entonces los muertos empiezan a moverse de nuevo. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"When the dwarves that remain see you crash against the Soulsmiths, any who are able follow close behind you, burning with unbridled rage. You do your best to defend those too dazed or injured to help or run, but many are cut down by the Soulsmiths who weave through the crowd of undead.\n"
"\n"
"This entire attack was planned out meticulously, maybe even your presence was accounted for. You try to intercept a group that head towards the Stoneglider, but the horde of undead stop you each time. Several Soulsmiths board the Stoneglider, load barrels of volatile runes onto the platform, then send it hurtling towards Koganusan. There's nothing you can do, there's too many things to deal with at once.\n"
"\n"
"In the heat of battle you catch a glimpse of Prince Cintak standing over Princess Redilok, who clutches the new stump of her arm and tries to stem the bleeding. You try to reach them, but there's simply too many undead between you. It's not long before the prince is run through by one of the Soulsmith's black metal blades. He's then hefted into the air and unceremoniously pinned onto the back of the horrific slug creature who cries out as it's blubbery flesh is pierced. \n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] is much closer, she reaches the princess just in time to spare her from the same fate as the prince. Moments after she cuts down the Soulsmith, those that remain call out to one another, escaping with the body of the prince, following after their beast who now scampers deeper into the cavern.\n"
"\n"
"The undead remain, but without the threat of the gold-robed Soulsmiths probing for weaknesses or distractions, you're able to cut down the rest of them in short order. You rush to the princess's side. Undeterred by her missing arm, she stands, eyes piercing the dark of the cavern and staring towards those who took the prince. She claims that it'd take more than that to kill him, and that the Soulsmiths wanted him alive. [Companion Name] tries to stop the princess from following into the cavern, but she's undeterred.\n"
"\n"
"Only thing you can do is follow after."
msgstr ""
"Cuando los enanos que quedan te ven lanzarte contra los forjaalmas, todos los que pueden te siguen de cerca, ardiendo de una rabia desatada. Haces lo que puedes por defender a quienes están demasiado aturdidos o heridos para ayudar o huir, pero muchos caen bajo los forjaalmas que se mueven entre la multitud de no muertos.\n"
"\n"
"Todo este ataque se planeó meticulosamente; quizá incluso contaban con tu presencia. Intentas interceptar a un grupo que se dirige hacia el Deslizalosas, pero la horda de no muertos te lo impide cada vez. Varios forjaalmas suben al Deslizalosas, cargan barriles de runas volátiles en la plataforma y lo lanzan a toda velocidad hacia Koganusan. No puedes hacer nada; hay demasiadas cosas de las que ocuparse a la vez.\n"
"\n"
"En pleno combate, ves de reojo al príncipe Cintak de pie junto a la princesa Redilok, que se agarra el muñón recién abierto de su brazo e intenta contener la hemorragia. Intentas llegar hasta ellos, pero hay demasiados no muertos entre vosotros. No pasa mucho antes de que una de las hojas de metal negro de los forjaalmas atraviese al príncipe. Luego lo alzan en el aire y lo clavan sin miramientos en el lomo de la horrible criatura babosa, que chilla cuando le perforan la carne grasienta. \n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] está mucho más cerca y llega hasta la princesa justo a tiempo para librarla del mismo destino que el príncipe. Momentos después de que abata al forjaalmas, los que quedan se llaman entre sí y huyen con el cuerpo del príncipe, siguiendo a su bestia, que ahora se escabulle hacia el interior de la caverna.\n"
"\n"
"Los no muertos siguen ahí, pero sin la amenaza de los forjaalmas de túnica dorada buscando puntos débiles o distracciones, acabas con el resto en poco tiempo. Corres al lado de la princesa. Sin dejarse amilanar por el brazo que le falta, se levanta, con la mirada clavada en la oscuridad de la caverna, hacia quienes se llevaron al príncipe. Asegura que haría falta más que eso para matarlo y que los forjaalmas lo querían vivo. [Companion Name] intenta impedir que la princesa los siga a la caverna, pero ella no se deja disuadir.\n"
"\n"
"Lo único que puedes hacer es ir tras ella."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ23"
msgstr "MQ23"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Prince Procurement - After the Soulsmith attack on the Linking, you and "
"[Companion Name] follow after Princess Redilok who is out for blood. Will "
"you find the prince at the end of the path, or lose another royal in the "
"process?"
msgstr ""
"Rescate principesco: Tras el ataque de los forjaalmas en el Enlace, "
"[Companion Name] y tú seguís a la princesa Redilok, que está sedienta de "
"sangre. ¿Encontraréis al príncipe al final del camino o perderéis a otro "
"miembro de la realeza en el intento?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll focus on breaking up the bigger rocks."
msgstr "Yo me encargo de romper las rocas más grandes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Light? We're close to the surface?"
msgstr "¿Luz? ¿Estamos cerca de la superficie?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You hold a lantern aloft as the three of you jog through the cavern, barely illuminating the ancient tunnels. [Companion Name] continually tries to stop the princess - at least long enough to properly tend to her missing arm - but Redilok forces herself onward.\n"
"\n"
"Another blast echoes down the winding passage in front of you, the sudden rush of wind nearly knocking you off your feet. You find the source not long after. The Soulsmiths collapsed the cave behind them, the rubble still settling as rocks shift into place."
msgstr ""
"Sostienes un farol en alto mientras los tres avanzáis a paso ligero por la caverna, aunque apenas ilumina los antiguos túneles. [Companion Name] intenta una y otra vez detener a la princesa (al menos el tiempo suficiente para atenderle como es debido el brazo que le falta), pero Redilok se obliga a seguir adelante.\n"
"\n"
"Otra explosión resuena por el sinuoso pasadizo que tenéis delante, y la repentina ráfaga de viento casi te tira al suelo. Poco después encuentras su origen. Los forjaalmas han derrumbado la cueva a su paso, y los escombros aún se están asentando mientras las rocas se acomodan en su sitio."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Those damn cowards!"
msgstr "¡Malditos cobardes!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Both of you, give me a hand, will you?"
msgstr "Vosotros dos, echadme una mano, ¿queréis?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I seem to have just lost one. And then some."
msgstr "Parece que acabo de perder una. Y algo más."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We want to, princess, but we can't."
msgstr "Queremos hacerlo, princesa, pero no podemos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You're injured, and by the time we cut through this, they'll be long gone."
msgstr ""
"Estás herida y, para cuando consigamos abrirnos paso, ya estarán muy lejos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We should go back to Koganusan, regroup, and come back."
msgstr "Deberíamos volver a Koganusan, reagruparnos y regresar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "If they took [Companion Name] would you say the same?"
msgstr "Si se hubieran llevado a [Companion Name], ¿dirías lo mismo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I see your point."
msgstr "Entiendo lo que quieres decir."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Can you do one of those doorway thinggies you did before to get us to the "
"other side of these rocks?"
msgstr ""
"¿Puedes hacer uno de esos chismes de puerta que hiciste antes para llevarnos"
" al otro lado de estas rocas?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I can only set the destination to somewhere I've been before, it won't help "
"here."
msgstr ""
"Solo puedo fijar como destino un sitio en el que ya haya estado; aquí no "
"servirá de nada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Then we'll have to go through. When we rescue the prince, can you get us "
"back to the capitol?"
msgstr ""
"Entonces tendremos que atravesarlas. Cuando rescatemos al príncipe, ¿podrás "
"llevarnos de vuelta a la capital?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't think so. The further the destination, the more magic it takes out "
"of me. We're quite a ways from home."
msgstr ""
"No creo. Cuanto más lejos está el destino, más magia me consume. Estamos "
"bastante lejos de casa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If we're lucky, some of the survivors will realize I'm a bit limited and "
"will wait for us."
msgstr ""
"Si tenemos suerte, algunos de los supervivientes se darán cuenta de que mis "
"poderes son algo limitados y nos esperarán."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Or... they'd be sensible and get themselves home, leaving us out here to "
"this foolish mission alone."
msgstr ""
"O... serán sensatos, se irán a casa y nos dejarán aquí solos con esta misión"
" absurda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Do you want to rest while we get this stone moved, then?"
msgstr "¿Quieres descansar mientras apartamos esta piedra, entonces?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hey now. I said I can't make a doorway through it, I didn't say I was gonna "
"sit around and let you do all the work."
msgstr ""
"Eh, oye. He dicho que no puedo abrir una puerta a través de ella, no que "
"vaya a quedarme sentada dejando que hagáis todo el trabajo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You set your jaw and take out your tools. The rock is dense and you're "
"worried about a cave-in, but Redilok extends her hand and begins moving "
"stone with her magic. Smaller boulders lift into the air and are thrown "
"backward, crashing into the cavern walls far behind you."
msgstr ""
"Aprietas la mandíbula y sacas tus herramientas. La roca es densa y te "
"preocupa un derrumbe, pero Redilok extiende la mano y empieza a mover piedra"
" con su magia. Las rocas más pequeñas se elevan por los aires y salen "
"despedidas hacia atrás, estrellándose contra las paredes de la caverna muy "
"por detrás de vosotros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Please don't blow up, please don't blow up, please don't blo-"
msgstr "Que no explote, que no explote, que no explo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Whew..."
msgstr "Uf..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The three of you make short work of the blockage and climb out of the caverns through what appears to have been a natural entrance to the cave system. The sun is just beginning to set over the western horizon, which initially gives you pause. It'd taken a while to get out of the caves, but the Soulsmiths are on foot as well, many of which are injured. There's a good chance they'd have to stop nearby.\n"
"\n"
"You and [Companion Name] see it at the same time. A thin trail of smoke in this distance, not too far from you. A camp, it has to be."
msgstr ""
"Los tres despejáis el bloqueo en un periquete y salís de las cavernas por lo que parece haber sido una entrada natural al sistema de cuevas. El sol empieza a ponerse en el horizonte occidental, lo que al principio te hace dudar. Habéis tardado bastante en salir de las cuevas, pero los forjaalmas también van a pie, y muchos están heridos. Es muy probable que hayan tenido que detenerse cerca.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] y tú lo veis a la vez: un fino hilo de humo a lo lejos, no muy lejos de vosotros. Tiene que ser un campamento."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Either of you any good at trackin'?"
msgstr "¿Alguno de vosotros sabe rastrear?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... ugh. This is all a bit overwhelmin' for me."
msgstr "Yo... uf. Todo esto me supera un poco."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The sun's so bright... grass is too smelly. Dwarves belong in the ground, "
"not out in all this mess."
msgstr ""
"El sol brilla tanto... la hierba huele demasiado. Los enanos somos de bajo "
"tierra, no de todo este jaleo de aquí fuera."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yes, but we don't need to be. They clearly didn't think they'd be followed, "
"because they've set up camp just over the hill."
msgstr ""
"Sí, pero no nos hace falta. Está claro que no pensaban que los seguirían, "
"porque han acampado justo al otro lado de la colina."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well then, let's get after 'em!"
msgstr "¡Pues entonces, a por ellos!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We will. You're going to stay put. I promise you we'll get him back."
msgstr ""
"Iremos. Tú te vas a quedar aquí. Te prometo que lo traeremos de vuelta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're giving me an order?"
msgstr "¿Me estás dando una orden?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm fine. Don't need any babyin'."
msgstr "Estoy bien. No hace falta que me hagáis de niñeras."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm not asking. It seems like you'll hardly make the trek to their camp, let"
" alone be ready for another fight."
msgstr ""
"No te lo estoy pidiendo. Parece que apenas aguantarías la caminata hasta su "
"campamento, y mucho menos otra pelea."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, course I'm a little tired. I got my arm blown off and half the royal "
"court got butchered in front of me, then they stood back up and tried to "
"gnaw on me."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, claro que estoy un poco cansada. Me han volado el brazo y han "
"descuartizado a media corte real delante de mí, y luego se han levantado y "
"han intentado mordisquearme."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Speaking of you arm... you should tend to that wound, because your wrappings"
" are already coming undone."
msgstr ""
"Hablando de tu brazo... deberías curarte esa herida, porque las vendas ya se"
" están soltando."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We've got this, alright?"
msgstr "Nosotros nos encargamos, ¿vale?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Redilok jabs her stump towards [Companion Name] and looks like she's about to say something protest before she realizes she's dripping blood on her boot. She sits with a grumble and waves you off. That's about as good of a blessing as you figure you're going to get.\n"
"\n"
"As you get closer to camp, the two of you start to move more carefully, crawling on your stomachs through the plain's waist-high grass. The Soulsmiths may not have expected you to make it through the cave-in, but that didn't stop them from protecting themselves by littering the ground with volatile runes. [Companion Name] crawls towards one, trying to slowly pry it out of the ground with her knife.\n"
"\n"
"Slowly but surely, she wiggles it out of the ground, then passes it back to you, then moves onto the next one. As tempting as it may be to keep it for later, keeping a small pile of bombs in your backpack it bound to lead to an untimely end. You'll have to carefully destroy them.\n"
"\n"
"You roughly know how the magic works from your time creating similar charges with Gloob way back in Azamire, but these are far more complex."
msgstr ""
"Redilok apunta con el muñón hacia [Companion Name] y parece a punto de protestar, hasta que se da cuenta de que está goteando sangre sobre su bota. Se sienta refunfuñando y os despide con un gesto de la mano. Es más o menos la mejor bendición que crees que vas a obtener.\n"
"\n"
"A medida que os acercáis al campamento, empezáis a moveros con más cuidado, arrastrándoos boca abajo entre la hierba de la llanura, que os llega a la cintura. Puede que los forjaalmas no esperaran que superarais el derrumbe, pero eso no les impidió protegerse sembrando el suelo de runas volátiles. [Companion Name] se arrastra hasta una e intenta sacarla poco a poco del suelo con su cuchillo.\n"
"\n"
"Lentamente pero sin pausa, la va sacando del suelo, te la pasa y continúa con la siguiente. Por muy tentador que sea guardarlas para más adelante, llevar un montoncito de bombas en la mochila seguramente acabaría en un final prematuro. Tendrás que destruirlas con cuidado.\n"
"\n"
"Sabes más o menos cómo funciona la magia gracias a cuando creaste cargas parecidas con Gloob, allá en Azamire, pero estas son mucho más complejas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They have to pay."
msgstr "Tienen que pagar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Who... was that?"
msgstr "¿Quién... era esa?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As [Companion Name] very delicately extracts the volatile runes and passed them off, you slowly wither away their power. It's a nerve-wrecking process, and you feel time moving by glacially slow as you crawl closer and closer towards the Soulsmith's camp.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually, you find yourself just outside the camp. You look over the wretched summoners, and one stands out among the elites: An elderly woman whose robes are instead lined with light strips of blue and green instead of gold. Someone important, doubtlessly, though you don't remember seeing her during the attack on the Linking. Dozing by the fire, patrolling around the slug monster, and even cozying up with a few resting cultists are a dozen or so large wolf-like creatures the Soulsmiths seem fond of. These ones are a lot larger than those they attacked Azamire with, though. Watching one of them nuzzle one of the murderers and seemingly beg for a scrap of food... makes you feel strange. These creatures may be summoned beasts, but they are alive and maybe even close with those who brought them to life. \n"
"\n"
"Back in the tunnels, the monsters ended the lives of dozens of dwarves, but it's not like they had a choice. You know as much from the creatures you've summoned yourself. You will them to do something, and they obey. \n"
"\n"
"You'll try to end them quickly.\n"
"\n"
"You pry your eyes away and find Prince Cintak's corpse, still pinned to the slug creature by the black metal blade he was stabbed with. [Companion Name] scoots close and whispers to you."
msgstr ""
"Mientras [Companion Name] extrae con muchísimo cuidado las runas volátiles y te las pasa, tú vas debilitando su poder poco a poco. Es un proceso que destroza los nervios, y sientes que el tiempo pasa a paso de glaciar mientras os arrastráis cada vez más cerca del campamento de los forjaalmas.\n"
"\n"
"Al final, te encuentras justo a las afueras del campamento. Observas a los despreciables invocadores, y una destaca entre las élites: una anciana cuya túnica está ribeteada con finas franjas azules y verdes en lugar de doradas. Sin duda, alguien importante, aunque no recuerdas haberla visto durante el ataque al Enlace. Dormitando junto al fuego, patrullando alrededor del monstruo babosa e incluso acurrucadas con algunos sectarios que descansan, hay una docena o así de las grandes criaturas parecidas a lobos que tanto parecen gustar a los forjaalmas. Aunque estas son mucho más grandes que las que usaron para atacar Azamire. Ver cómo una de ellas le hace carantoñas a uno de los asesinos y parece suplicarle un trozo de comida... te produce una sensación extraña. Puede que estas criaturas sean bestias invocadas, pero están vivas y quizá incluso unidas a quienes les dieron la vida. \n"
"\n"
"En los túneles, los monstruos acabaron con la vida de decenas de enanos, pero no es que tuvieran elección. Lo sabes por las criaturas que has invocado tú. Les ordenas que hagan algo, y obedecen. \n"
"\n"
"Intentarás acabar con ellas rápido.\n"
"\n"
"Apartas la mirada y encuentras el cuerpo del príncipe Cintak, todavía clavado a la criatura babosa con la hoja de metal negro con la que lo apuñalaron. [Companion Name] se acerca y te susurra."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Why'd they take him, and only him?"
msgstr "¿Por qué se lo han llevado a él, y solo a él?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't know. The Soulsmiths were able to control those dead Dwarves during "
"the Linking, maybe it has something to do with that?"
msgstr ""
"No lo sé. Los forjaalmas pudieron controlar a esos enanos muertos durante el"
" Enlace, ¿quizá tenga algo que ver con eso?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Figure they'll tell us if we ask?"
msgstr "¿Crees que nos lo dirán si se lo preguntamos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'd have to leave one alive for that."
msgstr "Para eso tendríamos que dejar a uno con vida."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Guess not then."
msgstr "Pues supongo que no."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hey, [Player Name]?"
msgstr "Oye, ¿[Player Name]?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I didn't want to ask in front of the princess..."
msgstr "No quería preguntarlo delante de la princesa..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Do you think the prince is still alive?"
msgstr "¿Crees que el príncipe sigue vivo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...Well, we lived through the explosion and we're made of flesh. He's made "
"of stone and magma..."
msgstr ""
"...Bueno, nosotros sobrevivimos a la explosión y estamos hechos de carne. Él"
" está hecho de piedra y magma..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Guess it's a good thing we didn't save some of those explosive runes then, "
"huh? Wouldn't have minded putting them to good use."
msgstr ""
"Menos mal que no guardamos algunas de esas runas explosivas, ¿eh? No me "
"habría importado darles un buen uso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "If he is alive, and then we blew him up..."
msgstr "Si está vivo y luego lo volamos por los aires..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well... we'd be lucky if we were only banished from both Dwarven kingdoms."
msgstr ""
"Bueno... tendríamos suerte si solo nos desterraran de los dos reinos enanos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] grimaces at the thought. After a moment, she turns her "
"attention towards the camp. She nods towards the Soulsmiths, and you nod "
"back. No point in waiting."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] hace una mueca al pensarlo. Tras un momento, centra su "
"atención en el campamento. Señala con la cabeza a los forjaalmas y tú "
"asientes. No tiene sentido esperar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You clash against the Soulsmith Elites, knowing that they're going to use their summoned creatures to frontline for them like they did with the undead back during the Linking. As the elites fall, the vessel attached to the slug monster whirrs to life and bathes the area in flashes of green light, and the elites rise again. It doesn't stop you.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually, the monster runs out of bodies to throw at you, and the leader of this band of Soulsmiths throws herself at you directly, but even she falls. As you strike the killing blow, she commands the slug beast to escape, then falls silent in the tall grass of the plains. Following the orders of its master, the beast tears through the field, slimy arms tearing chunks out of the ground as it scuttles north. You keep pace with it, barely, but when you or [Companion] strike it, your weapons bounce off it, it's thick flesh seemingly resistant to conventional weaponry.\n"
"\n"
"Suddenly, Prince Cintak stirs. It's hard to tell if the man is trying to free himself, or if his corpse is just being flung about, but sure enough, he is able to sink his feet into the monster's meat and push. The black metal sword that pinned him to the beast slides out from it's body with a nauseating squelch and the prince tumbles to the ground. Both you and [Companion Name] let the monster run, quickly attending to the prince instead. He lives, though the weapon that bound him to the slug is still firmly stuck within his stone body. For now, you're just happy he's in one piece. You watch as the Soulsmith's Shambling Beast drags itself far to the north and wish you could give chase, but it's a problem for another day.\n"
"\n"
"Both of the royals support one another as the four of you head back down into the tunnels to reunite with the rest of the survivors. The molten Flamberians cheer with relief at the sight of their prince and surround him, offering to help tend his wounds or swear revenge on those who attacked the Linking. The Nalidasi greet the princess much the same. The wounded have been tended to through a mix of cauterization and sterilization from the party's booze, and many of the decorative tapestries have been torn to fashion bandages.\n"
"\n"
"Once everyone is settled, the magically inclined amongst the Nalidasi join together and open a large doorway in the wall of the Stoneway tunnel, bringing you right to the smoking crater that was once the station you left from. Stone buildings all around you have been leveled by a blast that far outweighs the Soulsmith's attack on the Linking. Now you know what they did with the Stoneglide.\n"
"\n"
"Both the Archivist and king Oyadazminis look upon the blast sight with anger and pain, but then relief upon seeing your group step out from the ashes. The man's eyes are wet with tears as he embraces his daughter, originally having feared the worst. He pulls you aside after breaking apart from the princess, and begs for your aid. He promises access to the Archive, the treasury, and whatever else you may desire in exchange for purging the Soulsmith blight from the land. Despite the Archivist trying in vain to slightly temper the king's impassioned promises of remuneration, his resolve is similarly hardened.\n"
"\n"
"Koganusan is going to war, and you will help guide them to victory."
msgstr ""
"Te enfrentas a las élites forjaalmas, sabiendo que usarán a sus criaturas invocadas como primera línea, igual que hicieron con los no muertos durante el Enlace. A medida que caen las élites, el recipiente unido al monstruo babosa se activa con un zumbido y baña la zona con destellos de luz verde, y las élites se levantan de nuevo. Eso no te detiene.\n"
"\n"
"Al final, el monstruo se queda sin cuerpos que lanzarte, y la líder de esta banda de forjaalmas se lanza directamente contra ti, pero también cae. Cuando le asestas el golpe mortal, le ordena a la bestia babosa que huya y luego queda en silencio entre la alta hierba de la llanura. Siguiendo las órdenes de su ama, la bestia atraviesa el campo a toda prisa, arrancando trozos de tierra con sus brazos viscosos mientras se escabulle hacia el norte. Le sigues el ritmo a duras penas, pero cuando [Companion] o tú la golpeáis, vuestras armas rebotan: su gruesa carne parece resistente a las armas convencionales.\n"
"\n"
"De repente, el príncipe Cintak se mueve. Cuesta saber si intenta liberarse o si su cadáver simplemente se zarandea, pero, efectivamente, consigue hundir los pies en la carne del monstruo y empujar. La espada de metal negro que lo clavaba a la bestia sale de su cuerpo con un chapoteo nauseabundo y el príncipe cae rodando al suelo. Tanto [Companion Name] como tú dejáis escapar al monstruo y os ocupáis enseguida del príncipe. Está vivo, aunque el arma que lo unía a la babosa sigue firmemente clavada en su cuerpo de piedra. Por ahora, te alegras de que esté entero. Ves cómo la Bestia tambaleante de los forjaalmas se arrastra lejos hacia el norte y desearías poder perseguirla, pero eso es un problema para otro día.\n"
"\n"
"Los dos miembros de la realeza se apoyan el uno en el otro mientras los cuatro volvéis a bajar a los túneles para reuniros con el resto de supervivientes. Los flamberianos fundidos lanzan vítores de alivio al ver a su príncipe y lo rodean, ofreciéndose a curarle las heridas o jurando venganza contra quienes atacaron el Enlace. Los nalidasi reciben a la princesa de forma muy parecida. Han atendido a los heridos mediante una mezcla de cauterización y esterilización con el alcohol de la fiesta, y han rasgado muchos de los tapices decorativos para hacer vendas.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando todo el mundo se ha calmado, los nalidasi con dotes mágicas se unen y abren una gran puerta en la pared del túnel de la Vía de Piedra que os lleva directamente al cráter humeante que antes era la estación de la que partisteis. Los edificios de piedra a vuestro alrededor han quedado arrasados por una explosión mucho mayor que el ataque de los forjaalmas al Enlace. Ahora sabes qué hicieron con el Deslizalosas.\n"
"\n"
"Tanto el Archivero como el rey Oyadazminis contemplan la zona de la explosión con ira y dolor, pero luego con alivio al ver a vuestro grupo salir de entre las cenizas. Al rey se le llenan los ojos de lágrimas al abrazar a su hija, ya que se temía lo peor. Tras separarse de la princesa, te lleva aparte y te suplica tu ayuda. Promete acceso al Archivo, al tesoro y a cualquier otra cosa que desees a cambio de purgar la tierra de la plaga de los forjaalmas. Aunque el Archivero intenta en vano moderar un poco las apasionadas promesas de recompensa del rey, su determinación es igual de firme.\n"
"\n"
"Koganusan va a la guerra, y tú los ayudarás a alcanzar la victoria."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ24"
msgstr "MQ24"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Repairing What Remains - The Soulsmiths successfully hijacked the Stoneglide"
" and loaded it with explosives while those attending the Linking were "
"preoccupied on all sides by assailants. Their efforts resulted in a massive "
"swathe of Koganusan being reduced to rubble. Any amount of relief will go a "
"long way towards caring for the populace."
msgstr ""
"Reparar lo que queda: Los forjaalmas lograron secuestrar el Deslizalosas y "
"cargarlo de explosivos mientras los asistentes al Enlace estaban ocupados "
"con atacantes por todos los flancos. Su ataque redujo a escombros una enorme"
" franja de Koganusan. Cualquier ayuda contribuirá mucho a cuidar de la "
"población."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Her house simply isn't enough. How about a proper cookhouse? Maybe she'll be"
" able to get some help then, too?"
msgstr ""
"Su casa no basta. ¿Qué tal una buena casa de comidas? ¿Quizá así también "
"consiga algo de ayuda?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hopefully this will work a bit better than her home."
msgstr "Ojalá esto funcione un poco mejor que su casa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"King Oyadazminis and the Archivist move with purpose through the ruined "
"market district of Koganusan, handing out food to those who lost their homes"
" and businesses, comforting others, and lending a hand where they can. "
"Though it's a small comfort to those figuring out how to go on, it's still "
"more than enough to get some following in their footsteps if they're able. "
"The pair catch your eye and rush over after excusing themselves from a small"
" group of young dwarves."
msgstr ""
"El rey Oyadazminis y el Archivero recorren con decisión el arruinado "
"distrito del mercado de Koganusan, repartiendo comida a quienes han perdido "
"sus casas y negocios, consolando a otros y echando una mano donde pueden. "
"Aunque es un pequeño consuelo para quienes intentan averiguar cómo seguir "
"adelante, basta para que algunos sigan su ejemplo en la medida de sus "
"posibilidades. La pareja te ve y se acerca a toda prisa tras disculparse "
"ante un pequeño grupo de jóvenes enanos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I never thought there'd be a day where I'm pleased to see two humans waiting"
" for me, but these are trying times. "
msgstr ""
"Nunca pensé que llegaría el día en que me alegraría de ver a dos humanos "
"esperándome, pero corren tiempos difíciles. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I haven't had the chance to properly thank you for returning my daughter to "
"me, and unfortunately I am rather tied down at present."
msgstr ""
"No he tenido ocasión de agradeceros como es debido que me devolvierais a mi "
"hija y, por desgracia, ahora mismo estoy bastante ocupado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We can see that. It feels rare to see someone of your station handling a "
"crisis hands on."
msgstr ""
"Ya lo vemos. No es habitual ver a alguien de tu rango ocupándose de una "
"crisis en persona."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Would you rather I leave it to those beneath me?"
msgstr "¿Preferirías que se lo dejara a mis subordinados?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No, not at all. If anything, I find it refreshing, and it's clear your "
"people do too."
msgstr ""
"No, en absoluto. Si acaso, me parece refrescante, y está claro que a tu "
"pueblo también."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I just wish I could have prevented it in the first place..."
msgstr "Ojalá hubiera podido evitarlo desde el principio..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I wish [Companion Name] and I could have done more."
msgstr "...Ojalá [Companion Name] y yo hubiéramos podido hacer más."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Excuse me for speaking out of turn, but from the reports I've seen, it "
"sounds as though there wouldn't have been a single survivor were it not for "
"your efforts."
msgstr ""
"Disculpad que hable sin que me corresponda, pero, según los informes que he "
"visto, parece que no habría habido ni un solo superviviente de no ser por "
"vuestros esfuerzos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We owe you quite the debt, but it'll be some time before we can properly "
"return the favor."
msgstr ""
"Tenemos una gran deuda con vosotros, pero pasará algún tiempo antes de que "
"podamos devolveros el favor como es debido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We're not worried about it in the slightest, we're just trying to do what we"
" can to prepare to drive the Soulsmiths out of here for good."
msgstr ""
"No nos preocupa lo más mínimo; solo intentamos hacer lo que podemos para "
"prepararnos y echar de aquí a los forjaalmas para siempre."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You have my blessing and what I can spare of my men, though free hands are "
"in short supply."
msgstr ""
"Tenéis mi bendición y los hombres que pueda prestaros, aunque escasean las "
"manos libres."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Speaking of which... If you find yourself in need of a bit more than I can "
"offer..."
msgstr ""
"Hablando de eso... Si necesitáis algo más de lo que yo puedo ofreceros..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm sure that the townsfolk would be even more willing to lend a hand with a"
" bit of food in their bellies, or if you're able to help cure what ails "
"them."
msgstr ""
"Seguro que la gente de la ciudad estaría aún más dispuesta a echar una mano "
"con algo de comida en el estómago, o si podéis ayudar a curar sus males."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm sure we can figure something out, can't we [Player Name]?"
msgstr "Seguro que se nos ocurre algo, ¿verdad, [Player Name]?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Not sure where to start, you decide on the easiest of the options you can think of. Food. Easy to make in bulk, and something that everyone needs. You ask around until you hear of a kindly woman named Zotty, who has been taking care of as many of the districts kids as she can. From what you gather, she was a baker, but her business was destroyed in the attack, a story like many others in Koganusan. When you visit her house on the edge of the ruined district, you see a line of several kids line up by the door, each of them getting a small but well-seasoned portion of stew and a bit of bread.\n"
"\n"
"Zotty is a bit wary of you at first, but your reputations proceed you both, and she simply says that any help you can offer is more than enough. It's clear she doesn't expect much, but you hope to prove her wrong."
msgstr ""
"Sin saber muy bien por dónde empezar, te decides por la opción más sencilla que se te ocurre: comida. Es fácil de hacer en grandes cantidades y todo el mundo la necesita. Preguntas por ahí hasta que oyes hablar de una amable mujer llamada Zotty, que ha estado cuidando a todos los niños del distrito que ha podido. Por lo que averiguas, era panadera, pero su negocio quedó destruido en el ataque, una historia como tantas otras en Koganusan. Cuando visitas su casa, en el límite del distrito en ruinas, ves una fila de varios niños junto a la puerta, y cada uno recibe una ración pequeña pero bien sazonada de estofado y un poco de pan.\n"
"\n"
"Al principio Zotty desconfía un poco de ti, pero vuestra reputación os precede a los dos, y se limita a decir que cualquier ayuda que podáis ofrecer es más que suficiente. Está claro que no espera mucho, pero confías en demostrarle que se equivoca."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#. Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Do we just plant these in the ground or..?"
msgstr "¿Esto se planta en el suelo sin más o...?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The devastation left by the Soulsmith attack has both fortunately and unfortunately left behind no small number of plots free of their original buildings. All it takes is a small chat with the king and one of them is requisitioned from its deceased owner and then attributed to the two of you. You draft up and begin construction on a sizeable cookhouse, capable of feeding a large portion of those displaced by the attack, and giving new purpose to a few as well, should they choose to help Zotty.\n"
"\n"
"Building the structure goes much faster than expected. When townsfolk see you working on the structure, many come to help for any number of reasons. Dwarven pride, giving back to their community, or even trying to help the two of you in return for saving as many as you could at the Linking. Before you know it, the dwarven cookhouse stands tall amidst the rubble, ready to feed those in need. Zotty admires the building with her hands on her hips, save for a couple small dabs at her eyes when she thinks you aren't looking."
msgstr ""
"La devastación que dejó el ataque de los forjaalmas ha dejado, por suerte y por desgracia, no pocas parcelas libres de sus edificios originales. Basta una breve charla con el rey para que una de ellas se requise a su difunto propietario y se os asigne a los dos. Hacéis los planos y empezáis a construir una casa de comidas considerable, capaz de alimentar a gran parte de los desplazados por el ataque y de dar un nuevo propósito a algunos de ellos, si deciden ayudar a Zotty.\n"
"\n"
"La construcción va mucho más rápido de lo esperado. Cuando la gente del pueblo os ve trabajando en el edificio, muchos acuden a ayudar por todo tipo de razones: el orgullo enano, el deseo de devolver algo a su comunidad o incluso el de ayudaros a cambio de haber salvado a tantos como pudisteis en el Enlace. Antes de que te des cuenta, la casa de comidas enana se alza entre los escombros, lista para alimentar a los necesitados. Zotty admira el edificio con las manos en las caderas, salvo por un par de toquecitos en los ojos cuando cree que no la estás mirando."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"When I said I wanted a spot of help, I was expecting a bag of tubers, or "
"maybe a scrap of meat."
msgstr ""
"Cuando dije que quería un poco de ayuda, me esperaba un saco de tubérculos "
"o, como mucho, un trozo de carne."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Didn't expect you to drop a whole bleedin' building on my head!"
msgstr ""
"¡No esperaba que me plantarais un maldito edificio entero en la cabeza!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hopefully it'll be a good starting point. Lots of folks from around town "
"pitched in, and there's a ton of cookware and raw foods as well."
msgstr ""
"Esperemos que sea un buen punto de partida. Mucha gente de la ciudad ha "
"echado una mano, y también hay un montón de utensilios de cocina y alimentos"
" crudos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's more than I'll be able to handle alone. You two bring an army to help "
"me keep the place runnin' too?"
msgstr ""
"Es más de lo que podré llevar yo sola. ¿Habéis traído también un ejército "
"para ayudarme a mantener esto en marcha?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Not quite, but we figure if it's anything like building the place, once you "
"start whipping up meals, others will start leaping over the counter to help "
"you out."
msgstr ""
"No exactamente, pero creemos que, si pasa lo mismo que con la construcción, "
"en cuanto empieces a preparar comidas, los demás saltarán el mostrador para "
"ayudarte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You think I'm lettin' just any schmuck make food for the town?"
msgstr "¿Crees que voy a dejar que cualquier pelagatos cocine para el pueblo?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm pleased the Nalidasi have left such an impression on you as to make you "
"think we can do anything."
msgstr ""
"Me alegra que los nalidasi os hayan causado tan buena impresión como para "
"pensar que somos capaces de todo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But let me tell you, cooking is not a strongsuit of our kind."
msgstr ""
"Pero dejadme deciros que la cocina no es el punto fuerte de los nuestros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We've seen a few displays of... less proper ettique, but you all seem to "
"take such pride in your craftsdwarfship, I almost find it hard to believe "
"the Nalidasi don't treat food the same."
msgstr ""
"Hemos visto algunas muestras de... una etiqueta menos refinada, pero os "
"enorgullecéis tanto de vuestra artesanía enana que casi me cuesta creer que "
"los nalidasi no traten la comida igual."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Let's just say that there's a reason you've seen our crafts and not our fine"
" dining experiences."
msgstr ""
"Digamos que hay una razón por la que habéis visto nuestra artesanía y no "
"nuestra alta cocina."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I swear, folks are more inclined to start chewing gravel and wash it down "
"with ale than to enjoy a proper meal half the time."
msgstr ""
"Os lo juro, la mitad de las veces la gente prefiere masticar grava y bajarla"
" con cerveza antes que disfrutar de una comida como es debido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I was tryin' to do my best to fix that before my bakery got blown to bits."
msgstr ""
"Intentaba arreglarlo como podía antes de que mi panadería saltara por los "
"aires."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Any ideas on where we could find you some help, then?"
msgstr "¿Alguna idea de dónde podríamos encontrarte ayuda, entonces?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We just gotta give folks something they cannot possibly mess up. Cobblestone"
" Soup."
msgstr ""
"Solo tenemos que darle a la gente algo que sea imposible de estropear. Sopa "
"de adoquines."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...doesn't seem all that much better than the gravel you mentioned..."
msgstr "...no parece mucho mejor que la grava que has mencionado..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Zotty lets out a hearty chuckle before digging in her pocket and handing "
"over a pouch of what looks like small bits of quartz. She assures you that "
"they'll grow into Stonemelons, which are used in a soup that's hearty and "
"filling, and practically impossible to mess up."
msgstr ""
"Zotty suelta una carcajada sonora antes de rebuscar en su bolsillo y "
"entregarte una bolsita de lo que parecen pequeños trozos de cuarzo. Te "
"asegura que se convertirán en melones de piedra, que se usan en una sopa "
"contundente y saciante, y prácticamente imposible de estropear."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This feels a little unorthodox."
msgstr "Esto parece un poco heterodoxo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I should probably wash my pickaxe."
msgstr "Debería lavar el pico."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The stonemelons grow strong with little supervision, which doesn't surprise "
"you based on the name. Continuing to live up to their title, these small "
"boulder-like melons look nearly identical to any ordinary rock you'd see out"
" and about, except that they're almost perfectly spherical orbs. They're "
"heavy, but you manage to lug your harvest back to Zotty's new cookhouse."
msgstr ""
"Los melones de piedra crecen fuertes con poca supervisión, lo cual no te "
"sorprende, viendo cómo se llaman. Y hacen honor a ese nombre: estos pequeños"
" melones con forma de roca son casi idénticos a cualquier piedra corriente "
"que verías por ahí, salvo porque son esferas casi perfectas. Pesan, pero "
"consigues llevar tu cosecha a rastras hasta la nueva casa de comidas de "
"Zotty."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Proper dwarven farmers, the lot of you! Hardly seen any Stonemelons this "
"size in my days, almost as good as my ol' pappy Xon could grow."
msgstr ""
"¡Granjeros enanos de verdad, eso es lo que sois! Pocas veces he visto "
"melones de piedra de este tamaño en mi vida, casi tan buenos como los que "
"cultivaba mi viejo papá Xon."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm glad you're impressed, though almost surprised you could tell them apart"
" from any old rock."
msgstr ""
"Me alegra que te impresionen, aunque casi me sorprende que sepas "
"distinguirlos de cualquier piedra."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Clear as day to my dwarvern eyes, surprised you don't see it."
msgstr ""
"Para mis ojos enanos está claro como el día, me sorprende que tú no lo veas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Clear as day? But we don't get any sunlight down here..."
msgstr "¿Claro como el día? Pero aquí abajo no nos llega la luz del sol..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's awfully clear though, ain't it?"
msgstr "Pues está clarísimo, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I guess so..."
msgstr "Supongo..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, how do we get these open? Should have plenty of knives around."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, ¿y cómo los abrimos? Seguro que hay cuchillos de sobra por aquí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Our knives are for cuttin' up veggies and carvin' out meat. Step aside."
msgstr "Nuestros cuchillos son pa' cortar verduras y trinchar carne. Aparta."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Zotty grabs a pickaxe from the wall she seems to have brought out for just "
"this purpose. She brings it down on the melon several times to no avail - to"
" the point you're concerned you brought her an actual rock - until "
"eventually, the melon cracks open like a geode. Inside, the stonemelon is "
"filled with white flesh, which Zotty then extends out to you. You scrape a "
"bit off and are surprised by its rubbery texture, and the fact that it's "
"almost savory, like smoked meat. Zotty waves her hand towards your pile and "
"gets to work cutting open a few more herself."
msgstr ""
"Zotty coge de la pared un pico que parece haber traído justo para esto. Lo "
"descarga sobre el melón varias veces sin éxito (hasta el punto de que te "
"preocupa haberle traído una piedra de verdad) hasta que, por fin, el melón "
"se abre como una geoda. Por dentro, el melón de piedra está lleno de pulpa "
"blanca, que Zotty te ofrece. Raspas un poco y te sorprende su textura "
"gomosa, y que tenga un sabor casi salado, como la carne ahumada. Zotty "
"señala tu montón con la mano y se pone a abrir unos cuantos más ella misma."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A bit of this, and a bit of that..."
msgstr "Un poco de esto, y un poco de aquello..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And serve!"
msgstr "¡Y a servir!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You do a better job of mashing the stonemelons to bits than splitting them "
"perfectly in half like Zotty does in the beginning until she gives you a few"
" pointers. You slowly but surely make your way through the pile, leaving "
"behind a crime scene that'd inspire fear in all but the bravest of produce."
msgstr ""
"Al principio se te da mejor hacer papilla los melones de piedra que "
"partirlos perfectamente por la mitad como hace Zotty, hasta que te da unos "
"cuantos consejos. Poco a poco vas acabando con el montón, dejando atrás una "
"escena del crimen que aterrorizaría a cualquier producto de la huerta salvo "
"al más valiente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The two of you done makin' a mess?"
msgstr "¿Habéis terminado de liarla, vosotros dos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Think so! What do ya do with 'em now?"
msgstr "¡Creo que sí! ¿Y qué se hace con ellos ahora?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I ain't just gonna tell ya, I'm gonna show ya."
msgstr "No os lo voy a decir sin más, os lo voy a enseñar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I know the two of ya' got some proper worldsaving to go do, but if everyone "
"here starves by the time you get back, what's it for?"
msgstr ""
"Sé que vosotros dos tenéis que ir a salvar el mundo como es debido, pero si "
"aquí todo el mundo se muere de hambre antes de que volváis, ¿de qué sirve?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I won't keep ya long, promise."
msgstr "No os entretendré mucho, lo prometo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Zotty starts the stoves and begins carving out the melon flesh, dicing and seasoning it with a handful of herbs. Once her pot of water begin to boil, she tosses the prepared flesh back in, then combines it with some meat and veggies and stirs. Once done, she pours it into the hollowed out shell of the stonemelon and pushes it towards the two of you.\n"
"\n"
"The Nalidasi may not value cooking much, but with food like this, it's sure to change."
msgstr ""
"Zotty enciende los fogones y empieza a vaciar la pulpa del melón, cortándola en dados y sazonándola con un puñado de hierbas. Cuando el agua de su olla empieza a hervir, echa dentro la pulpa preparada, la mezcla con algo de carne y verduras y remueve. Cuando termina, lo vierte en la cáscara vaciada del melón de piedra y os la acerca a los dos.\n"
"\n"
"Puede que los nalidasi no valoren mucho la cocina, pero con comida como esta, seguro que eso cambia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Before either you or [Companion Name] can finish cooking your first pots, both Nalidasi and many of the Flamberian survivors from the Linking start trickling into the cookhouse, asking how they can help - in exchange for a bit of food of course - and Zotty begins barking out orders like a trained general. Flamberians heat their bodies and are used as stoves, much to the amusement of both races of dwarves. Zotty moves through the kitchen with purpose, correcting well-intentioned helpers and directing them to watch you and [Companion Name] as examples.\n"
"\n"
"It takes a while, but those in the cookhouse start to produce Cobblestone Soup that Zotty is willing to serve to the long line of hungry survivors of the market district disaster. The two of you do so well Zotty is reluctant to let you go, until King Ozadazminis himself offers himself and the Archivist as replacements during a visit to the building's opening night. Zotty grumbles and mentions that good help is hard to find, but allows to you go after making sure you've both eaten your fill."
msgstr ""
"Antes de que [Companion Name] o tú terminéis de cocinar vuestras primeras ollas, tanto nalidasi como muchos de los supervivientes flamberianos del Enlace empiezan a llegar a la casa de comidas preguntando cómo pueden ayudar (a cambio de algo de comida, claro), y Zotty empieza a dar órdenes como un general curtido. Los flamberianos calientan sus cuerpos y hacen de fogones, para diversión de ambas razas de enanos. Zotty se mueve por la cocina con decisión, corrigiendo a los ayudantes bienintencionados y pidiéndoles que se fijen en [Companion Name] y en ti como ejemplo.\n"
"\n"
"Lleva un tiempo, pero los de la casa de comidas empiezan a preparar una Sopa de adoquines que Zotty está dispuesta a servir a la larga fila de supervivientes hambrientos de la catástrofe del distrito del mercado. Lo hacéis tan bien que a Zotty le cuesta dejaros marchar, hasta que el propio rey Oyadazminis se ofrece, junto con el Archivero, a sustituiros durante una visita a la noche de inauguración del edificio. Zotty refunfuña y comenta que es difícil encontrar buena ayuda, pero os deja marchar después de asegurarse de que habéis comido hasta hartaros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ25"
msgstr "MQ25"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Slug Slayer - There's only one thing you've seen that can pierce the "
"Soulsmith slug monster's thick flesh, and it's currently embeded within the "
"chest of the Flamberian Prince. Surely he's willing to part with it... if he"
" can."
msgstr ""
"Matababosas: Solo hay una cosa que hayas visto capaz de atravesar la gruesa "
"carne del monstruo babosa de los forjaalmas, y ahora mismo está clavada en "
"el pecho del príncipe flamberiano. Seguro que está dispuesto a desprenderse "
"de ella... si puede."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Should come to a point here, maybe a handle made of..."
msgstr "Aquí debería acabar en punta, quizá con un mango hecho de..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Looks sharp enough to me."
msgstr "A mí me parece lo bastante afilado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You wander outside of the room Prince Cintak has been being kept in, but "
"were blocked by Princess Redilok before you could see the man.You and "
"[Companion Name]'s plan is absurd, but if you intend to take down the "
"Shambling Beast, you see no other path forward. You lay it out in detail to "
"Princess Redilok, who blanches at the thought."
msgstr ""
"Merodeas fuera de la habitación en la que tienen al príncipe Cintak, pero la"
" princesa Redilok te cierra el paso antes de que puedas verlo. El plan que "
"tenéis [Companion Name] y tú es absurdo, pero si queréis acabar con la "
"Bestia tambaleante, no veis otra salida. Se lo explicas con todo detalle a "
"la princesa Redilok, que palidece solo de pensarlo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You want to what?"
msgstr "¿Que queréis qué?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll be careful, I promise."
msgstr "Tendremos cuidado, lo prometo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh, right. You'll carefully rip the spike of unknown material out of Prince "
"Cintak's chest and close him up before he bleeds out."
msgstr ""
"Ah, claro. Arrancaréis con cuidado la púa de material desconocido del pecho "
"del príncipe Cintak y lo cerraréis antes de que se desangre."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Which of you is the surgeon, hm? I'm sure my father has an axe or something "
"you could use..."
msgstr ""
"¿Cuál de los dos es el cirujano, eh? Seguro que mi padre tiene un hacha o "
"algo que podáis usar..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...I know the concept is scary, but we're going to ask the prince what kind "
"of... wound care his people even use."
msgstr ""
"...Sé que la idea da miedo, pero vamos a preguntarle al príncipe qué tipo "
"de... cuidados de heridas usa su pueblo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We've banadaged ourselves up countless times, but I'm not really sure where "
"we'd start with someone made of stone and lava."
msgstr ""
"Nos hemos vendado a nosotros mismos incontables veces, pero no sé muy bien "
"por dónde empezaríamos con alguien hecho de piedra y lava."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And we're not going to be the ones operating on him, don't worry."
msgstr "Y no seremos nosotros quienes lo operen, no te preocupes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I remember being introduced to someone at the Linking that seemed to be a "
"big-shot in Flamberian society because they were a doctor."
msgstr ""
"Recuerdo que en el Enlace me presentaron a alguien que parecía un pez gordo "
"de la sociedad flamberiana por ser médico."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If he's still around, he would have come back with the rest of the "
"survivors. He'd be the surgeon."
msgstr ""
"Si sigue por aquí, habrá vuelto con el resto de supervivientes. Él sería el "
"cirujano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...fine."
msgstr "...Está bien."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But if the prince doesn't make it, I'll see you both tried for treason. You "
"won't leave Koganusan alive."
msgstr ""
"Pero si el príncipe no sobrevive, me encargaré de que os juzguen a los dos "
"por traición. No saldréis de Koganusan con vida."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Redilok seems to mull on the idea, before stepping aside and opening the door to his room. Prince Cintak is in rough shape. He put on a brave front while trekking back to the Dwarven capital, but the events of the Linking have doubtlessly worn away at the man. His breaths are labored, and the twisted black metal rod peircing his chest seems to have fused more with him. Despite his state, he still manages a smile as the three of you enter the room. After catching him up on current events, you detail your reason for visiting. You want to pry the metal from his chest and fashion it into a weapon to kill the Shambling Beast the Soulsmiths attacking the Linking with.\n"
"\n"
"He digests the words for only a moment before praising the idea, reiterating that it seems to be the only thing that's pieced the beast's flesh, and that he's more than willing to help and details what he knows. First-aid for Flamberians seems to be more akin to working on a forged good than a living being, but you suppose that that makes sense for a being comprised of stone and magma. His people use emerald-tipped blades that are magically enhanced to cut into thier rocky exteriors. Then, for a wound that'll be as severe as his, a concoction of golden stardust and sporlyle would be able to help his body seal the wound, but he'd need to be hammered closed, like working on a platebody.\n"
"\n"
"Princess Rodilok nearly faints as the man details beating on his chest with hammers to close the wound.\n"
"\n"
"You decide to search for your doctor first. He's easy to find, as the man has been helping treat some of the more severely wounded folks in the Nalidasi market district, which has gone a long ways towards lightening some of concern that the Flamberians were behind the attack. When you detail your plan for working on the prince, Doctor Hacksmith is able to draw up a detailed schematic for this emerald blade that Cintak mentioned, but all of the doctor's handwriting is next to indesipherable. At least the diagram is detailed enough for you to work on."
msgstr ""
"Redilok parece darle vueltas a la idea antes de apartarse y abrir la puerta de su habitación. El príncipe Cintak está en mal estado. Mostró valentía durante el camino de vuelta a la capital enana, pero los sucesos del Enlace sin duda le han pasado factura. Respira con dificultad, y la retorcida barra de metal negro que le atraviesa el pecho parece haberse fusionado aún más con él. A pesar de su estado, consigue sonreír cuando los tres entráis en la habitación. Después de ponerlo al día, le explicas el motivo de vuestra visita: queréis arrancarle el metal del pecho y convertirlo en un arma para matar a la Bestia tambaleante con la que los forjaalmas atacaron el Enlace.\n"
"\n"
"Digiere tus palabras solo un momento antes de elogiar la idea, insistiendo en que parece lo único que ha atravesado la carne de la bestia y en que está más que dispuesto a ayudar, y te cuenta lo que sabe. Los primeros auxilios para los flamberianos parecen más propios de trabajar una pieza forjada que de tratar a un ser vivo, pero supones que tiene sentido para un ser hecho de piedra y magma. Su pueblo usa hojas con punta de esmeralda potenciadas mágicamente para cortar su exterior rocoso. Después, para una herida tan grave como la suya, un brebaje de polvo estelar dorado y esporlila ayudaría a su cuerpo a cerrar la herida, pero habría que cerrarla a martillazos, como quien trabaja un peto.\n"
"\n"
"La princesa Redilok casi se desmaya cuando él describe cómo le golpearán el pecho con martillos para cerrar la herida.\n"
"\n"
"Decides buscar primero a tu médico. Es fácil de encontrar, ya que ha estado ayudando a tratar a algunos de los heridos más graves del distrito del mercado nalidasi, lo que ha contribuido mucho a disipar parte de la sospecha de que los flamberianos estaban detrás del ataque. Cuando le explicas tu plan para operar al príncipe, el doctor Hacksmith consigue dibujar un esquema detallado de la hoja de esmeralda que mencionó Cintak, pero la letra del doctor es prácticamente indescifrable. Al menos el diagrama es lo bastante detallado para que puedas trabajar con él."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I wonder how Flamberian bodies handle stardust..."
msgstr ""
"Me pregunto cómo reaccionan los cuerpos flamberianos al polvo estelar..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Can't imagine something like this would have a regenerative effect on human "
"flesh... Maybe the opposite."
msgstr ""
"No me imagino que algo así tenga un efecto regenerador en la carne humana..."
" Quizá todo lo contrario."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"When king Oyadazminis said that you'd have the backing of the whole kingdom when it came to getting them ready to go against the Soulsmiths, you didn't expect the level of support he decided to show. When one of his aids found you and [Companion Name] hammering out prototypes of the emerald tool in the palance courtyard, Oyadazminis himself had his people gather your things and walked you through the capitol until you found a lovely, well-stocked workshop built within the stalk of a large plant that you've never seen anywhere outside of the cavern. The workshop itself is outfitted with dozens of tools and workstations you couldn't even begin to guess at the function of. He bought the workshop from the owner, who tried to protest up until the kings' aids draped him in jeweled necklaces and sacks of gold were dropped in front of him until he couldn't see over the pile. In exchange, him and his workers found a perfect balance of handing you tools before you even asked for them, pointers in working with emerald, and giving you space when you needed it.\n"
"\n"
"After a few dozen failed attempts, you finally create a blade that was strong enough to chip away at stone with nary a scratch, and that is without the magical enhancements the prince mentioned. The former workshop owner - an older dwarf with gold-blonde hair who introduced himself as Kajc -  takes the blade and plunges it into the wall, before leaning back and stroking his chin."
msgstr ""
"Cuando el rey Oyadazminis dijo que tendríais el respaldo de todo el reino a la hora de prepararlo para enfrentarse a los forjaalmas, no esperabas el nivel de apoyo que decidió mostrar. Cuando uno de sus ayudantes os encontró a [Companion Name] y a ti forjando a martillazos prototipos de la herramienta de esmeralda en el patio del palacio, el propio Oyadazminis hizo que su gente recogiera vuestras cosas y os acompañó por la capital hasta que encontrasteis un taller precioso y bien surtido, construido dentro del tallo de una gran planta que nunca habías visto fuera de la caverna. El taller en sí está equipado con decenas de herramientas y puestos de trabajo cuya función ni siquiera alcanzas a adivinar. Le compró el taller al dueño, que intentó protestar hasta que los ayudantes del rey lo cubrieron de collares enjoyados y le dejaron delante sacos de oro hasta que no pudo ver por encima del montón. A cambio, él y sus trabajadores encontraron el equilibrio perfecto entre pasarte las herramientas antes incluso de que las pidieras, darte consejos para trabajar la esmeralda y dejarte espacio cuando lo necesitabas.\n"
"\n"
"Tras unas cuantas decenas de intentos fallidos, por fin creas una hoja lo bastante fuerte como para picar piedra sin un solo rasguño, y eso sin las mejoras mágicas que mencionó el príncipe. El antiguo dueño del taller, un enano mayor de pelo rubio dorado que se presentó como Kajc, coge la hoja y la clava en la pared, antes de echarse hacia atrás y acariciarse la barbilla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Now, that's a fine tool you've got there, folks."
msgstr "Vaya, qué buena herramienta tenéis ahí, amigos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What'd you say it was for, again?"
msgstr "¿Para qué decíais que era?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Eh... it might be better if you don't know."
msgstr "Eh... quizá sea mejor que no lo sepas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Fine then, keep your secrets."
msgstr "Muy bien, guardaos vuestros secretos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Make sure you come on back here though if you've got more stuff to work on."
msgstr ""
"Pero aseguraos de volver por aquí si tenéis más cosas en las que trabajar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I suppose my workshop is more the king's workshop, so it's not like I'd be "
"able to stop you even if I wanted to."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que mi taller es más bien el taller del rey, así que tampoco podría "
"impedíroslo aunque quisiera."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And how do you feel about that?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo te sientes al respecto?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh, it's wonderful! Do you know how long its been since I've had to help "
"make something important?"
msgstr ""
"¡Ah, es maravilloso! ¿Sabéis cuánto tiempo hace que no tengo que ayudar a "
"hacer algo importante?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's just been random bits and bobs for years. A ring here, a golden egg "
"that'll sit on a shelf collecting dust for ages there."
msgstr ""
"Llevo años haciendo cachivaches sueltos. Un anillo por aquí, un huevo de oro"
" que pasará siglos en una estantería cogiendo polvo por allá."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"At least this fancy poker you've got is going to be used for something. "
"Makes me feel useful."
msgstr ""
"Al menos este atizador tan elegante que tenéis va a servir para algo. Me "
"hace sentir útil."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You head back to the palace with your emerald tool and hand it off to the "
"princess, who promises she'll make it capable of withstanding the staggering"
" heat of Cintak's blood. She mentions few things can handle someone as hot "
"as him, and you get the feeling that she stopped talking about his blood a "
"long while ago, but you let her babble, as she's clearly nervous about the "
"whole ordeal of cutting open her not-so-secret love. Eventually she shoos "
"you away, to get you working on the potion that should help seal up the "
"prince once Hacksmith is done cutting the metal out of his body."
msgstr ""
"Vuelves al palacio con tu herramienta de esmeralda y se la entregas a la "
"princesa, que promete hacerla capaz de soportar el tremendo calor de la "
"sangre de Cintak. Comenta que pocas cosas pueden aguantar a alguien tan "
"ardiente como él, y te da la sensación de que hace rato que dejó de hablar "
"de su sangre, pero la dejas parlotear, ya que está claramente nerviosa por "
"todo el asunto de abrir en canal a su no tan secreto amor. Al final te echa "
"con un gesto para que te pongas a trabajar en la poción que debería ayudar a"
" cerrar al príncipe cuando Hacksmith termine de sacarle el metal del cuerpo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Just... stay still!"
msgstr "¡Tú... estate quieto!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Finally."
msgstr "Por fin."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You come back with the sparkling concoction and bring it into the bedroom-"
"turned-surgery suite. A few Flamberians have joined Doctor Hacksmith, their "
"purpose seemingly to be there to heat up the Prince's body, and then help "
"hammer him closed afterward. The princess presents your emerald blade, now "
"with glowing runestones etched into its hilt. Hacksmith presses one and the "
"blade glows red, waves of heat scorching the air around it. The doctor tests"
" the blade lightly on his own leg, then takes your potion and dribbles a few"
" drops on the wound. Just as easily as the blade cut stone, your elixir "
"quickly helps his rocky flesh knit back together."
msgstr ""
"Vuelves con el brebaje centelleante y lo llevas al dormitorio convertido en "
"quirófano. Unos cuantos flamberianos se han unido al doctor Hacksmith, "
"aparentemente para calentar el cuerpo del príncipe y luego ayudar a cerrarlo"
" a martillazos. La princesa presenta tu hoja de esmeralda, que ahora tiene "
"piedras rúnicas brillantes grabadas en la empuñadura. Hacksmith pulsa una y "
"la hoja brilla en rojo, con oleadas de calor que abrasan el aire a su "
"alrededor. El doctor prueba la hoja con suavidad en su propia pierna, luego "
"coge tu poción y deja caer unas gotas sobre la herida. Con la misma "
"facilidad con la que la hoja cortó la piedra, tu elixir ayuda rápidamente a "
"que su carne rocosa vuelva a cerrarse."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think we're about ready to begin."
msgstr "Creo que estamos casi listos para empezar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Prince, I apologize that we hardly have an ideal room, staff, or tools to "
"treat you."
msgstr ""
"Príncipe, te pido disculpas: no tenemos ni la sala, ni el personal ni las "
"herramientas ideales para tratarte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Your family is well known to mine, I know I'm in good hands."
msgstr "Tu familia es bien conocida por la mía; sé que estoy en buenas manos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll do my best."
msgstr "Haré todo lo que pueda."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You'd better be alright, Cinny. "
msgstr "Más te vale salir de esta, Cinny. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You say that when you're worse off than me. You're missing a whole arm."
msgstr "Lo dices tú, que estás peor que yo. Te falta un brazo entero."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But I'm stable. They're practially cutting your heart out!"
msgstr ""
"¡Pero yo estoy estable! ¡A ti prácticamente te van a arrancar el corazón!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Cintak pulls the princess close and whispers something in her ear, which seems to help her settle, and blush. You turn away to let the two of them have their moment, but soon enough, everyone's ferried out of the room.\n"
"\n"
"The surgery is long. Several times you and [Companion Name] have to settle Princess Redilok from interrupting, but she hardly seems that intent on entering. Just the idea of having to wait outside and feeling like she can't help further drives her up the wall.\n"
"\n"
"After multiple hours, you begin to hear loud thuds from the Prince's room. Hammering Cintak's chest back closed sounds lightly terrifying, but you trust the Flamberians know their own anatomy better than you do. Eventually, the door swings open, and Hacksmith declares his work done, before handing you the rock of dark twisted metal. After a quick peek to check in on the Prince, you let Redilok stay with him herself, then head back to the workshop to fashion a weapon out of the weird material."
msgstr ""
"Cintak atrae a la princesa hacia sí y le susurra algo al oído, lo que parece calmarla y hacer que se ruborice. Te das la vuelta para dejarles su momento, pero enseguida todos son conducidos fuera de la habitación.\n"
"\n"
"La operación es larga. Varias veces, [Companion Name] y tú tenéis que impedir que la princesa Redilok interrumpa, aunque no parece tener tanto empeño en entrar. Es solo que la idea de tener que esperar fuera y sentir que no puede hacer nada más la saca de quicio.\n"
"\n"
"Tras varias horas, empiezas a oír fuertes golpes en la habitación del príncipe. Que estén cerrando el pecho de Cintak a martillazos suena un poco aterrador, pero confías en que los flamberianos conocen su propia anatomía mejor que tú. Al final, la puerta se abre y Hacksmith declara terminado su trabajo antes de entregarte el trozo de metal oscuro y retorcido. Tras echar un vistazo rápido al príncipe, dejas que Redilok se quede con él a solas y vuelves al taller para forjar un arma con ese extraño material."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you beat the metal rod into a speartip, something becomes distrubingly clear. The metal that was burried inside the prince is alive. [Companion Name] suggests the name Soulsteel, keeping in line with the Soulsmiths' unoriginal naming conventions, and the name sticks. The dwarves in the workshop are more fascinated than horrified by the material and frequently suggest... unconventional smithing methods to combat the metal's unwillingness to take shape the way you want it to. You try hammering it for hours on end, taking turns with [Companion Name] and Kajc. You try etching it in acid, heating it and cooling it in a way that'd make any other metal crack, all to no avail. The only thing that works is when you... speak with it. The Soulsteel doesn't speak back, but it wavers in all sorts of fashions, communicating in a language you haven't got the slightest clue on how to begin desciphering.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually, you manage to learn its version of positive and negative wiggles, you're able to tell it that you intend to kill off the beast it originally came from, to which it seems thrilled. At least, you think that's what it is trying to communicate to you. It stops resisting being shaped and you're able to use it to make the cutting edge of a long, curved blade. You don't like how the metal seems to shiver whenever it is close to something, but you can't think of any other way to cut through the beast it came from. For now, this will have to do."
msgstr ""
"Mientras forjas a golpes la barra de metal para convertirla en una punta de lanza, algo se vuelve inquietantemente claro: el metal que estaba enterrado dentro del príncipe está vivo. [Companion Name] propone el nombre de aceroalmas, en línea con la poco original costumbre de los forjaalmas a la hora de poner nombres, y el nombre se queda. Los enanos del taller están más fascinados que horrorizados por el material y sugieren a menudo métodos de herrería... poco convencionales para combatir la resistencia del metal a tomar la forma que quieres. Intentas martillearlo durante horas, turnándote con [Companion Name] y Kajc. Pruebas a grabarlo con ácido, a calentarlo y enfriarlo de una forma que haría agrietarse a cualquier otro metal, todo en vano. Lo único que funciona es... hablar con él. El aceroalmas no responde, pero ondula de todo tipo de formas, comunicándose en un idioma que no tienes ni la menor idea de cómo empezar a descifrar.\n"
"\n"
"Al final, consigues aprender su versión de los meneos positivos y negativos y puedes decirle que pretendes acabar con la bestia de la que salió, algo que parece entusiasmarlo. Al menos, eso es lo que crees que intenta comunicarte. Deja de resistirse a que le des forma y puedes usarlo para hacer el filo de una hoja larga y curva. No te gusta cómo parece estremecerse el metal cada vez que está cerca de algo, pero no se te ocurre otra forma de atravesar a la bestia de la que salió. Por ahora, tendrá que bastar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ26"
msgstr "MQ26"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Misty Mystery - The Soulsmith's Shambling Beast was last seen dragging its "
"pitiful form north from the center of the Stoneway. As long as it didn't "
"change directions, that'd place it somewhere within the Misty Thicket... an "
"incredibly dense bog covered in a perpectual blanket of mist. The perfect "
"place to go searching for a monster."
msgstr ""
"Misterio brumoso: La Bestia tambaleante de los forjaalmas fue vista por "
"última vez arrastrando su lamentable cuerpo hacia el norte desde el centro "
"de la Vía de Piedra. Si no cambió de dirección, eso la situaría en algún "
"lugar del Matorral brumoso... una ciénaga increíblemente densa cubierta por "
"un manto perpetuo de niebla. El lugar perfecto para ir a buscar a un "
"monstruo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What's going on up here?"
msgstr "¿Qué está pasando aquí arriba?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh my."
msgstr "Madre mía."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It feels good to be outside the caverns that hold the Nalidasi capital, but unfortunately, it's not like your planned adventure is going to be particularly fun. You take in a deep breath of fresh air and wipe off a layer of dust that you're sure has been perptually stuck to your body during your subterranean stay, despite your adherance to basic hygenie. You and [Companion Name] take the time to map out the area, lining up your current position with where the Linking took place, and then plotting the trajectory of where the Shambling Beast could have shuffled off to, assuming it stayed the same course across an unknown amount of distance. It should be somewhere within the Misty Thicket, though you can't begin to wager where, you'll just have to deal with that once you get there.\n"
"\n"
"A long shot, but the best you've got, considering the current circumstances."
msgstr ""
"Sienta bien estar fuera de las cavernas que albergan la capital nalidasi, pero, por desgracia, tampoco es que la aventura que tienes planeada vaya a ser especialmente divertida. Respiras hondo el aire fresco y te quitas una capa de polvo que juras que se te ha quedado pegada al cuerpo durante toda tu estancia subterránea, a pesar de cumplir con la higiene básica. [Companion Name] y tú os tomáis el tiempo de trazar un mapa de la zona, situando vuestra posición actual respecto al lugar donde tuvo lugar el Enlace y trazando luego la trayectoria por donde podría haberse marchado la Bestia tambaleante, suponiendo que mantuviera el mismo rumbo a lo largo de una distancia desconocida. Debería estar en algún lugar del Matorral brumoso, aunque no te atreves a apostar dónde; ya te ocuparás de eso cuando llegues.\n"
"\n"
"Es una posibilidad remota, pero es lo mejor que tienes, dadas las circunstancias."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's... quite a ways away, isn't it?"
msgstr "Está... bastante lejos, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't suppose the Nalidasi have a second, smaller, portable Stoneglider, "
"that doesn't need rails, huh?"
msgstr ""
"Supongo que los nalidasi no tendrán un segundo Deslizalosas, más pequeño y "
"portátil, que no necesite raíles, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It'd be a mix of amazing and terrifying if they did. If I was moving that "
"fast over land, it'd only be a matter of time before I hit something a "
"little too big."
msgstr ""
"Sería una mezcla de asombroso y aterrador que lo tuvieran. Si me moviera tan"
" rápido por tierra, solo sería cuestión de tiempo que chocara con algo "
"demasiado grande."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I imagine it'd look a little like a balloon filled with red paint hitting a "
"wall."
msgstr ""
"Me imagino que se parecería a un globo lleno de pintura roja chocando contra"
" una pared."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe it is best they keep those on rails, eh?"
msgstr "Quizá sea mejor que los mantengan sobre raíles, ¿eh?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's so much distance to cover on foot. We'll have to keep ourselves stocked"
" up along the way."
msgstr ""
"Es muchísima distancia para recorrer a pie. Tendremos que ir abasteciéndonos"
" por el camino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Just like travelling to the capitol! Feels like that was so long ago. I won-"
msgstr ""
"¡Como cuando viajamos a la capital! Parece que fue hace muchísimo tiempo. Me"
" pregun..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Both of you drop into combat position as you hear a shout from the cliffs up"
" above you. Several loud growls and snarls follow, followed by several "
"swears and exclamations of 'bad doggy'. You look to [Companion Name] who "
"shrugs and starts climbing the cliffside."
msgstr ""
"Los dos adoptáis posición de combate al oír un grito en los acantilados de "
"arriba. Le siguen varios gruñidos y rugidos fuertes, y después varias "
"palabrotas y exclamaciones de «¡perrito malo!». Miras a [Companion Name], "
"que se encoge de hombros y empieza a escalar el acantilado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Who's a good monster?"
msgstr "¿Quién es un monstruo bueno?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You are! Yes you are!"
msgstr "¡Tú! ¡Sí, tú!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You weren't too sure what you'd find when you climbed the cliffface, but it wasn't a young Flamberian dwarf being chased by half a dozen Rockwolves. The young man dangles from a twiggy looking tree growing out of the mountainside while Rockwolves jump up to nip at his heels, trying to grab a bite.\n"
"\n"
"The moment that the two of you pull yourselves up over the side, the Rockwolves turn towards you. They snarl and start angling towards the pair of you instead, until a brief moment of familiarity washes over them. A Rockwolf with an outer shell of a sandy-looking stone carefully approaches you, then flips over at your feet in submission. These wolves must have been from the same pack as the one you fought when you first arrived at the Perilous Peaks, it's the only thing that explains their current behavior. The large rock-covered wolves gaze down at you, seemingly waiting for your next move. Some yawn and lay down, or snarl at the Flamberian as he tries to push his way over to you. The Rockwolves are immense creatures, easily twice your size, which make the Flamberian look even smaller in comparison."
msgstr ""
"No sabías muy bien qué te encontrarías al escalar la pared del acantilado, pero desde luego no a un joven enano flamberiano perseguido por media docena de lobos de roca. El joven cuelga de un árbol de aspecto endeble que crece en la ladera de la montaña mientras los lobos de roca saltan para morderle los talones, intentando darle un bocado.\n"
"\n"
"En cuanto los dos subís por el borde, los lobos de roca se giran hacia vosotros. Gruñen y empiezan a acercarse a vosotros en su lugar, hasta que un breve momento de familiaridad los invade. Un lobo de roca con un caparazón de piedra de aspecto arenoso se te acerca con cuidado y luego se tumba panza arriba a tus pies en señal de sumisión. Estos lobos deben de ser de la misma manada que el que combatiste cuando llegaste a los Picos Peligrosos; es lo único que explica su comportamiento actual. Los enormes lobos cubiertos de roca te miran desde arriba, como si esperaran tu siguiente movimiento. Algunos bostezan y se tumban, o le gruñen al flamberiano mientras intenta abrirse paso hasta ti. Los lobos de roca son criaturas inmensas, fácilmente el doble de tu tamaño, lo que hace que el flamberiano parezca aún más pequeño en comparación."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Um... Good doggies?"
msgstr "Eh... ¿Perritos buenos?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I figured they'd be out for revenge after we..."
msgstr "Pensaba que querrían vengarse después de que nosotros..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Took care of the big one."
msgstr "Nos encargáramos del grande."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Seems that we're the big ones, now."
msgstr "Parece que ahora los grandes somos nosotros."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We are? You hardly come up to the things' shoulder."
msgstr "¿Ah, sí? Apenas le llegas al hombro a ese bicho."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Tell that to it. Seems pretty supplicant to me."
msgstr "Díselo a él. A mí me parece bastante sumiso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How in the names of the Great Flame did you two do that? "
msgstr "¿Cómo, en nombre de la Gran Llama, habéis hecho eso vosotros dos? "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We had a run in with their leader a while back, and it seems that they "
"aren't too mad that we... turned it into jerky."
msgstr ""
"Tuvimos un encontronazo con su líder hace un tiempo, y parece que no están "
"muy enfadados porque lo... convirtiéramos en cecina."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Incredible. Animal Behaviorial Specialist Brunite at your service. Humans "
"are a rarity in these parts..."
msgstr ""
"Increíble. Brunite, especialista en comportamiento animal, a vuestro "
"servicio. Los humanos son una rareza por estos lares..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, normally they are, at least. The last time I saw some was actually..."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, normalmente lo son, al menos. La última vez que vi alguno fue, de "
"hecho..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wait. You were at the Linking! You saved our prince!"
msgstr ""
"Un momento. ¡Estuvisteis en el Enlace! ¡Salvasteis a nuestro príncipe!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, we helped out a bit."
msgstr "Bueno, echamos una mano."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Please, please, you're far too modest. I doubt any of us would have gotten "
"out of there alive were it not for your efforts."
msgstr ""
"Por favor, por favor, sois demasiado modestos. Dudo que ninguno de nosotros "
"hubiera salido de allí con vida de no ser por vuestro esfuerzo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And... me doubly so, it'd seem. Thank you for saving me once again."
msgstr "Y... yo el doble, por lo visto. Gracias por salvarme otra vez."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We didn't have to do much, we're able to get a better vantage up here "
"anyway."
msgstr ""
"No tuvimos que hacer mucho; de todos modos, desde aquí arriba tenemos mejor "
"vista."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh? And what are you scouting out, if I may ask?"
msgstr "¿Ah, sí? ¿Y qué estáis explorando, si se puede saber?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're headed out to the Misty Thicket. It'll be quite the journey."
msgstr "Vamos de camino al Matorral brumoso. Será todo un viaje."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What'd you learn about the behaviors of the Rockwolves? That they're hungry?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué has aprendido sobre el comportamiento de los lobos de roca? ¿Que tienen"
" hambre?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, actually, yes."
msgstr "Pues, la verdad, sí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They seem to designate members of their pack to hunt, while others serve "
"other purposes."
msgstr ""
"Parece que designan a algunos miembros de la manada para cazar, mientras que"
" otros cumplen otras funciones."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"For example, the one at your feet there, its stone hide is closely related "
"to sandstone. Hunters will sharpen their teeth by gnawing on its hide, like "
"you'd sharpen your blade on a whetstone."
msgstr ""
"Por ejemplo, el que tienes a tus pies, su piel de piedra es muy parecida a "
"la arenisca. Los cazadores se afilan los dientes royendo su piel, igual que "
"tú afilarías tu espada en una piedra de afilar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Sounds... useful, actually."
msgstr "Suena... útil, la verdad."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They metabolize both meat and stone, with different Rockwolves prioritizing "
"different stone and mineral types to change their hides in accordance with "
"what the pack needs."
msgstr ""
"Metabolizan tanto carne como piedra, y cada lobo de roca prioriza distintos "
"tipos de piedra y mineral para cambiar su piel según lo que necesite la "
"manada."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'd imagine you were acting in self-defense when you fought against the pack"
" earlier. Well, it seems they're missing a handful of crucial roles now."
msgstr ""
"Imagino que actuasteis en defensa propia cuando luchasteis antes contra la "
"manada. Bueno, parece que ahora les faltan unos cuantos papeles cruciales."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe there's something that can be done for your journey..."
msgstr "Quizá se pueda hacer algo para vuestro viaje..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Brunite details his plans. He'd originally wanted to use the wolves as mounts to help his people return back to their home once things were sorted with the Soulsmiths, but maybe with your help, he could expidite his plans, in exchange for letting you bring some of the wolves with you. They already seem plenty docile with you around, what's the harm in trying, right? \n"
"\n"
"You return to the capitol, and run the idea of starting a breeding program for the Rockwolves to the king, who simply laughs and waves his hand, seemingly letting the Archivist write down and deal with aquiring the materials to set up a place to store, raise, and train wolves, assuming they don't break out and eat you."
msgstr ""
"Brunite os detalla sus planes. En un principio quería usar a los lobos como monturas para ayudar a su pueblo a volver a casa una vez resuelto lo de los Forjaalmas, pero quizá con vuestra ayuda podría acelerar sus planes, a cambio de dejaros llevar algunos lobos con vosotros. Ya parecen bastante dóciles cuando estáis cerca, ¿qué hay de malo en intentarlo?\n"
"\n"
"Vuelves a la capital y le planteas al rey la idea de empezar un programa de cría de lobos de roca. Él se limita a reír y hace un gesto con la mano, dejando al parecer que el Archivero lo anote y se encargue de conseguir los materiales para montar un lugar donde guardar, criar y adiestrar lobos, suponiendo que no se escapen y os coman."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I feel soggy and miserable."
msgstr "Estoy calado hasta los huesos y me siento fatal."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I just want to find the beast and get back home."
msgstr "Solo quiero encontrar a la bestia y volver a casa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The wolves are equal parts stone and organic, and with sufficent meat and "
"sources of minerals, they grow much faster than you'd ever expect. In "
"conjunction with preparing a route to the Misty Thicket, you frequently stop"
" in to help Brunite with the Rockwolf study, creating wolves that didn't "
"seem to appear naturally before. Soon enough, by the time you're ready to "
"head out, you have three wolves with hides made of a material similar to "
"quartz, hoping it'd be light enough for travel but hard enough to protect "
"the beasts from any kind of dangerous monsters you may come across in the "
"countryside."
msgstr ""
"Los lobos son a partes iguales piedra y materia orgánica, y con suficiente "
"carne y fuentes de minerales crecen mucho más rápido de lo que jamás "
"esperarías. Mientras preparas una ruta hacia el Matorral brumoso, te pasas a"
" menudo a ayudar a Brunite con el estudio de los lobos de roca, creando "
"lobos que no parecían existir antes en la naturaleza. Al poco tiempo, para "
"cuando estáis listos para partir, tenéis tres lobos con pieles de un "
"material parecido al cuarzo, con la esperanza de que sea lo bastante ligero "
"para viajar pero lo bastante duro para proteger a las bestias de cualquier "
"monstruo peligroso que os encontréis por el campo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I can't believe it! Rockwolves feel like they were made to be domesticated. "
"Most of them are generally of good temperment, and they're so friendly too!"
msgstr ""
"¡No me lo puedo creer! Parece que los lobos de roca estuvieran hechos para "
"ser domesticados. La mayoría tienen buen carácter, ¡y además son muy "
"cariñosos!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Milkbone here hardly stops licking me! I'm shocked at how fast they can grow"
" under controlled conditions, too, it reminds me of growing crystals as a "
"boy."
msgstr ""
"¡Milkbone no para de lamerme! También me sorprende lo rápido que crecen en "
"condiciones controladas; me recuerda a cuando cultivaba cristales de niño."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Are you sure that Milkbone isn't just seeing if you'd be a good addition to "
"her hide? Flamberians are mostly stone, right?"
msgstr ""
"¿Seguro que Milkbone no está comprobando si serías un buen añadido para su "
"piel? Los flamberianos sois casi todo piedra, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... hadn't considered that."
msgstr "No... no lo había pensado."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] be nice, I'm sure she's just a friendly, mostly feral wolf."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name], sé amable. Seguro que solo es una loba cariñosa, salvaje "
"en su mayor parte."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Are you sure you want to join us though, Brunite? The Misty Thicket is a "
"long ways away."
msgstr ""
"¿Seguro que quieres venir con nosotros, Brunite? El Matorral brumoso queda "
"muy lejos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We're just scouting a path and locating that monster that attacked the "
"Linking, but we'll almost definitely get into some trouble at some point."
msgstr ""
"Solo vamos a explorar un camino y localizar al monstruo que atacó el Enlace,"
" pero es casi seguro que en algún momento nos meteremos en líos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And miss the opportunity to see how the first wolves we've bred behave in "
"uncontrolled conditions? Not a chance!"
msgstr ""
"¿Y perderme la oportunidad de ver cómo se comportan los primeros lobos que "
"hemos criado en condiciones no controladas? ¡Ni hablar!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Atop the quartz rockwolves, you make extrodinary time. The beasts are fast, incredibly easy to care for, and defend themselves well enough that you feel comfortable sleeping through the night without anyone on watch. Despite his shaky introduction, Brunite proves to be quite capable while travelling to the Misty Wetlands with you, though he does still jump a bit whenever Milkbone licks him, wondering if [Companion Name]'s joke held any truth.\n"
"\n"
"Finding the Shambling Beast will be like finding a needle in a haystack - and that's if it's even here in the first place - but you trudge into the wetlands regardless. The Misty Wetlands have both mist and wetland in abundance, and you frequently have to stop and cut your way through underbrush or use lumber to cross particularly deep stretches of water, especially with your heavy Rockwolves accompanying you."
msgstr ""
"A lomos de los lobos de roca de cuarzo avanzáis a un ritmo extraordinario. Las bestias son rápidas, muy fáciles de cuidar y se defienden lo bastante bien como para que os sintáis cómodos durmiendo toda la noche sin nadie de guardia. Pese a su accidentada presentación, Brunite demuestra ser muy capaz durante el viaje a los Humedales brumosos, aunque todavía da un respingo cada vez que Milkbone lo lame, preguntándose si la broma de [Companion Name] tenía algo de cierto.\n"
"\n"
"Encontrar a la Bestia tambaleante será como buscar una aguja en un pajar, y eso si es que está aquí, pero aun así os adentráis en los humedales. En los Humedales brumosos abundan tanto la bruma como los humedales, y a menudo tenéis que pararos para abriros paso entre la maleza o usar madera para cruzar tramos de agua especialmente profundos, sobre todo con vuestros pesados lobos de roca acompañándoos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They started it."
msgstr "Empezaron ellos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I wonder what they may have..."
msgstr "Me pregunto qué tendrán..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you sink your axe into yet another tree to cross another endless stretch "
"of water, a flaming bolt glances your shoulder and sinks into the thick "
"bark. You drop your axe and whip your head around to see the burning "
"shilloette of a Flamberian far behind you, with a hefty crossbow held aloft."
" You cry out and everyone dives into the water, narrowly avoiding further "
"projectiles. A volley of similar bolts follows soon after, peppering the "
"ground and trees around you, your party, and mounts. You poke your head out "
"of the water and see [Companion Name] fire a bolt of magic that freezes the "
"water in the air, providing a thin shield against the attacks' bolts."
msgstr ""
"Mientras clavas el hacha en otro árbol más para cruzar otro tramo "
"interminable de agua, un virote en llamas te roza el hombro y se hunde en la"
" gruesa corteza. Sueltas el hacha y giras la cabeza para ver la silueta "
"ardiente de un flamberiano a lo lejos, con una pesada ballesta en alto. Das "
"un grito y todos se tiran al agua, esquivando por poco más proyectiles. Poco"
" después llega una andanada de virotes parecidos que acribilla el suelo y "
"los árboles a tu alrededor, a tu grupo y a las monturas. Asomas la cabeza "
"del agua y ves a [Companion Name] lanzar un rayo de magia que congela el "
"agua en el aire y forma un fino escudo contra los virotes del ataque."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Those look like Flamberians!"
msgstr "¡Parecen flamberianos!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I fear you're right. I hope the two of you are... capable of dealing with "
"them?"
msgstr ""
"Me temo que tienes razón. Espero que vosotros dos seáis... capaces de "
"ocuparos de ellos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If we have to. Any clue on why they're out here, and what problem they'd "
"have with us?"
msgstr ""
"Si no queda más remedio. ¿Alguna idea de por qué están aquí y qué problema "
"tienen con nosotros?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I mean, you're one of them, no?"
msgstr "Bueno, tú eres uno de ellos, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not all Flamberians were too interested in peace with the Naladasi."
msgstr ""
"No a todos los flamberianos les interesaba demasiado la paz con los "
"naladasi."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm sure the defectors have some way of identifying one another, and I'm "
"sure I don't look the part."
msgstr ""
"Seguro que los desertores tienen alguna forma de reconocerse entre ellos, y "
"seguro que yo no doy el perfil."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Any idea on if this will cause any problems for us later on down the line?"
msgstr "¿Alguna idea de si esto nos causará problemas más adelante?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh, I highly doubt it! There's a reason why they're hiding all the way out "
"here."
msgstr "¡Oh, lo dudo mucho! Por algo se esconden tan lejos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Those that are willing to reject the Naladasi with violence aren't welcome "
"in our kingdom."
msgstr ""
"Quienes están dispuestos a rechazar a los naladasi con violencia no son "
"bienvenidos en nuestro reino."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Plus, they fired first."
msgstr "Además, dispararon primero."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That's enough for the two of you. Brunite gets your mounts to cover while "
"you and [Companion Name] do your best to move towards the Flamberians as "
"quietly as you can through the wetland bogs. Shrouded by the mist and "
"setting sun, you're upon them before they even know it. You reach up from "
"the water and drag one of the attackers under, silencing them as quickly as "
"you can. The Flamberian next to him cries out, and the group is thrown into "
"chaos."
msgstr ""
"Con eso os basta a los dos. Brunite pone a cubierto vuestras monturas "
"mientras [Companion Name] y tú hacéis lo posible por avanzar hacia los "
"flamberianos con el mayor sigilo posible a través de las ciénagas. Ocultos "
"por la bruma y el sol poniente, estáis encima de ellos antes de que se den "
"cuenta. Sacas el brazo del agua y arrastras a uno de los atacantes hacia el "
"fondo, silenciándolo lo más rápido que puedes. El flamberiano que está a su "
"lado da un grito y el grupo se sume en el caos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Has to be what we're looking for."
msgstr "Tiene que ser lo que buscamos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Here we are."
msgstr "Aquí estamos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You and [Companion Name] pant in the mist, happy to be done with such messy "
"work. Killing monsters is one thing, but it's always a little bit different "
"to be fighting against human - or human adjacent - opponents, even if "
"they're the aggressors. Brunite brings your rockwolves over once the sounds "
"of fighting die down, trying to avert his eyes from the dead dwarves in the "
"water."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name] y tú jadeáis entre la bruma, contentos de haber terminado "
"un trabajo tan sucio. Matar monstruos es una cosa, pero siempre es un poco "
"distinto luchar contra rivales humanos, o casi humanos, aunque sean ellos "
"los agresores. Brunite trae a vuestros lobos de roca cuando cesan los "
"sonidos de la lucha, intentando apartar la vista de los enanos muertos en el"
" agua."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You two are... efficient."
msgstr "Vosotros dos sois... eficientes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm sorry. They didn't seem to be too interested in talking through things."
msgstr "Lo siento. No parecían muy interesados en hablar las cosas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We didn't have much choice in the matter."
msgstr "No tuvimos mucha elección."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh, don't get me wrong, I won't shed any tears for them."
msgstr ""
"Oh, no me malinterpretéis, no voy a derramar ni una lágrima por ellos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They probably feared we'd give them up to Flamberian authorities if we found"
" them out here, and thought it'd be better to silence us."
msgstr ""
"Seguramente temían que los entregáramos a las autoridades flamberianas si "
"los encontrábamos aquí, y pensaron que era mejor silenciarnos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The two of you are just... "
msgstr "Vosotros dos sois... "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I can't think of many people who could move that quickly and leave that much"
" death in their wake. Regardless of the reason."
msgstr ""
"No se me ocurren muchas personas capaces de moverse tan rápido y dejar tanta"
" muerte a su paso. Sea cual sea el motivo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Brunite grimaces as Milkbone starts to sniff the corpse of one of the "
"attackers, and pulls her away from the body. You and [Companion Name] start "
"to go through the defectors' posessions and find a map and various plans "
"they'd made. Several drafts of ransom notes which lead you to believe they "
"intended to kidnap Prince Cintak at some point... they were ambitious if "
"nothing else. They seemed to have a nearby camp, but what interests you far "
"more is an old ruined castle, the Flamberians had marked, circled, and drawn"
" several warnings of \"Death\" and \"Stay away\" around. Seems like a good "
"place to start your search. As you get closer to the old ruined castle, you "
"find tracks that stick out in the murk. Tracks made by hundreds of pairs of "
"arms."
msgstr ""
"Brunite hace una mueca cuando Milkbone empieza a olfatear el cadáver de uno "
"de los atacantes y la aparta del cuerpo. [Companion Name] y tú empezáis a "
"revisar las pertenencias de los desertores y encontráis un mapa y varios "
"planes que habían trazado. Varios borradores de notas de rescate os hacen "
"pensar que pretendían secuestrar al príncipe Cintak en algún momento... "
"ambición no les faltaba. Parece que tenían un campamento cerca, pero lo que "
"te interesa mucho más es un viejo castillo en ruinas que los flamberianos "
"habían marcado, rodeado con un círculo y llenado de advertencias como "
"«Muerte» y «No os acerquéis». Parece un buen sitio para empezar la búsqueda."
" Al acercaros al viejo castillo en ruinas, encontráis huellas que destacan "
"en el lodo. Huellas hechas por cientos de pares de brazos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The Shambling Beast made a mess of a trail through the Misty Thicket, and you wager you'd be able to follow it all the way out pretty easily, now that you've found its trail. Downed trees, a huge gouge through the ground thats already filled with water, and occasional lumps of flesh are pretty telling that you're on the right track. As you get closer and closer to what you presume would be the castle, the stench of death seems to hang in the air, which is impressive for such a horrid bog that already doesn't smell like a bundle of roses.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you leave Brunite and the Rockwolves behind, trusting in your ability to move more quietly and take up less space than huge beasts with stone for fur. You follow the trail until you find what the Flamberians detailed on their map. Row upon row of corpses are pinned to the outer walls of a ancient castle. All of the bodies are seemingly frozen in space, but doubtlessly alive, since the wall adornments seem to moan and twitch from time to time. The mist-shrouded moat surrounding the castle does little to brighten the image in your mind. You let out an involentary shiver as you gaze up at the macbre sight.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] pulls you away, sure that the monster you're looking for is within the walls. This is definitely not something you can take on alone. It's time to see just how serious King Oyadazminis is about going to war, because it'll take quite the siege to bring down these walls. The journey back is much faster than your journey in, perhaps in part due to the back you know you'll have dry feet for the first time in a while. It's still quite the trek to return to the capitol, but it's comparatively smooth sailing than your trip to the Misty Thicket."
msgstr ""
"La Bestia tambaleante dejó un rastro desastroso a través del Matorral brumoso, y apuestas a que podrías seguirlo hasta el final sin mucha dificultad ahora que lo has encontrado. Árboles derribados, un enorme surco en el suelo ya lleno de agua y algún que otro trozo de carne dejan bastante claro que vais por buen camino. Cuanto más os acercáis a lo que suponéis que es el castillo, más parece flotar en el aire el hedor a muerte, lo cual tiene mérito en una ciénaga tan horrible que ya de por sí no huele precisamente a rosas.\n"
"\n"
"Los dos dejáis atrás a Brunite y a los lobos de roca, confiando en vuestra capacidad para moveros con más sigilo y ocupar menos espacio que unas bestias enormes con piedra por pelaje. Seguís el rastro hasta encontrar lo que los flamberianos detallaban en su mapa. Hileras e hileras de cadáveres están clavadas en las murallas exteriores de un antiguo castillo. Todos los cuerpos parecen congelados en el sitio, pero sin duda están vivos, ya que los adornos de la muralla gimen y se retuercen de vez en cuando. El foso envuelto en bruma que rodea el castillo no ayuda mucho a mejorar la imagen que tienes en la cabeza. Se te escapa un escalofrío al contemplar la macabra escena.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] te aparta, con la certeza de que el monstruo que buscáis está tras las murallas. Desde luego, esto no es algo a lo que podáis enfrentaros solos. Es hora de ver hasta qué punto va en serio el rey Oyadazminis con lo de ir a la guerra, porque hará falta todo un asedio para derribar estas murallas. El viaje de vuelta es mucho más rápido que el de ida, quizá en parte porque sabes que tendrás los pies secos por primera vez en mucho tiempo. Sigue siendo una buena caminata hasta la capital, pero en comparación es coser y cantar frente al viaje al Matorral brumoso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ27"
msgstr "MQ27"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Bring Down The House - The weapon to defeat the Shambling Beast is ready, "
"and a path to the Soulsmith's Ruin is cleared. Prince Cintak and Princess "
"Redilok will lead their people into battle, with you and [Companion Name] at"
" the head. "
msgstr ""
"Derribar la casa: el arma para derrotar a la Bestia tambaleante está lista y"
" se ha despejado un camino hasta la Ruina de los Forjaalmas. El príncipe "
"Cintak y la princesa Redilok guiarán a sus pueblos a la batalla, con "
"[Companion Name] y contigo al frente. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I can't wait to see them in action."
msgstr "Estoy deseando verlos en acción."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We should get some rest."
msgstr "Deberíamos descansar un poco."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The path to the Misty Keep is plotted, a weapon to slay the Shambling Beast is strapped to your back, and things are slowly returning to normal in Koganusan. As you walk through the outer courtyard of the palace, you notice a large number of guards out and training against one another, with the occasional Flamberian even dotting their ranks - holdovers from the Linking that haven't been able to start the trek back to their homeland yet, and have decided to accompany the prince until he sees it fit to return.\n"
"\n"
"When you enter the throne room, King Oyadazminis looks down from his seat with a knowing expression."
msgstr ""
"El camino a la Fortaleza brumosa está trazado, llevas a la espalda un arma capaz de matar a la Bestia tambaleante y las cosas vuelven poco a poco a la normalidad en Koganusan. Al cruzar el patio exterior del palacio, ves a un gran número de guardias entrenando unos contra otros, con algún que otro flamberiano entre sus filas: rezagados del Enlace que aún no han podido emprender el viaje de vuelta a su tierra y que han decidido acompañar al príncipe hasta que él considere oportuno regresar.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando entras en la sala del trono, el rey Oyadazminis te mira desde su asiento con expresión cómplice."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're ready, aren't you?"
msgstr "Estáis listos, ¿verdad?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I believe we are."
msgstr "Creo que sí."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's been many long years since we actively sought dealings with your kind, "
"but what transpired at the Linking has given me much to think about."
msgstr ""
"Han pasado muchos años desde que buscamos tratos con los vuestros, pero lo "
"que ocurrió en el Enlace me ha dado mucho en qué pensar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Though I doubt most humans would be willing to help even a fraction as much "
"as the two of you have, perhaps we've been... avoidant, for far too long."
msgstr ""
"Aunque dudo que la mayoría de los humanos estuvieran dispuestos a ayudar ni "
"una fracción de lo que habéis ayudado vosotros dos, quizá hayamos estado... "
"demasiado tiempo evitándolos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Once those who attacked my people are burried in thier marsh, we'll send an "
"envoy or two around. Let your people know that we'd be willing to entertain "
"more than a few tourists, from time to time."
msgstr ""
"En cuanto quienes atacaron a mi pueblo estén enterrados en su ciénaga, "
"enviaremos a uno o dos emisarios. Decidle a vuestra gente que estaríamos "
"dispuestos a recibir a algo más que unos pocos turistas de vez en cuando."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The world would be much better off for it."
msgstr "El mundo saldría ganando."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You know they would be. We'll see if your fancy nobles can stay standing "
"after a single glass of fine Naladasi liqour."
msgstr ""
"Ya sabes que sí. Veremos si vuestros elegantes nobles se mantienen en pie "
"después de un solo vaso de buen licor naladasi."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But, as much as I'd like to, I can't entertain the thought of festivities "
"yet."
msgstr ""
"Pero, por mucho que me gustaría, todavía no puedo pensar en celebraciones."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We've read over your reports and path to the Soulsmiths' keep."
msgstr ""
"Hemos leído vuestros informes y el camino a la fortaleza de los Forjaalmas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As the king has so kindly promised, our people are at your disposal, though "
"we'll be joining you as well."
msgstr ""
"Como el rey ha prometido tan amablemente, nuestro pueblo está a vuestra "
"disposición, aunque nosotros también os acompañaremos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As will my daughter... Try as I might, she refuses to stay off the "
"battlefield, despite her injuries. The..."
msgstr ""
"Y también mi hija... Por más que lo intento, se niega a mantenerse lejos del"
" campo de batalla, pese a sus heridas. El..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...Prince, seems to have taken a liking to my daughter, and is joining her. "
msgstr "...príncipe parece haberle cogido cariño a mi hija y la acompaña. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We'd be fortunate to have the four of you alongside us, but wouldn't that "
"be... dangerous for you all?"
msgstr ""
"Sería una suerte teneros a los cuatro a nuestro lado, pero ¿no sería eso... "
"peligroso para todos vosotros?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What kind of father would I be if I let my daughter fight my battles for me?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué clase de padre sería si dejara que mi hija librara mis batallas por mí?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The king has also expressed interest in making sure nothing... untoward occ-"
msgstr ""
"El rey también ha mostrado interés en asegurarse de que no ocurra nada... "
"indebi..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Ahem. We've prepared several wagons. I hear that your little breeding "
"program with the Rockwolves has gone well?"
msgstr ""
"Ejem. Hemos preparado varios carros. He oído que vuestro pequeño programa de"
" cría de lobos de roca ha ido bien, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We feel they'd be far better for handling any outdoor excursions than our "
"current beasts of burden. Brunite was more than happy to help create some "
"wolves that could help."
msgstr ""
"Creemos que serían mucho mejores para cualquier salida al exterior que "
"nuestras actuales bestias de carga. Brunite estuvo encantado de ayudar a "
"criar algunos lobos que pudieran servir."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It sounds like we're just about ready then, yes?"
msgstr "Parece que estamos casi listos, ¿no?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll head out to prepare."
msgstr "Vamos a prepararnos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you leave the palace, the most of training guards have already mobilized, with the remainer saluting the two of you as you pass by. You meet Brunite at the caverns set aside for the Rockwolf breeding program, and even he dawns an axe and simple armor. He brings the two of you your wolves, then takes a seat upon Milkbone and takes off down a long line of pens, cutting open the fences as he runs along, a growing pack of Stonewolves following behind him as he charges through the caverns and out of the caverns.\n"
"\n"
"It's a little startling to see just how many wolves can be made in the right conditions, and hope that Brunite hasn't made too much of a fuss in the capitol. Despite the sight, many citizens cheer after you as you race through the city and out into the fresh air above. The pack slows as you step outside to see a large procession of Naladasi with armed wagons, some topped with braziers you imagine are to ward off the mists of the thicket.\n"
"\n"
"There are numerous shouts as you arrive, but not because of you, it's because of the similarly sized horde growing in the distance. A large, orderly rank of Flamberians march towards the Naladasi, carrying large waving banners that make the whole army appear as if they're on fire. You spot Prince Cintak flag down king Oyadazminis, and the two of them march out to meet the army. An hour passes before the army continues its advance, banners now down. Hopefully that's a good thing?\n"
"\n"
"The Prince announces that due to the silence that followed after the Linking, the Flamberians had reason to suspect the Naladasi had attacked the procession and kidnapped him, but he's informed his mother - the queen - of the full situation, and the army that was sent to attack the Naladasi are instead joining them to attack Soulsmiths. Apperently.\n"
"\n"
"The journey back out to the Misty Thicket starts tense, but as more and more stories are traded between the rank and file, the dwarves stoke one another's passion towards their shared enemy, and find themselves growing closer in the process.\n"
"\n"
"The wagons are pulled around to create a wall of sorts a few hours out from the Misty Keep, and you and [Companion Name] keep yourselves busy by helping to prepare the massive bolts that'll be loaded into the ballista-carrying wagons."
msgstr ""
"Al salir del palacio, la mayoría de los guardias que entrenaban ya se han movilizado, y el resto os saluda a los dos a vuestro paso. Te reúnes con Brunite en las cavernas reservadas al programa de cría de lobos de roca, y hasta él se ha puesto un hacha y una armadura sencilla. Os trae vuestros lobos, luego se sube a Milkbone y sale disparado por una larga hilera de corrales, abriendo las cercas a su paso, con una manada cada vez mayor de lobos de piedra siguiéndolo mientras atraviesa las cavernas y sale de ellas.\n"
"\n"
"Resulta un poco inquietante ver cuántos lobos se pueden criar en las condiciones adecuadas, y esperas que Brunite no haya armado demasiado alboroto en la capital. Pese al espectáculo, muchos ciudadanos os vitorean mientras recorréis la ciudad a toda velocidad y salís al aire libre. La manada aminora el paso al salir y veis una gran procesión de naladasi con carros armados, algunos coronados con braseros que imaginas que sirven para ahuyentar la bruma del matorral.\n"
"\n"
"Al llegar se oyen numerosos gritos, pero no por vosotros, sino por la horda de tamaño similar que crece a lo lejos. Una gran formación ordenada de flamberianos marcha hacia los naladasi, con grandes estandartes ondeantes que hacen que todo el ejército parezca estar en llamas. Ves al príncipe Cintak hacer señas al rey Oyadazminis, y los dos salen al encuentro del ejército. Pasa una hora antes de que el ejército siga avanzando, ya con los estandartes bajados. Con suerte, eso es buena señal, ¿no?\n"
"\n"
"El príncipe anuncia que, por el silencio que siguió al Enlace, los flamberianos tenían motivos para sospechar que los naladasi habían atacado la procesión y lo habían secuestrado, pero él ha informado a su madre, la reina, de toda la situación, y el ejército enviado a atacar a los naladasi se une a ellos para atacar a los Forjaalmas. Al parecer.\n"
"\n"
"El viaje de vuelta al Matorral brumoso empieza tenso, pero a medida que las historias se intercambian entre la tropa, los enanos avivan su pasión compartida contra el enemigo común y acaban acercándose en el proceso.\n"
"\n"
"A unas horas de la Fortaleza brumosa, los carros se colocan formando una especie de muralla, y [Companion Name] y tú os mantenéis ocupados ayudando a preparar los enormes virotes que se cargarán en los carros que llevan balistas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I just have to reel them in before the shadows do."
msgstr "Solo tengo que atraparlos antes de que lo hagan las sombras."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We did what we could."
msgstr "Hicimos lo que pudimos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You're pleased to take a bit of time to yourself, even if it is to do more work. The journey over had been long and tiring, constantly riding between the ranks and guiding troops. The Flamberian queen has repeatedly called for your attention, but with as many moving parts as this war procession has had, you simply haven't had the time. Thankfully, Prince Cintak has reassured you that his mother is aware of the stakes and your part in keeping everything moving, and is more than happy to wait. You lay down after having earned your rest, and try to calm your nerves before finally falling to sleep.\n"
"\n"
"After nowhere near enough time, you open your eyes to the daylight, you realize... there shouldn't be daylight. You were in a covered wagon. You look around and notice that four Flamberians have lifted your cot and carried you out in front of the queen. [Companion Name] is in a similarly dazzed, groggy state as yourself, both of you seemingly having been tired and secure enough to sleep through the... basically kidnapping. Prince Cintak stands beside his mother, mortified, and shoots you an apologetic look."
msgstr ""
"Te alegra tener un poco de tiempo para ti, aunque sea para seguir trabajando. El viaje ha sido largo y agotador, cabalgando sin parar entre las filas y guiando a las tropas. La reina flamberiana ha pedido tu atención una y otra vez, pero con tantas piezas en movimiento en esta procesión de guerra, sencillamente no has tenido tiempo. Por suerte, el príncipe Cintak te ha asegurado que su madre es consciente de lo que está en juego y de tu papel para que todo siga en marcha, y que está más que dispuesta a esperar. Te tumbas tras haberte ganado el descanso e intentas calmar los nervios antes de que el sueño te venza por fin.\n"
"\n"
"Al cabo de un tiempo que no se parece en nada a suficiente, abres los ojos a la luz del día y te das cuenta de que... no debería haber luz del día. Estabas en un carro cubierto. Miras a tu alrededor y ves que cuatro flamberianos han levantado tu catre y te han llevado ante la reina. [Companion Name] tiene la misma cara de sueño y aturdimiento que tú; al parecer, los dos estabais lo bastante cansados y os sentíais lo bastante seguros como para dormir durante... prácticamente un secuestro. El príncipe Cintak está junto a su madre, muerto de vergüenza, y te lanza una mirada de disculpa."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It is a pleasure to finally see the faces of my son's saviors. "
msgstr "Es un placer ver por fin los rostros de los salvadores de mi hijo. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I apologize for disrupting your sleep, but I wished to make myself known to "
"you before we are to head into battle alongside one another."
msgstr ""
"Os pido disculpas por interrumpir vuestro sueño, pero deseaba presentarme "
"antes de que entremos juntos en batalla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I- I- Good morning, your excellency, queen..."
msgstr "Yo... yo... Buenos días, excelencia, reina..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Rest, child. I've done away with my name long ago, like all those who ascend"
" to my rank. You may refer to me as the Flame. "
msgstr ""
"Descansa, criatura. Renuncié a mi nombre hace mucho, como todos los que "
"ascienden a mi rango. Puedes llamarme la Llama. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I tried to get her to hold off a while longer, but she was insistant."
msgstr "Intenté que esperara un poco más, pero insistió."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Pleased to meet you, your grace, but... may I ask why you've brought us "
"here?"
msgstr ""
"Es un placer conoceros, alteza, pero... ¿puedo preguntar por qué nos habéis "
"traído aquí?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"From what I've heard, the two of you are the reason my son still breathes. "
msgstr ""
"Por lo que he oído, vosotros dos sois la razón de que mi hijo siga "
"respirando. "

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My nation is in your debt, as am I. Were it not for your efforts, my people "
"would have surely clashed against the Naladasi, and we'd be all the worse "
"for it."
msgstr ""
"Mi nación está en deuda con vosotros, igual que yo. De no ser por vuestro "
"esfuerzo, mi pueblo sin duda se habría enfrentado a los naladasi, y todos "
"habríamos salido perdiendo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We were just doing what is right. The Soulsmiths... they've torn apart so "
"many homes, our own included."
msgstr ""
"Solo hicimos lo correcto. Los Forjaalmas... han destrozado muchísimos "
"hogares, el nuestro incluido."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm just glad we were able to get to him in time."
msgstr "Me alegro de que llegáramos a tiempo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "As am I."
msgstr "Y yo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I just wanted to bring it to your attention that I'm endlessly thankful for "
"your assistance, and for your efforts, I wish to reward you once we return "
"to our homeland. I'd like to-"
msgstr ""
"Solo quería haceros saber que os estoy infinitamente agradecida por vuestra "
"ayuda, y por vuestro esfuerzo deseo recompensaros cuando volvamos a nuestra "
"tierra. Me gustaría..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"She wants to show off that she can give you more than the Naladasi and keep "
"you around as my personal bodyguards."
msgstr ""
"Quiere presumir de que puede daros más que los naladasi y quedarse con "
"vosotros como mis guardaespaldas personales."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, we're flattered, but..."
msgstr "Bueno, nos halaga, pero..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My darling little lava rock is right! You're heroes and should be treated as"
" such! AND I find it outrageous that that cheapskate king has you sleeping "
"in a cart!"
msgstr ""
"¡Mi querida piedrecita de lava tiene razón! ¡Sois héroes y se os debe tratar"
" como tales! ¡Y me parece indignante que ese rey tacaño os tenga durmiendo "
"en un carro!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Are you sure the two of you want to be on the front lines?"
msgstr "¿Seguro que queréis estar en primera línea?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Perhaps the three of you, or four since my precious son seems to have a "
"thing for that cute little Naladasi princess, can wait back here while we "
"level the castle of those rotten Soulsmiths for ever daring to-"
msgstr ""
"Quizá vosotros tres, o cuatro, ya que mi precioso hijo parece estar colado "
"por esa monada de princesa naladasi, podáis esperar aquí atrás mientras "
"arrasamos el castillo de esos Forjaalmas podridos por atreverse a..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh Flames, mother!"
msgstr "¡Por las Llamas, madre!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Shush dear, you can't fault a mother for trying to keep her baby safe."
msgstr ""
"Calla, cielo, no puedes culpar a una madre por intentar proteger a su niño."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Since you're all so determined to join us on the battlefield, see to it that"
" he's safe, will you?"
msgstr ""
"Ya que estáis todos tan decididos a acompañarnos al campo de batalla, "
"aseguraos de que esté a salvo, ¿queréis?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Of course, we'll do our best to make sure as many people make it back alive "
"as we can."
msgstr ""
"Por supuesto, haremos todo lo posible para que vuelva con vida tanta gente "
"como podamos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Please do... I can't lose my son a second time."
msgstr "Hacedlo, por favor... No puedo perder a mi hijo por segunda vez."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The queen seems to be at least partially assuaged by this and nods her head. The Flamberians that carried you out now pick your cots up and carry you back to the wagon, and you try to digest what just happened.\n"
"\n"
"After a couple more hours, the camp begins to shuffle once more. The dwarves break down camp and begin to move out once more. You and [Companion Name] mount your Rockwolves and lead the way, guiding the group across the more percarious bits of terrain and waiting for them to create paths to get wagons across large stretches of water when required. The castle looms in the distance, almost seemingly a source of the Misty Thicket's fog itself. The walls covered in corpses only shake the resolve of the dwarves for a moment, though you hear several utterances of how sick the people inside must be.\n"
"\n"
"Soulsmiths line the walls, along with summoned beasts that remind you of bats, with mouths that are far too large.\n"
"\n"
"Wagons are pulled up to form an armored wall, and then, everyone bursts into motion. Several large balls of energy soar over the walls of Misty Keep, but are burned away by Flamberian mages, or sent far off course by Naladasi mages interferring with their course. Four of the wagons' walls fall away to reveal giant ballista, which are loaded with bolts created just last night. You and [Companion Name] move through the ranks and direct their fire, and the balista shots land true. When they sink into the wall, glowing runestones across their surface glow bright, then explode, ripping large sections of the ancient castle apart. You hear and see King Oyadazminis let out a battlecry as he hefts a large javilen towards the ramparts and snaps his fingers just before contact, causing the bolt to explode in a dazzling ball of light that blows twenty Soulsmiths apart. The Archivist twists his staff in the air and halts another ball of green energy above the army before sending it back over the wall towards whatever sent it in the first place, causing the entire castle to shake with the impact.\n"
"\n"
"Soulsmiths fire all manner of bolt, arrow, and magic towards the dwarves, and they return fire, but the evergrowing swarm of bat-like creatures harass the them. You watch as several dwarves are picked up by the beasts and are dropped into the moat around the castle, where large, dark shadows quickly pull the soliders under the water. Bats are burned away, and more balista shots are loosed at the walls, but with the force you're now taking, one of the balls of green energy makes it through your defenses and crashes into one of the wagons, leaving it a smoldering pile of scrap. The bats grow further in number, and your find a startling number of dwarves being carried away, while the Flamberian Queen seems to be frozen in shock. You grab a length of rope with a hook on the end, meant to scale the walls, and instead use it to fish out a dwarf from the water. Many others around you follow suit, while the back ranks cover you."
msgstr ""
"Esto parece tranquilizar al menos en parte a la reina, que asiente. Los flamberianos que te sacaron recogen ahora vuestros catres y os llevan de vuelta al carro, y tú intentas asimilar lo que acaba de pasar.\n"
"\n"
"Unas horas después, el campamento vuelve a ponerse en movimiento. Los enanos levantan el campamento y se ponen de nuevo en marcha. [Companion Name] y tú montáis en vuestros lobos de roca y abrís camino, guiando al grupo por los tramos de terreno más peligrosos y esperando a que creen pasos para cruzar los carros por grandes extensiones de agua cuando hace falta. El castillo se alza a lo lejos, casi como si fuera el origen mismo de la niebla del Matorral brumoso. Las murallas cubiertas de cadáveres solo hacen flaquear la determinación de los enanos un instante, aunque oyes varios comentarios sobre lo enfermos que deben de estar los de dentro.\n"
"\n"
"Los Forjaalmas cubren las murallas, junto con bestias invocadas que te recuerdan a murciélagos, con bocas demasiado grandes.\n"
"\n"
"Los carros se colocan formando una muralla blindada y, entonces, todo el mundo se pone en movimiento. Varias grandes bolas de energía vuelan por encima de las murallas de la Fortaleza brumosa, pero los magos flamberianos las consumen con fuego o los magos naladasi las desvían muy lejos de su trayectoria. Cuatro de los carros abren sus paredes y dejan al descubierto balistas gigantes, que se cargan con los virotes fabricados la noche anterior. [Companion Name] y tú recorréis las filas dirigiendo el fuego, y los disparos de las balistas dan en el blanco. Cuando se clavan en la muralla, las piedras rúnicas de su superficie brillan con fuerza y luego explotan, arrancando grandes secciones del antiguo castillo. Oyes y ves al rey Oyadazminis soltar un grito de guerra mientras lanza una gran jabalina hacia las almenas y chasquea los dedos justo antes del impacto, haciendo que el proyectil estalle en una deslumbrante bola de luz que despedaza a veinte Forjaalmas. El Archivero gira su báculo en el aire y detiene otra bola de energía verde sobre el ejército antes de devolverla por encima de la muralla hacia lo que la lanzara en primer lugar, y el impacto hace temblar todo el castillo.\n"
"\n"
"Los Forjaalmas disparan toda clase de virotes, flechas y magia contra los enanos, y estos responden al fuego, pero el enjambre cada vez mayor de criaturas parecidas a murciélagos los acosa. Ves cómo las bestias levantan a varios enanos y los dejan caer al foso que rodea el castillo, donde grandes sombras oscuras arrastran rápidamente a los soldados bajo el agua. Los murciélagos arden y se disparan más balistas contra las murallas, pero con la presión que estáis sufriendo, una de las bolas de energía verde atraviesa vuestras defensas y se estrella contra uno de los carros, dejándolo convertido en un montón de chatarra humeante. Los murciélagos son cada vez más, y ves a un número alarmante de enanos siendo arrastrados, mientras la reina flamberiana parece paralizada por la conmoción. Coges un trozo de cuerda con un gancho en el extremo, pensado para escalar las murallas, y lo usas para pescar a un enano del agua. Muchos otros a tu alrededor siguen tu ejemplo, mientras las filas de retaguardia os cubren."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Today, the beast dies."
msgstr "Hoy muere la bestia."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's over."
msgstr "Se acabó."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You do what you can, hauling as many dwarves out of the water as you have time for. Tons of hooks fly into the water once the others catch wind of your idea. You haul up more dwarves than you can count, but as you reel in another, your rope goes taught and is ripped from your hands, then goes slack. Whatever is in the water is very, very, big.\n"
"\n"
"The Flame is ripped from her trance-like state. It wasn't shock, the woman was preparing. The thicket behind the dwarves cracks and screams as a wave of golden fire washes overhead like a wave crashing on the beach. The sky is blotted out by golden flame that sweeps through the air and rips through the majority of the Soulsmiths' bats and crashes against the wall, lighting the corpses ablaze. Where they were still before, the living wall now screams at your forces, with many of them tearing away bits of their body and turning it into balls of black magic which they then pelt you with.\n"
"\n"
"Each one explodes in black flashes with concussive force, sending those they hit to the ground. Another wagon is destroyed as a volley of green magic comes over the wall once more. Soulsmiths atop the wall fire at the undefended dwarves, but both races return with their own bolts in turn. Princess Redilok stands atop one of the balista wagons and charges the bolt that is fired from it. It connects with the south-western tower, and explodes with startling force. The tower groans and collapses due to the damage, Soulsmiths try in vain to jump from its collapsing weight, but land in the water amongst whatever monster they have patrolling the depths."
msgstr ""
"Haces lo que puedes y sacas del agua a tantos enanos como te da tiempo. Montones de ganchos vuelan al agua cuando los demás se enteran de tu idea. Sacas más enanos de los que puedes contar, pero al tirar de otro más, la cuerda se tensa, te la arrancan de las manos y luego se afloja. Lo que sea que hay en el agua es muy, muy grande.\n"
"\n"
"La Llama sale de golpe de su aparente trance. No era la conmoción: la mujer se estaba preparando. El matorral detrás de los enanos cruje y chilla cuando una ola de fuego dorado pasa por encima como una ola rompiendo en la playa. El cielo desaparece tras una llama dorada que barre el aire, arrasa con la mayoría de los murciélagos de los Forjaalmas y se estrella contra la muralla, prendiendo fuego a los cadáveres. Donde antes estaba inmóvil, la muralla viviente ahora chilla a tus fuerzas, y muchos de ellos se arrancan trozos del cuerpo y los convierten en bolas de magia negra que luego os lanzan.\n"
"\n"
"Cada una estalla en destellos negros con una fuerza contundente que tira al suelo a quienes alcanza. Otro carro queda destruido cuando una nueva andanada de magia verde cruza la muralla. Los Forjaalmas de lo alto de la muralla disparan contra los enanos indefensos, pero ambas razas responden con sus propios virotes. La princesa Redilok se sube a uno de los carros con balista y carga el virote que se dispara desde él. Impacta en la torre suroeste y estalla con una fuerza asombrosa. La torre cruje y se derrumba por los daños; los Forjaalmas intentan en vano saltar antes de que se venga abajo, pero caen al agua, entre el monstruo que sea que patrulla las profundidades."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's time! Their forces are scattered!"
msgstr "¡Es la hora! ¡Sus fuerzas están dispersas!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ready the rope bolts!"
msgstr "¡Preparad los virotes con cuerda!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "For those who died at the Linking!"
msgstr "¡Por los que murieron en el Enlace!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "For all the lives the Soulsmiths have claimed!"
msgstr "¡Por todas las vidas que se han cobrado los Forjaalmas!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Only two of the four balista carts still stand, but it's enough. Ropes are already tied to the large bolts which are launched and burried into the top of the drawbridge. Brunite sees to the Rockwolves and orders them to charge away from the keep, pulling the ropes taught. Another pair of bolts are launched. Then another. Then another. You lose another of the carts to a group of Soulsmiths that has flown over the wall atop giant versions of the bats that swarmed you before the golden flames burned the from the sky, but they're eventually cut down.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, the drawbridge gives and comes crashing down. The path into the Misty Keep is open.  Wolves are unteathered and then sent back towards the keep, their stony bodies deflecting some of the smaller projectiles as they crash into the ranks of Soulsmiths on the other side of the gate. Flamberian and Naladasi charge side-by-side across the bridge, some stopping to pull up comrades from the water. As dwarf and Soulsmith fall, an all too familiar sight that brings back memories of the Linking washes over you. A pulse of green light, then the dead begin to move once more. The Shambling Beast is here.\n"
"\n"
"You charge amongst the dwarves with [Companion Name] at your side, and you find yourself face-to-face with a Soulsmith. A butcher. A monster. She raises her staff towards you, but is carved down by Prince Cintak, who leads the charge. The man yells to those around him to clear a path.\n"
"\n"
"The Shambling Beast crawls towards you, endless rows of arms churning the earth beneath it. You lift your Soulmetal-lined Blade and charge through the crowd."
msgstr ""
"Solo dos de los cuatro carros con balista siguen en pie, pero basta. Ya hay cuerdas atadas a los grandes virotes, que se disparan y se clavan en lo alto del puente levadizo. Brunite se ocupa de los lobos de roca y les ordena alejarse a la carrera de la fortaleza, tensando las cuerdas. Se dispara otro par de virotes. Y otro. Y otro. Perdéis otro de los carros a manos de un grupo de Forjaalmas que ha sobrevolado la muralla a lomos de versiones gigantes de los murciélagos que os acosaban antes de que las llamas doradas los borraran del cielo, pero al final acaban con ellos.\n"
"\n"
"Por fin, el puente levadizo cede y cae con estrépito. El camino a la Fortaleza brumosa está abierto.  Desatan a los lobos y los mandan de vuelta hacia la fortaleza; sus cuerpos de piedra desvían algunos de los proyectiles más pequeños mientras se lanzan contra las filas de Forjaalmas al otro lado de la puerta. Flamberianos y naladasi cargan codo con codo por el puente, y algunos se paran a sacar a sus compañeros del agua. Mientras caen enanos y Forjaalmas, te invade una escena demasiado familiar que te devuelve recuerdos del Enlace. Un pulso de luz verde, y los muertos vuelven a moverse. La Bestia tambaleante está aquí.\n"
"\n"
"Cargas entre los enanos con [Companion Name] a tu lado y te encuentras cara a cara con una Forjaalmas. Una carnicera. Un monstruo. Alza su báculo hacia ti, pero el príncipe Cintak, que encabeza la carga, la abate de un tajo. Les grita a los que lo rodean que abran paso.\n"
"\n"
"La Bestia tambaleante se arrastra hacia ti, con interminables hileras de brazos removiendo la tierra bajo ella. Alzas tu hoja revestida de metal de almas y cargas entre la multitud."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With each stroke of your blade, its Soulsteel edge seems to quiver with delight. You find the blade actively pulling towards its source and relishing in the pain it inflicts upon the Shambling Beast. You carve through the beast, the blade pulls you further, and you climb atop the spongey flesh of the creature. \n"
"\n"
"Hundreds of arms grasp at you as it tries in vain to pull you off, but [Companion Name] batters them away, ripping a spike of Soulsteel from the monster and weilding it like a mallet, repeatedly crashing down upon the beast. Your sword continues to delight in cleaving through flesh, but you wrest control of it long enough to drive the sword into cage fused with the back of the Shambling Beast.\n"
"\n"
"With that, another pulse of green light is unleashed and you're thrown from the creature, leaving your sword wedged in the metal of the cage. As you sail through the air, you see the undead begin to drop, but the Soulsmiths fight on. However, without support from the undead, they're far outnumbered by the dwarves. \n"
"\n"
"The Shambling Beast is dead. You've won.\n"
"\n"
"You feel nothing but relief as you crash into the ground, and everything goes dark."
msgstr ""
"Con cada golpe de tu hoja, su filo de aceroalmas parece estremecerse de placer. Notas que la hoja tira activamente hacia su origen y se deleita con el dolor que inflige a la Bestia tambaleante. Atraviesas a la bestia, la hoja te arrastra más allá y trepas sobre la carne esponjosa de la criatura. \n"
"\n"
"Cientos de brazos intentan agarrarte mientras trata en vano de quitarte de encima, pero [Companion Name] los aparta a golpes, arranca un pincho de aceroalmas del monstruo y lo blande como un mazo, descargándolo una y otra vez sobre la bestia. Tu espada sigue deleitándose al cortar carne, pero recuperas el control el tiempo suficiente para clavarla en la jaula fusionada con el lomo de la Bestia tambaleante.\n"
"\n"
"En ese momento se desata otro pulso de luz verde y la sacudida te arroja lejos de la criatura, dejando la espada encajada en el metal de la jaula. Mientras surcas el aire, ves que los no muertos empiezan a caer, pero los Forjaalmas siguen luchando. Sin embargo, sin el apoyo de los no muertos, los enanos los superan con creces en número. \n"
"\n"
"La Bestia tambaleante ha muerto. Habéis ganado.\n"
"\n"
"No sientes más que alivio al estrellarte contra el suelo, y todo se vuelve negro."

